  {:id "2605192330" :title "etzhayyim Extended Land Sovereignty — 海洋 / 河川 / 大気 / 軌道への寄付受付拡張" :status "proposed" :status_note "UNCLOS (海洋) / 水利権 (河川) / Chicago Convention (大気) / Outer Space Treaty (軌道) の各 framework と dual-recognition pattern。stewardship-only claim (operational sovereignty を主張しない) で国際法と整合。S0-S5 段階展開" :path "90-docs/adr/2605192330-etzhayyim-extended-land-sovereignty-ocean-river-air-orbit.md"}
  {:id "2605192345" :title "etzhayyim Steward Succession — donor 死亡時の steward 継承手続き + 多世代 stewardship continuity" :status "proposed" :status_note "donation 時 successor 事前指定 required (primary + backup 2 名以上)。trigger events: 死亡 / 昏睡 / 長期消息不明 / 自発的 step-down / Non-Aligned 認定。Council Lv6+ 3 名以上で activation。fallback paths: council-appointed / corpus-direct / community-trust / dissolution-to-corpus。Multi-generational plan (Gen 1→2→3) 対応" :path "90-docs/adr/2605192345-etzhayyim-steward-succession.md"}
  {:id "2605192400" :title "etzhayyim Eros / Gore Boundary — Council Lv6+ judging framework + LLM-assisted classification + precedent registry" :status "proposed" :status_note "3 層 framework: Layer 1 LLM pre-classification (T1-T5 rubric) → Layer 2 Council Lv6+ 3 名 deliberation (T2/T4 borderline のみ) → Layer 3 Precedent Registry。EthicsContentClassifierCell (Pregel) + Claude Sonnet 4.6 baseline + Murakumo Gemma local fallback" :path "90-docs/adr/2605192400-etzhayyim-eros-gore-council-judging.md"}
  {:id "2605192415" :title "etzhayyim Religious-Corp Daemon Architecture — Pregel cell catalog + 3階層 actor hierarchy + Murakumo 常駐化 + LangGraph 実行 roadmap" :status "proposed" :status_note "15+ religious-corp cells を catalog: CharterAttestation* (3) / Land* (4) / Economic (5) / Force (2) / Ethics (1) / Membership (2) / CouncilDeliberation (1, generic)。Tier A (Per-Adherent PhenotypeAgent) / Tier B (Per-Domain leader+replica) / Tier C (Per-Decision Council)。Murakumo 12-tribes Mac mini fleet 上 launchd 常駐 + kotodama CLI 実行 + cell-key quarterly rotation。S0-S11 testnet deploy roadmap" :path "90-docs/adr/2605192415-etzhayyim-religious-corp-daemon-architecture.md"}
  {:id "2605201400" :title "etzhayyim kuni-umi (国生み) — planetary-scale infrastructure robotics fleet actor" :status "proposed" :status_note "labor_liberation pillar の最大 throughput path。orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kuni-umi/ (Tier B per-domain leader) + 6 cells (site_survey / deployment_planning / construction_orchestration / commissioning / audit_witness / decommission) + 6 lexicons (com.etzhayyim.apps.etzhayyim.kuniUmi.*) + 3 DMN (jurisdiction-eligibility / counterparty-classification / proportionality-check) + BPMN scaffold。open-* utility lexicons (denki/gas/water/network/power/rail/airplane/ports) × open-robo (Giemon Otete/Mimi/Te/Atama) × open-ot (WASM PLC IEC 61499) × UNSPSC 18,345 agent fleet を貫通する施工 workflow を 4 phase Pregel super-step で orchestrate。Land sovereignty (terrestrial + ocean + river + atmosphere + orbit) + Charter Rider §2 + 三層 enforcement + Witness N>=2 invariant を constitutional gate として実装。S0 (本 ADR) → S1 solo survey → S2 single-utility prototype (community microgrid) → S3 multi-utility → S4 multi-site fleet → S5 extended sovereignty" :path "90-docs/adr/2605201400-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-planetary-infra-fleet.md"}
  {:id "2605201500" :title "kuni-umi S1 — solo survey (1 Giemon Otete + 1 Mimi stationary witness base-station + SiteSurveyCell live)" :status "proposed" :status_note "kuni-umi S0 spec の最小 viable 実物検証。Single Otete (mobile RGB-D/LIDAR) + Mimi tripod base-station (chem/multispectral/camera) で N=2 witness invariant を最小コストで満たす。Target plot: 山中湖 LandRegistry donation (LandDonationProcessingCell も同時 validate)、寒冷期は Tokyo workshop garden 代替。SiteSurveyCell cell.py reference + 8 acceptance criteria + 7 risks/mitigations + hardware/DID provisioning checklist。S1 PASS → S2 (community microgrid single-utility prototype) へ。施工なし — survey のみ。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605201500-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-s1-solo-survey.md"}
  {:id "2605201600" :title "kuni-umi S2 — community microgrid (1 MW class single-utility electric prototype, kuni-umi Phase 2–4 × open-ot 7 loops end-to-end)" :status "proposed" :status_note "kuni-umi が初の real-capital deployment を実行する milestone。University campus 1 MW microgrid を target topology に、open-ot PROTOTYPE-MICROGRID.md §1 (asset inventory 9 種) + §2 (7 loops) + §3 (8 FBType, 3 implemented) を end-to-end commission。Giemon fleet: 6 Otete + 8 Mimi + 2 Hitogata (humanoid 別 ADR 発注 critical-path)。BoM USDC 1.5-2M + fleet CAPEX USDC 200k + 20% contingency = total USDC 2.3-3.1M。Phase 2 で governance vote (population > 100) + Public Fund grant evaluation の 2 escalation 必須。Construction: 8 sub-phase × 10-12 weeks。Commissioning: 7 open-ot loops 順次起動 + 90-day pilot acceptance。10 acceptance criteria + 9 risk/mitigation + donation-only 制約下での energy-cost-recovery path (Public Fund operating grant default)。Constitutional alignment 9 article 全て pass。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605201600-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-s2-community-microgrid.md"}
  {:id "2605201701" :title "kuni-umi S3 — multi-utility integrated (electric + water + network on S2 site, BoM consolidation algorithm + cross-utility witness coordination + multi-target commissioning)" :status "proposed" :status_note "S2 site 上に water (open-water reservoir + mains + AMI 80) + network (open-network PoP + 8 distribution + Wi-Fi 7 mesh) を overlay、religious-corp の utility trinity を同一 community に提供する pattern を確立。BoM consolidation algorithm (OR-Tools CP-SAT MIP solver + 4 shared-op rules: trench/conduit/building-entry/scaffold; Charter Rider + counterparty + 国内 supply preference constraints; 15% savings target) で ADR-2605201400 Open Question 3 解消。Cross-utility witness: 12 cluster simultaneous (electric 4 + water 3 + network 5 + shared-op 2)、shared-op で per-utility independent signature invariant。Multi-target commissioning: open-ot continuation × open-water steward handover × open-network NMS handover の 3 destination 並行。Fleet: 12 Otete + 12 Mimi + 4 Hitogata (humanoid +2 別 ADR 追加発注)。Construction: 8 sub-phase × 7-9 weeks (shared trench で工期短縮)。Budget: +USDC 1.5-2.1M (cumulative USDC 3.8-5.2M)。13 acceptance criteria + 9 risk + 6 open questions。Constitutional alignment 9 article 全 pass。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605201701-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-s3-multi-utility.md"}
  {:id "2605201801" :title "kuni-umi S4 — multi-site fleet (≥5 archetype concurrent sites, fleet rebalance algorithm, cross-site BoM consolidation, Pregel-native edge orchestration, Quad introduction)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Religious-corp が point organization から fleet of sites への qualitative scaling milestone。5 archetype: A university (継続) / B rural (山中湖 expansion) / C religious community (神社・寺・教会 partnership) / D workers' cooperative (生協・漁協・農協) / E disaster recovery (能登・東日本 復興地)。FleetRebalanceCell (新規 cell on naphtali) が weekly Hungarian-method assignment を実行、Constitutional filter で witness invariant + Council inter-prefecture gate enforce。Cross-site BoM consolidation (3 ヶ月 horizon batch quotes + shared-logistics MIP, ≥20% savings target)。Edge orchestration: per-site Atama (NixOS RT + LangGraph + Wasmtime) + NATS JetStream over CF Tunnel; constitutional invariant 'no site→site direct mesh, Murakumo Tier 1 as single root of trust' を新規導入 (federation refusal)。Council Lv6+ supermajority on fleet portfolio composition の新規 constitutional gate。Council 5 seat に per-archetype primary responsibility 割当。Quad v1 (4-leg, 4 units) 初投入、open-robo 別 ADR 発注 critical-path。Fleet: 20 Otete + 6 Hitogata + 24 Mimi + 4 Quad = 54 robots。Budget +USDC 6.3-8.8M (cumulative USDC 10.1-14.0M)。15 acceptance criteria + 11 risk/mitigation + 6 open questions。Constitutional alignment 10 article 全 pass。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605201801-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-s4-multi-site-fleet.md"}
  {:id "2605201900" :title "kuni-umi S5 — extended sovereignty deployment (S5a river / S5b ocean / S5c atmosphere / S5d orbit, stewardship-only invariant, 4 new robot classes, final roadmap phase)" :status "proposed" :status_note "kuni-umi roadmap 最終 phase。Religious-corp が ADR-2605192330 extended sovereignty doctrine を physical deployment で初めて exercise する definitional moment。4 sub-stage 段階展開 (international complexity ascending): S5a river (河川法 + 水利使用許可) → S5b ocean (UNCLOS coastal + 漁協 partnership) → S5c atmosphere (Chicago Conv. + ICAO HAPS) → S5d orbit (OST + 宇宙活動法 + ITU + JAXA launching state)。Stewardship-only operational invariant: religious-corp は ownership field 持たず、sovereign state authority と dual-recognition pattern で coexist; international conflict 時は state authority に最終 deferral (mission.parallel_governance_to_state ↔ §1.12.A 解釈)。4 new robot class: Suii (water/amphibious crawler) / Tairyou (marine surface + ROV) / Sora (HAPS install) / Hoshi (cleanroom satellite integration, NOT in-space)。Witness invariant adapted for remote domains (S5b 3-witness surface+ROV+onshore; S5d satellite onboard + 2 ground stations)。Budget: USDC 12.7-28.4M (orbital launch dominate)、religious-corp Treasury sensitivity 極限値、S5d defer option を constitutional に許容。Cumulative S1-S5: USDC 22.8-42.4M capex + ongoing 1.85-3.55M USDC/yr。Constitutional alignment 10 article 全 pass、§parallel_governance の definitional moment。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605201900-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-s5-extended-sovereignty.md"}
  {:id "2605202100" :title "kotodama-cell-runner launchd LaunchAgent — operationalising Tier 1 常駐稼働 on the Murakumo fleet" :status "proposed" :status_note "ADR-2605192415 §7.1 + ADR-2605201400-1900 (kuni-umi S0-S5) で spec 完成済みの religious-corp + kuni-umi daemon を Murakumo Mac mini fleet で 常駐起動するための OS-level boot path を closure。3 artefact: (1) 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/pyproject.toml に `[project.scripts] kotodama-cell-runner = kotodama.cell_runner_main:main` 追加で CLI を PATH-resolvable に、(2) 50-infra/cluster/murakumo/cell-runner/com.etzhayyim.kotodama-cell-runner.plist を @@PLACEHOLDER@@ 形式 template として固定 (litellm/ameno-daemon plist と同 pattern、no personal paths in git per GitGuardian lesson)、(3) install.sh が --node 12-tribe allowlist 検証 + uv sync + --health pre-flight check + bash parameter expansion 経由 placeholder substitution + sanity gate (@@-marker residue check) + idempotent launchctl reload。`start_cell` の subprocess spawn / MstCheckpointSaver / MST listener / healthz / swarm heartbeat は引き続き staged TODO — 本 ADR scope は OS-level boot path のみ。Plutil syntax + bash substitution + kotodama-cell-runner --health smoke 全 PASS 検証済 (2026-05-20 dev laptop)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605202100-etzhayyim-kotodama-cell-runner-launchd.md"}
  {:id "2605211845" :title "etzhayyim org cleanup completion + kami-engine-sdk standalone publication" :status "accepted" :status_note "Closes the long-running etzhayyim [MOVED → etzhayyim/root] cleanup. 15 MOVED-tagged repos physically deleted (0 remaining). public-global was MOVED-tagged but never actually imported — fetched into 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-public-global/ before deletion to reconcile the description (commit 690135d3). kami-engine-sdk republished as standalone read-only mirror at github.com/etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk (monorepo SoT preserved); npm scope renamed @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk → @etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk in 7 files (commit d302f274). Standalone-mirror policy = explicit one-by-one decision, no bulk; kami-engine-sdk is the only carve-out at the time of this ADR. Operational note: a concurrent 6-wave religious-corp cell substrate commit plan (yoro / shinka / etzhayyim-sdk-py / joucho / council + cross-cutting) committed 5 waves (64804ab2..0b6bfa55) to PR #254 but the cross-cutting wave was lost to a parallel git reset --hard origin/main; PR #254 closed without merge in favour of the user's parallel reconstruction. SUPERSEDED (kami-engine-sdk only, 2026-06-01, ADR-2606011500 stage 1 / PR #655): the 'monorepo SoT + read-only mirror' arrangement is INVERTED — kami-engine-sdk converted subrepo → git-submodule pinned at etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk@ccb315c, which is now the source of truth; the monorepo tracks it via gitlink." :path "90-docs/adr/2605211845-etzhayyim-org-cleanup-completion-and-kami-engine-sdk-standalone.md"}
  {:id "2605222330" :title "etzhayyim.com substrate violation — transition window" :status "accepted" :status_note "Documents the current transient Charter §2 substrate violation introduced this session to unblock the yoro UI on etzhayyim.com. Five fixes shipped (bundle hashes / ad-tech URL scrub / xrpc-proxy worker / Kysely guard soften / apex /xrpc routing + GET→POST normalization) restore visible UI but at the cost of: (a) 100% etzhayyim.com DID corpus (0 etzhayyim.com actors) still served from Kotoba/Datomic via softened ADR-2605111200 guard, (b) MST + IPFS + Base L2 anchor substrate not yet wired, (c) deployed bundle still contains AdSense/GA4/ExoClick code paths (URLs noop'd at runtime but source not yet rebuilt). Five hard exit criteria recorded. Authoritative for the runtime substrate state until superseded." :path "90-docs/adr/2605222330-etzhayyim-com-substrate-violation-transition-window.md"}
  {:id "2605231100" :title "karute.etzhayyim.com — FHIR R5 EMR Phase 1" :status "proposed" :status_note "Adds the electronic medical record (電子カルテ) actor on the etzhayyim kotoba substrate. PHI flows through the ADR-2605181100 encrypted envelope (`com.etzhayyim.encrypted.record` with `innerType = com.etzhayyim.karute.*`); public meta + LOINC/ICD-10/RxNorm codes + DIDs + timestamps live plaintext for discovery and timeline construction. 7 inner-type FHIR R5 lexicons (patient/encounter/soapNote/observation/condition/medicationRequest/serviceRequest) + 13 XRPC contracts (7 create procedures + 6 query methods + healthKarute + chartSummary + fhirBundle export + terminologyBinding/coverageSnapshot/referral public records). 3-axis split: Liability/Custody/Settlement all resolve to etzhayyim. Drug-drug interaction check runs as upstream agent.chat step on createMedicationRequest with contraindication-blocks-default semantics. SuperApp mobile-first Svelte 5 UI scaffolded (Home / Chart / Orders / Talk tabs, SOAP editor with S/O/A/P blocks, RxComposer with InteractionAlert override flow, VitalsForm with LOINC-coded refs + interpretation, FHIR R5 Bundle export assembler client-side). Phase 1 ships actor manifest + lexicons + ADR + UI scaffold; Phase 2 (lefthook PHI-plaintext-guard hook, consent-capability ADR + iryo billing bridge, pharmacy dispense, on-device SOAP-assist) deferred." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231100-karute-emr-phase1.md"}
  {:id "2605231401" :title "karute consent capability + iryo billing bridge" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closes the substrate hop between etzhayyim (PHI custody, USDC self-pay) and vendor iryo.etzhayyim.com (Kotoba/Datomic + Stripe + DPC/DRG insurance billing) without weakening the 3-axis-split rule (ADR-2605172400). Introduces `com.etzhayyim.consent.capability` — an Ed25519-signed delegation token (granter/grantee/purpose/scope/expiresAt/constraints) stored as a public AT Protocol record in the granter's PDS. 6 purpose values (insurance-billing / second-opinion / data-portability / research-deidentified / emergency-disclosure / legal-disclosure). XRPC surface (4): grantConsent / revokeConsent / listConsent / requestIryoBilling. Actor manifest pipelines added for all 4. PatientPortalView grant/revoke UI integrated. Single primitive serves clinician-peer second opinion, vendor billing bridge, patient-initiated portability, research opt-in. Constitutional guarantees preserved: vendor calls remain progressive enhancement; substrate boundary unchanged; capability metadata public (signature verifiable) but record ciphertext still requires key-wrap. Revocation observable but not retroactive — mitigated by audit webhook + downstream-redistribution constraint." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231401-karute-consent-capability-iryo-bridge.md"}
  {:id "2605231603" :title "Per-record rekey + tombstone protocol" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closes ADR-2605181100 §5.3 (group rekey on member removal) + §5.4 (forward-secrecy follow-up) for the etzhayyim substrate. Introduces `com.etzhayyim.encrypted.tombstone` — an Ed25519-signed record that binds prior↔successor envelope CIDs (3 kinds: `rekey`/`redact`/`sealed`) with 3 scopes (`single-record`/`channel-window`/`group-rekey`). Karute XRPC surface (3): `rekeyRecord` / `redactRecord` / `listTombstones`. Logical-present view algorithm specified for consumers. Consent-revocation-flush protocol formalized — `revokeConsent` triggers automated rekey of every envelope whose key-wrap set included the revoked grantee. Forward secrecy guarantee: new readers cannot decrypt prior records under rekey'd keys. Limitation acknowledged: cached-key recipients retain access to historical ciphertext (fundamental cryptographic limit — mitigated by contractual obligation + audit webhook event flow). Charter-authorized override path exists for `regulator-order` reason." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231603-per-record-rekey-tombstone-protocol.md"}
  {:id "2605231700" :title "Audit webhook subsystem (constitutional observability)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closes the consent observability gap from ADR-2605231400 §'Revocation semantics' + ADR-2605231603 §'Audit emission'. Introduces `com.etzhayyim.audit.event` — a typed, PHI-free, Ed25519-signed, hash-chained event record written to the subject's PDS (typically the patient). 13 eventType values cover consent.{granted,revoked,invoked,expired} / encrypted.{write,read,keyWrap.issued,keyWrap.refused} / tombstone.{rekey,redact,sealed} / billing.{requested,claim.statusChanged} / phi.guard.violation. `auditChainPrev` forms a per-(actor, subject) hash chain detecting silent omission. Per-(subject) timeline aggregates events from every actor that touches their data, enabling clinician-licensure board / regulator subpoena patterns. Karute XRPC `listAuditEvents` exposes the timeline. PatientPortalView audit-log card displays the feed. Events are public-within-subject-PDS by design — PHI-aware redaction deferred to Phase 4." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231700-audit-webhook-subsystem.md"}
  {:id "2605231900" :title "karute deployment topology — DID Worker + LangServer Pod + CF Pages" :status "proposed" :status_note "Operationalizes karute (ADR-2605231100/1400/1603/1700) by specifying the concrete CF Worker + k3s Pod + CF Tunnel + CF Pages layout. Single public origin `karute.etzhayyim.com` resolves three concerns: `/.well-known/did.json` (DID Document, served by karute-did-web Worker), `/xrpc/*` (proxied to lg-karute Pod via CF Tunnel `karu7t3e.etzhayyim.com`), and `/*` (Svelte SuperApp static bundle on CF Pages). lg-karute Pod uses the 2-container ADR-2605171800 pattern (Python langgraph server + TS @etzhayyim/sdk-checkpointer sidecar) with PHI sealing mandatory (ETZ_CHECKPOINTER_ENCRYPT_CELLS=did:web:karute.etzhayyim.com). PVC 16Gi ReadWriteOnce Retain. Pregel module ships as Phase 1 stub at `kotodama.projects.karute.pregel:app` — 31-pipeline StateGraph that mirrors actor-manifest.edn nodes; every node returns `{status: stub}` until substrate seams wire in Phase 3. ALSO provisions `did:web:audit.etzhayyim.com` DID Worker (closes ADR-2605231700 substrate-wide audit-target gap — every actor's emission step now has a real target). End-to-end deploy: `50-infra/karute-deploy.sh` orchestrates 6 stages (did-worker / audit-worker / k8s-pod / cf-tunnel / pages-deploy / smoke) with idempotent --only flags." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231900-karute-deployment-topology.md"}
  {:id "2605232000" :title "Agent-led autonomous deploy — e7m actor + e7m agent-token + capability-gated authority" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closes the 'how does an autonomous agent actually deploy a new actor?' gap. (1) Declarative `actor.toml` per actor — read by `etzhayyim actor deploy --actor <name>` (Go implementation in 70-tools/etzhayyim-cli/actor.go). Stages typed (cf-worker / cf-pages / k8s / docker-build / cf-tunnel / cmd / smoke) with `require_cap` scope NSIDs. (2) `etzhayyim agent-token --lxm <nsid> --ttl <sec>` mints Ed25519-signed JWS (single scope per token, max TTL 3600s); signing key from macOS Keychain or --key-file. (3) `com.etzhayyim.consent.capability` purpose enum extended with `deploy-execution` — Steward issues a 24h capability binding agent DID to a scope set; e7m actor deploy gates each stage against the capability. 3-tier credential model: T1 cloud-provider creds (CF API token / GHCR PAT / k8s context, long-lived from 1Password), T2 deploy capability (hours-to-day, PDS record, revocable), T3 scoped per-call JWS (60-300s, in-memory). Every stage emits a `DEPLOY_EVENT` audit row (Phase 1: stderr structured JSON; Phase 2: POST to audit.etzhayyim.com aggregator). Smoke verified: `etzhayyim actor deploy --actor karute --dry-run --only pages-build` parses actor.toml, evaluates the stage, emits DEPLOY_EVENT, completes. JWT mint verified: `etzhayyim agent-token --lxm deploy.cfWorker:karute-did-web --ttl 300 --key-file test.b64` produces a valid Ed25519 JWS decodable by the standard `jwt`/`jose` libraries. 2 new lexicons (com.etzhayyim.deploy.agentToken, com.etzhayyim.deploy.deployEvent)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605232000-agent-led-autonomous-deploy.md"}
  {:id "2605231230" :title "etzhayyim-esign actor — DID-bound, MST-recorded, L2-anchored document signing" :status "proposed" :status_note "Religious-corp native replacement for DocuSign / Adobe Sign / RazorpaySign. Phase 0 closed this session: 7 lexicons under com.etzhayyim.esign.* (envelope/signature/completedEvent/anchoredEvent records + requestEnvelope/signEnvelope/declineEnvelope procedures), actor scaffold at orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-esign/ (procedures return 501 NotYetImplemented), DID Worker scaffold + deployed at 50-infra/etzhayyim-esign-did-web/ (route esign.etzhayyim.com/.well-known/did.json bound at CF, Worker version cfb3b6c0). DNS for esign.etzhayyim.com (AAAA @=100:: proxied) still missing on the etzhayyim.com zone — Worker unreachable from public DNS until that one-time CF dashboard step lands. etzhayyim lawfirm DocuSign passthrough (com.etzhayyim.apps.lawfirm.eSign*) retained but scoped to fiat receipts + India counsel intake only (ADR-2605192115 §4); religious-corp documents MUST use com.etzhayyim.esign.*. Phase 1 wires requestEnvelope through @etzhayyim/sdk + ipfs-pinner for Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP minutes (deadline 2026-06-19); Phase 2 adds Base Sepolia anchor via EsignAnchor.sol; Phase 3 adds mainnet + geth-private mirror; Phase 4 integrates Adherent SBT mint affirmation." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231230-etzhayyim-esign-actor-did-bound-mst-anchored.md"}
  {:id "2605231451" :title "Level System Unification — society6 Kyu/Dan canonical scale + 信者 7段 + dojo 帯 + joucho S-D 正規化 + 自他非分離体験ゲート" :status "proposed" :status_note "Person rank の SoT を society6 Kyu 6 → Dan 10 に固定。信者 7段 (MEMBERS.md 誓/修/献/証/護/議/老) と dojo 帯 (白〜Shihan3 = Kyu 7-1 + Dan 1-5 + Shihan 1-3) を society6 Kyu/Dan に正規化。joucho S-D は object-axis として person rank に非変換 (Wellbecoming = 動的軌跡 invariant)。Elder ↔ Dan 10 peg を信者経由のみに限定し、Council/Elder の意思決定権を Charter 軌道に揃える。D6 自他非分離体験ゲート (Non-Duality Embodiment Gate) を Kyu 1 → Dan 1 の一度きり追加: 反個人主義 ontology / 縁起 / 万人祭司 を概念ではなく身体で知っていることを Dan 領域 entry の前提とする。Accepted methods は Default path (瞑想 Vipassana/Zazen/内観, ブレスワーク Holotropic/SOMA/Wim Hof, 感覚遮断, 断食/修行) + Sacramental path (アヤワスカ Santo Daime/UDV/curandero, シロシビン 米国オレゴン/豪/カナダ例外, ペヨーテ/サン・ペドロ NAC等) — Council Lv6+ ≥3 multisig で拡張可。Attestation は新 Lexicon com.etzhayyim.apps.etzhayyim.nonDualityAttestation (本 ADR で予約) を self-attested AT Record + (optional but recommended) Dan+ witness DID counter-signature で記録 (信者 Lv4 証 shou と同 pattern)。§D6.5 法的明示: 日本国内 DMT/シロシビンは controlled、§1.12 Transparent Religious Force routing-around は個人薬物使用を免責しない、Default path のみで完全通過可能。D6.7 Council challenge は ≥30-day appeal window + Council ≥3 multisig 判定で invalid 時は Dan-derived 権限失効。:S6Rank ノードに dojo_belt / shinja_lv / non_duality_attested を derived property として保持、:NonDualityAttestation label を新設。Follow-up: Lexicon JSON 起草、society6 watcher で EtzhayyimMembership.join() + nonDualityAttestation を subscribe、dojo UI と society6 UI の Dan 表記一致、Yoro Auth Gate の 信者 CTA → joining ritual wiring (mode=adherent flow)。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605231451-level-system-unification.md" :depends_on ["2605172600" "2605192100" "2605192230"] :related ["MEMBERS.md" "20-actors/society6/CLAUDE.md" "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-dojo/CLAUDE.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-joucho/CLAUDE.md"]}
  {:id "2605231501" :title "agent-driven UNSPSC supply flows — business-model wiring for 18,346-actor commodity automation" :status "proposed" :status_note "Defines the canonical wiring between the 18,346 UNSPSC LangGraph actors (commit 9cd4fe73d) and the religious-corp economic-body contracts (Charter / Tithe / Public Fund / Force / Sanctions / Council / Surplus Router / Wellbecoming). Introduces the AgentAuthorityToken (AAT) — a soulbound ERC-721+ERC-5192 token analogous to AdherentRegistry but for AI agents, minted by a Steward who holds an Adherent SBT. Four canonical purposes (donation-in-kind / internal-allocation / surplus-routing / operational-supply) extend the esign purpose enum; purchase/sale/subscription remain prohibited. Charter-compliance gate library (charters / sanctions / force / counterparty / eros-gore) ships as TS stubs with NotImplementedError; production stubs reach Phase 4. Phase 1 landed this session: 2 new lexicon namespaces (com.etzhayyim.agent.authority + com.etzhayyim.unspsc.processManifest) + esign envelope/requestEnvelope/signature extensions + AgentAuthorityToken.sol Foundry scaffold (11/11 forge tests passing) + charter-compliance-gate.ts library scaffold + ADR. Phases 1.5/2/3/4 deferred. Initially authored as 2605231400 but renumbered to 2605231500 to avoid ID collision with kotoba-datomic ADR registered at the same minute." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231501-etzhayyim-agent-driven-unspsc-supply-flows.md"}
  {:id "2605231525" :title "No-Server-Key Religious-Corp Architecture — etzhayyim infra holds zero signing capability; member-write model + 5-stage flip roadmap" :status "proposed" :status_note "Constitutional invariant: etzhayyim-operated infrastructure (Workers, K8s pods, CronJobs, CI runners, hosted bots) MUST NOT hold private keys, signing tokens, or master credentials. All writes are signed by the member, donor, contributor, or community operator. etzhayyim provides public read surfaces only (AT firehose relay, kotoba-datomic-projection L0 indexer, DID Document serving via Council-Safe-signed static blob, lexicon publication, contract verification via read-only RPC, IPFS pinning, static asset serving). 13-row server-secret inventory enumerated (YATA_DONATE_PRIVATE_KEY / DATABASE_URL / B2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / B2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY / MAPILLARY_ACCESS_TOKEN / RUNPOD_API_KEY / ODPT_API_KEY / EMBED_AUTH_TOKEN / SS_REPO_SIGNING_KEK / AUTH_KEYS_KEK / RESEND_API_KEY / DISPATCHER_INTERNAL_SECRET / YATA_AGENT_ADMIN_KEY) with per-row member-write replacement. 5-stage flip roadmap: A USDC signer removal (donate.ts verify-only via Base L2 RPC; EIP-1193 wallet flow in Studio billing + auth sign-up — APPLIED), B bulk-ingest community-operator handover (13 maps pods republished to etzhayyim-community/*, ETZHAYYIM_SUBSTRATE_MODE=mst, relay subscribe — scaffold APPLIED, GitHub org creation pending), C identity-signing devolution (did:web:etzhayyim.com multi-controller with Council 5-of-7 Safe via ERC-1271, did:web:authn.etzhayyim.com per-agent device-generated ES256, SS_REPO_SIGNING_KEK 30-day quarantine drop — Stage C-1 scaffold APPLIED, C-2/C-3/C-4 pending Council ratify), D external-API liability handover (RESEND/B2/Mapillary/RunPod/ODPT/EMBED to community-operator-owned credentials — scaffold APPLIED), E internal-HMAC dissolution (DISPATCHER_INTERNAL_SECRET + YATA_AGENT_ADMIN_KEY removed in final PR — pending Stages A-D). Acceptance criteria: `e7m verify --no-server-key` invariant added (9th constitutional check, scans wrangler.jsonc / k8s manifests / docker-compose / GitHub Actions for 13 forbidden env names; `// no-server-key: read-only` marker exemption for documented rollback windows). Charter Rider v2.0 §1.5 PLATFORM POSTURE amendment proposed (CHARTER-RIDER.md Annex A, Council 5-of-7 ratify pending). Companion runbooks: 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-yatabase/RUNBOOK-USDC-DONATE.md (Stage A operator), 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-maps/bulk-ingest/COMMUNITY-OPERATOR-HANDOVER.md (Stage B), 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-auth/STAGE-C-IDENTITY-SIGNING-DEVOLUTION.md (Stage C), _working/STAGE-D-EXTERNAL-API-HANDOVER.md (Stage D), 50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web/STAGE-C1-DID-CUTOVER.md + cutover-stage-c1.sh (Stage C-1 Council signing flow)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231525-no-server-key-religious-corp-architecture.md"}
  {:id "2605232300" :title "kotoba-datomic — engine architecture options exploration (Hummock fork / RW fork / GraphAr+MV no-fork) (SUPERSEDED by 2605262130)" :status "superseded" :superseded_by "2605262130" :authoritative false :status_note "EXPLORATORY ONLY — NOT ADOPTED. Captures numerical comparison of 4 options for the kotoba-datomic projection engine layer: (A) Hummock fork as yata-slate (150-230K new LOC, 44-67 person-months, completion risk 50%, strategic independence ★★★), (B) Kotoba/Datomic full fork as yata-wave (57-99K new LOC, 20-29 person-months, completion risk 85%, strategic independence ★), (D) RW upstream + Apache GraphAr + MV with no fork — 'yatabase' configuration (30-50K new LOC, 20-32 person-months, completion risk 90-95%, strategic independence ★★, 7-axis weighted score 8.4/10 = numerically dominant). (C) SlateDB fork rejected early — pure KV LSM lacks Pregel epoch semantics required for LangGraph super-step / Hummock barrier isomorphism. (E) Lance dropped per user direction. Bulk graph frameworks surveyed and triaged: Apache Giraph ✗ dormant, Spark GraphX ✗ deprecated, Spark GraphFrames △ overkill, Apache HAMA ✗ Attic, NVIDIA cuGraph ✗ CUDA-only (Mac Silicon incompatible), GraphScope △ Stage-2 candidate via GraphAr external connection, timely-dataflow △ research, Materialize ✗ BSL incompatible with Charter Rider. 5 strategic findings recorded: (1) Hummock epoch = LangGraph Pregel super-step internal isomorphism, (2) Mac Silicon unified memory forces CPU/GPU per-node co-location not either/or, (3) data sovereignty achievable without engine fork via GraphAr/Parquet open format, (4) GraphAr append-only chunk semantics integrate with MST immutability, (5) options compose evolutionary D→D+plugin→D+B-partial→A across 2026-2029+. 7 open questions deferred (GraphAr religious-corp extension upstream contribution, witness quorum + GraphAr chunk hash unification, Arrow Flight UDF server topology for 18,345 agents, GraphQL Subscription / barrier alignment, MLX production stability benchmark, Lance re-introduction conditions, Solidity Base L2 event → RW source connector). Decision deferred pending: Council 5-of-7 multisig (post-2026-06-19), GraphAr Apache Incubator graduation outlook, Mac Silicon MLX production benchmark, religious-corp constitutional weight on engine ownership vs format ownership. Future decision ADR will reference this as input." :path "90-docs/adr/2605232300-kotoba-datomic-engine-options-exploration.md"}
  {:id "2605241500" :title "etzhayyim Dataset CID Substrate — DataLad + git-annex (directory remote) + sidecar IPFS pinner, CIDs anchored as datasetPin records on PDS" :status "proposed" :status_note "Defines how the monorepo references large (10TB+) training / reference / baien datasets without putting bytes in git. Six layers: (1) DataLad superdataset at 90-docs/baien/datasets/ — pointers + provenance commits; (2) git-annex SHA256E catalog; (3) `directory` special remote `local-store` at ${ETZ_DATASET_ROOT}/annex-store/<subdataset>/ — bytes at rest on a per-machine external volume; (4) sidecar IPFS pinner (`e7m-dataset publish-ipfs`) walks the directory remote, runs Kubo `/api/v0/add` per annex object, composes a SHA256E-key → IPFS-CID map JSON, pins the map and returns its root CID; (5) Kubo data root co-located on the same volume — substrate-compliant distribution layer; (6) com.etzhayyim.substrate.datasetPin records on PDS — religious-corp-canonical receipt. The `type=external externaltype=ipfs` route is deliberately NOT taken because every in-the-wild `git-annex-remote-ipfs` returns FAILURE for CHECKPRESENT / REMOVE; the sidecar pinner sidesteps that class of failure. Phase 1 smoke (2026-05-24 JST) verified end-to-end: 2 random blobs → annex add → copy --to local-store → publish-ipfs → map CID `bafkreiep2df7htkfdkzamahpbr6gmqatmkfxth2fzl3nmizd2ksldf5z2q` round-trip; per-entry `ipfs cat` returned bytes with matching SHA-256 on the deciding Mac (volume `/Volumes/260317`, Kubo peer `12D3KooWGRn…`). Follow-ups: HF `add` flow, real PDS emit (currently dry-run), SHA256E backend default (smoke used DataLad's text2git default of MD5E), Charter Rider scanner availability (currently warn-only when kotodama unimportable; tighten with ETZ_DATASET_CHARTER_STRICT=1), second always-on replica." :path "90-docs/adr/2605241500-etzhayyim-dataset-cid-substrate.md" :depends_on ["2605170900" "2605171800" "2605172000" "2605192200"] :related ["2605231300" "2605232500"]}
  {:id "2605231737" :title "e7m PDS / yoro substrate probes — operator + MCP surface for timeline-class debugging" :status "active" :status_note "Closes the 'how does the operator (or an agent) debug yoro timeline-class failures through a sanctioned surface' gap that surfaced during the 2026-05-23 timeline-load incident. Three root causes diagnosed by ad-hoc curl + grep + wrangler: (1) deployed yoro-ui bundle's minified `atQuery` emitted POST for every XRPC because the source fix had not been rebuilt — patched in-place on static/assets/index-KYx0b32R.js (`Rf(\"POST\",t,a,void 0,o)` → `Rf(\"GET\",t,void 0,a,o)`, 1-byte diff) and redeployed as kotodama-yoro Version a054ad4d-f5d7-4803-8a0d-7cac4a727685; (2) kotoba `collectFeed` 500'd with `Could not find repo: did:web:yoro.etzhayyim.com` because the configured pds.etzhayyim.com has no repo for that DID — try/catch added to return empty feed instead of 500, redeployed as yoro-xrpc-adapter Version a60f975d-a578-429e-bc26-3a42de1aa7fe; (3) no sanctioned operator surface existed for any of the probes — closed by this ADR. Adds to 70-tools/e7m (Python operator CLI + MCP server): `e7m pds describe-server | list-repos | describe-repo | resolve-handle | xrpc | create-account` and `e7m yoro probe` (composite). Host aliases: atproto | pds | yoro | apex, or full URL. 6 new MCP tools exposed via e7m-mcp; the write-class `create-account` is intentionally CLI-only (mirrors the prune_approve carve-out — substrate mutation stays operator-attributed). `e7m pds xrpc` POST to non-safelisted NSIDs requires explicit `--allow-write`. Smoke verified: `e7m --json yoro probe` returns ok=true with 5 checks after today's fixes; MCP round-trip (initialize → tools/list → tools/call etzhayyim_yoro_probe) returns 22 tools total (16 baseline + 6 new) and runs the probe end-to-end. Wheel build verified via `uv build --wheel`. Implementation: new e7m/src/e7m/pds.py (~270 lines, httpx-based) + thin wrappers in commands.py + subcommand wiring in __main__.py + tool entries in mcp_server.py. Downstream `did:web:yoro.etzhayyim.com` PDS seed is now a one-liner `e7m pds create-account --host pds --handle yoro.etzhayyim.com --did did:web:yoro.etzhayyim.com --invite <CODE>` blocked on operator obtaining the invite code (correct boundary)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231737-e7m-pds-yoro-substrate-probes.md" :depends_on ["2605172000" "2605192100" "2605211000"] :related ["2605222330" "2605211000"]}
  {:id "2605312000" :title "NDL (国立国会図書館) OAI-PMH metadata ingest on the etzhayyim kotoba substrate" :status "active" :status_note "Migrates the National Diet Library ingest from the vendor yatabase RW adapter (etzhayyimcojp, untouched) into an etzhayyim open-data worker, slice 1 = OAI-PMH metadata only (SRU image+IIIF+OCR path deferred to slice 2 — needs B2→IPFS blob + OCR endpoint re-point + datomic write). Files: ingest/ndl.py (7 Zeebe tasks: createRun/oai.plan/acquireCursor/oai.fetchWindow/verifyVisibility/advanceCursor/completeRun), ndl_worker_main.py (dedicated Zeebe worker), test_ndl_worker.py (offline-green, fixtures are REAL captured NDL records so the test is not circular). PARSE RE-GROUNDED vs the live feed (vendor assumptions failed): online filter = setSpec ndl-dl-open (NDL_OAI_SETS-overridable; vendor's ndl-dl-online/B00000/jpro-* labels are absent → would drop every record); stable id ndl_id = OAI header identifier R100000039-I{n} = a catalogue key, NOT a digital PID — digital_pid + IIIF manifest_url populated ONLY when a real dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/{n} URL is present (absent on oai_dc → bib-level metadata; no synthesised manifests); domain table vertex_ndl_bib_item (collection com.etzhayyim.apps.ndl.bibItem). Persistence: resumable OAI checkpoint + vertex_ndl_bib_item in worker-local kotoba ingest_ndl.db SQLite (resumption depends only on this); ingest.core spine (run/cursor/artifact) called best-effort via _spine() since the spine is still RW-coupled (db_sync.sync_cursor wants KOTOBA_URL — spine kotoba migration incomplete), so missing KOTOBA_URL degrades to a logged warning, never aborts. KOTOBA HANDOFF: domain-fact writes go through a single seam ingest.ndl._persist_items; the RW→kotoba-datomic refactor (vendor ADR-2605302130) swaps that one function for com.etzhayyim.apps.kotoba.datomic.transact into an etzhayyim-owned graph (never vendor kotobase-kg-v1) — performed kotoba-side per user direction ('refactor は kotoba 側が行います'); kotoba datomic client intentionally NOT ported here. VERIFICATION: fetch+parse+paging+resume IS live-verified (200/200 real records matched ndl-dl-open; multi-page resume from checkpoint = 800 cumulative records over 4 pages, 800 rows=800 distinct ndl_id idempotent, zero bogus manifests across 800 records); the kotoba datomic write is in-cluster/gated (not verifiable here); worker registration is syntax-compiled but imports not import-resolved (first in-cluster start is the check)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605312000-ndl-oai-ingest-etzhayyim.md" :depends_on ["2605172000" "2605172400"] :related ["2605172000" "2605172400"]}
  {:id "2605312101" :title "Open-data KG ingest (public-internet sources) on the etzhayyim kotoba substrate" :status "active" :status_note "Continues ADR-2605312000 (NDL): migrates the vendor yatabase kg_ingest public/open-data family (kg_ingest.py _SOURCES) onto etzhayyim. New: ingest/kg_open.py (registry-driven, 7 Zeebe tasks createRun/plan/acquireCursor/fetchSource/verifyVisibility/advanceCursor/completeRun) + kg_open_worker_main.py + test_kg_open_worker.py (real-fixture grounded). THIS SLICE = live-grounded clean-public sources: wikidata (SPARQL CC0) + crossref (REST CC0) + openstreetmap (Overpass ODbL) — fetch→extract→persist verified end-to-end against live endpoints 2026-05-31 (wikidata 5/5, crossref 3/3, osm 5/5 real ward names; PII screen drops email/phone/SSN/マイナンバー/postal). Same canonical entity shape {id,qid,type,label_ja,label_en,source_id,license,extractor,confidence} the kotoba datomic writer consumes. EXCLUDED: hf_rebel/hf_conceptnet (already covered by ingest.hf_dataset); egov_laws (REDUNDANT — e-Gov already ingested by ingest.houbun api/2 full corpus; AND vendor adapter broken: GETs /api/1/lawdata + json.loads but live e-Gov v1 returns XML, working JSON is v2); japan_company_registry/gBiz (OUT OF SCOPE per user direction 2026-05-31 — not migrated; token-gated open data, the earlier ready-but-gated port was removed from kg_open.py). Vendor cutover/removal sequence (gates G1-G3 + kotoba handoff) tracked in 90-docs/2605312200-open-data-ingest-vendor-cutover-runbook.md. Persistence: spine best-effort via _spine (RW-coupled); canonical entities in worker-local kotoba ingest_kg_open.db; single _persist_entities seam = the kotoba-side RW→datomic swap target (com.etzhayyim.apps.kotoba.datomic.transact, etzhayyim-owned graph, NOT vendor kotobase-kg-v1). VENDOR REMOVAL NOT DONE — it is the post-cutover step: unlike NDL's standalone ndl_ingest.py, these adapters are entries in one shared _SOURCES registry consumed by the LIVE commercial yatabase/kotobase product (server.py scheduler + kg_handlers reads); MIGRATION-rw-to-kotoba-datomic.md is explicit 'NOT a cutover … RW not retired until the 7-step gate passes'. So git rm in etzhayyimcojp waits on that cutover (disable scheduler/redirect reads first), not this port. Kotoba datomic write itself is in-cluster/gated = not verifiable here." :path "90-docs/adr/2605312101-open-data-kg-ingest-etzhayyim.md" :depends_on ["2605312000" "2605172000"] :related ["2605312000" "2605172000" "2605172400"]}
  {:id "2605231300" :title "baien distill ReAct loop — LangGraph analyze → fetch_dataset → validate → train → evaluate → commit" :status "accepted" :status_note "Specifies the 6-node ReAct loop for distilling weak-category improvements into LoRA adapters on the baien trunk (microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-bf16). analyze reads prior microbench JSONL to identify weak categories; fetch_dataset pulls HF datasets (default) or falls back to select_teacher for synthetic generation; validate runs Charter Rider scanner + JSON parse + token-length filters; train executes peft+trl LoRA on q/k/v/o projections (r=16, alpha=32, dropout=0.05, lr=2e-4, cosine warmup); evaluate runs e7m bench micro on the merged adapter; commit_node promotes (append to distilled-models.jsonl + codegen registry) or aborts (discard adapter dir) on Δ vs baseline. iter-00 smoke 2026-05-24 validated end-to-end (12 examples / 3 SGD steps / Δ=-0.380 → abort fired correctly); minimum-informative tier formalised in ADR-2605242400 as --n-per-category 200 --max-iter 2." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231300-baien-distill-react-loop.md"}
  {:id "2605231601" :title "baien context extension — Stage 1 RoPE scaling probe + Stage 2 YaRN+LoRA + Stage 3 LongRoPE continual" :status "accepted" :status_note "3-stage roadmap for extending baien (microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-bf16) effective context beyond the pretrained 4k ceiling toward 16k. Stage 1 = training-free RoPE theta scaling smoke (baseline / linear×4 / NTK×4 head_dim=128) executed 2026-05-23 on EVO-X2 CPU bf16 — result: identical 2/5 = 40% pass rate across all three configs (ctx_8k_summary / ctx_10k_roster / ctx_12k_needle all FAIL with attention-quality failure modes, not range failures). Per snapshot recommendation: do NOT promote to Stage 2 on this evidence alone; expand prompt set 5→20+, add 4k regression run, investigate multi-modal token interaction first. Stage 2 (YaRN + LoRA on long-ctx corpus) + Stage 3 (LongRoPE continual pretraining) remain spec-only until Stage 1 evidence is broadened." :path "90-docs/adr/2605231601-baien-context-extension.md"}
  {:id "2605232400" :title "baien Core 3 / Core 4 lm-eval-harness bench strategy revision — switch _generative → _completions" :status "accepted" :status_note "Reframes the baien lm-eval-harness Core 4 bench strategy (IFEval / GPQA / MMLU-Redux / Global PIQA) after the 2026-05-23 snapshot run showed _generative variants take ~28h/task on EVO-X2 CPU bf16 (untenable for an iteration loop). Decision: switch the Core 3 (excluding IFEval which is generative-only by construction) from _generative to _completions (loglikelihood scoring), reducing wall from ~28h to ~30 min per task. Authoritative for the next baien snapshot (frontier-bench-snapshot-260524.md follow-up). Note: this ADR ID 2605232400 collides with the kotoba-datomic Tier D blob closure ADR registered at the same JST minute — both rows coexist in this registry (TOML [[adrs]] is an array, not a unique-keyed map); resolution is via the `path` field." :path "90-docs/adr/2605232400-baien-core3-bench-strategy-revision.md"}
  {:id "2605232500" :title "baien Move 1 — image graft self-training (SigLIP + 1.58-bit projector + frozen BitNet trunk, Phase A/B/C/D corpus tiers)" :status "accepted" :status_note "First of the 7 baien Move grafts (multi-modal capability landing). Move 1 = image: SigLIP-base-patch16-224 (frozen) → 1.58-bit projector (trainable, ~8.5M params) → BitNet b1.58 2B-4T-bf16 trunk (frozen). Phase tiers: A=100 samples (pipeline validation only), B=1k samples ~250 SGD steps ~40min (minimum-informative), C=10k ~6.7h, D=50k ~33h overnight. Phase A real-train smoke 2026-05-24 ran 10 actual samples (target=100) / 3 SGD steps / 0/4 visual_microbench (degraded from baseline 2/5 = 40%) — confirms the smoke=destructive pattern formalised in ADR-2605242400. Encoder freeze rule per ADR-2605241900 invariant: all modality encoders MUST be frozen; only projector + trunk LoRA are trainable; total inference budget ≤2GB @4k ctx." :path "90-docs/adr/2605232500-baien-mx-move1-image-graft-self-training.md"}
  {:id "2605241900" :title "baien edge-target invariant — WASM-32 + iPhone 12+ + Android 4GB; trunk ≤4B BitNet 1.58; total ≤2GB @4k / ≤2.5GB @16k" :status "accepted" :status_note "Constitutional invariant for baien (edge tier): baien MUST run on all three of (1) WASM-32, (2) iPhone 12+, (3) Android 4GB. Trunk ≤4B BitNet 1.58 (microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-bf16 current). Cumulative inference budget ≤2GB @4k ctx / ≤2.5GB @16k ctx including all modality encoders. ALL modality encoders MUST be frozen (only projector + trunk LoRA learnable). Frontier-beating is explicitly NOT a goal — separate `baien-server-*` and `baien-XL-*` tiers carve out larger budgets (ADR-2605242100 4-tier ladder). 8 constitutional ceilings spelled out in detail; Council Lv6+ supermajority required to amend any ceiling." :path "90-docs/adr/2605241900-baien-edge-target-invariant.md"}
  {:id "2605241930" :title "baien Move 4 — audio graft (HuBERT-base / Whisper-tiny encoder + 1.58-bit projector, edge-tier on-demand load)" :status "accepted" :status_note "4th Move of the baien multi-modal graft sequence. Audio: HuBERT-base or Whisper-tiny.en encoder (frozen, encoder selection depends on use case — HuBERT for speech-rep / Whisper for transcribe) → 1.58-bit projector → frozen BitNet trunk. Edge-tier on-demand modality loading required to respect ADR-2605241900 cumulative encoder budget (loading audio + image + video simultaneously breaches the 2GB ceiling). Charter Rider §2(d) gore boundary scanned at audio modality boundary (audio transcripts run through canonical scanner before write)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605241930-baien-mx-move4-audio-graft.md"}
  {:id "2605241940" :title "baien Move 7 — 3D graft (TripoSR / Hunyuan3D-2 image→3D + moderngl 4-view render + Florence-2 multi-view caption)" :status "accepted" :status_note "7th Move (capstone) of the baien multi-modal graft sequence. 3D capability comes via 2D + caption augmentation, NOT via a native 3D encoder (which would breach the edge invariant): image→3D via TripoSR or Hunyuan3D-2 → moderngl 4-view render → Florence-2 multi-view caption → standard image-graft (Move 1) pipeline on the augmented 2D + text supervision. Companion to ADR-2605202115 (baien-graft-3d-augmented-dataset). Edge tier sees the dataset only at training time; inference path is bit-identical to Move 1 image." :path "90-docs/adr/2605241940-baien-mx-move7-3d-graft.md"}
  {:id "2605242100" :title "baien-server / baien-XL carve-out from edge invariant — 4-tier ladder (edge / bonsai / server / XL)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Carves the baien lineage into 4 tiers with separate target envelopes: (1) edge (ADR-2605241900 invariant, ≤4B trunk, ≤2GB inference); (2) bonsai (compressed-but-not-edge, ≤8B trunk, on-prem laptop/desktop); (3) server (no edge constraint, frontier-competing on selected benchmarks, runs on Murakumo fleet); (4) XL (research-scale, post-Council). Shared invariants across all 4 tiers: Charter Rider applies, Murakumo-only inference (no commercial GPU rental per ADR-2605215000 + CHARTER-RIDER.md §2(i)), Apache 2.0 + Rider license. Frontier-beating remains explicitly non-goal for edge tier; server and XL tiers may target frontier benchmarks but inherit all other constitutional constraints." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242100-baien-server-xl-carve-out.md"}
  {:id "2605242110" :title "baien Move 5 — video graft (VideoMAE-base + 1.58-bit projector, 4 modal configs A/B/C/D)" :status "accepted" :status_note "5th Move of the baien multi-modal graft sequence. Video: VideoMAE-base encoder (frozen) → 1.58-bit projector → frozen BitNet trunk. 4 modal configs: (A) video-only, (B) video+audio, (C) video+text, (D) video+audio+text — config selection depends on use case and edge-tier on-demand modality loading per ADR-2605241900. Edge tier loads video encoder on-demand (frame-sampled inference) to respect cumulative encoder budget. Server/XL tiers (ADR-2605242100) may load all modality encoders eagerly." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242110-baien-mx-move5-video-graft.md"}
  {:id "2605242120" :title "baien Move 6 — robotics graft (edge = scene description only / server = OpenVLA-style action head post-Council)" :status "accepted" :status_note "6th Move of the baien multi-modal graft sequence. Robotics: tier-split for safety reasons per Charter Rider §2(h) (no harm) + §2(a) (no autonomous weapons). Edge tier ships scene-description capability only (no action output to robot controller). Server tier may add an OpenVLA-style action head, but ONLY post-Council ratification (Council Lv6+ supermajority required). Companion to wadachi (ADR-2605242000) and kuni-umi (ADR-2605201400-2605201900) autonomous-mobility / planetary-infra robotics actors — those actors do NOT use baien Move 6 today; they use task-specific stacks under their own governance gates." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242120-baien-mx-move6-robotics-graft.md"}
  {:id "2605242400" :title "baien smoke is destructive finding — Move 1 Phase A + distill iter-00 honest signal; minimum-informative training tier" :status "accepted" :status_note "Formalises the lesson from two same-day real-train runs (Move 1 Phase A: 0/4 vs baseline 2/5; distill iter-00: Δ=-0.380 abort). Both run ≤3 SGD steps from a random-init head and produce strictly worse outputs than the frozen baseline — the pattern is mechanical (3 SGD steps from random init under Adam+bf16 defaults push the trainable head into a degenerate region; the frozen trunk then completes the disrupted prefix into template loops). Decision: (a) Phase A is pipeline validation, not learning; (b) minimum-informative tier = Phase B (1000 samples, ~250 SGD steps, ~40min) for Move 1, --n-per-category 200 --max-iter 2 (~30 min) for distill; (c) operator gate against publishing smoke-tier adapters to distilled-models.jsonl — new entries require ≥250 SGD steps OR ≥+5pp microbench improvement over baseline. Companion: trl 1.4.0 API drift fixes in 70-tools/baien-distill/src/baien_distill/nodes/train.py (drop max_seq_length, add use_cpu=not torch.cuda.is_available(), migrate dataset schema to {prompt, completion})." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242400-baien-smoke-is-destructive-finding.md"}
  {:id "2605242600" :title "Baien federated training via ameno WebGPU — smartphone-participable LoRA round (R0 scaffold)" :status "accepted" :status_note "R0 scaffold landed via PR #273 (commit 0134acb1d, 8 files / 992 LoC). Smartphone / browser participation in baien post-train via WebGPU LoRA-only autograd (rank-16 on q/k/v/o_proj), frozen BitNet trunk + frozen modality encoders per ADR-2605241900. 5-layer architecture (L1 WebGPU kernel / L2 ameno PWA loop / L3 lexicon + DID / L4 Murakumo aggregator / L5 MST + L2 anchor). 11 constitutional gates (G1 trunk+encoders frozen / G2 LoRA rank-16 q/k/v/o_proj only / G3 IPFS+MST upload / G4 member passkey ES256 / G5 Murakumo-only aggregation / G6 on-device Charter Rider scan / G7 Adherent SBT gate / G8 Wellbecoming gate / G9 Byzantine median/Krum + DP-Gaussian / G10 round-frozen baseModelCid / G11 no per-delta payout). R0 deliverables landed: this ADR + lexicon com.etzhayyim.baien.distributedTrainDelta + 20-actors/ameno/src/train.ts throw-on-use scaffold + 70-tools/baien-distill/src/baien_distill/nodes/federated_aggregate.py dry-run-only planner + 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/baien_federated_aggregator/ Council-attestation-gated cell (import-time RuntimeError, L5-routing-around pattern from CLAUDE.md row 35). R1 ADR (2605242630) + R1a framework (PR #276) build directly on top." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242600-baien-federated-train-via-ameno-webgpu.md"}
  {:id "2605242630" :title "Baien federated R1 — single-device WebGPU LoRA backward-pass PoC" :status "accepted" :status_note "R1 ADR (PR #274) + R1a framework (PR #276 commit 0de4c354e, 10 files / 1524 LoC) both landed. R1 ADR fixes: (a) 3-row device matrix (iPhone 12 / Adreno-650+ Android / M-series desktop), (b) numerics fallback table (path A fp16 desktop / path B fp32-grad-accumulator mobile DEFAULT / path C full-fp32 last-resort), (c) OPFS Adam-state on-disk format, (d) 16-example microbench shard with .cid sidecar (sha256-b3582a53486b8438da88d86d16d95c9c0565628e9794d958b3a7506c97745bf7) for round-replay parity, (e) success criteria 3 consecutive lossAfter < lossBefore × 0.98 + OPFS kill+resume ±1e-4 reproducibility, (f) device-side abort conditions. R1a delivered: 20-actors/ameno/src/train.ts orchestration rewrite + train/{opfs,device,shard,charter-rider,kernels}.ts siblings (every framework piece except WebGPU autograd dispatch itself); WGSL sources for LoRA forward / backward (main_dA + main_dB) / Adam (bias-corrected with exp2/log2 for mobile-fp16 stability) committed in final form; dispatch wrappers stay throws with R1b markers. R1b remaining: WebGPU autograd dispatch via transformers.js layer-replacement OR @tensorflow/tfjs-backend-webgpu bridge + per-device run-log capture for the 3-consecutive-runs success criterion. signDeltaManifest + publishDeltaRecord stay throws (R2)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242630-baien-federated-r1-webgpu-backward-poc.md"}
  {:id "2605242500" :title "baien ternary silicon + tsukuru fab — religious-corp first-party RTL/装置設計 charter (生命のコア)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Upper charter for religious-corp自前半導体 ('半導体は生命のコア', user 2026-05-24). 6 decisions: (1) self-design 2 ASICs (iwakura inference / fuigo training) + 8 fab equipment categories with RTL/CAD/mechanical/robotics owned by religious-corp under Apache 2.0 + Charter Rider; (2) tsukuru.etzhayyim.com is the sole orchestration SSoT (NOT tukuru.etzhayyim.com — vendor stays out of religious-corp silicon orchestration; tsukuru ISIC C26 EUV lane from ADR-0061 is the natural extension); (3) 8-equipment scope mirroring industry vendors (ASML/AMAT/Lam/TEL/Axcelis/Ebara/KLA/Advantest/ASE) with open-source toolchain only (yosys/Verilator/cocotb/SymbiYosys/KiCad/FreeCAD/OpenSCAD/ROS 2); (4) Charter Rider §2(a)(c) Council Lv6+ ≥3 multisig gate via com.etzhayyim.silicon.silenForceReview Lexicon — REQUIRED before chip ships; (5) Phase 1 deliverable = RTL + cocotb sim only, FPGA/MPW/fab build are separate ADRs post-Council; (6) silicon = land-trust-analogue inalienable (no sale, lease to SBT holders only). 4-phase roadmap (Phase 1 scaffold this wave / Phase 2 FPGA / Phase 3 MPW TSMC N5/N3 / Phase 4 Rapidus 2nm 千歳 / Phase 5 自家 fab超長期)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242500-baien-ternary-silicon-and-tsukuru-fab-charter.md"}
  {:id "2605242515" :title "iwakura (磐座) — baien ternary 専用推論 ASIC architecture" :status "proposed" :status_note "Inference ASIC die for baien edge. 256×256 multiplier-less ternary PE grid (65,536 PE × 1 GHz = 65 Tera-ternary-ops/s peak; ~620 gates per PE vs ~5,200 for INT8 mult = 8.4× density gain). Radix-3 weight packing (5 ternaries per byte = 25% DRAM bandwidth saving). 16 MB on-die SRAM for KV cache scratch + 2 GB LPDDR5X-7500 ×2 on-package = 120 GB/s. Zero-skip dispatcher gates ~33% of PE clocks (animation power -30%). Image encoder (SigLIP) hard-wired in iwakura-1; audio/video/3D on generic PE. Host I/F: USB4 dongle (edge) / PCIe Gen4 x4 (workstation) / WASM-SIMD shim (browser fallback). TDP 3-5 W edge / 15 W workstation. Foundry target TSMC N5 MPW eShuttle (Phase 3 post-Council). EMPIRICAL STATUS (2026-06-01, RTL→GDSII session): Phase-1 RTL implemented + verified, NOT a stub — radix3_decoder + pe_array (weight-stationary ternary matvec, generate-for over canonical ternary_pe, no fork; CLOCK_GATE=1 wires zero_skip_dispatcher into per-PE accumulator gating) + zero_skip_dispatcher + behavioural sram_scratch/lpddr5x_ctrl (radix-3 unpack on read) + iwakura_top live compute tile. cocotb (Verilator 5.048 + cocotb 2.0.1): 9 suites / 18 tests green incl. 200+ randomized matvec vs ref, 65,536-block exhaustive dispatcher (BitNet dist → 35.0% gated), 200 clock-gate bit-identical cases; all RTL Verilator -Wall lint clean. SYNTHESIS (yosys 0.65, generic gates + sky130 open PDK std-cell area AGREE): whole-PE density 3.69× (sky130) / 3.68× (GE); multiplier-only 11.9× / 12.7× → ADR 8.4× estimate validated, conservative. P&R→GDSII (OpenLane2 2.3.10, sky130hd, pe_array): DRC 0 / LVS 0 / antenna 0; GDSII produced; post-route multi-corner STA f_max ≈ 93 MHz (slow ss_100C_1v60 sign-off) / 160 MHz (tt) / 211 MHz (ff), hold positive all corners; die 53,120 µm². HONEST: sky130 = 130nm open PDK, NOT the N5 production target (Phase 3, Council-gated); 93-160 MHz vs 1 GHz N5 target = expected ~26×-older-node process gap. pe_array is time-multiplexed (1 col/cycle); full 256×256 systolic skew + pipeline regs = Phase 2. PHY ports placeholder. See 50-infra/silicon/{iwakura,synth,pnr}/README.md." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242515-iwakura-ternary-inference-asic.md"}
  {:id "2605242530" :title "fuigo (鞴) — baien hybrid ternary/BF16 training ASIC architecture" :status "proposed" :status_note "Training ASIC die. Asymmetric BitNet 1.58 training (forward = ternary, backward = BF16 STE) implemented as 2 separate systolic arrays both active simultaneously — closes the 7%/38% MFU gap of generic GPU (target MFU 70%+). Forward SA = 1024×1024 ternary PE (1 PetaTernary-ops/s peak; IP reused from shared-ip/ternary-pe). Backward SA = 8,192 BF16 MAC = 16 TFLOPS BF16. STE Glue unit bridges forward-ternary ↔ backward-BF16 master weight without GPU kernel-launch overhead. Lion optimizer hard-wired (Adam software emulation only; ADR-2605231300 recommends Lion + memory halved vs Adam). 4 × HBM3e ×24 GB = 96 GB @ 4.8 TB/s. libp2p NIC integrated on-die (ed25519 peer-ID burned at eFuse during shared-ip/libp2p-nic IP block init; Murakumo no-VKE mesh native per ADR-2605214000). CXL.mem 3.0 endpoint for multi-die memory pooling. TDP 350 W board / liquid-cooled 1U. Phase 1 = RTL + cocotb sim (forward path reuses ternary-pe IP). Foundry target TSMC N3 chiplet (Phase 3); Rapidus 2nm 千歳 second source (Phase 4 post-2027). Closes ADR-2605215000 inference-only-Murakumo to include training-only-Murakumo. EMPIRICAL STATUS (2026-06-01): forward path no longer a stub — fuigo_top instantiates the shared pe_array / ternary-pe IP (no fork; ACC_WIDTH=32 training accumulator), verified by test_fuigo_top.py (101 cases vs ref, Verilator+cocotb green, -Wall lint clean). Backward BF16 SA + STE glue + Lion + HBM3e/CXL/libp2p remain Phase-2 (the part NOT shared with iwakura)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242530-fuigo-hybrid-ternary-bf16-training-asic.md"}
  {:id "2605242545" :title "tsukuru fab 8-equipment Pregel charter — litho/depo/etch/implant/CMP/metrology/test/packaging" :status "proposed" :status_note "Self-design RTL/CAD/mechanical/robotics for 8 fab equipment categories (industry counterparts: ASML/Nikon/Canon for litho; AMAT/Lam/TEL for deposition + etch; Axcelis/AMAT for ion implant; Ebara/AMAT for CMP; KLA for metrology; Advantest/Teradyne for ATE; ASE/Amkor/TSMC AP/Samsung AP for packaging). 7 decisions: (1) per-step responsibility matrix mapping each equipment to a silicon_<step> Pregel cell; (2) common Pregel super-step contract (super_step(wafer_lot, telemetry, prior_attestations) → (next_wafer_lot, messages)); (3) open-source EDA stack only (yosys / Verilator / cocotb / SymbiYosys / KiCad / FreeCAD / OpenSCAD / ROS 2 / OpenLane); (4) public reference design strategy = transparent religious force per ADR-2605192315 (公開された RTL/CAD コモンズが力の独占を防ぐ); (5) Murakumo node assignment (judah for litho/depo/etch; dan for implant; naphtali for CMP+packaging; simeon for metrology iwakura-coloc; levi for test ternary-aware ATE); (6) Phase 1 scaffold this wave; (7) Phase 2 priority sequencing — Phase 2a silicon_test (ATE bring-up independence) / Phase 2b silicon_metrology (AI on iwakura) / Phase 2c silicon_packaging (fuigo chiplet) / Phase 3 silicon_litho (EUV, year-scale) / Phase 4 残り 4 工程. Charter Rider §2(a)(c) risk classification per equipment: HIGH (litho/implant) / MEDIUM (depo/etch/metrology) / LOW (cmp/test/packaging). 4 Lexicons under com.etzhayyim.silicon (chipManufacturingAttestation / silenForceReview / fabEquipmentTelemetry / waferLotAttestation)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605242545-tsukuru-fab-equipment-pregel-charter.md"}
  {:id "2605250500" :title "yakushi (薬師) pharmaceutical R&D charter — religious-corp first-party API + sterile fill-finish + supply chain (OTC ophthalmic triplet as Wave 1 reference)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Master charter establishing yakushi (薬師, 典薬寮系譜 + Yakushi Nyorai echo) as Tier-B religious-corp first-party pharmaceutical R&D actor. Wave 1 reference = OTC 抗アレルギー点眼薬 triplet (cromoglicate Na + naphazoline HCl + chlorpheniramine maleate — 全 80 年級 multi-gen safety, perpetually off-patent, PMDA/FDA/EMA OTC switched). Charter Rider §2 全条項 clearance (§2(e) anti-gatekeeping は constitutional 推進力)。14 constitutional gates (G1 OTC-only / G2 ICH Q3/M7 / G3 silen-pharma-review Council Lv6+ ≥3 / G4 QP co-sign / G5 AE public reporting / G6 no Rx no controlled / G7 CWC dual-use / G8 Annex 1 sterile / G9 witness N≥2 / G10 patient privacy / G11 wellbecoming label / G12 no commercial sale / G13 no server-key / G14 substrate boundary)。10 non-goals (N1 no new molecular entity / N2 no Rx / N3 no biologics / N4 no commercial / N5 no advertising / N6 no patent fence / N7 no insurance coupling / N8 no in-house animal testing / N9 no frontier model / N10 no vendor revenue path)。4-phase roadmap R0→R3 (R0 scaffold only this wave / R1 benchtop ≤1g / R2 pilot ≤100g + Annex 1 / R3 community-scale ~1000 bottles/batch)。Substrate boundary: MST + IPFS + Base L2 anchor via @etzhayyim/sdk; payment USDC + TitheRouter donation/kisha/grant/internal-promo only; inference Murakumo only. Murakumo fleet placement (R1+): naphtali (raw mat + cold chain), zebulun (synthesis + purification), levi (QC + AE + post-market), joseph (fill-finish), simeon (container), dan (packaging). 3 sub-ADRs (2605250515 API synthesis / 2605250530 sterile fill-finish + container / 2605250545 supply chain + 8 robotics specs)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605250500-yakushi-pharmaceutical-rd-charter.md"}
  {:id "2605250515" :title "yakushi Wave 1 — OTC 抗アレルギー点眼薬 3 API の合成・精製・QC 設計 (cromoglicate Na + naphazoline HCl + chlorpheniramine maleate)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Sub-ADR for 3 API identity, synthesis routes (DSCG 5-step Fisons 1965 / naphazoline 3-step Ciba 1942 / chlorpheniramine 4-step Schering 1949 — all perpetually off-patent open literature), raw material CWC + safety classification (HIGH §2(a) acetic anhydride OPCW Schedule 3 for DSCG Step 1; HIGH safety NaNH₂ 消防法 危険物 第3類 for chlorpheniramine Step 1-2), purification scheme (recryst + activated charcoal + (chlorpheniramine) prep-HPLC for ICH M7 PGI 4-chlorobenzyl chloride removal ≤1.5 µg/day), QC suite (HPLC purity / IR / NMR / KF / ICP-MS Q3D / GC headspace Q3C / LC-MS/MS M7 PGI / endotoxin LAL / microbial / sterility). 6 silen-pharma-review triggers." :path "90-docs/adr/2605250515-yakushi-otc-ophthalmic-api-synthesis.md"}
  {:id "2605250530" :title "yakushi Wave 1 — sterile fill-finish + primary container (BFS 5 mL 多用量点眼瓶 / Annex 1 GMP / preservative-free 設計)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Sub-ADR for LDPE BFS multi-dose 5 mL eye drop container (Wave 1 default — single-use unit-dose deferred to R3 ADR for multi-gen plastic waste review), preservative-free formulation (BAK 不使用 per §2(h) wellbecoming — long-term BAK corneal toxicity), aseptic processing unified across 3 化合物 (DSCG terminal autoclave marginal, SOP unification via 0.22 µm filtration + BFS Class A air), Annex 1 (2023 改訂) compliance scope (R2 3-batch consecutive media fill + CCIT R3 release gate), Hitogata class-A sterile sub-config (kuni-umi inheritance — 316L stainless + electropolished + VHP sterilizable), QC bridging attestation chain (API → bulk → filtration → fill → CCIT → sterility → endotoxin). 5 silen-pharma-review triggers." :path "90-docs/adr/2605250530-yakushi-sterile-fill-finish-and-container.md"}
  {:id "2605250545" :title "yakushi Wave 1 — 製薬 supply chain (excipient + WFI infra + cold chain) + 8 robotics class 設計 (Pregel cell 8 件と等価対応)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Sub-ADR for 8 supply chain categories (raw material API precursor / excipient / WFI utility / packaging primary / packaging secondary + labeling / cold chain logistics / spent material disposal / adverse event ingestion) — pharma_raw_material cell が 1+2 共有、pharma_packaging が 5+7 共有 → 結果 8 Pregel cells (+ pharma_post_market_surveillance + pharma_adverse_event = 10 total)。8 robotics class = 既存 6 reuse (Hitogata class-A sterile / Hitogata class-C clean / Otete chem-resist / Mimi pharma-analytical / Otete cold-chain / Funamori marine — silicon Wave 2 inheritance) + 新規 2 placeholder (Kusuko 薬子 single-use sterile autoloader R2+, Sukoyaka 健やか patient-side cold-chain last-mile R3+). GMP attestation chain (rawMaterial → API → purification → QC → fill-finish → packaging → cold chain → distribution → AE). Cold chain default 2-8°C unified (DSCG-driven; SOP single). AE reporting design = ameno PWA + XChaCha20 envelope (G10) + daily aggregated narrative (G5) + Council Lv6+ resale prohibition (Charter Rider §2(c))。Charter Rider §2 per-category 評価表。Funamori 海外 R3+ separate ADR 必須。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605250545-yakushi-pharma-supply-chain-and-robotics.md"}
  {:id "2605250600" :title "yakushi Wave 1b — OTC API catalog expansion (analgesic / oral antihistamine / H2 antagonist / topical) + 2 new dosage forms (oral tablet + topical cream-gel)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Wave 1b extension to master charter (ADR-2605250500) — Wave 1 triplet (eye drop sterile) を 9 化合物 + 2 dosage forms に拡張、Charter Rider §2 全条項 clearance + 14 gates + 10 non-goals 不変。Category A analgesic+antipyretic (oral tablet): acetaminophen (1893) / aspirin (1897 Bayer) / ibuprofen (1969 Boots, Hoechst-Celanese 3-step route post-1981 expired)。Category B oral H1 antihistamine: diphenhydramine HCl (1946) / cetirizine 2HCl (1987 UCB, off-patent ≥ 2007) / loratadine (1988 Schering, off-patent ≥ 2002 US / ≥ 2008 EU exclusivity)。Category C H2 antagonist: famotidine (1986 Yamanouchi, off-patent ≥ 2006)。Category D topical: clotrimazole 1% cream (1969 Bayer) / diclofenac Na 1% gel (1973 Geigy)。全 9 化合物 PMDA/FDA/EMA all-3 OTC switched 確認。明示的除外: pseudoephedrine (CMEA precursor controlled in US) / codeine (Rx全 jurisdiction) / dextromethorphan (marginal) / hydrocortisone (steroid bioprocess Wave 2 候補) / sodium hyaluronate (Streptococcus 発酵 bioprocess Wave 2) / omeprazole (chiral resolution Wave 1c 候補) / naproxen + miconazole + tetrahydrozoline (therapeutic 冗長)。**G7 enforcement extends to acetaminophen + aspirin + ibuprofen** (DSCG と同じ acetic anhydride OPCW Schedule 3 Step 1 issue)。**2 new Pregel cells**: pharma_tablet_manufacture (joseph, non-sterile class C — pre-blend → granulate → final blend + compression → coating → blister-pack) + pharma_topical_formulation (simeon, kuni-umi commissioning sibling — oil phase + aqueous phase emulsification 70-75°C → cooling → tube fill)。**Lexicon extension only** (新 lexicon 無し): apiInn knownValues 3→12 / fillFinishAttestation + lotAttestation に dosageForm field 10 knownValues / qcAttestation に dissolution/disintegration/friability/content-uniformity/viscosity/pH 追加 / silenPharmaReview scope に wave-1b-* triggers (api-addition + dosage-form-tablet-attestation + dosage-form-topical-attestation + tablet-press-equipment-qualification + topical-mixer-equipment-qualification + non-sterile-microbial-limit-baseline + wave-1b-launch-{pmda,fda,ema})。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605250600-yakushi-wave-1b-otc-api-catalog-expansion.md"}
  {:id "2605250615" :title "yakushi Wave 1c — Chiral synthesis (omeprazole PPI) + deferred OTC expansion (laxative / cough-expectorant)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Wave 1c extends yakushi from 12 → 19 化合物 + chiral resolution capability + new dosage forms (sachets, oral syrups). omeprazole (chiral S-enantiomer focus; crystalline-resolution-mandelate or prep-HPLC-chiral routes) is flagship API. Category E laxatives: polyethylene glycol 3350 / docusate sodium / senna extract / bisacodyl (all low/zero synthesis complexity). Category G cough-expectorant: guaifenesin / benzonatate (both 1-2 step routes, minimal G7 risk). **G7 risk = NONE** (omeprazole synthesis omits OPCW Schedule 3 precursors — contrast Wave 1b analgesics). **1 new Pregel cell**: pharma_chiral_resolution (levi node, omeprazole S-enantiomer separation). **New dosageForm knownValues**: sachet-powder-for-reconstitution / oral-liquid-syrup / oral-suspension (extends Wave 1b 10→13). **Charter Rider §2 全条項 clearance**: omeprazole § 2(h) wellbecoming margin (long-term PPI use → secondary hypomagnesemia/hypocalcemia risk, labeled). **Benzonatate PMDA jurisdiction margin**: Rx form exists in Japan; OTC elsewhere. R1 phase decision pending Japanese regulatory approval (benzonatate OTC application submitted 2023, decision expected 2024-2025). silenPharmaReview scope additions: wave-1c-chiral-resolution-baseline / wave-1c-laxative-formulation-baseline / wave-1c-cough-syrup-formulation-baseline / wave-1c-benzonatate-jp-marginal。" :path "90-docs/adr/2605250615-yakushi-wave-1c-chiral-synthesis-and-deferred-otc-expansion.md"}
  {:id "2605250630" :title "yakushi Wave 1c R1 — Chiral synthesis commissioning and benzonatate PMDA jurisdiction" :status "proposed" :status_note "R1 phase transitions Wave 1c R0 scaffold → operational readiness. Establishes Council Lv6+ ≥3 attestation baseline (silenPharmaReview scope: wave-1c-chiral-resolution-baseline + wave-1c-liquid-formulation-baseline). Defines omeprazole S-enantiomer benchtop PoC protocol (≤1g scale, two parallel routes: crystalline-resolution-mandelate via L-mandelic acid [65-75% yield] or prep-HPLC-chiral Chiralcel OD-H [70-95% yield], enantiomeric purity ≥99.5% ICH M7 Class 5). Specifies guaifenesin 100mg/5mL syrup + benzonatate suspension (100-150mg/5mL) liquid formulation QC baseline (USP <61>/<62> microbial limits, viscosity, pH). Documents benzonatate PMDA jurisdiction margin resolution (monitoring assignment until 2026-06-30 PMDA decision window closes; if approved by 2026-06-30, R1.5 amendment ADR-2605250645 unlocks manufacturing; if denied, benzonatate deferred to Wave 2). No amendment to 14 gates G1..G14 + 10 non-goals N1..N10. Council motion target: 2026-05; gate unlock target: 2026-06-30." :path "90-docs/adr/2605250630-yakushi-wave-1c-r1-chiral-commissioning.md"}
  {:id "2605250715" :title "tatekata (建方) — Construction Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold" :status "proposed" :status_note "Master charter establishing tatekata (建方, construction method / general practice) as Tier-B religious-corp construction infrastructure orchestration actor. Sibling of yakushi (pharma) + wadachi (mobility). R0 scope = infrastructure (≤2 story, ≤5000m², civil + MEP). 14 immutable constitutional gates G1–G14 (firmware open-source / IPFS photo pinning / witness quorum ≥2 robots / bilingual permits / Charter Rider compliance / trajectory determinism / no chemistry / vendor-free CAD / mesh transparency / personnel vetting / KPI caps / energy budget / schedule calendar / waste tracking). 10 non-goals N1–N10 (no high-rise, housing, nuclear, hazmat, tunnels, major bridges, historical, deep-sea, design, budgeting). 4-phase roadmap R0→R3 (R0 scaffold / R1 benchtop / R2 pilot ≤100m² / R3 community-scale). 5 Pregel cells (foundation_excavation, structural_assembly, mep_installation, finishing_handoff, commissioning) — all import-time RuntimeError. Murakumo placement (naphtali/joseph/zebulun/simeon/levi). Parent = ADR-2605201400 (kuni-umi infrastructure). Charter Rider §2(a)(g) clearance (no weapons, supply chain ethics). Witness = ADR-2605191524 swarm broadcast." :path "90-docs/adr/2605250715-tatekata-construction-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605250730" :title "tatekata Wave R1 — Benchtop site survey PoC (reserved, placeholder)" :status "proposed" :status_note "R1 activation ADR (reserved). Will establish Council Lv6+ ≥3 attestation baseline + SME civil engineer onboarded + Giemon benchtop PoC (0.5m × 0.5m excavation, depth ≤1m). Replaces RuntimeError with LangGraph stub bodies. Authored post-R0 ADR merge + Council review window." :path "90-docs/adr/2605250730-tatekata-construction-r1-benchtop-poc.md (reserved)"}
  {:id "2605250745" :title "tatekata Wave R2 — Pilot site ≤100m² (reserved, placeholder)" :status "proposed" :status_note "R2 expansion ADR (reserved). Pilot confined site (≤100m², ≤2 stories, prefab assembly). Giemon + Otete + manual subcontractors. Incident <baseline. Material waste logged. Site permit + 30-day public comment." :path "90-docs/adr/2605250745-tatekata-construction-r2-pilot-site.md (reserved)"}
