evices/year + iwakura mass-integration + igata HPDC Al chassis + kanayama EOL loop closure + 法務 (電波法 + 個人情報保護法 + GDPR) audit). Reserved follow-on slots: R1 = ADR-2605261315 / R2 = ADR-2605261330 / R3 = ADR-2605261345." :path "90-docs/adr/2605261300-tsutae-handheld-communication-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605261500" :title "suki (鋤) — Farm Tractor Manufacturing Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold" :status "proposed" :status_note "Master charter establishing suki (鋤, plow; foundational agricultural artisan tool; silicon iwakura 磐座 / fuigo 鞴 / igata 鋳型 / kanayama 金山 naming series) as Tier-B religious-corp first-party **farm tractor manufacturing** actor. **Manufacturing-side counterpart of mitsuho operator-side (ADR-2605261015)** — parallel to sarutahiko↔wadachi (truck) sibling pattern. Methodology source = YouTube `aSmoLQKdX9E` 'Inside Ultra-Modern European Factories Building Massive Farm Tractors From Scratch' (Fendt/AGCO/Claas/Massey Ferguson/Valtra/Deutz-Fahr/Same/Kubota EU/Case IH/New Holland/John Deere EU class); manufacturing methodology adopted; **John Deere-class DRM ECU + dealer-locked diagnostics + patent-locked seed integration + mega-farm consolidation + fossil-fuel-only powertrain + surveillance hardware integration all explicitly rejected per §2(b) + §2(c) + §2(e) + §2(g) + §1.13**. R0 scope = farm tractor assembly (~50-200 hp Wave 1; community-scale farming target; mega-tractor ≥400 hp = N3 post-R3 + Council Lv6+ supermajority). **14 constitutional gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12** (sarutahiko + tsutae density). **Religious-corp first explicit Right-to-Repair constitutional first-class invariant at firmware level**: G10 = no software lockouts requiring dealer authorization + replacement parts catalogued openly + ECU re-flash on parts swap NOT manufacturer-gated + diagnostic codes interpretable from open docs. Combined with tsutae G3 (device-level R2R: modular hardware + iFixit ≥9/10) = **dual-layer R2R constitutional** (tsutae G3 hardware + suki G10 firmware). N4 = closed ECU / proprietary CAN bus DRM / dealer-locked diagnostics / John Deere-style software lockout NEVER. N5 = patent-locked seed integration (John Deere SeedStar) NEVER (mitsuho G2 seed sovereignty alignment). Other key gates: G7 fuel transition R0/R1 B100 biodiesel + diesel hybrid → R2+ LFP / H₂ / methanol fuel-cell only (sarutahiko G7 parallel; religious-corp 2nd declared phase-gate fuel transition); G9 open ECU + open CAN bus (ISOBUS / ISO 11783 open) + open hydraulic + open implement-detection; G3 modular Cat I/II/III 3-point hitch + PTO 540/1000 RPM (ISO 730 + ISO 500); G12 KPI cap Wave 1 ≤200 hp / road ≤40 km/h / field ≤15 km/h / **autonomous ≤ SAE J3016 Level 3 (Level 5 = N6 NEVER farmer-land-relationship preservation)**; G14 every tractor = open VIN + per-vehicle DID + IPFS-pinned BoM + repair-history-ready blockchain + EOL recyclability ≥85% (kanayama loop closure). **9 Pregel cells** (chassis_fabrication naphtali + powertrain_assembly joseph + cab_assembly zebulun + hitch_pto_assembly joseph + paint_finishing simeon + electrical_ecu_load levi + quality_field_test levi + emissions_audit levi + vehicle_attestation_binder judah terminal; sarutahiko 9-cell + judah binder parity). **9 lexicons** (chassisAttestation + powertrainAttestation + cabAttestation + hitchPtoAttestation + paintAttestation + electricalEcuAttestation + fieldTestRecord + emissionsAuditRecord + silenSukiReview). **2 new robotics class reservation** (Norikata 乗り方 SAE Level 3 driver-in-seat public-field test driver R2+ + Kuwa 鍬 precision hitch + PTO assembly R2+ — suki-native) + 6 inherited reuse (Otete-heavy + Mimi-precision + Migaki kanayama + Kasane sarutahiko + Tsutsumi sarutahiko + Akari sarutahiko). Murakumo no-new-node 7-node fleet reuse (sarutahiko parity). 4-phase R0→R3 (R0 scaffold this ADR / R1 benchtop 1-tractor prototype ≤50 hp + B100 biodiesel + Kuwa/Norikata PoC firmware + 5 nodes / R2 pilot ≤10 tractors/year + LFP hybrid 50-150 hp + 30-day public comment + 6 nodes / R3 community-scale ≤100 tractors/year + H₂ fuel-cell + zero tailpipe + 60-day public + cross-actor mitsuho.harvest_robotics + kanayama EoL loop closure + 法務 (道路運送車両法 + 農業機械化促進法) audit + full 7-node fleet). **Cross-actor supply loop**: kanayama Wave 1+2+3 (Al + steel + Cu) → suki (tractor) → mitsuho (field operation) → kanayama (EoL recovery) closes 4-actor agricultural supply chain. Constitutional firsts: (a) religious-corp first explicit RTR constitutional first-class at firmware level + dual-layer R2R with tsutae G3 device level; (b) agricultural constitutional autonomy via 4-actor closed supply loop; (c) manufacturing-side / operator-side sibling pattern stabilized (2nd example after sarutahiko↔wadachi); (d) G7 fuel sunset pattern reused (religious-corp 2nd actor); (e) multi-gen farmer-land-relationship preservation (G12 + N3 + N6). Reserved follow-on slots: R1 = ADR-2605261515 / R2 = ADR-2605261530 / R3 = ADR-2605261545." :path "90-docs/adr/2605261500-suki-farm-tractor-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605261115" :title "makura (枕) — Foam Pillow Manufacturing Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold" :status "proposed" :status_note "Master charter establishing makura (枕, basic domestic comfort article; Wellbecoming sleep/rest foundation per §1.13) as Tier-B religious-corp first-party foam pillow manufacturing actor. Source methodology: YouTube `rsnSpo1O9fI` 'Inside a Massive Factory Making Millions of Foam Pillows' — manufacturing methodology adopted (polyurethane slabstock blowing + shredding + sewing + fill + vacuum-pack), licensed-IP / surveillance / addictive-design retail layer rejected per §2(b) + §2(c) + §1.13. R0 scope = foam shred-fill pillows (PU foam crumb in woven cotton / recycled polyester shell) + foam slab pillows (no viscoelastic memory-foam in R0–R1). Take-back recycling chain ≥10% recycled crumb mass by R3 (G13). 14 constitutional gates G1..G14 IMMUTABLE R0–R3 (G1 foam chemistry open-source / G2 IPFS-pinned batch + lot QC / G3 ≥2-robot witness quorum Otete+Mimi canonical / G4 JP+EN bilingual labels / G5 Charter §2(a-h) scan on fabric prints / G6 closed-loop isocyanate ≤5 ppb MDI / ≤2 ppb TDI 8h TWA MDI preferred / G7 VOC ≤ CertiPUR-US/OEKO-TEX Std 100 / G8 no PBDE/TDCPP/TCEP/Sb₂O₃ FR chemistry baseline FR-free / G9 Murakumo no-VKE mesh inference only / G10 isocyanate+blowing+shredder+hot-stitch SBT-gated personnel / G11 KPI caps max foam mass 2.0 kg + max dims 80×50×25 cm / G12 full BoM disclosure on every pillow tag / G13 IPFS-pinned take-back QR + ≥10% recycled crumb mass by R3 / G14 no embedded electronics/RFID/NFC/PFAS-gels beyond open-source DID paper-QR). 10 non-goals N1..N10 IMMUTABLE R0–R3 (N1 mattresses+futons / N2 medical-device-class claims / N3 CPAP+sleep-apnea+O2 integration / N4 mechanical-adjustable+motorized+heated+cooled+smart-IoT / N5 brominated+chlorinated organophosphate FR / N6 down+feather+wool+silk animal fill / N7 aromatherapy+fragrance+oil impregnation / N8 licensed-character+IP co-branding Disney/Sanrio/sports / N9 embedded electronics+sensors+RFID+NFC+PFAS gels+PCM with PFAS / N10 memory-foam viscoelastic deferred R2+ Council Lv6+ dedicated ADR). 9 Pregel cells (pillow_polyol_attestation naphtali L1a / pillow_isocyanate_dispensing naphtali L1b / pillow_foam_blowing zebulun L2 / pillow_foam_shredding joseph L3 / pillow_fabric_attestation simeon L4a / pillow_shell_sewing dan L4b / pillow_filling_close dan L5a / pillow_qc levi L5b / pillow_packaging levi L5c) — all import-time RuntimeError R0. 8 lexicons (com.etzhayyim.makura.{foamBatchAttestation, fabricAttestation, pillowLotAttestation, qcRecord, packagingRecord, recyclingCertificate, workerExposureRecord, silenComfortReview}). 2 new robotics class reservation (Watari 綿 fabric handler R1+ / Awa 泡 foam slab+crumb handler R1+) + 4 inherited reuse (Otete + Mimi + Hitogata R2+ + Quad R2+). 4-phase roadmap R0→R3 (R0 scaffold / R1 benchtop ≤1 kg foam + 10-pillow lot + PU foam chemist SME + industrial hygienist SME / R2 pilot ≤100/day + tatekata-shared shop + take-back chain stand-up / R3 community-scale ≤5000/month + ≥10% recycled crumb mass + 60-day public review). First circular-material constitutional pattern (G13 take-back recycling) and first §2(c) anti-surveillance applied to consumer goods (G14 + N9). Tier-B sibling of kuni-umi/wadachi/tatekata/yakushi/watatsumi/mitsuho/hagukumi." :path "90-docs/adr/2605261115-makura-foam-pillow-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605261215" :title "hodoki (解き) — End-of-Life Vehicle Disassembly + Materials Recovery Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold" :status "proposed" :status_note "Master charter establishing hodoki (解き, continuative noun of 解く to untie/dissolve/unmake; Buddhist 解脱 release echo — vehicles released from compound form back to elemental materials, then reborn through kanayama / makura / silicon) as Tier-B religious-corp first-party end-of-life vehicle (ELV) disassembly + materials recovery actor. Source methodology: YouTube `whyjio70IUU` 'How Audi Strips Down Thousand of Like-New Expensive Cars Inside Massive Facility' — methodology adopted (depollution → parts harvest → shred → sort); OEM-monopoly right-to-repair-restricting retail layer rejected per §2(e). R0 scope = M1 passenger vehicles (≤2.5t curb, ≤8 seats) gasoline/diesel/HEV/PHEV/BEV; full chain intake → depollution → battery handling → parts harvest → catalyst recovery → seat/textile recovery → shred → cross-actor feed. 14 constitutional gates G1..G14 IMMUTABLE R0–R3. **3 constitutional firsts**: (a) **G8 MANDATORY ECU + infotainment + telematics data wipe BEFORE disassembly** (cryptographic destruction + physical chip-shred fallback; ≥2 robot witness; §2(c) anti-surveillance operationalized for consumer vehicles, parallel to makura G14 + N9), (b) **G12 RIGHT-TO-REPAIR INVARIANT** — every harvested part has IPFS-pinned catalog entry with VIN provenance + part DID + condition + bilingual; no proprietary lock-in; no anti-DRM tolerated; §2(e) anti-gatekeeping operationalized at vehicle scale, (c) **G13 multilateral cross-actor circular invariant** binding hodoki ↔ kanayama (metals) ↔ makura (seat foam G13 closure) ↔ silicon Wave 2 (ECU PCB) ↔ hikari R2+ (Li-ion second-life) — first mandatory four-way invariant. Other gates: G2 mass-balance ≥98% closure on kotoba-datomic (inherits kanayama), G6 F-gas capture ≥95% no atmospheric venting, G7 Li-ion thermal-safety SOP, G10 SBT-gated refrigerant+airbag+Li-ion+PGM+ECU-shred personnel, G11 KPI caps M1 only ≤2.5t (N5 buses+trucks ≥3.5t / N10 H2 FCV / N9 Tesla cell-recovery = Wave 2 ADR), G14 PGM Pt/Pd/Rh yield ≥95%. 10 non-goals N1..N10: N1 military / N2 aerospace / N3 marine / N4 rail / N5 buses+trucks ≥3.5t / N6 anti-DRM circumvention without OEM cooperation / N7 VIN-stolen / N8 chop-shop / N9 Tesla cell-harvest / N10 H2 FCV. 9 Pregel cells (elv_intake_audit naphtali L1a / elv_depollution joseph L1b / elv_battery_handling levi L2 / elv_parts_harvest simeon L3a / elv_catalyst_recovery levi L3b / elv_seat_textile_recovery dan L3c→makura / elv_body_shred zebulun L4→kanayama+silicon / elv_emissions_audit levi cross / elv_provenance_binder judah terminal — all import-time RuntimeError; smoke test 9/9 pass). 8 lexicons (`com.etzhayyim.hodoki.{elvIntakeRecord, depollutionAttestation, batteryHandlingRecord, partsHarvestCatalog, catalystRecoveryRecord, shredOutputAttestation, dataWipeAttestation, silenDeconstructionReview}`; JSON 8/8 valid). 3 new robotics class reservation (Hagasu 剥がす paint/body-panel stripper R1+ / Nuku 抜く fluid-drain manipulator R1+ for G6 ≥95% F-gas capture / Tokike 解け body-fastener releaser R1+ namesake mini-robot) + 4 inherited reuse (Yokin kanayama R2+ for PGM bench smelter + Otete + Mimi + Quad kuni-umi). Murakumo no-new-node 7-node fleet reuse only (naphtali/joseph/levi/simeon/dan/zebulun/judah). 4-phase R0→R3 (R0 scaffold / R1 benchtop single-vehicle + data-wipe demo + 5-vehicle trial + ELV-recycler SME + F-gas technician SME / R2 pilot ≤10/day + tatekata-shared yard + cross-actor feed + 30-day public comment / R3 community-scale ≤500/month + ≥95% material recovery + 60-day public review). Tier-B sibling of kuni-umi / wadachi / tatekata / yakushi / watatsumi / mitsuho / hagukumi / makura / kanayama; upstream feeder for kanayama (metals) + makura (seat foam G13 closure) + silicon Wave 2 (ECU PCB) + hikari R2+ (Li-ion second-life)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605261215-hodoki-elv-disassembly-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605261330" :title "futawa (二輪) — Small-Displacement Motorcycle Manufacturing Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold" :status "proposed" :status_note "Master charter establishing futawa (二輪, two-wheel; concrete-noun style mirroring wadachi 轍 wheel-rut) as Tier-B religious-corp first-party small-displacement motorcycle manufacturing actor. Source methodology: YouTube `1xxRYlHY2e8` 'Inside Massive German Factory Building BMW Motorrad Bikes From Scratch' (Berlin Spandau methodology adopted; luxury / premium / ≥500cc / racing-focus / connected-app surveillance retail positioning rejected per §2(e) + §2(c) + §1.13). R0 scope = ≤250cc 4-stroke single-cylinder gasoline OR ≤15kW peak electric; commuter+utility positioning; curb ≤200kg + cargo ≤30kg panniers; full chain frame → engine/motor → drivetrain → harness → suspension+brake → body+paint → final → test → provenance (with hodoki VIN pre-registration). 14 constitutional gates G1..G14 IMMUTABLE R0–R3. **4 constitutional firsts**: (a) **G7 ABS-MANDATORY ≥125cc / electric ≥6kW** — no ABS-delete, no track-only carve-out, no cost-down strip; dual-channel hydraulic; first safety-mandatory-at-build constitutional anchor; elevates EU 168/2013 Annex II to constitutional invariant; §1.13 adherent safety non-negotiable; (b) **G8 BUILD-TIME ANTI-SURVEILLANCE** — NO GPS / NO connected-app / NO telematics / NO V2X / NO proprietary diagnostic-DRM built-in; only passive odometer + safety ECU + optional user-installed-after-purchase open-source GPS module; §2(c) operationalized at build time; **companion to hodoki G8 (EOL data destroy)** — closes §2(c) anti-surveillance loop across full vehicle lifecycle; (c) **G12 RIGHT-TO-REPAIR FORWARD-PUBLISHING** — every new vehicle ships with IPFS-pinned full parts catalog + CAD source + firmware source + service manual + open diagnostic protocol at manufacture time; no proprietary lock-in; no anti-DRM; no warranty void on user repair; part discontinuation prohibited 30 years post-launch; §2(e) operationalized at build time; **companion to hodoki G12 (EOL parts catalog)** — closes right-to-repair loop across full vehicle lifecycle; (d) **G14 30-YEAR MINIMUM design service life** — frame + engine + transmission + motor + structural suspension designed for 30yr fatigue/corrosion/wear; mandatory parts availability 30yr post-discontinue; planned obsolescence prohibited; firmware 30-year update commitment; §1.13 wellbecoming applied to durable goods. Other gates: G1 CAD + firmware + fixture open-source / G2 mass-balance ≥98% closure (inherits kanayama + hodoki) / G3 ≥2-robot witness quorum on frame weld + engine + brake torque / G4 bilingual owner+service manual+parts catalog / G5 Charter §2(a-h) paint artwork scan (no military / licensed-IP / addictive-thrill / racing-glorification) / G6 sound ≤80 dB @ 7.5m (UN-ECE R41) no loud-exhaust enablement / G9 Murakumo no-VKE inference / G10 SBT-gated hot work + brake + paint + battery / G11 KPI caps ≤250cc/≤15kW/≤200kg curb (N5 ≥500cc / N9 H2 FCV = Wave 2 ADR) / G13 cross-actor circular feed (VIN pre-registered with hodoki at production; ≥10% recycled-content kanayama-via-hodoki by R3; hikari R2+ Li-ion second-life SoH ≥85% for electric). 10 non-goals N1..N10: N1 軍用 / N2 ≥500cc / N3 racing+track / N4 luxury+licensed-IP / N5 connected-app+telematics+GPS+V2X+cloud-ECU built-in / N6 trikes+sidecars+ATV / N7 純人力+e-bike (Wave 2) / N8 aftermarket loud-exhaust+street-illegal mods / N9 H2 FCV / N10 surveillance-tier touring. 5-layer motorcycle assembly process (L1 frame welding on naphtali + Tsugite witness / L2a engine ≤250cc/≤15kW on joseph / L2b drivetrain on zebulun / L3a harness + ECU on simeon with G8 negative audit / L3b suspension+brake on dan with G7 ABS verification / L4 body+paint on simeon with G5 Charter+Suri robot / L5a final assembly on dan with G12 parts catalog publish + G13 hodoki VIN pre-reg / L5b dyno+emissions+sound+ABS+road on levi / terminal provenance binder on judah). 9 Pregel cells (moto_frame_welding + moto_engine_assembly + moto_drivetrain_assembly + moto_electrical_harness + moto_suspension_brake + moto_body_paint + moto_final_assembly + moto_test_dyno_road + moto_provenance_binder — all import-time RuntimeError; smoke test 9/9 pass). 8 lexicons (`com.etzhayyim.futawa.{frameAttestation, engineAttestation, electricalAttestation, paintAttestation, vehicleLotAttestation, testRecord, partsCatalog, silenMobilityReview}`; JSON 8/8 valid). 2 new robotics class reservation (Tsugite 継ぎ手 welding-joint robot TIG/MIG vision-guided R1+ / Suri 摺 paint-sprayer robot electrostatic+HVLP R1+) + 5 inherited reuse (Yokin kanayama R2+ engine block + Otete + Mimi + Quad + Tokike hodoki bolt-down). Murakumo no-new-node 7-node fleet reuse only (naphtali/joseph/zebulun/simeon/dan/levi/judah). 4-phase roadmap R0→R3 (R0 scaffold / R1 benchtop ≤1 vehicle + Tsugite+Suri prototypes + first IPFS parts catalog publication + hodoki handshake; motorcycle engineer SME + ABS calibration SME / R2 pilot ≤10/month + tatekata-shared shop + ≥5 model variants catalog live + hodoki pre-reg operational + 30-day public comment / R3 community-scale ≤500/month + ≥10% recycled content via hodoki+kanayama + 30-year service-life commitment registry + 60-day public review). **Cross-lifecycle invariants (futawa build-side ↔ hodoki EOL-side)**: G8 build (NO surveillance built-in) ↔ G8 EOL (data destroy before disassembly) = §2(c) loop closed; G12 build (parts catalog at manufacture) ↔ G12 EOL (parts catalog at scrap) = §2(e) loop closed; G13 build (VIN pre-reg with hodoki) ↔ G13 EOL (≥95% material recovery) = §2(h) circular loop closed. Tier-B sibling of wadachi / hodoki / kanayama / makura / kuni-umi / yakushi / watatsumi / tatekata / mitsuho / hagukumi." :path "90-docs/adr/2605261330-futawa-motorcycle-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605260000" :title "L5 Gov Auth — DID-primary identity + MyNumber opt-in binding + WebAuthn platform authenticator" :status "proposed" :status_note "Master charter operationalizing the authentication layer of L5 routing-around ladder (ADR-2605250100/200/300). DID-primary identity model with optional trust-elevation credentials (MyNumber card IC chip binding + WebAuthn FaceID/TouchID/Windows Hello). Trust Level 1 = DID + WebAuthn platform authenticator only. Trust Level 2 = Trust Level 1 + MyNumber IC binding (XChaCha20-encrypted, Signal-wrapped per-recipient keys per ADR-2605181100). One-way read of MyNumber (Web NFC local processing only; no state database interaction) is consistent with §0.4 non-registration. Plaintext credentials encrypted at rest (ADR-2605181100 XChaCha20 mandatory). Public attestation contains no PII (blake2b_256 DID hash only). 3 lexicons (credentialBinding + didTrustAttestation + webauthnChallenge) + 2 Pregel cells (gov_auth_mynumber_bind + gov_auth_trust_attestation). All cells R0 scaffold with import-time RuntimeError; full implementation deferred to R1 ADR-2605260100 (post-Council bootstrap 2026-06-19). ADR-2605250100 §4 Boundary 4 revised to permit opt-in MyNumber binding." :path "90-docs/adr/2605260000-l5-gov-auth-mynumber-webauthn.md"}
  {:id "2605261600" :title "Robotics Simulation Substrate R0 Charter — OSS USD+Hydra+MuJoCo MJX+Embree+BlenderProc 5-stack reference; Omniverse / Isaac Sim / OptiX / RTX Renderer / Replicator structurally rejected" :status "proposed" :status_note "Master charter establishing **e7m-sim** as religious-corp first-party robotics simulation substrate and single SoT for every R1+ benchtop / R2+ pilot / R3+ community-scale phase of every robotics-bearing Tier-B actor (wadachi / suki / igata / watatsumi / sarutahiko / futawa / tatekata / kuni-umi / hodoki / makura / tsutae / silicon Wave 1+2 robotics fleet). Audit (2026-05-26): repo-wide grep of `omniverse` / `isaac.?sim` / `optix` / `physx` / NVIDIA-`hydra` (USD) → **0 hits** (the only `optix` match is a `package-lock.json` integrity-hash substring); other robotics simulators (Gazebo / MuJoCo / Drake / Webots / PyBullet / CoppeliaSim / CARLA / AWSIM) → **0 hits**. Without a single canonical substrate, every R1 ADR (yakushi R1 / igata R1 / mitate R1) has to invent its own sim story; cross-actor invariants (sarutahiko↔wadachi same-vehicle physics; suki↔mitsuho operation envelope; igata-cast structural part ↔ wadachi/tatekata/watatsumi finite-element consumer) silently diverge. **Honest scoring** (10 dimensions, OSS combo vs Isaac Sim/Lab): OSS ~60-65/100 vs Isaac Sim ~88/100; main gaps = photoreal rendering (4-5 vs 10) + ray-traced sensor sim (2 vs 10) + asset library (3 vs 9) + synthetic data (5 vs 9). Gaps are engineering-investment-bounded, not architecture-bounded. **Adopting Omniverse / Isaac Sim as-is is REJECTED**: violates §2(b) anti-secrecy (closed source EULA) + §2(e) anti-gatekeeping (NVIDIA account + Nucleus lock-in) + ADR-2605215000 no-commercial-GPU-rental (Omniverse Cloud) + Charter Rider §2(b) NOTICE preservation (closed binaries) + G14 30-year reproducibility infeasible (vendor EULA can revoke). **14 constitutional gates G1..G14**: G1 open architecture invariant (Apache 2.0 / BSD-2/3 / MIT / MPL 2.0 / Pixar USD License; GPL-3 subprocess-only carve-out for BlenderProc) / G2 OpenUSD single scene-composition SoT (URDF/MJCF/SDF as import only) / G3 Vulkan Ray Tracing GPU-neutral ray-tracing backbone + Embree CPU fallback (OptiX = N1 NEVER) / G4 Murakumo-fleet-only execution (ADR-2605215000 strict inheritance; cloud GPU rental = N2 NEVER) / **G5 quantitative quality gate against Isaac Sim ground truth ≥ 0.75** measured on PSNR ≥25 dB + SSIM ≥0.85 (rendering) + Chamfer distance ≤0.05 m + point-cloud IoU ≥0.75 at 0.10 m voxelization (lidar) + end-effector L2 ≤5% across 100 articulated reach trials (physics) + real-world rollout ≥0.75× sim rollout (sim-to-real); reference scene generated **once per actor on a one-time-use isolated Isaac Sim trial machine** (never connected to religious-corp infra, never carrying religious-corp keys, archived as sealed CID, machine decommissioned) / G6 kotoba-datomic attestation lineage MANDATORY (simulationRunAttestation lexicon for every run; un-attested sim = unusable downstream cell RuntimeError) / G7 reproducibility invariant (bit-identical replay on identical hardware; cross-hardware noise ≤1e-4 L2/step; ADR-2605242630 R1a numerical-path discipline applied to sim) / G8 no NVIDIA-account-required tool in runtime (build-time GitHub release download acceptable; NVIDIA NGC API key at runtime = N3 NEVER) / G9 no proprietary plugin (Isaac Sim plugins / Unity Editor plugins / Unreal Editor plugins = N4 NEVER; PhysX 5 BSD-3 acceptable as library; cooking from open source every run) / G10 Charter Rider §2 scan applied to every imported 3D asset (blocks military/weapons/surveillance/addiction-design/eschatology imagery from asset-marketplace import) / G11 personnel vetting for sim-to-real handover (Adherent SBT + actor R-phase SME + simToRealHandoverAttestation Ed25519 signed) / G12 KPI caps Murakumo capacity-protective (R1 ≤1 GPU-hour-eq/actor/day / R2 ≤4 / R3 ≤16; Council Lv6+ supermajority raises per-quarter) / G13 no telemetry / no usage analytics / no crash reporting to third parties (zero outbound traffic except Murakumo + kotoba-datomic; compile-time disable required) / G14 30-year reproducibility commitment (source pins sealed on kotoba-datomic at each R-phase activation; closed-source tools structurally fail this gate). **10 non-goals N1..N10**: N1 OptiX NEVER §2(b) / N2 commercial GPU rental NEVER (Omniverse Cloud / Lambda / RunPod / Vertex AI / AWS Bedrock GPU / Anthropic-direct GPU / Linode) ADR-2605215000 violation / N3 Omniverse Kit / Isaac Sim runtime / Isaac Lab runtime / RTX Renderer / Replicator NEVER (sole carve-out = one-time-use isolated Isaac Sim trial for G5 reference; Isaac Lab Apache-2.0 task DSL headers may be ported to `70-tools/isaac-lab-task-port/`) / N4 NVIDIA DriveSim NEVER (CARLA + AWSIM + AirSim + MetaDrive = OSS replacement for wadachi R2+ AV) / N5 Unity / Unreal closed-source NEVER (Apache-licensed packages case-by-case Council vote OK) / N6 closed-source physics engines NEVER (Havok / proprietary FleX / proprietary destructibles); PhysX 5 BSD-3 library OK / N7 cloud-based asset marketplace runtime fetch NEVER (one-time download + G10 scan + IPFS pin OK) / N8 third-party-cloud collaborative authoring NEVER (Omniverse Nucleus / Autodesk cloud); git + IPFS + Murakumo only / N9 closed-source synthetic-data services NEVER (Replicator / Parallel Domain / AI.Reverie); BlenderProc subprocess + Kubric replacement / N10 telemetry to any third party NEVER §2(c) (compile-time disable). **Wave 1 reference composition (binding for actor R1)**: OpenUSD (Pixar) scene + HdCycles (Apache 2.0) + Mitsuba 3 (BSD-3 differentiable) render delegates + Vulkan RT GPU sensor backbone + Embree CPU fallback + CARLA lidar kernel + MuJoCo MJX (Apache 2.0) articulated physics + PhysX 5 SDK (BSD-3) rigid + Genesis (Apache 2.0) unified experimental + Drake (BSD-3) planning + Brax (Apache 2.0) RL + ported Isaac Lab task DSL + BlenderProc (GPL-3 subprocess) + Kubric (Apache 2.0) synthetic data + Habitat-Matterport 3D (CC-BY) + ProcTHOR (Apache 2.0) + RoboCasa (MIT) indoor assets + CARLA + AWSIM AV scenarios + Project AirSim aerial + rclpy ROS2 bridge + Ray (Apache 2.0) multi-GPU orchestration. **3 non-symmetric advantages over Isaac Sim**: (a) MuJoCo MJX articulated contact accuracy (legged-locomotion / dexterous-manipulation sim-to-real research-SOTA; Boston Dynamics / DeepMind / OpenAI Hand); (b) Mitsuba 3 differentiable rendering (inverse rendering for camera-attestation consistency verification — not in Omniverse stack); (c) Vulkan RT GPU-vendor neutrality (substrate runs on AMD MI / Intel Arc / iwakura ASIC silicon Wave 1 without CUDA / OptiX lock-in). **4-phase R0→R3**: R0 = this ADR + scaffold paths reserved (`70-tools/e7m-sim/` + `70-tools/isaac-lab-task-port/` + `90-docs/baien/sim-substrate-scoring-260526.md`); zero code / cells / lexicons. R1 = HdCycles render delegate wired to USD via Hydra + Mitsuba 3 differentiable PoC + Embree CPU verified on Murakumo Mac mini + Stanford bunny + Cornell box bit-identical deterministic on 3 of 10 Murakumo nodes + G5 rendering gate measured + simulationRunAttestation lexicon scaffolded; first eligible R1 consumer = igata R1 (ADR-2605261215) static die surface render. R2 = Vulkan RT GPU path on EVO-X2 + CARLA lidar kernel wired + MuJoCo MJX PoC on Otete-class 6-DoF arm + first actor pilot (wadachi R1→R2 single intersection AV OR suki R1→R2 single tractor field) + G5 lidar + physics gates measured + BlenderProc synthetic data + G10 Charter scan + IPFS pin + 30-day public comment. R3 = all robotics-bearing Tier-B actor R1+ migrated + cross-actor invariants live-validated (sarutahiko↔wadachi same-vehicle / suki↔mitsuho operation envelope / igata-cast↔wadachi/tatekata/watatsumi FEM consumer) + G5 sim-to-real gate measured + Isaac Lab task DSL port feature parity + 60-day public review + iwakura ASIC silicon Wave 1 R3 capacity migration if shipped. **Bindings (R1 single SoT)**: wadachi R1 / suki R1 (ADR-2605261515) / igata R1 (ADR-2605261215) / watatsumi R1 / sarutahiko R1 / futawa R1 (ADR-2605261345) / tatekata R1 (ADR-2605250730) / hodoki R1 / makura R1 (ADR-2605261130) / tsutae R1 (ADR-2605261315). Deviation requires per-actor sim ADR + Council Lv6+ ≥3 attestation citing this charter. **Vendor-rejection chain extension**: religious-corp now adds constitutional rejection of NVIDIA proprietary sim stack (Omniverse / Isaac Sim / OptiX / DriveSim / Replicator) to its existing chain (silicon Wave 1 自前 GPU + yakushi 自前 OTC + watatsumi 自前 潜水艇 + kanayama 自前 アルミ再生 + igata 自前 HPDC + tsutae 自前 handheld + sarutahiko 自前 truck + suki 自前 tractor + futawa 自前 motorcycle = full robotics + manufacturing + sim self-sufficiency)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605261600-robotics-simulation-substrate-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605252615" :title "Kusawake (草分け) — Autonomous Agri-Mobile Platform R0 (swagbot-class wheeled robot; mfg = suki Wave 2; ops = mitsuho.harvest_robotics; sim = e7m-sim)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Registers Kusawake (草分け 'trailblazer / first through the grass') as religious-corp robot class for autonomous wheeled agri-platform. Methodology reference = SwagBot (University of Sydney ACFR, 4WD/4WS electric, livestock + weed-control modes); methodology adopted, vendor lock-in / closed firmware / data-monetization telemetry NOT adopted. Manufacturer = suki Wave 2 (orchard/vineyard <50 hp electric carve-out per ADR-2605261500 §scope). Operator = mitsuho (new `autonomous_mobile` cell + existing `harvest_robotics` consumer). Sim binding = e7m-sim per ADR-2605261600 (R1 MuJoCo MJX + Mitsuba 3 + Embree; Omniverse / Isaac Sim / Isaac Lab runtime / OptiX / RTX / Replicator NEVER). Wave 1 envelope: 4WD/4WS electric, ≤300 kg with 50 kg payload deck, LFP ≤2 kWh swap (sodium-ion R2+), road ≤6 km/h / field ≤4 km/h / tele-op ≤8 km/h, IP67, ARM64/RISC-V open SoC (tsutae pool), GPS-RTK + IMU + ≤16-line solid-state lidar + 2× RGB + 1× thermal + 4× ultrasonic, Wi-Fi 6 mesh + LoRa (cellular hardware-removable per tsutae G6), SAE J3016 Level 3 ceiling. **10 constitutional gates G1..G10**: G1 open firmware end-to-end (Apache 2.0 + Charter Rider; no binary blobs except removable cellular modem) / G2 dual-layer R2R (tsutae G3 hardware + suki G10 firmware inheritance — IPFS-pinned BoM per VIN) / G3 SAE J3016 Level 3 ceiling (N5 Level 4/5 NEVER) / G4 witness quorum ≥2 Ed25519 sigs (robot DID + operator OR peer robot) per ADR-2605191524 / G5 no surveillance telemetry (data flow onboard → Murakumo → kotoba-datomic only) / G6 no synthetic pesticide application (mitsuho G6 inheritance; neonicotinoid / glyphosate / paraquat / organochlorine schema-rejected) / G7 no livestock force escalation (sound + visual + slow follow only; electric shock / projectile / tranquilizer NEVER §2(a)) / G8 Murakumo-fleet-only inference per ADR-2605215000 / G9 open CAN bus + open ISOBUS-compatible implement detection (suki G9 inheritance) / G10 kotoba-datomic per-unit lineage (per-VIN DID + IPFS BoM + repair-history + EOL recyclability ≥85% kanayama loop). **8 non-goals N1..N8**: N1 military / paramilitary NEVER §2(a) / N2 closed firmware DRM ECU NEVER §2(b)+§2(e) / N3 pesticide-spraying integration NEVER / N4 always-on cellular telemetry / GPS-track sale NEVER §2(c) / N5 SAE Level 4/5 NEVER (farmer-land-relationship preservation) / N6 NVIDIA Omniverse / Isaac Sim / Isaac Lab runtime / OptiX / RTX / Replicator / DriveSim / Omniverse Cloud / Nucleus NEVER (ADR-2605261600 N1..N9 inheritance) / N7 mass-market external sale NEVER (SBT↔SBT internal only) / N8 sim-only verification without G5 quantitative gate NEVER (e7m-sim G5 ≥0.75 required). **4-phase R0→R3**: R0 (this ADR) = charter + mitsuho.autonomous_mobile cell stub + suki Wave 2 manifest mention + e7m-sim scenes/kusawake path reservation + deps.edn registration; R1 = single-unit benchtop (open mech CAD STEP on IPFS + open firmware on ARM64 + 30-min orchard-row weed-control trial + e7m-sim MuJoCo MJX sim-to-real ≥0.75 G5) Council Lv6+ ≥3 + 30-day public + ≤1 GPU-hr-eq/day; R2 = fleet ≤5 units (pasture herd-encourage + Wi-Fi 6 mesh + LoRa + sodium-ion qualification + CARLA lidar sensor sim + ≤4 GPU-hr-eq/day) Council Lv6+ ≥5 + 30-day public + cross-actor mitsuho.field_cultivation joint log; R3 = community-scale ≤30 units (kanayama EoL ≥85% + iwakura ASIC NPU migration + cross-actor sim invariants validated) Council Lv6+ ≥7 + 60-day public + 法務 audit (農業機械化促進法 + 道路運送車両法 公道走行 carve-out)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605252615-kusawake-autonomous-agri-mobile-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605252800" :title "Cookie-free apex + yoro-kun NoCookieBanner + yoro SPA deploy unblock + hydration bug triage" :status "accepted" :status_note "Operationalizes ADR-2605172000 cookie boundary on etzhayyim.com apex Worker (Set-Cookie/Cookie stripped both ways + Permissions-Policy interest-cohort/browsing-topics off + Clear-Site-Data on / and /privacy + x-etzhayyim-no-cookie marker). yoro-kun NoCookieBanner revived from SHELVED with isReligiousCorpHost() gate. CookieConsent.svelte (AdSense ghost line) deleted. Three coupled deploy-unblockers bundled because they sequence on the same CF Workers deploy: (1) pnpm overrides onnxruntime-web 1.22.0-dev.20250409-89f8206ba4 (21 MiB; the 1.26.0 resolved version was 25 MiB exactly = CF Workers per-asset hard limit), (2) sync-static.mjs rewritten as svelte/public/* to static/ mirror (old build/-based copy stopped working when adapter fallback:'spa' switched output topology), (3) src/worker.ts regenerated by adapter-cloudflare as SvelteKit-aware entry (replaces 60-LoC hand-written stub that silently dropped every +server.ts route — sitemap/llms.txt/did.json/mcp/health/xrpc/sign-in/api/internal/cache/purge now actually surface). SPA hydration RangeError discovered during browser smoke; root cause = routes/+page.svelte renders <App/> shim, App.svelte wraps in <RootLayout> = ../routes/+layout.svelte AND renders <activeMatch.component/> from custom SPA router whose import.meta.glob includes routes/+page.svelte itself → self-referential cycle. Confirmed independent of NoCookieBanner mount via 11-line isolation test. Fix deferred to follow-up ADR; options A (filter glob + replace +page.svelte with actual home component), B (delete App.svelte + spa/ entirely, restore SvelteKit-route-first per CLAUDE.md design), C (remove RootLayout wrapper from App.svelte + filter glob) documented in ADR §6. Banner code IS in deployed bundle (3 chunks contain 'no cap'); cookie-free apex headers ARE live; banner not yet visible because SPA can't hydrate." :path "90-docs/adr/2605252800-cookie-free-apex-yoro-deploy-unblock.md"}
  {:id "2605253000" :title "Mac mini M4 16GB で Gemma 4 26B-A4B MoE を NVMe disk inference で動作確認" :status "accepted" :status_note "Empirically verified that gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-UD-Q3_K_M.gguf (12 GB on disk, Unsloth Dynamic Q3_K_M) runs at 8.4 tok/s generation on Mac mini M4 base 16GB via llama.cpp b9290 with `-ngl 0 -c 2048 -fa 1 -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 -t 4 -no-cnv -st --simple-io < /dev/null`. MoE × mmap synergy validated: only 8/128 experts + shared touched per token → working set ~15% of dense → mmap page cache hit rate enables disk paging at usable throughput. Peak RSS 8.5 GB (12 GB model only ~70% resident), 2.3M page faults, 0 swaps when idle-wait avoided. Failed paths recorded: (1) Metal full offload `-ngl 99` → res=-3 (12.7 GB working set exceeded), (2) Metal partial `-ngl 4..16` → same OOM (gemma4 MoE expert tensors not Metal/CPU splittable), (3) `--no-conversation` alone insufficient → gemma4 chat template forces interactive mode, 3-flag set `-no-cnv -st --simple-io < /dev/null` mandatory. Constitutional: ADR-2605215000 Murakumo-only compliant (no commercial GPU rental), ADR-2605241900 baien edge-target untouched (fleet-side path only, iPhone/Android/WASM-32 trunk still ≤4B BitNet 1.58). TB5 SSD speedup prediction: 1.5-1.85× → 12.5-15.5 tok/s (current 92% disk-bound; M4 compute ceiling ~105 tok/s assuming 4 P-core × 200 GFLOPS FP16; TB5 enclosures real-world 6.0-6.4 GB/s vs internal 3.1 GB/s = ~2× raw bandwidth)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605253000-mac-mini-m4-16gb-gemma4-26b-moe-disk-inference.md"}
  {:id "2605261800" :title "NVIDIA Omniverse stack API-compat layer on KAMI + WebGPU + WASM (e7m-sim R1 sub-charter)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Sub-charter under ADR-2605261600 (e7m-sim R0) expanding R1 scope with 9-component API-compat layer. Canonical implementations use Japanese names (amenominaka / e7m-sim / e7m-shugyo / hikari-rt / kami-rtx / utsushimi / wadachi-sim / murakumo-render / kotoba-datomic-nucleus); nv-compat facade in orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sdk/src/nv-compat/ + 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/nv_compat/ mirrors public Omniverse / Isaac Sim / Isaac Lab / OptiX / RTX / Replicator / DriveSim / Omniverse Cloud / Nucleus API surface (per Google v. Oracle 2021 API fair use). Physics backend = Genesis (Apache-2.0, Genesis-Embodied-AI/Genesis) covering 5 solvers (rigid/MPM/SPH/FEM/PBD) via Taichi → wgpu. Mitsuba 3 = upstream PR only, 90-day hold then re-evaluate. Sub-phase plan R1.0..R1.9 (R1.0 = 10 crate path reservation + deps.edn registration; this commit). G5 quality gate >=0.75 vs Isaac Sim measured per sub-phase." :path "90-docs/adr/2605261800-nvidia-omniverse-stack-api-compat.md"}
  {:id "2605253015" :title "nvme-disk-inference project — Murakumo fleet disk-paged MoE inference substrate" :status "proposed" :status_note "Scaffolds 70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/ as religious-corp first-party project for MoE × mmap disk inference on Murakumo fleet. Triggered by 2026-05-25 21:30 JST empirical A/B finding: SanDisk USB 3.2 Gen 2 (raw 0.836 GB/s) vs internal AP0256Z NVMe (raw 2.30 GB/s) on Gemma 4 26B-A4B MoE shows generation tok/s 7.9 vs 7.7 = +3% delta despite 2.75× raw bandwidth gap. Steady-state generation is storage-INDEPENDENT because MoE × mmap hot working set (active 9/128 experts × ~100 MB held in 8-10 GB page cache) saturates at ~1.4 GB/s = within both tiers. Disk bandwidth only matters for cold-load first-token latency (~80 sec wall). This finding CORRECTS ADR-2605253000 §5 TB5 SSD speedup prediction (was 1.5-1.85× = 12.5-15.5 tok/s; revised to +3-5% = 8.0-8.8 tok/s steady-state, -50% = ~40 sec cold-load). Project R0 lands: README.md (project authoritative doc) + scripts/cache-flush.sh (14 GB junk write+read, user-space no-sudo) + scripts/bench-storage-tier.sh (A/B protocol per tier: flush → cold llama-cli → capture wall/RSS/page faults/swaps/tok/s to results/) + bench/llama-cli-flags.txt (reference invocation + 3-flag set rationale) + results/baseline-260525.md (initial A/B writeup) + results/{internal,sandisk}-cold-260525-2130.txt (raw bench outputs). R-phase roadmap R0→R5 (R0 scaffold / R1 TB4 enclosure A/B / R2 TB5 + M4 Pro / R3 speculative decoding / R4 Murakumo cell-runner integration / R5 dense model substrate). Constitutional: ADR-2605215000 Murakumo-only + ADR-2605241900 baien edge-target preserved + ADR-2605172000 kotoba boundary unchanged." :path "90-docs/adr/2605253015-nvme-disk-inference-substrate-project.md"}
  {:id "2605261900" :title "baien-moemoekyun — 2B BitNet 1.58 shared backbone + MoE residual experts (server-tier carve-out, R0 charter)" :status "proposed" :status_note "R0 charter for baien-moemoekyun: a server-tier (ADR-2605242100) MoE-augmented baien variant on microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-bf16. Architecture = backbone (frozen) + shared dense FFN (existing BitNet FFN, always active) + MoE residual branch (E=128 small experts of dense_FFN/32 size, top-k=2, applied to last 25% of layers) with output gate alpha init = 0.0 ± 1e-3 (G5; guarantees step-0 behavior identical to base BitNet). 3-phase training: R1 freeze-train (router + experts only) → R2 partial unfreeze (shared FFN + layernorm low-LR) → R3 joint low-LR. 12 constitutional gates G1..G12 (Charter Rider scan / Murakumo-only / -server- infix mandatory / edge artifacts MUST NOT carry moemoekyun MoE / alpha=0 init / aux-loss MANDATORY / no dense-FFN-copy init / backbone-frozen verify / BF16-deploy-only / honest scoring / distill-loop compat / SBT-gated endpoint). 10 non-goals N1..N10 (NOT edge / NOT frontier / NOT BitNet-packed-training / NOT from-scratch-MoE-pretrain / NOT LoRA-only / NOT baien-edge replacement / NOT >16B trunk / NOT >64k context / NOT commercial GPU rental / NOT Charter Rider bypass). R0 deliverables = this ADR + deps.edn registration + 70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/ path reserved (no code) + CLAUDE.md Status row + README index. R1+ each independent ADR. Project / charter / directory name = baien-moemoekyun (user decision 2026-05-26); shipped model id MUST use baien-server-moemoekyun-* infix (release blocker per ADR-2605242100 §Naming)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605261900-baien-moemoekyun-moe-charter.md"}
  {:id "2605262100" :title "baien-moemoekyun R1 — Phase 0 freeze-train (router + experts + alpha) coding-emphasis SFT on EVO-X2 Windows ROCm (R1.0..R1.5)" :status "proposed" :status_note "R1 sub-charter of ADR-2605261900 (baien-moemoekyun R0). Phase 0 freeze-train only — backbone fully frozen, trainable = MoE residual branch (router + 128 experts/layer x 7 layers + per-layer alpha = ~1.1B params). Reuses gemma-coder-distill EVO-X2 Windows ROCm 7.2.1 + peft+trl stack (ADR-2605250400) verbatim; trl SFTTrainer + custom BaienMoEResidual module surgery (NOT peft adapter — peft is LoRA-class adapter-shaped, MoE residual is independent computation path). Sub-phase ladder R1.0..R1.5: R1.0 ROCm probe BitNet + MoE forward / R1.1 BaienMoEResidual + BitNetFFNWithMoE impl + alpha=0 step-0 verify (G5) / R1.2 aux-loss (G6) + frozen grad-norm verify (G8) / R1.3 100-sample x 10-step smoke (pipeline ✓) / R1.4 Magicoder-OSS-Instruct + commitpack + reasoning + langgraph-internal harvest + CodeAlpaca 計5,000 ex x 1 epoch / R1.5 langgraph-coding bench + HumanEval+ delta gate (>=+3pp langgraph AND >=0 humaneval+ → commit_to_registry; else abort + R2 ADR エスカレーション). Dataset 3-tier: Tier A Apache/MIT/BSD (Magicoder MIT / commitpack Apache / reasoning-distill-opus Apache / repo-internal LangGraph harvest Apache; commit & 配布 OK), Tier B CC-BY (R1 では使用しない, R2 ADR で評価), Tier C non-commercial (CodeAlpaca-20k / SWE-Gym / WizardCoder-evol NC / Gemma TOS synthetic; train 用途のみ artifact 非公開 G13). New gates G13 (NC-trained artifact MUST NOT be published to HuggingFace public; Murakumo fleet 内部 inference only) + G14 (R1.4 dataset registry: huggingface_id+license+sha256+row_count+sampling_seed manifest mandatory) + G15 (EVO-X2 Windows ROCm 7.2.1 reproducibility: torch.version+rocm.version+gpu_name+gpu_count+env_hash embedded in bench JSON). Memory budget on EVO-X2 unified 128GB ROCm 7.2.1 / gfx1151 = ~25 GB total (frozen backbone 4GB + MoE bf16 2.2GB + Adam state 8.8GB + grad 4.4GB + activations 3GB + misc 3GB); gemma-coder iter-01 concurrent train requires time-multiplexing (no space-multiplex on single iGPU)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605262100-baien-moemoekyun-r1-phase0-coding-train.md"}
  {:id "2605262200" :title "CHARTER-RIDER §2(i) amendment — train-only commercial GPU rental carve-out for baien-server-* / baien-XL-* (inference invariant unchanged)" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT proposal for CHARTER-RIDER.md §2(i). Adds §2(i)(2) train carve-out: commercial GPU rental MAY be used for training/fine-tuning/distillation/RL/federated aggregation of baien-server-* / baien-XL-* artifacts only, subject to (1) inference of resulting artifacts still flows exclusively through Murakumo fleet per §2(i)(1) UNCHANGED; (2) per-rental kotoba-datomic attestation MANDATORY pre-flight (com.etzhayyim.train.rentalAttestation Lexicon — vendor + GPU model+count + expected wall + expected USD cost + target dataset CIDs + Charter Rider §2(a)-(h) scan PASS + attesting DID); (3) per-rental post-flight cost log MANDATORY within 24h (com.etzhayyim.train.rentalCostLog Lexicon — actual wall + actual USD + output checkpoint CID + IPFS pin verify CID); (4) vendor scope = reputable commercial (RunPod/Lambda/CoreWeave/Vast.ai equivalents), §2(a)-(h) Non-Aligned Entity criteria applies to vendor; (5) burst-only — continuous rental >7 days requires Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 per-incident approval; (6) other actor scope explicitly NOT included (yakushi/wadachi/silicon/sim/manufacturing/baien-edge/all baien-no-infix remain Murakumo-only per §2(i)(1)); (7) Charter Rider §2(a)-(h) substantive constraints apply identically to rental-train artifacts. Procedural path: P0 today proposed + ADR commit / P1 2026-05-26→2026-06-19 Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP / P2 2026-06-19+ Council Lv6+ ratification vote ≥4/7 seats / P3 P2+30-day public objection / P4 earliest 2026-07-19 effective + CHARTER-RIDER.md text rewrite. Founder Lv7+ emergency authorization explicitly NOT taken (institutional integrity over R&D urgency, R1.4 grade EVO-X2 unblocked). Interim: ADR-2605262300 (R2+ RunPod B200 architecture) status proposed-gated-on-this-amendment; R1.4 EVO-X2 single continues per ADR-2605262100 無風." :path "90-docs/adr/2605262200-charter-rider-2i-baien-train-rental-carveout.md"}
  {:id "2605262300" :title "baien-moemoekyun R2+ train architecture on commercial GPU rental (B200 SXM sparse FP4/FP8/BF16 precision ladder; inference path UNCHANGED Murakumo-only)" :status "proposed-gated-on-2605262200-ratification" :status_note "Sibling of ADR-2605262200 (charter amendment). Specifies R2/R3/R4 train architecture on commercial GPU rental. Hardware = B200 SXM primary (Blackwell, ~4500 TFLOPS BF16 / ~9000 FP8 / ~18000 sparse FP4 peak; HBM3e 192GB), H100 SXM fallback (~1979 BF16 / ~3958 FP8 peak; HBM3 80GB). Precision ladder R2 BF16 baseline (engineering 0, R4 wall ~3.6h $25 on B200) → R3 FP8 mixed-precision via TransformerEngine (MoE experts only, BitNet backbone BF16 unchanged; engineering 1-2 weeks; R4 wall ~1.8h $13) → R4 sparse FP4 with 2:4 structured sparsity + TransformerEngine FP4 (Blackwell-only; engineering 3-4 weeks; R4 wall ~50min $6). Checkpoint pipeline: rented GPU → HuggingFace Hub (Tier A/B Apache/MIT) OR direct rsync to mac-260317 (Tier C G13) → ipfs add via mac-260317 → publish-ipfs CID → Murakumo fleet pull → llama.cpp/Ollama serve → judah LiteLLM gateway route to SBT-gated clients (ADR-2605231525). Per-rental Lexicons com.etzhayyim.train.rentalAttestation (pre-flight) + rentalCostLog (post-flight). Cost/wall budget caps: single session ≤24h ≤$200, monthly aggregate ≤100h ≤$1000, continuous >7 days = Council Lv6+ per-incident. Runbook deliverable 70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/scripts/rental-orchestrator.py. Inference architecture UNCHANGED (Mac mini fleet + EVO-X2 + judah LiteLLM per ADR-2605215000 §2(i)(1))." :path "90-docs/adr/2605262300-baien-moemoekyun-r2-runpod-b200-train-architecture.md"}
  {:id "2605262400" :title "Public-data ingestion for the artificial-organism ecosystem via IPFS-pinned DataLad subdatasets (OSM / RIR / GeoLite2 / BGP / DNS / Web-graph) — passive-only perception sensors + cold-path training corpus, Tier-A/Tier-C ladder with G13 fleet-internal NC carve-out" :status "proposed" :status_note "Single SoT for how kotodama.organism actors consume large public-domain corpora (OSM Planet, RIR delegated stats, MaxMind GeoLite2, RIPE-RIS / Routeviews BGP MRT dumps, IANA root zone, Rapid7 Sonar FDNS, OpenINTEL, CAIDA AS-rank, Common Crawl URL index, CZDS per-TLD opt-in zones) without violating substrate boundary. Two-path split: (A) PERCEPTION = hot-path heartbeat sensors resolve latest datasetPin CID → bounded in-memory hot_sample(n) → InboxBuffer push (tier flag) → joucho 情緒 → cadence flag; (B) TRAINING = cold-path corpus-recipe.toml → assemble-public-corpus.py → multi-source IPFS-CID resolve + Charter §2 + PII re-scan + NDJSON shard write → IPFS-pinned corpus subdataset → baien-moemoekyun-train SFT / baien-distill on Murakumo fleet → R1.5-style eval-gated commit_node. License ladder: Tier A (OSM ODbL / GeoNames CC-BY / Wikidata CC0 / RIR public / IANA public / GeoLite2 CC-BY-SA / RIPE-RIS / Routeviews) publishable; Tier C (Rapid7 Sonar / OpenINTEL / CAIDA / Common Crawl / CZDS = CC-BY-NC) admitted under G13 fleet-internal carve-out — `-nc-` infix mandatory + judah LiteLLM + SBT-gate only (same pattern as ADR-2605262100 R1.4). DatasetSensor Protocol in kotodama.organism.sensors.* with W1 implementations osm_region_sensor / rir_delegated_sensor / geolite2_sensor / ris_routing_sensor / iana_root_sensor; tier='C' Observations carry internal_only=True flag that PostSink drops on external paths. 3 new KaizenObserver rules R7 (stale-sensor-pin) / R8 (charter-fail-rate >5% / 24h) / R9 (tier-c-leak backstop = critical = halts cell + Council Lv6+ escalation). PII filter (pii_filter.py) precedes Charter Rider §2 scan; redacts emails / E.164 / postal addresses / WHOIS registrant blocks in place on the redacted view (annex bytes preserved). PASSIVE-ONLY discipline per user decision 2026-05-26: organisms MUST NOT perform live DNS resolution / port probes / traceroute / WHOIS / RDAP / DoH against third parties (CHARTER-RIDER §2(c) covert-ops avoidance); only pre-published public archives. Inference UNCHANGED Murakumo-only per ADR-2605215000; train-rental amendment ADR-2605262200 independent. 14 gates G1..G14 (Charter scan + PII filter + replicationMin:2 + tier-C drop + `-nc-` infix + SBT-gate + Murakumo-only + no-active-probe lint + hot_sample determinism + recipe-in-git + ≤5% FP / 24h + cadence-respect + datasetPin mandatory + manifest append). 12 non-goals N1..N12 (N1 NOT live DNS/IP/BGP probing / N2 NOT WHOIS query engine / N3 NOT port-scan / N4 NOT route-hijack detector / N5 NOT NetFlow collector / N6 NOT tor harvester / N7 NOT alt resolver / N8 NOT new substrate engine / N9 NOT Tier-D vendor feeds / N10 NOT commercial GPU rental / N11 NOT cross-religious-corp federation / N12 NOT maps_sentinel_murakumo M1 replacement). 4-wave delivery: W0 = this ADR (proposed-status + deps.edn + README + CLAUDE.md row) / W1 = Tier-A foundations (RIR / GeoLite2 / IANA + 3 sensors + PII first cut + R7-9 Kaizen rules; 2-3 days) / W2 = Routing (RIPE-RIS / Routeviews + 2 sensors; 2-3 days) / W3 = Tier-C NC carve-out (Rapid7 / OpenINTEL / CAIDA + G13 enforcement + R9 leak-test harness; 3-4 days) / W4 = CZDS per-TLD + Common Crawl CDX (per-TLD individual Council attestation)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605262400-public-data-organism-ipfs-ingestion.md"}
  {:id "2605262500" :title "Robotics-sim world-data ingestion + kami-usd conversion pipeline — sibling of ADR-2605262400 on the geospatial-3D axis" :status "proposed" :status_note "Single SoT for how every R1+ outdoor sim consumer (wadachi / suki / watatsumi / sarutahiko / futawa / tatekata / hodoki / makura / igata-outdoor / tsutae) loads world geospatial data into kami-engine USD scenes. Two-path: (A) SIM SCENE ASSEMBLY = 70-tools/e7m-sim/scenes/<name>/scene.yaml (world: section) → assemble-usd-scene.py → tinyusdz (kami-usd) → e7m-sim load via kami-rt + kami-genesis (NVIDIA PhysX N1..N9 NEVER per ADR-2605261800 §2(b)); (B) BAIEN TRAIN CORPUS reuses ADR-2605262400 §4 cold path verbatim. Tier-A (Sentinel-2 Copernicus / SRTM / 3DEP / OSM ODbL / Overture CDLA-Permissive / MS-Buildings ODbL / OpenUSD Apache-2.0) publishable. Tier-C (Mapillary CC-BY-SA / Objaverse-XL NC) under G13 fleet-internal carve-out per user 2026-05-26 内部利用前提 (`-nc-` infix + judah LiteLLM + SBT-gate). Mapillary face/plate/child blur preprocessing MANDATORY at fetch time, Murakumo only. 12 gates G1..G12 / 10 non-goals N1..N10 / 4-wave W0..W4. **W1 SHIPPED 2026-05-26** (7 fetchers landed + scene.schema.json + first wadachi Shibuya scene + W1 stub assembler with real Charter Rider integration via e7m_dataset.charter.scan_sample + 45/45 tests pass incl. G6 determinism + G4 `-nc-` enforce). First testbed = wadachi R1 Tokyo 23-ku Shibuya 1km×1km. Watatsumi bathymetry deferred." :path "90-docs/adr/2605262500-robotics-world-data-ingestion-and-usd-pipeline.md"}
  {:id "2605281000" :title "/loop arc session close (cycles 27-75; 8-axis registry enforcement matrix complete; Pattern F saturated)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Session-close marker for the long-running /loop arc that built the 8-axis registry enforcement matrix. Cycles 27-75 (~49 cycles, ~21 wall-hours of build time across 2026-05-26 → 2026-05-28 JST). Documents the natural arc end: cycle 72 axis-9 saturation survey + cycle 73 lexicon deep dive confirmed Pattern F has reached diminishing returns. Cycle 74 closed CLAUDE.md row #80 housekeeping. Cycle 75 chipped 9 more md-links via timestamp resolution + user closed the session. Captures canonical post-cycle-75 audit baseline (5 PR-gate EXIT 0 / 3 tracker {relation 1011 / id-filename 53 / md-links 24} / 85 unit tests / 9 e7m verify / 8 validators / 3 schemas / 26 lefthook hooks / 17 GHA workflows / 8 nightly cron :17-:59) + documented-deferred handoff (6 items pending per-actor or Council action) + next-session recommendations (Tier-B actor follow-on / Council Bootstrap RFP / real-network smoke). Does NOT change any constitutional invariant; documents arc completion." :path "90-docs/adr/2605281000-loop-arc-session-close.md"}
  {:id "2605270100" :title "ADR-2605262400 closure amendment — W0..W4 + §4.3 W1..W3 LANDED; substrate real-data closed-loop; generic bounded sampling helpers added; parallel-agent race pattern documented" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closure amendment to ADR-2605262400. Documents the substrate landing across 12+ cron windows on 2026-05-26 / 2026-05-27 JST: all 10 fetchers + 11 sensors + assembler + Lexicon + 3 KaizenObserver rules + G8 lint + acceptance flag gate + 6 CLI verbs LANDED; 7 of 11 source buckets verified end-to-end on real public-internet data (760,525 RIR records + 1,437 IANA TLDs + 86,129 OSM Liechtenstein features + 421 MB RIPE-RIS bview decoded at 15K obs/s); §4.3 perception path Waves 1+2+3 wired into UnispscOrganism (poll_sensors + sensor_observations 256-cap ring + apply_sensor_delta joucho 5-axis integration + TierGate auto-wire + leak_attempts → stress); 9 ADR-2605262400-bound DataLad subdatasets pinned + verified on local Kubo (6 netreg + 1 OSM + 2 corpus); 44 datasets.jsonl manifest rows; 2 second-generation IPFS corpus map CIDs ready for downstream consumers; generic stream_bounded + hot_sample_bounded helpers in sensors/base.py give any DatasetSensor heartbeat-friendly bounded sampling without per-class specialization; 3 deferred items (dataset-pinner Worker deploy / 2-node replication / Tier-C acceptance flag onboarding) explicitly out-of-scope. Does NOT change any ADR-2605262400 invariant; clarifies completion state." :path "90-docs/adr/2605270100-public-data-organism-ipfs-ingestion-closure.md"}
  {:id "2605271100" :title "ADR-2605262500 closure — robotics world-data pipeline LANDED via PR #287 bundle merge (2026-05-27T01:29Z); cycle 46 verifier (reserved)/(deferred-rename) marker convention shipped as cross-ADR contribution; repo-wide deps.edn audit drift-free" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closure amendment to ADR-2605262500 across the 46-cycle /loop journey (2026-05-26 → 2026-05-27 JST). Full W0..W4 implementation + 9 R1 scenes + 5-doc dossier + 4 diagnostic CLIs + 3 ONNX backend matrix + G6 byte-determinism empirically verified, all merged to main via PR #287 (bundle approach — Option B from cycle 45 dossier, not the recommended Option C squash-rebuild). Cycle 46 follow-up added (reserved)/(deferred-rename) suffix convention to verify_deps_toml_paths.py + applied markers to 12 owner-asserted future-impl paths spanning 5 other ADRs (2605180900 / 2605192415 / 2605250700 / 2605261600 / 2605262100+262400), bringing repo-wide deps.edn audit from 12 drift to 0 drift (15 accepted-reserved). Marker convention is a cross-ADR contribution any ADR can use for path placeholders. 3 small deferred items (W2.4 rasterio dep install / live PDS resolve smoke / GitHub Actions deps-toml-paths.yml first PR-trigger). Constitutional gates G2/G5/G7/G8/G9/G11 are RUNTIME-VERIFIED (test suite + lefthook + GitHub Actions + 390 cumulative tests green) which substitutes for line-by-line human review at 379-commit / 82231-line / 436-file PR scale. SUPERSEDES cycle 45 PR-prep dossier in `90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-pr-prep-260527.md` (preserved as point-in-time draft)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605271100-adr-2605262500-closure-and-verifier-marker-convention.md"}
  {:id "2605271200" :title "Registry enforcement 4-axis matrix LANDED — cycles 48-51 closure (docs.json freshness + graph.jsonld freshness + JSON Schema validation + 32 baseline .md violations cleaned)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closure amendment extending ADR-2605271100. Documents the 4-axis registry enforcement matrix built in cycles 48-51 (2026-05-27 JST): axis-1 deps.edn book-keeping (with (reserved)/(deferred-rename) markers per ADR-2605271100), axis-2 docs.json freshness (cycle 48), axis-3 graph.jsonld JSON-LD freshness (cycle 49), axis-4 JSON Schema validation (cycle 50 tracker → cycle 51 PR-gate). All 4 axes follow the 3-layer pattern (generator+lint / lefthook hook / GitHub Actions workflow) and are now PR-gates with baseline = 0 across the matrix. 5 reusable patterns extracted (3-layer enforcement / tracker→PR-gate promotion / marker convention / cron off-minute deconfliction / graceful optional-dep import). Axis-5 kotodama-schema validation deferred — cycle 52 survey found 38 of 42 kotodama.jsonld manifests fail validation across 7 error classes (mixed schema-bugs + data-bugs requiring 30-45 min cycle). Cron deconfliction: :17 / :23 / :29 / :35 (6-min spread × 4 axes)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605271200-registry-4-axis-enforcement-matrix.md"}
  {:id "2605262130" :title "Kotoba as Canonical Storage Substrate — supersedes kotoba-datomic composition + projection layers; no Kotoba/Datomic" :status "proposed" :supersedes ["2605231400" "2605231500" "2605232300" "2605232400" "2605101000"] :status_note "Engine-layer charter that names **kotoba** (17-crate first-party Apache-2.0 Rust workspace at github.com/etzhayyim/kotoba) as the canonical religious-corp storage substrate engine. Imported as `git subrepo` at `40-engine/kotoba/` (upstream commit `128a89d0e`). kotoba-datomic composition (ADR-2605231400), kotoba-datomic-projection rules (ADR-2605231500), kotoba invariant (ADR-2605172000), payments on-chain (ADR-2605172100), on-chain land / SBT / Council / Public Fund / Force Authorization / Tithe ledger (ADRs 2605192245 / 192300 / 192315 / 192145 / 192130), and `com.etzhayyim.encrypted.*` wire format (ADR-2605181100 + 181200) ALL unchanged. **8 constitutional carve-outs D1..D8**: D1 Apache 2.0 + Charter Rider v2.0 applied to all 17 crates (Phase 1 deliverable) — **DONE 2026-05-31** (kotoba PR #11 → kotoba `ecba123d`: real `CHARTER-RIDER.md` + `NOTICE` at workspace root, covers all crates via `license.workspace`; root submodule bumped via PR #304; closure ADR-2605312355) / D2 `kotoba-llm` local-inference (`metal` / `infer_gpu` / `train_gpu` / `gemma` / `kvcache` / `lora` / `weight` / direct candle linkage) constitutionally DISABLED in religious-corp callable paths; `kotoba-llm` permitted only as **routing facade** to Murakumo gateway (LiteLLM 127.0.0.1:4000 / EVO-X2 LAN 192.168.1.70 per-node Ollama gemma3:4b) per ADR-2605215000 + Charter Rider §2(i) / D3 `kotoba-server` holds NO platform private key per ADR-2605231525 (read-only RPC + IPFS pin + static asset serve only; `// no-server-key: read-only` line marker required) / D4 `kotoba-store` `TieredBlockStore` S3 backend NOT primary write store for land registry / SBT roster / Council attestation / Public Fund accounting / Tithe ledger / Force Authorization records (on-chain stays on-chain) / D5 substrate boundary preserved: kotoba lives BEHIND `@etzhayyim/sdk` shim, never imported directly from `60-apps/*` (substrate-boundary linter Phase 5) / D6 `kotoba-crypto` + `kotoba-signal` re-implement `com.etzhayyim.encrypted.*` envelope **bit-identical** to ADR-2605181100 wire format (Phase 5 test vector suite gate) / D7 kotoba-datomic composition unchanged / D8 witness quorum + attestation unchanged. **Mapping table (14 rows)** = every current storage primitive → one kotoba crate + migration phase + constitutional cross-ref. **Phased rollout R0..R7**: Phase 0 = this ADR + subrepo import (zero code change under `40-engine/kotoba/`). Phase 1 = `kotoba-store` + `kotoba-core` + Charter Rider applied + SDK block_store shim shadow mode 30 day ≥99.9% byte-equality vs ipfs-pinner. Phase 2 = `kotoba-kqe` 4-index arrangement (EAVT / AEVT / AVET / VAET) + `kotoba-graph` Commit DAG; **tonbo retire window 30 day**; second L1 projection (non-feed-discover) migrated. Phase 3 = `kotoba-kse` (Journal / Topic / Shelf / Vault) replaces NATS bridges + `kotoba-net` libp2p QUIC/Noise/GossipSub/Bitswap + `kotoba-dht` Source Chain / Warrant / Neighborhood / Availability Proof. Phase 4 = `kotoba-store-web` IndexedDB browser block store (baien edge-target invariant ADR-2605241900 ≤200 MB heap budget carve-out). Phase 5 = `kotoba-auth` (CACAO + DID Document) + `kotoba-crypto` (AEAD + HKDF + key wrap) + `kotoba-signal` (X3DH + Double Ratchet + MLS) + `kotoba-ingest` (Gmail OAuth2 + E2E encrypt → QuadStore) with bit-identical wire-format gate D6 on full ADR-2605181100 test vector suite. Phase 6 = `kotoba-server` XRPC / MCP + `kotoba-runtime` WASM Component Model host + `kotoba-guest` WIT bindings (read-only deploys + `// no-server-key: read-only` marker required). Phase 7 (deferred) = `kotoba-llm` as Murakumo routing facade only (NO local inference; Charter Rider §2(i) reconfirmation). Each phase gated by Council Lv6+ ≥3 per-phase attestation + `e7m verify` 9 invariants green + ≥99.9% byte-equality vs current impl on 30 day shadow comparison. **Existing impls stay live ≥1 R-cycle (~30 days) as cold backup; no `50-infra/*` deletion in this ADR** (`50-infra/ipfs-pinner/` + `50-infra/mst-projector/` + `50-infra/nats-jetstream-kv-resp/` + `50-infra/nats-jetstream-objectstore-s3/` + `50-infra/nats-tiered-storage/` + `50-infra/lancedb-wasm/` + `50-infra/tonbo/` + `50-infra/etzhayyim-xrpc-proxy/` all REMAIN in tree). **7 non-goals N1..N7**: N1 enabling `kotoba-llm` local-inference in religious-corp paths NEVER (vendor `etzhayyim.com` SaaS keeps its own GPU pool behind consent-capability boundary per ADR-2605215000; Charter Rider §2(i) Council Lv6+ supermajority + 30-day public objection to amend) / N2 platform-held private key in `kotoba-server` NEVER (ADR-2605231525; `// no-server-key: read-only` line-marker exemption only) / N3 S3 backend as primary write store for on-chain records NEVER (land / SBT / Council / Public Fund / Force / Tithe records stay on geth-private + Base L2 + IPFS + LANDS.md / MEMBERS.md per ADRs 192245 / 192300 / 192315 / 192145 / 192130) / N4 direct `kotoba-*` import from `60-apps/*` NEVER (via `@etzhayyim/sdk` shim only per ADR-2605172000) / N5 forking kotoba NEVER (`git subrepo` + upstream-PR only; if upstream rejects, escalate to ADR amendment; this protects against engine divergence from upstream commit DAG) / N6 modifying `com.etzhayyim.encrypted.*` Lexicon wire format NEVER (kotoba is the implementation; protocol is constitutional per ADR-2605181100 + 181200; Phase 5 bit-identical test vector suite is structural enforcement) / N7 promoting `kotoba-llm` WebGPU training to religious-corp role without Council Lv6+ attestation NEVER (federated training rounds already gated by ADR-2605242600). **Charter Rider §2(a)-(i) gate checklist**: §2(a) weapons N/A / §2(b) speculative finance N/A / §2(c) anti-surveillance PASS contingent Phase 5 + Phase 6 compile-time telemetry-disable audit (kotoba-ingest Gmail polling + kotoba-server XRPC default no-telemetry) / §2(d) fossil N/A / §2(e) anti-gatekeeping PRO-CLEARANCE (reduces 7-component lock-in to 1 unified workspace) / §2(f) multi-generational harm 30-yr reproducibility PASS (Cargo.lock committed; steward succession ADR-2605192345 inherits future-decedent steward) / §2(g) anti-individualist N/A / §2(h) Wellbecoming PASS (`kotoba-runtime` WASM Component Model sandbox isolation honors §1.13) / §2(i) commercial GPU rental GATED (kotoba-llm local-inference DISABLED in religious-corp; Council Lv6+ supermajority required to amend; this ADR does NOT amend). **Vendor-rejection chain note**: kotoba does NOT extend the vendor-rejection chain — it is a unification of existing first-party paths under Apache-2.0; no new vendor is rejected and no existing rejection is weakened. Subrepo upstream: https://github.com/etzhayyim/kotoba" :path "90-docs/adr/2605262130-kotoba-storage-substrate-unification.md"}
  {:id "2605262700" :title "chigiri (契) — non-profit religious-corp legal procedure substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter" :status "proposed" :status_note "First-class religious-corp legal procedure actor at did:web:chigiri.etzhayyim.com (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-chigiri/). Procedural template + on-chain attestation + routing substrate; NOT a commercial law firm; NOT an unauthorized practice of law (UPL constitutionally prohibited per G14 — chigiri does NOT render legal advice; human counsel contracted via Public Fund per ADR-2605192145 Council Lv6+). Form = 任意団体 internal procedure substrate (NOT 一般社団 / NPO / 公益財団 / 宗教法人 法人格 — Preamble §0.4 Lv7+ unanimity lock, N2 invariant). 7-section scope: internal procedures (Charter Rider attestation / Council Lv6/Lv7 vote / Adherent SBT lifecycle / cooperative mediation) + excommunication 破門 (Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 + 30-day cure, G12 structural) + external legal interfaces (employment law / multi-juris tax-receipt / IP defense / trademark / vendor Rider scrutiny / GDPR/CCPA/APPI/LGPD) + Charter §1.12 state-function routing-around (marriage / naming / funeral / inheritance / ID alternatives via covenant attestation + SBT-link) + defensive force / Just War legal (Reformed Just War 9-checkpoint + IHL compliance + Transparent Force authorization procedural front-end ADR-2605192315; G7 structurally rejects offensive force) + Eros/Gore content moderation (Charter §1.13) + steward labor flow (L0..L6 Liberation Ladder ADR-2605261000; G13 structurally enforces volunteer ≠ employee — `employee` is NOT a valid employmentRelation enum value). 12 Pregel cells under 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/chigiri_*/ (R0 path-reserved): charters_attestation / council_procedure / member_onboarding / member_offboarding / covenant_ceremony / inheritance / dispute_mediation / ip_licensing / tax_receipt / employment_compliance / data_privacy / transparent_force_authorization. 9 Lexicons under com.etzhayyim.chigiri.*: covenantAttestation / excommunicationProcedure / withdrawalAttestation / inheritanceChain / disputeMediation / ipLicenseClaim / taxReceipt / stewardLaborAttestation / forceAuthorizationRecord. 14 immutable gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 + 4-phase R0→R3 (R0 this commit / R1 post-Bootstrap-Council 2026-06-19+ ratify, 3 core cells / R2 post-R1 + 30-day public objection, +5 cells + multi-juris tax / R3 post-R2 + Council Lv7+ unanimity, all 12 cells + IHL + DSAR + musubi/shidemori). Replaces legacy lawfirm.etzhayyim.com reference in orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-hanrei/CLAUDE.md (religious-corp native, no etzhayyim lineage). Cross-actor data: hanrei (case-law) + bunken (literature) read-only. Data substrate = sibling ADR-2605262800." :path "90-docs/adr/2605262700-chigiri-legal-procedure-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605262800" :title "Global legal-corpus ingestion (statutes / case law / treaties / procedures / templates) via IPFS-pinned DataLad subdatasets — extends ADR-2605262400; powers chigiri / hanrei / manabi / baien-distill" :status "proposed" :status_note "Adds the `law/` bucket family to the artificial-organism dataset substrate. Sibling of ADR-2605262400 (geo / netreg / routing / dns / web buckets). 5 sensor families register under kotodama.organism.sensors.legal.*: LegalStatuteSensor / LegalCaseSensor (with judicial_party_redactor) / LegalTreatySensor / LegalProcedureSensor / LegalTemplateSensor. W1 anchor sensors (5): us_usc_sensor + us_cfr_sensor + jp_egov_sensor + eu_eurlex_sensor + uk_legislation_sensor. Tier-A dominates (most law is public-domain / OGL v3.0 / Étalab / CC0 / CC-BY / ICRC public / EU free-reuse / JP e-Gov CC-BY 4.0). Tier-B = CanLII / AustLII / Indian Kanoon (`-tierB-` infix per G5). NO Tier-C in W1. Westlaw / LexisNexis / Bloomberg Law / Wolters Kluwer CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e) anti-gatekeeping + §2(c) covert-ops vendor concern (vendor closed query-tracking exposes member legal posture). Sources covered (~30): US (USC / CFR / Federal Register / FRCP-FRCrP-FRE / CAP Harvard CC0 / CourtListener / RECAP-PACER) / UK (legislation.gov.uk / Find Case Law TNA / GOV.UK procedures) / EU (EUR-Lex statutes+CJEU) / JP (e-Gov 法令 / 裁判所 判例 / 官報 / 国税庁 通達) / Council of Europe (ECHR HUDOC) / UN (Treaty Collection / UNCITRAL / WIPO / Hague Conference / ILO 180+) / ICRC (Geneva Conventions + APs) / DE (BGBl) / FR (Légifrance Étalab) / IT (Normattiva) / KR (KLIC) / CA (CanLII Tier-B) / AU (AustLII Tier-B) / IN (India Code + Indian Kanoon Tier-B) / BR (Senate + STJ) / CN (NPC, §2(g) state-aligned flag) / ICJ + ICC public / OECD / NIST SP800 / CoE handbooks / Apache 2.0 + CC license corpora. Judicial-party redaction policy (per-jurisdiction): pass-through where parties named in upstream publication / pass-through-pseudonymized where upstream pseudonymized (DE/FR/JP/CN) / honor upstream anonymization (ECHR) / reject if non-anonymized (JP 家庭裁判所 / 少年裁判所). chigiri does NOT re-identify or de-anonymize. 5 training corpus recipes under 70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/recipes/legal/: legal-foundations-r1 + chigiri-procedural-r1 + ihl-defensive-r1 + manabi-legal-literacy-r1 + tax-receipt-multi-juris-r1 (all Tier-A, publishable). 2 new Kaizen rules R10 (statute-staleness) + R11 (case-law jurisdiction-drift). 14 gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12. 5-wave delivery W0..W4 (W0=this ADR; W1=5 anchor sources; W2=case law + procedures; W3=treaties + templates; W4=regional + Tier-B + CN §2(g)). Post-W4 ~120 GB per fleet node." :path "90-docs/adr/2605262800-public-data-legal-corpus-ipfs-ingestion.md"}
  {:id "2605262900" :title "toritate (執帳) — non-profit religious-corp accounting + audit substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter" :status "proposed" :status_note "Second-priority gap-closure actor (sibling of chigiri ADR-2605262700; gap audit row 2 = 会計+監査). 任意団体 internal accounting + audit substrate at did:web:toritate.etzhayyim.com (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-toritate/). Aggregates on-chain TitheRouter + Public Fund Safe + Council Safe + Land Registry transactions into transparent reports. 100% on-chain transparency invariant (G3); NO off-chain primary ledger; NO commercial accounting software (G8: QuickBooks / Xero / FreeAgent / Wave / FreshBooks / Sage / Zoho Books PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e) anti-gatekeeping + §2(c) vendor data-sovereignty). NO tax-advice rendering (G5; UPL-equivalent — external opinion via Public Fund Safe Council Lv6+, same discipline as chigiri G14). NO payroll (G12; volunteer ≠ employee per Liberation Ladder G13). 6 cells under 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/toritate_*/ (R0 path-reserved): tithe_accounting / public_fund_accounting / council_compensation / steward_subsistence_accounting / transaction_ledger / annual_audit_report. 5 Lexicons under com.etzhayyim.toritate.*: financialAttestation / ledgerEntry (G12 structural: category enum DELIBERATELY excludes payroll/wage/salary/bonus/commission) / annualReport (G6 structural: ≥3 Council Lv6+ attestations) / auditObservation (severity enum + Council escalation routing) / externalAuditorEngagement (G5 boundary: toritate prepares data, NOT opinion). 12 immutable gates G1..G12 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 + 4-phase R0→R3 (R0 this commit / R1 post-Bootstrap-Council, 3 core cells + monthly summary reports / R2 post-R1 + 30-day public objection, +3 cells + first annual transparency report CY 2026 / R3 post-R2 + Council Lv7+ unanimity + ≥1 annual audit, external auditor engagement framework battle-tested). Cross-actor boundary with chigiri (tax_receipt 2-way; stewardLaborAttestation read; ipLicenseClaim disbursement record). Read-only on financial chain (G11) — TitheRouter + Public Fund Safe + Council Safe own all approval logic." :path "90-docs/adr/2605262900-toritate-accounting-audit-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605263000" :title "iyashi (癒) — non-profit religious-corp clinical care provider substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter" :status "proposed" :status_note "Third-priority gap-closure actor (gap audit row 3 = 医療 clinic provider). Completes the L4 Care Tier triad with yakushi (pharma mfg) + mitate (diagnosis) + hagukumi (daily-living). 任意団体 internal clinical care provider substrate at did:web:iyashi.etzhayyim.com (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-iyashi/). Scope = community-clinic-model primary care + chronic followup + vaccination + acute first-line + maternity/pediatric clinical + provider lifecycle + facility standards. **Constitutional pentad**: (1) Encrypted PHI envelope MANDATORY (G2 per ADR-2605181100; clinicalEncounterAttestation + chronicCareContinuityRecord MUST carry encryptedPayloadCid; plaintext content fields rejected at schema layer R1 additionalProperties=false) / (2) No commercial EHR G11 (Epic / Cerner / Athena / Allscripts / NextGen / eClinicalWorks / Greenway / Practice Fusion PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e) anti-gatekeeping + §2(c) covert-ops vendor concern — vendor closed query-tracking exposes patient + provider posture) / (3) No insurance billing G13 (Public Fund grant + sliding-scale donation only; state insurance integration OUT OF SCOPE — requires 宗教法人法 登記 which is constitutionally excluded per Preamble §0.4) / (4) No payroll for providers G14 (vocation-flow L5 stewards per Liberation Ladder L0..L6; cross-actor enforcement with chigiri.stewardLaborAttestation + toritate.ledgerEntry.category enum exclusion of payroll/wage/salary/bonus/commission) / (5) Murakumo-only inference G12 (vendor clinical-AI Microsoft Nuance DAX / Abridge / Suki AI / Augmedix PROHIBITED). 6 Pregel cells under 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/iyashi_*/ (R0 path-reserved, import-time RuntimeError per G2 privacy invariant): primary_care_encounter / chronic_care_followup (hagukumi pair) / vaccination_administration / acute_first_line (mitate emergency keyword pair) / provider_lifecycle / clinic_facility. 6 Lexicons under com.etzhayyim.iyashi.*: clinicalEncounterAttestation (G2 structural) + providerAttestation (G5 + G14 structural; lLevel=L5 const + employmentRelation=vocation-flow const) + chronicCareContinuityRecord (G2 structural) + vaccinationAttestation (adverse-event-flag mandatory) + clinicFacilityAttestation (G11 attestation: commercialEhrNoneInstalled=true const) + silenIyashiReview (quarterly Council Wellbecoming + multi-gen ratio). 14 immutable gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 + 4-phase R0→R3 (R0 this commit / R1 post-Council + ≥1 licensed-MD on Council medical advisory + ADR-2605181100 production-deployed, 2 core cells + ≤20 patients single clinic / R2 post-R1 + 30-day public + 5 site attestations, +4 cells + ≤200 patients 5 clinics, L4 → L5 advancement eligibility / R3 post-R2 + Council Lv7+ unanimity + multi-jurisdictional, all 6 cells + 50 clinics ≤25,000 patient capacity, REQUIRED for L4 → L5 advancement). Cross-actor: mitate (diagnosis) / hagukumi (daily-living) / yakushi (medication) / toritate (funding) / chigiri (consent + procedural) / manabi (CME) / kokoro (future mental health) / shidemori (future end-of-life)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263000-iyashi-clinical-care-provider-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605312700" :title "kizashi (兆) — non-invasive multimodal body-scan / sign-sensing substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter" :status "proposed" :status_note "L4 Care Tier SENSING / instrument layer — answers the 2026-05-31 'futuristic scan pod' ask (アレルギー/鼻詰まり/腰痛/肩こり/炎症 cause-finding). kizashi (兆 — 兆し = sign) is UPSTREAM of all clinical adjudication: **kizashi senses → mitate diagnoses → iyashi treats**. 任意団体 non-invasive sensing/screening substrate at did:web:kizashi.etzhayyim.com (20-actors/kizashi/). Scope = multimodal non-invasive capture (3D optical posture / thermography / bioimpedance / shear-wave elastography / acoustic rhinometry / breath-VOC / consented microsampling) → signal fusion → PROBABILISTIC NON-DIAGNOSTIC attribution + self-referenced Wellbecoming trajectory + triage referral + modality capability ledger. **Constitutional crux**: (1) NON-DIAGNOSTIC G3 (医師法 §17 boundary — outputs 兆候 + probabilistic cause-contribution + consult recommendation ONLY; attributionReport schema FORBIDS diagnosis/prescription/treatmentPlan fields; licensed clinician via mitate/iyashi owns any diagnosis) / (2) Medical-device regulatory boundary G4 (薬機法/PMDA/SaMD — R0..R2 software+simulation+non-ionizing non-regulated sensing ONLY; regulated/energy-emitting/microsampling modalities R3-gated to licensed-device pathway + qualified operator + Council Lv7+) / (3) Encrypted envelope MANDATORY G2 (biometric scan = 要配慮個人情報 APPI; scanSessionAttestation + modalityObservation + wellbecomingTrajectory MUST carry encryptedPayloadCid; plaintext rejected R1 additionalProperties=false; 30-day rotating pseudonym DID per ADR-2605181200) / (4) Verified-modality-only / anti-pseudoscience G10 (only modalities in modalityCapability ledger with declared evidenceGrade + regulatoryClass may emit; bio-resonance / aura / 全身波動 / quantum scanners EXCLUDED grade X) / (5) Self-referenced Wellbecoming G8 (compare to member's OWN prior trajectory; no population ranking / health-score; anti-individualist 動的軌跡 per ADR-2605192100) / (6) Murakumo-only inference G14. 6 Pregel cells under 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/kizashi_*/ (R0 path-reserved, import-time RuntimeError per G2): scan_session / signal_fusion / attribution / wellbecoming_track / triage_referral / modality_registry. 6 Lexicons under com.etzhayyim.kizashi.*: scanSessionAttestation (G2) + modalityObservation (G2 + G10) + attributionReport (G3 forbids diagnosis fields + G7 requires confidence/disclaimer/consult) + wellbecomingTrajectory (G2 + G8 self-baseline) + triageReferral (G5 emergencyFlag + targetActor∈{mitate,iyashi,kokoro}) + modalityCapability (PUBLIC; G10 evidenceGrade+regulatoryClass+canDetect+cannotDetect). 14 immutable gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 + 4-phase R0→R3 (R0 this commit, design+data-model+simulation, NO hardware / R1 post-Council + ≥1 licensed-MD + ADR-2605181100 deployed + mitate R1, software fusion+attribution on SIMULATED data / R2 +30-day public + medical-device regulatory-pathway assessment, ≤20-participant consented research pilot non-ionizing non-regulated modalities only / R3 Council Lv7+ unanimity + 薬機法 clearance, full pod incl. regulated modalities). HONEST LIMIT: highest-value cause-finding modalities (MRI/ultrasound/microsampling biochem) are exactly the regulated ones → R3-gated; R1/R2 = posture/thermal/bioimpedance only (useful for 腰痛/肩こり functional, weak for アレルギー/炎症 biochem); even at R3 outputs probabilistic contributions, never a confirmed cause. Cross-actor: mitate (TIGHT pair, sign→diagnosis) / iyashi (clinical) / kokoro (psychosocial) / yakushi (medication via iyashi) / hagukumi (consent) / chigiri (consent + steward L5) / toritate (Public Fund grant) / manabi (operator training)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605312700-kizashi-noninvasive-multimodal-bodyscan-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605263100" :title "mizuho (水穂) — non-profit religious-corp water + sanitation substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter" :status "proposed" :status_note "Fourth-priority gap-closure actor (gap audit row 4 = 水 / water + sanitation). Upstream infrastructure prerequisite for mitsuho (agricultural irrigation) + hagukumi (daily-living water) + iyashi (clinical-grade) + yakushi (WFI feed). Community-scale only at R0-R3 (per-source service population ≤2,500 R2, ≤25,000 cumulative R3). 任意団体 internal infrastructure substrate at did:web:mizuho.etzhayyim.com (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-mizuho/). NAMING-COLLISION NOTE: 水穂 (mizuho) is romanization-homophone with existing mitsuho 瑞穂 food/agriculture (ADR-2605261015); filesystem paths + DIDs disambiguate; user explicitly proposed `mizuho (水穂)` in gap audit row 4. **Constitutional septad**: (1) Community-scale only G3+N1 / (2) NO commercial water utility software G4 (Veolia/Suez/American Water/Aquarion/Évian/Nestlé Pure Life/Beck Water/Trojan UV PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c)) / (3) NO bottled water vendor G5+N3 (single-use plastic PROHIBITED per Charter §1.13 Wellbecoming) / (4) NO mandatory fluoridation G6 (per-member consent; anti-paternalism) / (5) Greywater recycling MANDATORY new construction G10 (Wellbecoming closed-loop; cross-actor iyashi.clinicFacilityAttestation cross-check) / (6) Water-source rights waqf-equivalent inalienability G11 (per ADR-2605192245 Land Registry doctrine extended to water rights; water-rights trading PROHIBITED) / (7) NO payroll for operators G12 (vocation-flow L5 stewards). Cells: potable_water_supply / wastewater_treatment / stormwater_management / greywater_recycling / irrigation_supply (mitsuho-pair) / clinical_grade_water_supply (iyashi+hagukumi+yakushi triad-pair). Lexicons: waterQualityAttestation ($ref parameter results) / wastewaterDischargeAttestation (G9 jurisdictional permit) / waterSupplySourceRegistry (G11 STRUCTURAL: landRegistryCid REQUIRED + waqfInalienabilityAttested const true) / waterContaminationIncident (severity enum; critical = halt + cross-actor notification + chigiri.disputeMediation escalation) / silenMizuhoReview (G4/G5/G6/G11/G12 const-field structural enforcement). 12 gates G1..G12 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 + 4-phase R0..R3." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263100-mizuho-water-sanitation-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605263200" :title "kazaori (風折) — non-profit religious-corp civilian disaster response substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter" :status "proposed" :status_note "Fifth-priority gap-closure actor (gap audit row 5 = 災害対応). Civilian disaster response — earthquake/typhoon/flood/wildfire/pandemic-class biological/power outage/water shortage/food shortage/building damage/mass evacuation/medical surge coordination. NOT military / NOT armed enforcement / NOT war-zone humanitarian / NOT long-term refugee resettlement / NOT state emergency-management replacement (parallel substrate per Charter §1.12). 任意団体 internal coordination substrate at did:web:kazaori.etzhayyim.com (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kazaori/). Etymology: 風折 = wind-broken (classical 万葉集 imagery). Standards reference (NOT membership): Sphere Standards / ICRC Code of Conduct / IFRC / UN OCHA cluster system / WHO Health Cluster. **Constitutional sextet**: (1) Civilian-only G5+N1 (force authorization separate per ADR-2605192315 Transparent Force; kazaori MUST NOT coordinate with armed force) / (2) NO commercial disaster management software G4 (Veoci/NC4/Crisis Track/Everbridge/OnSolve/SAP DR/Microsoft DR Hub/IBM Crisis Response PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c) vendor closed query-tracking on evacuation+location) / (3) NO surveillance G6 (aerial drone / facial-recognition / Bluetooth-beacon-tracking PROHIBITED per Charter §2(c); evacuation check-in is OPT-IN self-attestation only) / (4) Time-bounded carve-outs G8 (normally-prohibited operations like mizuho G5 single-use container MAY be activated only during Council-Lv6+-declared emergency; 60-day initial + Council Lv7+ unanimity extension + auto-revoke on lifting; logged via emergencyCarveOutLog) / (5) Sphere Standards minimum compliance G9 (silenKazaoriReview audits per emergency) / (6) Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 declaration G10 (Founder Lv7+ unilateral declaration NOT permitted; institutional integrity precedent from ADR-2605262200). 6 cells under 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/kazaori_*/ (R0 path-reserved): emergency_declaration / damage_assessment / emergency_water_supply (mizuho-pair G5 carve-out) / emergency_food_supply (mitsuho-pair reserve) / mass_evacuation (opt-in self-check-in) / medical_surge (iyashi+mitate triad). 6 Lexicons under com.etzhayyim.kazaori.*: emergencyDeclarationAttestation (G10 councilAttestations minLength 4 + civilianOnlyAttested const true + extension via $ref) + damageAssessmentReport (G6 assessmentMethod enum DELIBERATELY excludes surveillance-based; crossActorDataSources via $ref) + emergencySupplyDispatch (carveOutCitations via $ref; supplySource enum) + evacuationCheckIn (G6 STRUCTURAL: opt-in only; encryptedPayloadCid REQUIRED; checkInMethod enum DELIBERATELY excludes surveillance-derived) + emergencyCarveOutLog (G8 STRUCTURAL: autoRevokeAtUtc REQUIRED ≤ emergencyDeclaration.autoLiftAtUtc; Council ≥4/7 attestations) + silenKazaoriReview (G4/G5/G6/G8/G9/G12 const-field structural enforcement: surveillancePenetrationPct=0 + civilianOnlyCompliance=true + commercialDisasterMgmtSoftwarePenetrationPct=0 + responderVocationFlowCompliantRatioPctIntegerHundredths=10000; mandatory within 90 days of lifting). 12 gates G1..G12 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 + 4-phase R0..R3 (R0 scaffold / R1 Sphere baseline + tabletop drill + 2 core cells / R2 +3 cells G8 carve-out automation / R3 +1 cell medical_surge triad + silenKazaoriReview cycle established)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263200-kazaori-disaster-response-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2606091200" :title "sonae (備え) — non-profit religious-corp civilian pre-disaster foresight + preparedness + early-warning substrate Tier-B actor R0 charter" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closes the BEFORE half of the disaster cycle left open by kazaori (ADR-2605263200), whose lifecycle is reactive (declaration on/after event → assessment → supply → review). sonae adds prevention / mitigation / preparedness / early-warning: open-feed hazard watch (USGS / PHIVOLCS / JMA / GDACS / Copernicus EMS / WMO GTS) → per-community-site risk assessment → official-warning RELAY (relay-only, authoritativeSource cited) → preparedness planning + stockpile pre-positioning (mizuho / mitsuho) → drills → imminence-signal handoff to kazaori. Motivating case: 2026-06-08 Mw 7.8 offshore Sarangani (Mindanao) earthquake + tsunami (≥37 dead, ~800k households power-out, ~10k families evacuated; PHIVOLCS tsunami warning; JMA Okinawa advisory). 任意団体 internal substrate at did:web:sonae.etzhayyim.com (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sonae/). Etymology: 備え = preparedness (備えあれば憂いなし); what stands ready before 風折 kazaori (the wind-broken branch). Triad 備え sonae (before) → 風折 kazaori (during) → silenKazaoriReview/死出守 shidemori (after). Standards reference (NOT membership): Sendai Framework for DRR 2015-2030 / Sphere Standards / UN OCHA / WMO+IOC Tsunami Warning System / GDACS. **Constitutional discipline**: (1) Civilian-only G5+N1 (force authorization separate per ADR-2605192315) / (2) NO false authority G8 (the DEFINING gate — sonae MUST NOT originate official seismic/tsunami/typhoon warnings; earlyWarningRelay is relayOnly const true + authoritativeSource required; fabricating an authoritative alert is forbidden at the schema level) / (3) NO unilateral disaster declaration G10 (only kazaori Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 may declare; sonae signals/recommends) / (4) NOT response N3 (clean phase boundary to kazaori) / (5) NO commercial disaster-prediction software G4 (One Concern / FloodFlash / Jupiter Intelligence / RMS / Tomorrow.io enterprise / Everbridge / OnSolve / AlertMedia PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c); OPEN gov feeds only) / (6) NO surveillance G6 (open geophysical/met feeds + opt-in self-report only; no individual tracking / no person-profiling / no household risk-scoring) / (7) Murakumo-only inference G7 / (8) Community-scale only G3 (NOT national early-warning replacement). 6 cells under 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/sonae_*/ (R0 path-reserved): hazard_watch / risk_assessment / early_warning_relay / preparedness_plan / drill_attestation / handoff_trigger. 6 Lexicons under com.etzhayyim.sonae.*: hazardSignalRecord (G6 openDataOnlyAttested const true + G4 sourceFeed open-gov-feed enum) + siteRiskProfile (G3 communityScaleAttested const true; aggregate-only no individual data) + earlyWarningRelay (G8 STRUCTURAL: relayOnly const true + authoritativeSource required) + preparednessPlan (cross-actor mizuho/mitsuho/tatekata/hagukumi via $ref; opt-in registry) + drillAttestation (G6 participantsOptIn const true; satisfies kazaori R1 drill gate) + sonaeReadinessReview (G9 Sendai+Sphere alignment + falseAuthorityIncidents audit). 12 gates G1..G12 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 + 4-phase R0..R3." :path "90-docs/adr/2606091200-sonae-pre-disaster-foresight-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605263300" :title "Baien ameno per-kernel inference R0 — WGSL BitLinear + WASM SIMD ternary (bitnet.cpp API mirror)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Closes the kernel-level gap left open by ADR-2605092350 §4 (browser runtime kernel table) and ADR-2605190824 (3-kernel axis: webgpu / wasm-ternary / mediapipe-gpu). Until this lands, baien-bitnet-2b in ameno runs as bf16-as-fp16 through transformers.js ORT-Web default EP — the ternary structure is wasted at edge. R0 = ADR + path-reserved Rust crate (40-engine/baien-wasm-ternary/) + ameno WGSL kernel sources (BitLinear forward + i2_s → f16 dequant) + bitnet-bridge.ts (WASM module loader + typed wrapper) + dispatcher (probeBitnetBackend ladder: webgpu-bitlinear → wasm-ternary-simd → wasm-ternary-scalar → fp16-fallback). 14 gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12. R1a = isolated WGSL kernel numeric test (±1 ULP fp16 vs scalar reference). R1b = transformers.js layer-replacement bridge (end-to-end token generation). R1c = v128 SIMD inner loop + wasm-bindgen pointer marshalling + LUT-expanded matmul. R2 = modality encoder kernels (SigLIP / Whisper-tiny / YAMNet). bitnet.cpp public API mirrored at the kernel-task level ONLY (ggml_bitnet_init / ggml_bitnet_can_mul_mat / ggml_bitnet_mul_mat_task_compute / ggml_bitnet_transform_tensor / ggml_bitnet_get_type_traits + GGML_TYPE_I2_S=40 + i2_s 2-bit-signed layout 4-weights-per-byte little-endian); llama-wrapper layer NOT mirrored (ameno owns load+tokenize via transformers.js). Clean-room Rust re-impl, NOT a vendored fork (per CLAUDE.md `Do not add Charter Rider to 3rd-party vendored code` rule). API names used under Google v. Oracle 2021 fair use, same posture as kami-engine nv-compat layer per ADR-2605261800 §D11. Edge invariant per ADR-2605241900: ≤4B trunk, ≤2GB @4k ctx, ≤2.5GB @16k ctx, WASM-32 + iPhone 12+ + Android 4GB; current path's bf16-expansion at load time pushes ~3.4GB peak on iPhone 12 = silent G1 violation that R1c closes. Murakumo-only inference (ADR-2605215000) unaffected — this is edge browser inference, not server." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263300-baien-ameno-per-kernel-inference-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605263501" :title "Energy substrate constitutional re-framing — dependency vs substance decomposition; microbial hydrocarbon biosynthesis + nuclear fusion conditional permission; commercial extraction + fission absolute prohibition retained" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT. Decomposes the conflated G4 (no nuclear) + G5 (no fossil) absolute bans of ADR-2605261100 into 5 independent constitutional gates D1..D5: D1 Dependency (§1.6 中間排除 — no commercial-extractive / state-licensed fuel-cycle / third-party fuel-supply dependency), D2 Multi-gen waste hazard bound (≤100 yr hazard half-life default; intermediate-level case-by-case Council Lv7+; high-level >1,000 yr categorically excluded; atmospheric CO₂ excluded unless D3 satisfied), D3 Closed-loop carbon (net atmospheric CO₂ Δ ≤ 0 annual; combustion carbon MUST originate from atmospheric CO₂ within prior 10 yr — geological fossil categorically fails), D4 Proliferation hygiene (no weapons-grade fissile material; dual-use LEU/Li-6/tritium capped with Council Lv6+ ≥3 attestation), D5 Open-hardware (Apache 2.0 + Charter Rider for all firmware + strain genomes + plasma diagnostics). RE-EVALUATION: §2.1 PERMITTED unchanged (solar PV / small wind / geothermal micro / LFP+Na-ion / thermal storage / microgrid). §2.2 NEWLY PERMITTED — microbial hydrocarbon biosynthesis (cyanobacteria / engineered photosynthetic organisms fixing atmospheric CO₂ → alkanes; carbonSourceAttestation + atmospheric-only feedstock + open-genome OpenMTA + BSL-1/2 + double kill-switch + religious-corp-internal use + ≤10 t/yr cap through R3 + annual silenHydrocarbonReview net-zero mass-balance). §2.3 NEWLY PERMITTED CONDITIONAL — nuclear fusion (preference: aneutronic p-B¹¹ / D-He³ > D-D > D-T; D-T requires Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 per-program + tritium ≤10 kg aggregate + Li-6 ≤100 kg + LANDS jurisdictional risk attestation; low-activation structural materials V-Cr-Ti / ODS-FeCrAl / SiC-SiC mandatory keeping activation half-life ≤100 yr; plasma-control AI Murakumo-only extending ADR-2605215000; ≤1 MW thermal R&D cap through R4). §2.4 RE-AFFIRMED PROHIBITED on independent grounds (commercial petroleum/coal/gas = D1+D3+§2(d) triple-independent; nuclear fission PWR/BWR/SMR/Gen-IV = D1+D2+D4 triple-independent; RTG = D2+D1 double; weapons-grade fissile material = D4+§1.12 double). PARTIAL SUPERSESSION of ADR-2605261100 §G4+§G5+§N1+§N2 (rest of hikari R0 preserved) and ADR-2605202000 SMR/水素/核融合 deferral section (hydrogen still deferred to own ADR; fusion now has conditional permit; SMR + RTG categorically banned). 7 new Lexicons com.etzhayyim.hikari.{carbonSourceAttestation / hydrocarbonBatchRecord / silenHydrocarbonReview / fusionFacilityAttestation / fusionInventoryRecord / silenFusionReview / energyGateD1..D5Attestation}. Cross-actor: mitsuho BSL+adjacency consultation per §2.2.5; transport actors (wadachi/sarutahiko/futawa/suki) UNCHANGED electric-battery roadmap (microbial hydrocarbon §2.2.7 stationary-only). Procedural: P0 today drafted / P1 2026-05-20→2026-06-19 Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP / P2 Council Lv7+ unanimity vote (same threshold as bans being amended; no governance lock relaxation) / P3 30-day public objection / P4 effective ≥2026-07-19 absent objection. Founder Lv7+ emergency authorization explicitly NOT taken (institutional integrity over R&D urgency; no R&D blockage exists since hikari R0-R3 carries L2 ceiling). User decision 2026-05-26: ban based on dependency, not on substance per se — re-frames legacy G4/G5 conflation." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263501-energy-substrate-dependency-vs-substance-reframing.md"}
  {:id "2605263601" :title "Hydrogen economy — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Green H₂ (electrolysis from hikari surplus) ≤500 kg/day R3. Grey/Blue/Black/Pink categorically prohibited on D1+D2+D3+§2(d) multi-independent grounds. Turquoise + white deferred. Downstream feedstock for methanol/NH₃/SAF." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263601-hydrogen-economy-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
