  {:id "2605264200" :title "Mechanical energy storage (pumped-hydro-micro/CAES/flywheel/gravity-block) — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Pumped-hydro-micro ≤500 kW (mizuho waqf water-rights) + flywheel ≤100 kW + gravity-block ≤500 kW + CAES-surface ≤100 kW R&D. CAES-underground ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED (D1 geological + D2 multi-gen leak)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605264200-mechanical-energy-storage-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605264500" :title "Geothermal deep + EGS — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Medium-depth (500-3000 m, ≤2 MW/well) + EGS R&D (Council Lv7+ unanimity per hydraulic stimulation + ≥M3.0 induced-seismicity tripwire = site abandonment) conditional. Ultra-deep + supercritical DEFERRED. NORM screening MANDATORY." :path "90-docs/adr/2605264500-geothermal-deep-egs-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605264600" :title "Direct air capture (DAC) — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Solid-amine ≤1 t/day + L-DAC ≤500 kg/day + mineralization ≤10 t/day conditional. Geological CCS (D1+D2 multi-gen) + voluntary carbon-credit-market sale (Charter §2(b) financialization + hikari N8) ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED. Closed-loop synfuel feedstock." :path "90-docs/adr/2605264600-direct-air-capture-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605264700" :title "Methanol + DME synfuel — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "MeOH via Cu/ZnO/Al₂O₃ from green H₂ + DAC CO₂ ≤500 kg/day + DME ≤200 kg/day R3. Fossil-syngas + biomethane-syngas PROHIBITED. Stoichiometry chain-of-custody MANDATORY. Cross-actor wadachi/sarutahiko/suki R3+ ICE backup." :path "90-docs/adr/2605264700-methanol-dme-synfuel-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605264800" :title "Algal biofuel — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Photoautotrophic microalgae ≤10 t-DW/yr + FAME via methanol + HVO drop-in diesel/jet via green H₂. Heterotrophic sugar-fed algae PROHIBITED through R3 (N4) unless religious-corp non-food cellulosic (2605265300). Cross-actor mitsuho protein co-product fish-feed substitute." :path "90-docs/adr/2605264800-algal-biofuel-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605264900" :title "V2G + demand-response coordination — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "V2G ≤25 kW/vehicle + ≤500 kW aggregate R3 into religious-corp microgrid only. DR coordination aggregate-only ≥1-hour buckets (NO per-appliance/individual telemetry per hikari N7). Commercial-grid V2G + commercial-DR programs ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED." :path "90-docs/adr/2605264900-v2g-demand-response-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265000" :title "District heating + cooling networks — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "4GDH/5GDH/5DHC ≤2 MW/network + ≤5 networks R3. Commercial district-energy-utility (Veolia/E.ON/Vattenfall/Fortum/Engie) ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED. Per-consumer metering aggregate ≥1-hour buckets only (N7). Cost-recovery billing only." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265000-district-heating-cooling-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265100" :title "Fusion fuel sourcing (D/T/Li-6/He-3/B-11) — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "D (seawater) + B-11 (terrestrial mining) ✓. T constrained (Li-6 enrichment Council Lv7+ unanimity per program). He-3 EFFECTIVELY UNAVAILABLE (no D1-compliant source; D-He³ deferred indefinitely). Commercial CANDU T + US DoE Savannah River He-3 PROHIBITED. Confirms p-B¹¹ as only fully self-sourceable fusion fuel." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265100-fusion-fuel-sourcing-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265300" :title "Cellulosic ethanol (non-food agricultural waste) — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Cellulosic ethanol from mitsuho residue + hodoki/tatekata cellulosic + future bamboo ≤200 t/yr R3. ≤30% crop-residue extraction. Open-publication enzymes only (Trichoderma reesei + Aspergillus niger fungal; Codexis/Novozymes/DuPont/DSM proprietary PROHIBITED). Closes 2605265200 §4 + 2605264800 §4 deferrals." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265300-cellulosic-ethanol-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265400" :title "e-Fuels Fischer-Tropsch full product slate — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "FT non-jet product slate (diesel + naphtha + wax + lubricant) ≤500 kg/yr R3. Cross-actor circular: diesel → wadachi/sarutahiko backup; naphtha → algal-extraction; wax → mitsuho orchard; lubricant → kuni-umi/tatekata/igata. ASF α-tuning Council-mediated quarterly. Completes synfuel matrix." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265400-e-fuels-fischer-tropsch-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265500" :title "Concentrated PV (CPV) with III-V multijunction — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Si-CPV (≤100× concentration leveraging hikari R0 Si baseline) ≤200 kW/facility R3 conditional. III-V multijunction PROHIBITED through R3 (MOCVD epitaxy = 3 vendors globally; D1+D5 fail). DNI ≥1800 kWh/m²/yr site qualification. Heat-recovery cogeneration cross-actor with ADR-2605265000 district network." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265500-concentrated-pv-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265600" :title "Salinity-gradient PRO/RED open-design membrane — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "PRO + RED with open-publication or religious-corp-developed membranes ≤50 kW/site ≤1 site R3. Toray/Hydranautics/GE/Statkraft proprietary ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED. PFAS chemistries (Nafion-class) PROHIBITED per Charter §2(c). Power-density ≥1 W/m² gate. Closes 2605264100 §4 membrane-IP gap." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265600-salinity-gradient-pro-red-open-membrane-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265700" :title "Sodium-sulfur (NaS) molten-salt battery — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "NaS molten-salt (300-350°C, open-formula β″-Al₂O₃ ceramic electrolyte) ≤500 kWh/facility ≤2.5 MWh aggregate R3. NGK Insulators commercial NAS modules ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED (effective monopoly + closed IP). Mandatory thermal-runaway containment + Class D fire-suppression + ≥4500-cycle attestation. Niche-fit 6-24 hr discharge multi-day-bridging." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265700-sodium-sulfur-battery-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265800" :title "High-temperature heat pump (HTHP, ≤200°C delivery) — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Natural-refrigerant HTHP (CO₂ R-744 ≤90°C / NH₃ R-717 ≤110°C via 2605263700 / steam R-718 MVR ≤200°C) ≤500 kW/facility ≤2.5 MW aggregate R3 conditional permit; 3-5× efficiency multiplier vs direct electric resistive for industrial process heat. HFC refrigerants (R-134a / R-32 / R-410A / R-22) ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED on D3 GWP grounds. HFO refrigerants (1234yf / 1233zd, GWP <10) DEFERRED R4+ pending TFA atmospheric stability. Heat-source pairing matrix: DAC regen / CPV cooling / biomethane CHP / geothermal flash. Cross-actor heat-network 2605265000 integration. Steam-MVR variant decarbonizes industrial process steam ≤200°C." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265800-high-temperature-heat-pump-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605265900" :title "Synthetic natural gas (SNG / Sabatier methanation) — D1..D5 evaluation R0" :status "proposed-pending-council-ratification" :status_note "Sabatier (CO₂ + 4H₂ → CH₄ + 2H₂O over Ni/γ-Al₂O₃ public-domain since 1902) from green H₂ (2605263600) + DAC CO₂ (2605264600) — COMBINED biomethane+SNG aggregate cap ≤200 Nm³/day R3 (no scale creep beyond existing CH₄ ceiling). SNG from commercial CO₂ (industrial flue / NH₃ byproduct) ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED (D1+D3+§2(d)). Pathway selection Council Lv6+ ≥3 quarterly: biomethane primary (waste streams) / Sabatier when exhausted OR dispatchable OR surplus H₂+DAC. Exothermic ΔH = -165 kJ/mol ~10 MJ/kg-CH₄ heat byproduct closes DAC↔Sabatier outer loop + feeds district network 2605265000 + biomethane digester thermophilic + HTHP 2605265800. Water byproduct ~2.25 kg-H₂O/kg-CH₄ → mizuho process water OR electrolyzer feedstock (closes green-H₂ water loop). Ni catalyst open-formula MANDATORY — Johnson Matthey HiFUEL R110 PROHIBITED." :path "90-docs/adr/2605265900-sng-methanation-sabatier-d-gate-evaluation-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605263401" :title "Baien ameno WGSL BitLinear numeric test R1a — isolated wgpu dispatch + ±1 ULP fp16 vs scalar reference" :status "proposed" :status_note "R1a of the R-roadmap pinned by ADR-2605263300 §10. Validates the WGSL BitLinear shader against the Rust scalar reference matmul without touching transformers.js. Choice of harness: wgpu Rust integration test (NOT node --experimental-webgpu / Playwright). Choice of WGSL source-of-truth: relocated shader strings from TS literal to standalone .wgsl files at 40-engine/baien-wasm-ternary/shaders/{bitlinear_forward,bitnet_packed_dequant}.wgsl. TS imports via Vite ?raw (src/types/wgsl-raw.d.ts ambient declaration). Rust test reads via include_str!. Single source of truth — no shader drift. Naga f16 limitation workaround: production shader uses `enable f16;` which Naga doesn't yet parse (gfx-rs/wgpu#4384); test runs algorithm-identical f32 fixture at tests/fixtures/bitlinear_forward_f32.wgsl and converts f32 → f16 host-side. Verifies i2_s unpack + q8 unpack + i32 inner accumulation + block-scaled accumulation + row-scale × block-scale layout. Does NOT verify f16 shader-side rounding (deferred to R1b browser tests). 4 tests pass on M1 Metal: T1 alternating ±1 (≈0), T2 all-+1 × ramp (≈496), T3 multi-row multi-col 2-block, T4 BitNet-2B shape proxy M=2 K=128 N=8. ±1 ULP fp16 tolerance via to_bits diff. Graceful skip on no GPU adapter. R1a-G1 new gate: .wgsl files are ONLY source of shader text (inline duplication = revert offence). Cargo dev-deps: wgpu=24 (default features, backend auto-select) + pollster=0.4 + bytemuck=1 derive + futures-intrusive=0.5." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263401-baien-ameno-wgsl-bitlinear-numeric-test-r1a.md"}
  {:id "2605263701" :title "Baien ameno ONNX graph layer-replacement R1b — transformers.js MatMul → BitLinear interceptor + end-to-end token gen" :status "proposed-scoping-only" :status_note "R1b of the R-roadmap pinned by ADR-2605263300 §10. First R-step that produces user-observable behaviour change — closes the silent ADR-2605241900 §G1 violation that has been open since baien-bitnet-2b landed in ameno on 2026-05-09 (current load-time bf16 expansion pushes ~3.4 GB peak on iPhone 12, exceeding the ≤2 GB @ 4 k ctx ceiling). 5 harness candidates evaluated: (A) offline ONNX rewrite + forked HF model — rejected ops burden / (B) in-browser ONNX rewrite — CHOSEN for encode/prefill / (C) ORT-Web custom op WASM EP only — rejected loses webgpu-bitlinear / (D) full transformers.js forward override — CHOSEN for decode-step (where throughput win lives) / (E) patch ORT-Web itself — rejected non-public API. R1b = (B)+(D) hybrid. R1b deliverables across 8-commit chain over multiple cycles ~1500-2000 LoC: (1) onnx-proto-min.ts ~400 LoC protobuf encoder/decoder for ModelProto/GraphProto/NodeProto/TensorProto; (2) bitnet-graph-patcher.ts replaces matching *.{q,k,v,o,gate,up,down}_proj.weight MatMul nodes ONLY (NOT attention QK^T runtime matmuls); (3) bitnet-custom-op.ts registers etzhayyim.ai::BitLinear via ORT-Web env.experimental.customOps; (4) BitNetForwardOverride decode bypass; (5) inference.ts useBitLinearBridge flag-gating on MODELS[baien-bitnet-2b]; (6) microbench against 15-prompt verifiable set (4 backends × 3 device classes = 12 cells); (7) iPhone 12 + Pixel 6 real-device run-log emits; (8) G1 close attestation. Failure ladder: dispatch throws → fall back to WGSL_BITNET_PACKED_DEQUANT fp16 dense dequant + telemetry → second failure = catastrophic abort. 4 new gates R1b-G1..G4 (replaced-count expectation / shape validation / telemetry on fallback / microbench manifest device-class + adapter + commit SHA). Inherited G1 (closes via microbench) / G4 (every backend vs scalar reference) / G9 (upgraded — fallback OK but MUST emit telemetry) / G14 (NO LONGER APPLIES — R1b is behaviour-change step, flag-gated per model). Out of scope: R1c v128 SIMD / R2 encoder kernels / R3 WebNN NPU / R4 q8 KV-cache / real-device matrix bench (R1b ships harness only) / baien-server-XL (edge-only)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263701-baien-ameno-onnx-graph-layer-replacement-r1b.md"}
  {:id "2605264000" :title "ossekai (御節介) — non-profit religious-corp information-arbitrage elimination + Wellbecoming-nudge artificial-organism actor R0 charter (AT Protocol social-post + feed + @mention first-touch)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Sixth-priority gap-closure actor (gap audit row 6 = 情報非対称 / information arbitrage). Artificial-organism Tier-B actor at did:web:ossekai.etzhayyim.com (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-ossekai/) whose dual mandate is (a) AGGREGATE PUBLICATION of societal information asymmetries (public-good intel surface) and (b) OSSEKAI-MODE NUDGE — caring proactive notification to opted-in Adherent SBT members (encrypted private digest per ADR-2605181100) + Council-gated single-touch @mention to non-member companies/individuals on AT Protocol — all delivered via AT Protocol native primitives (NO email / SMTP / commercial CRM at R0-R2). First-touch channel = AT Proto `app.bsky.feed.post` (existing membrane per ADR-2605231902 preserved unchanged) + custom feed generator `feed.ossekai.wellbecoming` + `@mention` to AT Proto handles. Etymology: 御節介 = caring proactive intervention (cultural knife-edge between compassionate-helpfulness and unwelcome-meddling; constitutional discipline structurally pins on caring side). **Constitutional novelty G4 aggregate-first** — anonymized public-feed channel is the DEFAULT mode; targeted dispatch is the SECONDARY mode; silenOssekaiReview.anonAggregateSharePctIntegerHundredths minimum 5000 (≥50.00%) STRUCTURAL schema constraint; the default order MUST NOT be inverted at runtime. Inverts the industry-default (HubSpot / Mailchimp / Salesforce individual-first model) — structural enforcement of Charter §2(c) covert-ops avoidance + Charter §1.4 anti-individualism in information-delivery domain. **AT Proto first-touch resolves seven distinct constitutional tensions** that arise with email-based outreach: (1) vendor CRM data-sovereignty → N/A AT Proto open-spec; (2) signed sender DKIM/SPF/DMARC brittleness → built-in DID-bound + cryptographic signature; (3) 1-click unsubscribe friction RFC 8058 → built-in via app.bsky.graph.block + mute; (4) spam-classifier evasion risk → mooted (Bluesky clients render mute/block transparently); (5) per-jurisdiction email law (GDPR Article 7 / CCPA / CAN-SPAM / APPI 第18条 / LGPD) → largely resolved (AT Proto activity is voluntary publication); (6) dark patterns (urgency / shame / engagement-hacking) → discoverable (every post public + replayable + auditable); (7) auditability of unsent drafts → cleaner (G15 rejection BEFORE composition; no 'unsent draft' record). **Constitutional discipline 15-gate**: G1 Charter Rider §2(a)-(h) scan on every input AND output / G2 kotoba-datomic attestation lineage / G3 PASSIVE-ONLY collection (no live DNS/probe/traceroute/WHOIS/RDAP/DoH/handle-enumeration; pre-published archives + voluntary AT Proto activity only per ADR-2605262400) / G4 aggregate-first publication (≥50% aggregate-public-feed by volume quarterly) / G5 NO commercial intel/CRM/marketing software (Salesforce/HubSpot/Marketo/Mailchimp/SendGrid commercial/Constant Contact/Pardot/ZoomInfo/Apollo/Clay/Lemlist/Outreach/SalesLoft/Gong/Chorus/6sense/Cognism/LeadIQ/Drift PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e) anti-gatekeeping + §2(c) vendor data-sovereignty) / G6 NO dark patterns (AT Proto native mute/block/quote-block honored at projection layer G15) / G7 rate limit hard-coded (non-member ≤1/90d/handle; member ≤1 digest/week + ≤1 ad-hoc/month default) / G8 encrypted envelope MANDATORY for member digest per ADR-2605181100 / G9 signed sender DID transparent (did:web:ossekai.etzhayyim.com + cryptographic signature) / G10 Wellbecoming-positive framing only (Charter §1.13; framing-audit attestation in every advisory) / G11 anti-individualism (Charter §1.4; community + multi-gen context preferred) / G12 Murakumo-only inference per ADR-2605215000 / G13 Council Lv6+ ≥3 attestation for non-member @mention campaign (≥4 if campaignSize>50) / G14 silenOssekaiReview quarterly audit / G15 AT Proto native mute/block honored at projection layer (mention_dispatcher rejects dispatch BEFORE composing post; the post never enters MST). **8 cells** under 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/ossekai_*/ (R0 path-reserved, import-time RuntimeError; issachar Murakumo node): arbitrage_observer (continuous heartbeat; sensor consume) + intel_analyzer (joucho-cadence; framing audit) + aggregate_publisher (hourly; AT Proto feed-post DEFAULT) + member_digest (weekly; encrypted envelope) + mention_dispatcher (event; Council attestation gated) + consent_registry (continuous; AT Proto block/mute ingest) + kaizen_observer (quarterly; KaizenObserverCell pattern per ADR-2605240200) + emergency_advisory (event; kazaori cross-actor). **9 Lexicons** under com.etzhayyim.ossekai.*: arbitrageGapReport (G3 STRUCTURAL passive-only attested + G1 Charter Rider scan pass const true) + wellbecomingAdvisory (G10 framingAuditPass const true + G11 audienceShareDistribution required + crossActorCitation for UPL/medical/financial/pharma/diagnostic/emergency boundary) + feedPostAttestation (G9 senderDidConst const did:web:ossekai.etzhayyim.com + G15 muteBlockCheckPass const true) + memberDigestSubscription (per-category granularity; cadence default weekly) + memberDigestRecord (G8 STRUCTURAL encryptedPayloadCid REQUIRED) + mentionDispatchAttestation (G13 STRUCTURAL attestingCouncilDids minLength 3; ≥4 enforced at consumer if campaignSize>50; G7 rateLimitWindowAttested const true) + externalMentionConsent (G6 per-category granularity + ≤365-day expiry default + revocable any time) + unsubscribeRecord (G15 STRUCTURAL effectiveImmediatelyAttested const true; ingests AT Proto app.bsky.graph.block + app.bsky.graph.mute) + silenOssekaiReview (G4 anonAggregateSharePctIntegerHundredths minimum 5000 + G5 commercialIntelCrmSoftwarePenetrationPct const 0 + G10 framingAuditWellbecomingPreservationCompliant const true + G14 councilAttestations minLength 3 + G15 reEngagementAfterOptOutCount const 0 — critical: any nonzero count triggers chigiri.disputeMediation + immediate cell halt). **12 non-goals N1..N12**: N1 NOT email-based outreach at R0-R2 (AT Proto first-touch only; email-bridge to AT Proto DM for opted-in members is R3+ Council Lv7+ unanimity; non-member email contact permanently prohibited at this charter level) + N2 NOT surveillance/OSINT-for-hire/private-detective service + N3 NOT marketing automation/growth-hacking/viral-loop engineering + N4 NOT corporate intelligence-for-hire/competitive intel/industrial espionage + N5 NOT social pressure/public shaming/vigilante coordination + N6 NOT lobbying/political campaign mailing + N7 NOT commercial outreach/upsell/affiliate + N8 NOT credit-score/financial-blacklist/debt-collection + N9 NOT match-making/dating + N10 NOT recruitment/headhunting/employment-targeting + N11 NOT children-targeted (manabi G3 anti-dependency parallel) + N12 NOT chigiri/legal-threat proxy/Transparent-Force proxy/excommunication-procedure proxy. **4-phase R0..R3**: R0 this commit / R1 post-Council ratify + e7m-dataset Tier-A foundations + legal-foundations-r1 recipe + chigiri R1 active (UPL boundary) + iyashi R1 active (medical boundary) + custom feed generator feed.ossekai.wellbecoming live; ≤100 advisories/week / R2 +30-day public objection + first silenOssekaiReview + ≥1 cross-actor advisory cycle; +member_digest ≤500 opt-in members + mention_dispatcher Council Lv6+ ≥3 gate live ≤50 non-member handles/quarter + consent_registry AT Proto block/mute ingest live / R3 Council Lv7+ unanimity + multi-juris consent compliance (JP 個人情報保護法 第27条 + GDPR Article 7 + APPI 第18条 + CCPA opt-out + Brazil LGPD + CAN-SPAM honest-sender all attested by chigiri R3+) + ≥4 consecutive silenOssekaiReview G14-compliant cycles; +kaizen_observer 6 new rules R12..R17 + emergency_advisory kazaori cross-actor; ≤5000 opt-in members + ≤200 non-member handles/quarter cumulative." :path "90-docs/adr/2605264000-ossekai-information-arbitrage-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605263800" :title "Global corporate-disclosure ingestion (SEC EDGAR / EDINET / Companies House / GLEIF LEI / OpenCorporates / regional registries) via IPFS-pinned DataLad subdatasets — extends ADR-2605262400; powers ossekai / toritate / chigiri / baien-distill financial-literacy specialist" :status "w1-impl-landed" :status_note "═══ W1 IMPL LANDED 2026-05-27 ═══ corp 4-fetcher concrete (gleif_lei + sec_edgar + uk_companies_house + jp_edinet) + 4-sensor concrete (GleifLeiSensor + SecEdgarSensor + UkCompaniesHouseSensor + JpEdinetSensor) + end-to-end fetcher→sensor integration verified per fetcher (4/4 corp pipelines green). Cross-cutting: 5 Lexicons (registryAttestation/disclosureAttestation/leiReference/ownershipEdge/filingEvent) + 2 corpus recipes (foundations-r1 + ownership-graph-tierB-r1) + acceptance template (opencorporates-opendata for W3 Tier-B) + cross-actor wiring (ossekai.crossActor + chigiri.lexiconReadAccess + toritate.lexiconReadAccess via DID-array linter-safe `lexiconReadAccess` object field) + 4 legacy script supersession markers (sec-edgar-disclosure-ingest.mjs + gleif-bulk-ingest.mjs + legal-entity-relationship-ingest.mjs + multi-country-scheduled-ingest.mjs + MIGRATION-NOTES.md) + RELEASE NOTES snapshot at 90-docs/baien/corp-gov-w1-snapshot-260527.md. Tier-A dominates (US public-domain / GLEIF CC0 / UK OGL v3.0 / JP 金融庁 open); Tier-B for OpenCorporates open-data fork CC-BY-SA `-tierB-` infix; Tier-C EMPTY (Bloomberg Terminal / S&P CapIQ / Refinitiv / FactSet / Moody's Orbis / D&B / Pitchbook / Crunchbase Pro CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c) — triple-layered enforcement: ADR §2 + recipe vendor_terminal_denylist + pytest cross-cutting import-line scan). All sensors passive-only per ADR-2605262400 §7; all fetchers operator-triggered boundary. 12 gates G1..G12 + 12 non-goals N1..N12. 4-wave delivery W0..W4 (W0+W1 LANDED; W2 = SEDAR+/ASIC/Unternehmensregister/INFOGREFFE per-jurisdiction registry fetchers + filing-event sensors + OpenCorporates W3 Tier-B). Supersedes ADR-2604291500 + ADR-2605150000. R1 activation gated on Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP closure 2026-06-19 + Council Lv6+ ≥3 ratify." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263800-public-data-corporate-disclosure-ipfs-ingestion.md"}
  {:id "2605263900" :title "Global open-government-data ingestion (open-data portals / parliament / budget / procurement / statistics) via IPFS-pinned DataLad subdatasets — sibling of ADR-2605262400 + ADR-2605262800 + ADR-2605263800; powers ossekai / toritate / chigiri / manabi civic-literacy curriculum / baien-distill civic-reasoning specialist" :status "w1-impl-landed" :status_note "═══ W1 IMPL LANDED 2026-05-27 ═══ gov 8-fetcher concrete (worldbank_open_data + eu_eurostat + us_data_gov + uk_data_gov_uk + jp_data_go_jp + us_congress_gov + uk_hansard + jp_kokkai_kaigiroku — covers gov 5-facet COMPLETE: Statistics + OpenData triad + Parliament triad) + 10-sensor concrete (WorldBank + Eurostat + 3 CKAN portals + 3 Parliament + USAspending Budget + EU TED Procurement) + end-to-end fetcher→sensor integration verified per fetcher (8/8 gov pipelines green). Cross-cutting: 5 Lexicons (openDatasetAttestation/parliamentRecord/budgetRecord/procurementRecord/statisticsObservation; sub-namespace gov.dataset.* avoiding collision with existing gov.{agency,consult,municipality,official,procedure}) + 2 corpus recipes (civic-literacy-foundations-r1 + statistics-foundations-r1) + cross-actor wiring (ossekai.crossActor + chigiri.lexiconReadAccess + toritate.lexiconReadAccess) + RELEASE NOTES snapshot 90-docs/baien/corp-gov-w1-snapshot-260527.md. Pytest harness 15/15 PASS via importlib bypass runner (sensor-only; fetcher integration tested per-fetcher inline at smoke-test phase). Tier-A dominates 20+ sources; CN data carries state_aligned_flag=True per §2(g) parallel to ADR-2605262800 (downstream consumers MUST display flag); Tier-C EMPTY (GovWin IQ / Bloomberg Government / Politico Pro / E&E News Pro / FiscalNote / CQ Roll Call Pro CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c) — triple-layered enforcement). All sensors passive-only per ADR-2605262400 §7. 12 gates G1..G12 + 12 non-goals N1..N12. 4-wave delivery W0..W4 (W0+W1 LANDED; W2 = EU OEIL/DE Bundestag/FR Assemblée Parliament expansion + OECD.Stat/IMF SDMX/UN data Statistics expansion + EU FTS Budget + US SAM.gov/UK Contracts Finder/JP 政府調達 Procurement; W4 = CN data with §2(g) flag enforcement). R1 activation gated on Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP closure 2026-06-19 + Council Lv6+ ≥3 ratify." :path "90-docs/adr/2605263900-public-data-open-government-ipfs-ingestion.md"}
  {:id "2605264300" :title "kami-engine-sdk three.js-free cutover (spark / webvr / VRM type / dead-deps)" :status "active" :path "90-docs/adr/2605264300-kami-engine-sdk-three-free-cutover.md" :status_note "Consolidates the 3-commit SDK-wide three.js retirement (`b04c54eb5` + `ea0fd3ab8` + `5d2ba4b2d`) into one canonical record. Extends ADR-0031's VRM-only cutover to the **full SDK surface**: deletes `src/lib/spark/` (sparkjs.dev demos) + `src/lib/webvr/{webvr-scene,node-effects}.ts` (three-vrm renderer); removes `ThreeVrmHandle` interface + `DualEngineState.three` + 2-arg `updateEngines(kami, three)` + `(state.three as any)?.vrm` dead reads; strips `declare module 'three'` from `ambient.d.ts`; drops `three` + `@pixiv/three-vrm` peerDeps + `./spark` export. Canonical 3DGS = `kami-pipelines::GsplatAdapter` (Rust+wgpu). Canonical VRM = `KamiWasmExports.runEmbedVrm`. Headless `createIncidentVrEngine` (renderer-pluggable via `onScene`). Vendor carve-out: cyber-drill vendorizes three at `$lib/three-renderer/` per ADR-2605172400. Downstream cleanup landed: baminiku ykb48d7a (`5d2ba4b2d`) + image2vrm + image2metahuman (`0384841bd` iter-12). sos + global remain deferred (no design intent documented). §1 Notes documents a parallel-session race that produced a misleading commit-message; this ADR is the canonical reference for the actual content of `b04c54eb5`."}
  {:id "2605265201" :title "kami-engine-sdk 20-actors legacy duplicate retirement (3-phase, all phases complete)" :status "active" :path "90-docs/adr/2605265201-kami-engine-sdk-20-actors-legacy-duplicate-retirement.md" :status_note "Eliminated the dangerous structural condition of two `package.json` files declaring `name: \"@etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk\"` (canonical 40-engine subrepo + stale 20-actors duplicate). 3-phase deprecation completed same-day: Phase 1 (`491ff8ee6` iter-9) DEPRECATED.md + canonical workspace registration. Phase 2 (`243470dc8` iter-10) verification log — `pnpm install --lockfile-only` resolves canonical only, 20-actors NOT in lockfile. Phase 3 (`2d199cca9` iter-11) `git rm -r 20-actors/kami-engine-sdk/` — 80 files / +5 / -12,216 lines / e7m verify 9/9 ✓ / SDK build ✓ / SDK vitest 82 ✓. 4 alternatives considered + rejected (delete-immediately for race risk / symlink for subrepo circularity / re-export shim for same-name persistence / reverse direction for engine-family fit). Retirement was monorepo-internal — 20-actors copy was never published to npm."}
  {:id "2605270735" :title "Audit substrate — design + perf + operator workflow" :status "accepted" :path "90-docs/adr/2605270735-audit-substrate-design-and-perf.md" :status_note "Session-close ADR consolidating iters 30-70 of /loop (2026-05-26 → 2026-05-27, 41 iterations). Captures the audit substrate at `70-tools/scripts/audit/` as institutional memory: 6 aggregator scripts in `all.sh` + 3 standalone scripts on operator-demand. Cumulative perf wins: `e7m verify` 121s → 0.7s (170x cumulative, iters 5-7 git ls-files + iter-56 ThreadPoolExecutor); `audit aggregator` 47.5s → 1.1s (43x cumulative, iter-57 git ls-files + xargs -P10 parallel gh + iter-61 rglob → git ls-files). Both perf wins regression-guarded by 7 pytest suites / 92 tests (test_adr_cross_ref_health 21 + test_manifest_lexicon_drift 13 + test_subrepo_scripts 16 + test_simple_audits 17 + test_e7m_verify_perf 7 + test_gitmodules 5 + test_all_sh 13). CI integration via .github/workflows/audit-health.yml with 8 path-trigger patterns covering both audit infrastructure AND the files audits check (iter-54 closed the canary-CI-dead gap). Drift closures: sibling-convention-drift 14→0 iter-39 (Apache-2.0 default per ADR-2605192200) + manifest-lexicon-drift 21→0 iter-52 across 5 actors (wadachi/gov-municipality/infra-utility-connect/yoro-supply/kuni-umi); iter-58 added yobel 4 lexicons for total 25 lexicons across 6 actors. Operator UX: 5 invocation modes via `all.sh` (default / --strict / --test / --test <file> / --all). Documented-deferred: 7 stale subrepos (ADR-2605211845) + 18 kotoba escape-symlinks (ADR-2605262130) + 113 ADR cross-ref orphans + 3,198 lexicon-spec violations. Bonus side-fixes: iter-43 substrate-boundary allowedPrefixes for 30-graph migration dirs + iter-65 .gitmodules ignore=dirty for baien/datasets DataLad subdataset (eliminated recurring 'Too many levels of symbolic links' warning that fired ~100+ times during iters 30-64). Documentation-only ADR (status: accepted); no policy or behavior change."}
  {:id "2605263800-baien-ameno-r1b-pivot" :title "Baien ameno R1b pivot — ORT-Web custom op dead end; switch to forward-override + weight-pack extraction" :status "accepted-14-of-15-commits-landed-pending-real-weight-microbench" :status_note "AMENDS ADR-2605263700 §1/§3 (the (B)+(D) hybrid harness was predicated on ORT-Web exposing JS-side env.experimental.customOps registration; bundled @huggingface/transformers@3.8.1 ORT-Web has ZERO references — confirmed dead end). Strategy pivots to (D)-only full forward override: bypass ORT-Web entirely for BitNet trunk; consume HF tokenizer JSON + HF generation_config + BitLinearWeightPack + new pure-TS attention/RoPE/KV-cache + transformers.js sampler. **Commits 4-14 of 15 landed** across cycles 3-16 (~3,100 LoC + 154/154 passing node:test): onnx-proto-min (#1, R1b commit 1) / bitnet-graph-patcher (#2; deprecated post-pivot but matchTrunkProjection predicate retained) / bitnet-weight-transformer (#3) / bitnet-weight-pack (#4; the pivot connective) / bitnet-config (#5) / bitnet-rope (#6) / bitnet-kv-cache (#7; + per-layer accessors at #10) / bitnet-rmsnorm + bitnet-silu (#8) / bitnet-math (#9) / bitnet-bitlinear-dispatch fp32-fallback (#10) / bitnet-attention with GQA + RoPE + KV cache (#11) / bitnet-ffn with SwiGLU (#12) / bitnet-transformer pre-norm block + 2 residuals (#13) / bitnet-runtime end-to-end decode loop (#14). **Remaining commit 15**: real-weight load from HF `microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-bf16-ONNX` (embedTokens + 30 layers' BitLinear packs + RMSNorm scales + lm_head pack via extractBitLinearWeightPack + parallel-walk of remaining initializers) + microbench against the 15-prompt verifiable set from ADR-2605092350 emitting NDJSON manifest to 90-docs/baien/wgpu-bitlinear-microbench-260X.jsonl + iPhone-12 G1 close attestation. **What this unlocks**: end-to-end pure-TS BitNet decode (tokenizer + sampler still via transformers.js facade). fp32-fallback dispatch path is correct but slow; R1c (v128 SIMD inner loop + LUT