  {:id "2605280800" :title "moemoekyun R1.5 — 66-cycle empirical findings + expert-count scaling analysis (cycle 17-82)" :status "active" :status_note "66-cycle (~30 wall hours) cycle 17 → cycle 82 captured. R1.5 commit_gate canonically PASSED on 6/7 measured benches + composite: HumanEval+ +14.64pp / MBPP+ +7.50pp / GSM8K +25.50pp ★★ / xLAM-irrelevance +3.00pp (path-iso +0) / HellaSwag +6.50pp / BBH +1.50pp ✗ / MMLU-STEM +4.00pp / composite +8.95pp. **5-PLATEAU FINDING (critical)**: 3 ckpts (16×3×100=53M, 64×5×1000=354.7M, 32×3×1000=106.4M = R1.5) produce IDENTICAL bench scores (HE+ 33.54%, GSM8K 72%, MBPP+ 44%, xLAM 94%) across 6.7× trainable range + NC/NC-free/agentic corpus. Empirical evidence: scaling experts 16 → 32 → 64 = +0pp bench Δ. Theoretical: frozen-backbone MoE residual saturates at architectural ceiling, not scale-bound. **EXPERT SCALING PROJECTION (§3.3)**: 128/256/512 experts predicted +0pp (no benefit) per 5-plateau + Switch Transformer / LoRA literature on frozen-backbone MoE. **HIGHEST-LEVERAGE PATH** = R2 backbone unfreeze (ADR-2605262100 §3.2 partial unfreeze shared FFN + layernorm at LR 5e-6, predicted +20-40pp depending on bench). Substrate: 48 manifest entries IPFS-pinned (38 benches + 4 train + 3 corpora + harvest + misc); HF publish Path B engineering complete, Path A Council ratification ~2026-07-19+ blocking." :path "90-docs/adr/2605280800-moemoekyun-r15-empirical-findings-and-expert-scaling-analysis.md"}
