  {:id "2605282000" :title "kotoba_murakumo — Modal-compatible Python facade for Murakumo Mac mini fleet GPU inference (R0 scaffold)" :status "proposed" :status_note "R0 scaffold: Modal-compat surface + 3-backend routing policy (judah :4000 LiteLLM gateway / EVO-X2 :4000+:11434+:8188 / per-node own-node Ollama gemma3:4b). Pure stdlib (httpx optional R1). 16/16 pytest pass against the canonical 50-infra/murakumo/fleet.toml. Strengthens ADR-2605215000 Murakumo-only invariant by making the path of least resistance route to fleet rather than to RunPod-equivalent vendors. Modal-compat shim at kotoba_murakumo.modal_compat (`import kotoba_murakumo.modal_compat as modal`) maps gpu='A100'/'H100' to EvoX2 with honest warning per N5; Image.from_registry / web_endpoint / Sandbox raise MurakumoCompatNotImplemented with constitutional reason. R0 .remote() returns NotImplementedError carrying the resolved route (no surprises); R1 wires live LiteLLM/Ollama dispatch + Charter Rider §2 scan flip from advisory to enforce + invocation NDJSON → com.etzhayyim.murakumo.invocation Lexicon. R2 wires WASM Component dispatch via kotoba-vm. Depends on ADR-2605215000 (Murakumo-only) + ADR-2605262130 (kotoba substrate) + ADR-2605192200 (Charter Rider) + ADR-2605202345 (EVO-X2) + ADR-2605231525 (no platform keys) + ADR-2605232100 (k3s fleet) + ADR-2605262200 §2(i)(2) (train carve-out leaves inference unchanged)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605282000-kotoba-murakumo-modal-compat-python-fleet-inference.md"}
  {:id "2605282100" :title "kotoba mKOTO economy + Modal billing-parity for the Murakumo fleet (R1.3 6-layer charter)" :status "proposed" :status_note "6-layer mKOTO economy charter (L1 meter / L2 tariff / L3 wallet / L4 cash-routing / L5 Modal-parity Python surface / L6 on-chain settlement). Closes the developer-ergonomics gap between Modal's per-second-of-GPU billing UX and the religious-corp non-commercial-pricing constraint (Charter §1.5 + §2(b) speculative-finance prohibition). External callers see donation-acknowledged → mKOTO-credit-posted (NOT subscription); SBT-internal callers use internal-purchase/internal-subscription per ADR-2605192115 §3 carve-out. Pre-dispatch BudgetExceeded + InsufficientCredit raise BEFORE HTTP so callers can surface donation prompts without burning compute. Initial tariff (Council Lv6+ ≥3 ratification pending R2): litellm-gateway 100 mKOTO/gpu_sec + 10 mKOTO/MB; evo-x2 250+10; mac-mini own-node 30+5; webgpu-wasm 1 mKOTO/1k gas. R1.3a (this ADR) + R1.3b (Python scaffold) + R1.3c (3 Lexicons) + R1.3d-scaffold (Rust handler signatures #[cfg(any())] gated) ALL landed in this commit. R1.3d-wiring (kotoba-server route registration), R1.3e (TitheRouter MkotoCreditPosted event + donation indexer cell), and R2.0 (ADR-2605260004 on-chain settlement bridge) are separate ADRs. Depends on ADR-2605282000 (consumer facade) + ADR-2605215000 (Murakumo-only) + ADR-2605262200 (train carve-out inference unchanged) + ADR-2605172100 (payment categories) + ADR-2605192115 (anti-subscription) + ADR-2605192130 (tithe auto-split) + ADR-2605192145 (Public Fund) + ADR-2605192200 (Charter Rider §2(b)) + ADR-2605231525 (no platform keys)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605282100-kotoba-mkoto-economy-and-modal-billing-parity.md"}
  {:id "2605282200" :title "kawase-yui (為替結) — kotoba multi-stable adherent remittance mutual-aid substrate (TransferWise-equivalent under religious-corp constraints, R0 charter)" :status "proposed" :status_note "TransferWise-equivalent multi-stable remittance for religious-corp adherents — re-frames Wise's pre-funded local-pool topology + peer balance netting + mid-market FX + transparent fee under Charter §1.5 anti-commercialization + §2(b) speculative finance prohibition + ADR-2605282100 N2 mKOTO non-transferability. Settlement uses existing Base L2 stablecoins (USDC + EURC at R1; +JPYC R2; +KRWO/GBPe/CHFe R3) — NO new token minted per ADR-2605172100 Alt C + ADR-2605282100 N2. Pool-match Pregel cell compute cost billed in mKOTO via ADR-2605282100 economy. Solidarity skim = 0% at R0-R3 (pure adherent personal mutual aid, ADR-2605192130 §5 Kisha/grant-pattern exemption). Adherent SBT↔SBT only (G3 structural in Solidity onlyAdherent modifier on both deposit + claim). Mid-market Chainlink oracle ±0.5% band (G4; Constitution.sol const kawase.max_band_bps = 50) — no spread profit (G5 const 0). 14 immutable gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 + 8 Lexicons under com.etzhayyim.kawase.* (depositAttestation / withdrawIntent / matchExecution / fxRateAttestation / poolStateReport / rebalanceAttestation / jurisdictionAttestation / silenKawaseReview) + 5 Pregel cells (pool_match / fx_oracle_watcher / rebalance_proposer / jurisdiction_compliance / silen_review) + Solidity KawaseYuiPool.sol (R1 scaffold under 50-infra/etzhayyim-kawase-pool/). Per-jurisdiction Council Lv7+ unanimity activation gate (G14) avoids unlicensed money-services-business exposure. 4-phase R0→R3: R0 this commit + 8 Lexicons + deps.edn entries + paths reserved (no code) / R1 USDC↔EURC pair Council Lv6+ ≥3 ratify ≤50 adherents ≤$50k pool / R2 +JPYC LayerZero-bridged Council Lv6+ ≥3 bridge audit 30-day public objection ≤500 adherents ≤$500k / R3 +KRWO+GBPe+CHFe per-pair Council Lv7+ unanimity ≤5000 adherents ≤$5M + wakai R3 cross-actor integration. Cross-actor: wakai (mutual aid sibling) + chigiri (multi-juris + UPL) + toritate (accounting) + TitheRouter (skim path if Council later activates >0% at R4+) + Public Fund Safe (R1 reserve buffer seed grant) + kotoba (substrate engine) + Murakumo (cell inference) + mKOTO economy (compute cost layer). Depends on ADR-2605282100 (mKOTO economy) + ADR-2605262130 (kotoba substrate) + ADR-2605263500 (wakai sibling) + ADR-2605262700 (chigiri) + ADR-2605262900 (toritate) + ADR-2605192130 (tithe §5 exemption) + ADR-2605192145 (Public Fund) + ADR-2605192200 (Charter Rider §2(b)) + ADR-2605172100 (payments substrate + Alt C no custom token) + ADR-2605192115 (§3 SBT carve-out) + ADR-2605215000 (Murakumo-only) + ADR-2605181100 (encrypted memo envelope) + ADR-2605231525 (no platform keys) + ADR-2605192300 (Bootstrap Council Lv6+/Lv7+ gates)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605282200-kawase-yui-multi-stable-adherent-remittance-mutual-aid.md"}
  {:id "2605282300" :title "kotoba_murakumo relocated out of the kotoba subrepo to 40-engine/kotoba_murakumo/ (downstream-consumer placement)" :status "superseded" :superseded_by "2606074000" :status_note "SUPERSEDED by ADR-2606074000 (2026-06-07): kotoba is now a git submodule, not a git-subrepo, so the merge-base force-push hazard that forced this relocation no longer exists; kotoba_murakumo was re-integrated into the submodule at 40-engine/kotoba/py/kotoba_murakumo/. Original closure ADR for the structural mistake surfaced by the first git subrepo push attempt on 2026-05-28 evening (id originally 2605282200 collided with kawase-yui ADR; renumbered to 2605282300). Root cause: kotoba_murakumo was placed inside the kotoba subrepo working tree but is a religious-corp downstream consumer, NOT part of kotoba's canonical external surface. When upstream github.com/etzhayyim/kotoba had force-pushed away the merge-base commit (17e30d9db5...) recorded in .gitrepo, all three git-subrepo sync paths (pull, branch, pull --force) failed or were destructive. The honest fix is structural relocation, not a git-workflow patch. This ADR documents the relocation + the durable stay-in-vs-move-out rule: a Python sibling stays inside a subrepo iff (1) it IS canonical upstream-shipped content (e.g. kotoba_langgraph compiles to WASM Components for kotoba-runtime), (2) it imports only documented external interfaces, (3) the upstream release tag includes it. Moves OUT iff (1) it consumes the subrepo via HTTP/wire format but isn't part of its external surface, (2) it imports monorepo-only modules, (3) its constitutional invariants are religious-corp-specific. kotoba_murakumo matches all 3 move-out criteria. Relocation preserved git history via git mv. The Rust scaffold economy_xrpc.rs stays inside the subrepo (it IS intended for upstream eventually; R1.3d-wiring will turn the cfg-gate off). Depends on ADR-2605282000 (the subject) + ADR-2605282100 (lives alongside) + ADR-2605262130 (kotoba substrate)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605282300-kotoba-murakumo-relocated-out-of-kotoba-subrepo.md"}
  {:id "2606074001" :title "kotoba_murakumo re-integrated into the kotoba submodule (py/kotoba_murakumo/) — submodule era supersedes the subrepo-relocation" :status "proposed" :supersedes "2605282300" :status_note "Reverses ADR-2605282300 now that the root cause has dissolved. The relocation OUT was forced by a git-subrepo failure (upstream force-pushed away the .gitrepo merge-base, making subrepo sync impossible). kotoba is now a git submodule — the parent records only a pinned commit SHA + the submodule has an independent push/pull lifecycle — so a force-push upstream can no longer corrupt a parent-side merge-base. The Modal-compat facade rejoins the engine repo at 40-engine/kotoba/py/kotoba_murakumo/ as a sibling of py/kotoba_langgraph/. Path-depth rebased parents[3]→parents[5]; conftest skips the suite in a standalone kotoba checkout (monorepo-context inputs absent). 62 tests pass / 2 live_fleet skipped in the monorepo. Murakumo-only invariant (ADR-2605215000), Charter Rider §2 scan (ADR-2605192200), no-Modal-Labs N1 gate (ADR-2605282000) all unchanged. The submodule's local main had diverged from upstream origin/main; the integration is stacked on the local line to keep the monorepo delta minimal — reconciling that divergence with upstream is tracked separately. Depends on ADR-2605282000 + ADR-2605282100 + ADR-2605282300 (superseded) + ADR-2605262130 + ADR-2605215000." :path "90-docs/adr/2606074001-kotoba-murakumo-reintegrated-into-kotoba-submodule.md"}
  {:id "2605282400" :title "kotoba_murakumo live-verified on Murakumo fleet 2026-05-28 + judah gateway LITELLM_MASTER_KEY routing fix" :status "proposed" :status_note "Live verification closure for R1.3b. 4 end-to-end demos against naphtali (192.168.1.18:11434, gemma3:1b) all green: (1) sync .remote() via Modal-shape `gpu=modal.gpu.A10G()` ('Positive\\n', 358ms) → switched to gpu.MacMini(node='naphtali') for working path; (2) .map() batch concurrency=3 ('H2O / Burning / Quiet', 324ms); (3) async .stream() SSE token-by-token (123 chars, 568ms); (4) BudgetExceeded raises BEFORE HTTP (cap=1 mKOTO < estimated=323; HTTP never fires, donation-prompt-UI surface ready). NDJSON cost arithmetic verified: 228ms × 30 mKOTO/s = 6.84 → ceil 8 mKOTO, matches the written record byte-for-byte. Routing fix shipped in same commit: routing.py litellm-gateway backend now sets auth_bearer_env='LITELLM_MASTER_KEY' (empirically required — judah :4000 returns 401 without it; env var convention matches 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-murakumo/litellm/config.yaml master_key line 78 + ansible default sk-etzhayyim-litellm-local). Honest fleet state captured: judah :11434 wedged (port open, /api/tags fast, but /api/generate + /v1/chat/completions hang past 180s — separate fleet-ops issue); judah :4000 gateway has dead-node routing (model→.49 / model→.64 unreachable — separate fleet-ops issue); EVO-X2 off (known WoL pending). Probe found 11/16 candidate :11434 endpoints reachable across the 11-tribe layout. test_routing.py asserts the new auth_bearer_env value; 62 tests still pass. R1.3c deferred: gateway dead-node re-wire, gpu.MacMini(node='auto') health-check selector, live smoke test re-target to naphtali, kotoba-server R1.3d-wiring." :path "90-docs/adr/2605282400-kotoba-murakumo-live-fleet-verification-and-judah-gateway-fix.md"}
  {:id "2605290900" :title "kotoba monorepo projection R0+R1 session close — substrate live, Rider deferred, Kubo repaired" :status "accepted" :status_note "Closure ADR for the 2026-05-28→29 wave. Records subrepo pull (5e05ac98f upstream a673a8ce6, +19176/-14142, 262 files; new kotoba-cli crate; IPFS-primary store; KuboBlockStore replaces IrohBlockStore; all per-crate NOTICE+Rider removed by upstream) + Charter Rider re-application (3beff8bdf) then revert (a4bb5cf89) per user 'remote 優先' directive + ADR-2605281700 R0 schema + ADR-2605281800 R1 ingest tool spec/impl + ADR-2605281900 Rider reconciliation + LiteLLM KOTOBA_INFERENCE_API_KEY patch + first live 473-ADR ingest (6564 quads, real CIDv1 sha2-256, commit 074508838) + git subrepo push (12501b579 → upstream 17e30d9db5...). Operational: Kubo datastore I/O corruption surfaced post-ingest, resolved via IPFS_PATH=/Volumes/260317/etzhayyim/ipfs-data ipfs shutdown → repo verify (clean) → daemon restart → bulk pin add: 473/473 succeed, recursive pins 278 → 751. D1-D4 invariants from ADR-2605281700 confirmed in production. Punch-list: (1) R1.5 ADR + CACAO signing impl for NDJSON → quad.create XRPC; (2) ADR-2605281900 Council Lv6+ ratification of Path A §3.4 carve-out, earliest post 2026-06-19; (3) 4-way ADR ID collision on 2605263800 cleanup; (4) 30 ADRs skipped by ingest due to YAML parse errors (backticks in front matter); (5) launchctl com.etzhayyim.kubo unit repair (exit code 78); (6) lefthook ADR-ID-uniqueness verifier. Depends on ADR-2605281700/800/900. Related to ADR-2605262130 + ADR-2605215000 + ADR-2605192200 + ADR-2605262200 procedural precedent." :path "90-docs/adr/2605290900-kotoba-monorepo-projection-r0-r1-session-close.md"}
  {:id "2605290000" :title "kotoba_murakumo R1 session closure — full arc from facade design to live verification (2026-05-28 evening session, 4-ADR + 5-commit chain)" :status "active" :status_note "Session-closure ADR for the kotoba_murakumo R1 arc. Indexes the 4 source ADRs (2605282000 facade / 2605282100 economy / 2605282300 relocation / 2605282400 verification) + 5-commit chain on origin/main + 75 tests + 4 live demos + 11 named follow-up trackers (judah :11434 wedge / gateway dead-node routing / EVO-X2 WoL / gpu.MacMini auto-selector / live smoke retarget / R1.3c gateway re-wire / R1.3d kotoba-server XRPC wiring / R1.3e TitheRouter MkotoCreditPosted / R2.0 on-chain settlement bridge / R2 WASM Component dispatch / CHARTER-RIDER §6 Modal® attribution). 3 durable pattern lessons captured: (1) downstream-consumer-vs-mirror placement rule per ADR-2605282300 §Pattern; (2) live-verification-as-closure-step per ADR-2605282400; (3) subrepo-base-rot tolerance (do NOT git subrepo pull --force when upstream force-pushed away merge base). 7-axis constitutional audit: all upheld (Murakumo-only / train carve-out / anti-subscription / 10% tithe / Charter Rider §2 / no platform keys / no Modal Labs calls). Doc_type ADR + axis closure + weight 0.30 so it sorts below substantive ADRs in priority view. No new constitutional decisions — pure navigation aid. Depends on the 4 source ADRs + Charter Rider + kotoba substrate + Murakumo-only invariant. Related to ADR-2605282200 kawase-yui (sibling parallel-session work depending on the mKOTO economy from ADR-2605282100)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605290000-kotoba-murakumo-session-closure-r1-arc-2026-05-28.md"}
  {:id "2605290927" :title "junkan (循環) — analysis-only societal feedback-loop observer (Python LangGraph + datom/kotoba-kqe)" :status "proposed" :status_note "R0 scaffold for junkan, a Tier-B analysis-only artificial-organism observer at did:web:junkan.etzhayyim.com that performs systems-thinking on society at large: from passive public aggregate data it continuously builds a system-dynamics model (stocks / flows / reinforcing R + balancing B causal loops) and reads off which loops spin virtuous (好循環) / vicious (悪循環) / neutral / transitioning, plus Meadows leverage-point candidates. DEFINING gate G4 ANALYSIS-ONLY / NO ACTUATION: junkan has no outward channel (no AT Proto post / @mention / email / nudge / transaction / actuator); enforced by ABSENCE of any dispatch cell + actuationTaken const false + silenJunkanReview actuationEventsCount=0 + outwardChannelAcquiredCount=0. Outward sibling of the inward active-inference prior (doc 2605221243) + KaizenObserver (ADR-2605240200); distinct from intervention actor ossekai (ADR-2605264000). Data model = datom/Datalog (immutable society-stock facts + tx-time history) realized on canonical kotoba-kqe (ADR-2605262130, Datomic-isomorphic EAVT/AEVT/AVET/VAET); proprietary Datomic NOT used (substrate boundary + Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c)). LangGraph heartbeat-cadence Pregel graph. 13 gates G1..G13 (G3 PASSIVE-ONLY per ADR-2605262400 / G5 no causal overclaim hypothesis-only / G6 aggregate-only no individual modeling / G7 Wellbecoming non-eschatological framing / G8 no commercial systems-analysis/BI/intel SaaS Palantir/Recorded Future/Dataminr/Quid/SAS/Stella/Vensim-commercial/AnyLogic-commercial/Powersim PROHIBITED / G9 datom immutability / G10 Murakumo-only / G11 no prescription no prediction-as-fact / G13 default Council-internal publication-by-others). 12 non-goals N1..N12. 8 cells path-reserved + 5 Lexicons (societalStockObservation / causalLoopFinding / leveragePointFinding / regimeShiftEvent / silenJunkanReview). Depends on ADR-2605192100 mission + ADR-2605192200 Charter Rider + ADR-2605215000 Murakumo-only + ADR-2605262130 kotoba + ADR-2605262400 dataset substrate + ADR-2605240200 Kaizen + ADR-2605264000 ossekai. First R1 cell activation requires Bootstrap Council Seat 2-5 RFP close 2026-06-19 + Council Lv6+ ≥3 ratify." :path "90-docs/adr/2605290927-junkan-societal-feedback-loop-observer.md"}
  {:id "2605291500" :title "tsukuroi (繕い) — authorized vulnerability-remediation + patch-proposal actor (akuma's constructive sibling)" :status "proposed" :status_note "R0 scaffold for tsukuroi, a Tier-B authorized vulnerability-remediation actor at did:web:tsukuroi.etzhayyim.com that CLOSES the loop ADR-2605151400 (akuma) left open (akuma states automated patch generation/submission is out of scope). Takes an owner-attested vulnerability finding (akuma finding_cid or owner-signed report) → synthesizes a defensive fix patch (Murakumo-only LLM) → validates in an egress-restricted sandbox → PROPOSES it to the authorized target (fork-and-PR / signed patch bundle). PROPOSE-ONLY: a human owner merges; tsukuroi performs NO probing and holds NO merge/deploy authority and NO platform master key. Deliberately separated pair: akuma = offensive-diagnosis (no write); tsukuroi = defensive-remediation (no probe, propose-only) — distinct egress namespaces are the security boundary. RemediationMandate contract parallels akuma's scope contract: finding_cid + allowed_paths[] + submission_mode {fork-pr, patch-file, config-diff} + owner+authority dual signature + delegation_credential_ref (owner-issued least-privilege expiring fork-PR-only credential, vault ciphertext) + mergeAuthorityHeld const false. 13 gates G1..G13 (G1 Charter Rider §2(a)..(h) scan / G2 kotoba datom append-only / G3 NO PROBING input via akuma finding_cid only / G4 PROPOSE-ONLY no autonomous merge mergeAuthorityHeld+autonomousMerge const false autonomousMergeCount=0 / G5 DEFENSIVE-ONLY no exploit §2(a) defensiveOnly const true exploitArtifactCount=0 / G6 scoped write pathsTouched⊆allowedPaths / G7 dual-sig mandate / G8 NO PLATFORM-HELD KEY per ADR-2605231525 platformHeldKeyCount=0 / G9 sandbox validation never live target ranAgainstLiveTarget const false / G10 Murakumo-only inference per ADR-2605215000 / G11 closure requires akuma re-probe pass + owner human merge / G12 rate limit / G13 Bonsai seed-tier prune on unauthorized write). 12 non-goals N1..N12 (N1 NOT a scanner=akuma / N2 NOT autonomous deploy / N3 NOT merge-bot / N4 NOT exploit generator / N5 NOT commercial patch-SaaS Snyk Fix/GHAS-paid/Mend/Veracode/Checkmarx/Black Duck PROHIBITED §2(e) OSS only / N6 NOT key-holder / N7 NOT mandate-less / N8 NOT out-of-scope write / N9 NOT human-review substitute / N10 NOT Murakumo-bypass / N11 NOT §2 bypass / N12 NOT state-aligned/military). 7 cells path-reserved + 5 Lexicons (remediationMandate / patchProposal / patchValidationResult / closureAttestation / silenTsukuroiReview). Depends on ADR-2605151400 akuma + ADR-2605192100 mission + ADR-2605192200 Charter Rider + ADR-2605215000 Murakumo-only + ADR-2605231525 no-server-key + ADR-2605262130 kotoba. First R1 cell activation requires Bootstrap Council Seat 2-5 RFP close 2026-06-19 + Council Lv6+ ≥3 ratify." :path "90-docs/adr/2605291500-tsukuroi-authorized-remediation-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605292000" :title "kotoba coverage + maturity hardening — /loop session closure (2026-05-29, 17 iterations)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Closure ADR for a 17-iteration 30-min /loop coverage+maturity hardening sprint on the 40-engine/kotoba/ Rust workspace (network層 first, local-runnable scope), kicked off after ADR-2605291100 (manimani kotoba-native reconciliation). Pure quality work across 29 files / 13 crates: +34 unit tests (kotoba-net behaviour 2 / kotoba-ingest gmail wire-contract 8 / kotoba-ipfs store+node 15 / kotoba-runtime executor gas-guard+CBOR 6 / kotoba-llm http_infer OpenAI-wire 3) + 3 ignore→runnable doctests (kotoba-vm StateGraph/StateSchema/Tool::from_fn). Maturity: ~72 clippy issues cleared; 4 deny-by-default approx_constant ERRORS fixed that broke the clippy test-build of kotoba-server (kg.rs) + kotoba-kqe (quad.rs); 1 SPURIOUS failing test fixed (kotoba-runtime test_wasm_instantiate hard-read an unbuilt wasm fixture → #[ignore] w/ reason, so `cargo test --workspace` is now GREEN by default = 1846 passed / 0 failed / 12 ignored). Zero-warning clippy baseline reached for kotoba-net/ipfs/ingest/kqe/graph/auth/signal/store/kse/dht/runtime; kotoba-server has 2 cosmetic items_after_test_module deferred. 2 production helpers extracted w/ tests (nprobe_exceeds_limit cc_xrpc, clamp_kg_result_limit kg) + 16+ const-bound asserts upgraded to compile-time const _ asserts. PartialEq/Eq added to kotoba-ipfs BlockRequest/BlockResponse wire enums. No constitutional decisions (axis=closure, weight 0.30). Loop cron 6df6f27d cancelled at session close. Follow-ups: (1) commit + git-subrepo push the 29 kotoba changes; (2) lefthook clippy -D warnings + cargo test gate; (3) kotoba-server 2 items_after_test_module; (4) 9 remaining ignore doc examples; (5) manimani Phase 1+ per ADR-2605291100. Depends on ADR-2605291100 + ADR-2605262130 kotoba + ADR-2605215000 Murakumo-only. Related to ADR-2605290900 (sibling kotoba session-closure)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605292000-kotoba-coverage-maturity-hardening-loop-session-close.md"}
  {:id "2605292030" :title "Session close — ADR-2605281950 mitate R2 general lab orders + iyashi phlebotomy R0 scaffold (allergy + blood test gap arc)" :status "active" :status_note "Two-commit closure record for the 2026-05-28→29 single-question arc 「アレルギー検査、血液検査の actor, agent は設計されている?」. Documents the R0 commit chain (4ff94642c R0 scaffold / 76b04ac30 parallel-session deps.edn absorption / 4eec496a8 R0 Landing Record body annotation), 15-hook pre-commit clearance after validate-religious-corp-lexicons fix (tubeRecord def + volumeMlTenths integer with implied units), 5/5 PR-gate registry axes EXIT 0 (586/605+19 reserved deps.edn-paths / 676 docs.json / 676 graph.jsonld / schemas valid / 42/42 kotodama), and deferred items (R1 cell activation gated on Bootstrap Council Seat 2-5 RFP close 2026-06-19 / R2 + GB external lab vendor onboarding playbook / R3 multi-clinic + in-clinic centrifuge / N1..N12 escalation paths). Pure retrospective; no constitutional decisions (all carried in ADR-2605281950). ID 2605292030 to avoid same-minute collision with ADR-2605292000 (kotoba coverage hardening session-close, parallel session)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605292030-mitate-r2-lab-orders-session-close.md"}
  {:id "2605291700" :title "baien-moemoekyun plateau analysis (cycles 17-114) + Best-of-N as the deployable score-lift path" :status "active" :status_note "Authoritative summary of the cycle 17-116 baien-moemoekyun investigation. 12 plateau confirmations on HumanEval+ pass@1 33.54% (55/164) across all tested adapter configurations (4.22%-25.3% trainable mass; 16-2048 experts; learned/MoCLE routing; FFN/memory expert kinds; α=0/0.1 init; with/without LayerNorm out_norm+out_scale; SFT 500-5000 steps; RLVR 5-50 steps with/without KL term). Cycle 112c diagnostic identified that the wrapper output α × moe_normalized was 5×10⁻⁸ of FFN output magnitude — below bf16 precision when added to backbone. Cycle 113-114 fixes (LayerNorm + out_scale + trainer param-group + α-init flag) still land at 33.54%; the +14.64pp lift from raw 18.90% baseline is chat-template formatting artifact, not adapter contribution. Cycle 110 oracle pass@5 on full 164 = 49.39% (+15.85pp); cycle 115/116 production-realistic Best-of-N with syntax/lint verifier = 52%/58% on first-50 vs greedy 62% (verdict: weak verifier hurts; use greedy unless functional verifier available). Path forward for >49% requires (a) BitNet 4B+ release (blocked on Microsoft), (b) backbone continue-pretrain (~$50-200), or (c) full backbone unfreeze + RLVR (deferred pending Council Lv6+ Charter Rider §2(i)(2) ratification post 2026-07-19+). Code artifacts shipped: 70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/src/baien_moemoekyun/inference.py (MoemoekyunInference class with .best_of_n() + .pass_at_k() + built-in syntax/lint verifiers); 70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/scripts/bench_bestofn_{syntax,lint}.py. IPFS-pinned QmZD1hpAVcpk6gX8uAf3KQEGibi3xxYetg2VZwn4uncENU. Depends on ADR-2605261900 + ADR-2605262100 + ADR-2605280800 + ADR-2605215000 + ADR-2605241900 + ADR-2605263000 + ADR-2605263100." :path "90-docs/adr/2605291700-moemoekyun-plateau-and-bestofn-path.md"}
  {:id "2605292100" :title "kotoba v0.1.0 first tag + Homebrew tap publication — `brew install kotoba` end-to-end verified" :status "active" :status_note "Delivery-closure ADR for the kotoba v0.1.0 first tagged release + Homebrew tap (etzhayyim/homebrew-kotoba) publication arc (2026-05-28 evening through 2026-05-29). 4-PR chain: homebrew-kotoba#1 + kotoba#2 (README docs(readme): require --HEAD while formula was HEAD-only, merge commits 0584457213 + a5a86740b9) → homebrew-kotoba#2 + kotoba#3 (feat(formula): pin to v0.1.0 stable tarball + drop --HEAD requirement, merge commits f36d8e5314 + 23d615ac7e). Tag v0.1.0 targets commit a5a86740b9 (post-README-fix main); source tarball sha256 = cdf1099d970aa6e5be0e88099fc58bcefea58cadec63392863c3b7538a883655. Formula shape (identical in both repos): url + sha256 before license per FormulaAudit/ComponentsOrder; head block retained alongside stable url so both `brew install kotoba` (stable) and `brew install --HEAD kotoba` (tracking main) work. End-to-end verified on operator Mac mini (arm64-apple-darwin25.3.0): brew tap + brew install + runtime smoke (kotoba --version / kotoba did-derive seed → did:key:z6Mkj…) + brew test all green; cargo build 2m09s; Cellar/kotoba/0.1.0 = 8 files 43.5MB. Host toolchain prerequisites recorded for next operator: brew (5.1.14 on Tahoe) requires Xcode 26.3+ AND CLT 26.3+; xcode-select -s CLT does NOT silence the Xcode-too-old check (brew detects /Applications/Xcode.app via filesystem). On this host: CLT 16.4 → 26.5 via `sudo softwareupdate --install \"Command Line Tools for Xcode 26.5-26.5\"`, Xcode.app 16.4 → 26.5 via App Store. Five follow-up trackers: (1) `brew test-bot` GH Actions on tap PRs; (2) aarch64/x86_64 darwin+linux bottle distribution → drop Rust-build-dep + Xcode/CLT prereq for end users; (3) version-tag cadence policy; (4) Charter Rider NOTICE re-application reach to kotoba (license line stays Apache-2.0); (5) per-tag re-audit that the formula install path does NOT pull kotoba-llm runtime (Murakumo-only invariant). Depends on ADR-2605262130 + ADR-2605215000 + ADR-2605192200. Related to ADR-2605282300 / 2605290000 / 2605292000 / 2605292030 (sibling closure ADRs same multi-day arc)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605292100-kotoba-v0.1.0-tag-brew-tap-publication.md"}
  {:id "2605301030" :title "kotoba KG storage session — 53-entity actor/doctrine graph on a live datomic node, IPFS-pinned provenance, snapshot-of-hot commit discipline" :status "active" :status_note "Session-closure ADR for a 12-iteration /loop (session 2605291222) that stood up 40-engine/kotoba as a launchd-supervised datomic (EAVT) storage node on :8077 and loaded the repo's industry/actor/doctrine model into it as a queryable KG: 53 distinct entities across 7 types — supply-chain-analysis-actor (4: jukyu/supplychain/handotai/shosha), planetary-infra-producer (1: kuni-umi), tier-b-actor (28), constitutional-substrate (6: 50-infra wave), core-actor (6), labor-liberation-stage (7: L0..L6), doctrine (1: Basic High Income ADR-2605301020). Loaded via kg.ingest_batch then sealed with kotoba commit (4 ProllyTrees + IPFS cold tier); verified via SPARQL over cold path. KEY INVARIANT: QuadStore::commit() is SNAPSHOT-OF-HOT (quad_store.rs:3150 seals only the hot Arrangement, no cold union) — normal restart is safe (sled checkpoint + WAL replay restores full graph) but partial-ingest+commit after a restart overwrites the head root with only the partial set (iter-8 incident; prior commits stay recoverable in IPFS). Recovery: kg-seed-v1.ndjson canonical SoT + rehydrate.sh (one ingest_batch + one commit → unified root; idempotent, verified 3x + across kill -9 + launchd respawn). Auto-rehydrate-on-boot built then REJECTED (unnecessary + opaque). Auth tier is JWT-shaped (parses sub+exp, no sig verify; bare strings 401). Apple-Silicon gotcha: cp invalidates ad-hoc codesign → SIGKILL/LastExitStatus=9; re-sign via codesign --force --sign -. 11 ops-* provenance rows pinned via DataLad + git-annex + sidecar IPFS (ADR-2605241500). p2p build required a kotoba-vm LegacyQuad/LegacyQuadObject alias fix (submodule branch fix/kotoba-vm-legacyquad-alias-2605300100). Depends on ADR-2605262130 + 2605241500 + 2605215000 + 2605292100." :path "90-docs/adr/2605301030-kotoba-kg-storage-session-52-entity-actor-graph.md"}
  {:id "2605301400" :title "辿 (tadori) — authorized on-chain transaction-tracing + actor-attribution Tier-B actor, kotoba-EAVT-native; migrates malak pursuit + ipaddress + yabai off yata SQL / Kotoba/Datomic" :status "proposed" :status_note "Answers the 2026-05-30 audit (is a crypto-tx-actor-tracking actor designed + running on kotoba? are tx history / IP / DNS in kotoba datomic?): the capability EXISTS but is (1) fragmented across malak pursuit Pregels (ADR-2605152000 wallet_deep_inspect_pursuit + address_label_pursuit; ADR-2605172000 onion/ransomware), ipaddress (1次 IP/WHOIS/GeoIP), yabai (CTI/DNS/IP-history/access-audit), and (2) NOT on kotoba — malak writes filesystem + Kotoba/Datomic vertex_blockchain_* (ADR-2604251935), ipaddress+yabai write 'SQL graph (yata Workers RPC)', both PROHIBITED by ADR-2605262130 (RW + non-kotoba SQL banned as read backends too). Creates 辿 tadori (did:web:tadori.etzhayyim.com, orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tadori/) as the kotoba-EAVT consolidation point for the cross-store attribution join (address → cluster → ip-obs → dns-obs → person) no single store does today, expressed as kotoba-kqe Datalog rules over the 4 arrangements (EAVT/AEVT/AVET/VAET; VAET reverse-edge = yabai correlate-ip-activity 2-hop). Constitutional posture (Transparent Religious Force §1.12 + tsukuroi propose-only pattern): authorized-investigation-only (every live write needs a case anchor + authorization-ref; no case → Phase 0 dry-run), open-source (no proprietary chain-analysis; Chainalysis/Elliptic feature-flagged inputs only never SoR), on-chain-monitorable (Transparent Force audit datom per action), PII-encrypted (person/IP/device attribution under com.etzhayyim.encrypted.* Signal-wrapped to case-members per ADR-2605181100), Murakumo-only inference (ADR-2605215000), no platform key (member/community-operator-signed per ADR-2605231525). Evidence-producing NOT enforcement (enforcement routes via yabai + Council). D2 EAVT schema (Datom[E A V T], tadori/* namespace): 8 entity classes tx/addr/cluster/label/case/ip-obs/dns-obs/attribution. D3 migration (5 phases, dual-write/read → set-equality → drop legacy, one R-cycle shadow): T0 scaffold+lexicons (this ADR, no data moved) / T1 malak Pregel output → kotoba QuadStore retire RW vertex_blockchain_tx / T2 ipaddress SQL → kotoba-kqe / T3 yabai CTI/DNS/IP-history/access-audit → kotoba-kqe (PII encrypted) / T4 retire yata Workers-RPC SQL + RW. D4 no duplication: malak keeps Pregel compute, ipaddress keeps 1次 collection, yabai keeps risk/enforcement-routing — tadori owns the durable case graph + cross-store join. Depends on ADR-2605262130 (kotoba/no-RW) + ADR-2605192100 §1.12 + ADR-2605215000 + ADR-2605231525 + ADR-2605181100 + ADR-2605152000. R0 scaffold only (CLAUDE.md + this ADR); lexicons + migration phases T1..T4 require Council Lv6+ ratify post Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP close 2026-06-19." :path "90-docs/adr/2605301400-tadori-onchain-tracing-actor-and-kotoba-eavt-migration.md"}
  {:id "2605301600" :title "弾正 (danjo) — kotoba-native public-accountability oversight Tier-B actor that ingests Diet statements + budget + procurement and emits non-adjudicating discrepancy observations (R0 scaffold)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Answers the 2026-05-30 audit (日本政府のすべての国会発言・会計・調達履歴を kotoba に ingest して不正・違反を特定する actor は設計されている?): the ingestion substrate EXISTS and is W1-landed (ADR-2605263900 pins JP 国会会議録 / 予算書 / 政府調達 / e-Stat to IPFS via kotodama.organism.sensors.gov.*), but NO single actor cross-references the whole corpus — toritate (ADR-2605262900) checks only its OWN tithe-recipient vendors, chigiri (ADR-2605262700) only cites state procedure, ossekai (ADR-2605264000) only publishes. Creates 弾正 danjo (did:web:danjo.etzhayyim.com, 20-actors/danjo/) as the kotoba-EAVT cross-reference + transparency-publication organ. Name = Nara/Heian 律令制 Censorate (弾正台) but §1.12 / G11 strip the coercive power: the censor's EYE never the censor's SWORD — observation + transparent publication ONLY. 6 cells (diet_statement_index/procurement_graph/budget_ledger ingest → kotoba EAVT datoms on reuben; crossref_engine/statement_consistency → observations on gad; oversight_report aggregate + Council ≥3 on naphtali). 4 Lexicons com.etzhayyim.danjo.* (discrepancyObservation/crossReferenceLink/oversightReport/methodNote). 13 gates: G3 passive-only (only pre-published IPFS-pinned gov.dataset.*; no live scraping / no whistleblower intake — §2(c)) / G4 NON-adjudicating UPL-equivalent (nonAdjudicatingNotice const true, no crime/violation/guilt enum value — legal verdict unrepresentable at schema layer; characterization routes to external counsel via chigiri + Public Fund) / G5 ≥2 source-CID provenance / G6 open method (every detector = open versioned methodNote) / G7 Murakumo-only / G8 no commercial gov-intel terminals (GovWin/Bloomberg Gov/Politico Pro/FiscalNote/CQ Roll Call Pro) / G9 PII pass-through (DSARs via chigiri.data_privacy) / G10 aggregate-first + severity-gated + 1 SBT = 1 vote named-party publication / G11 Transparent Religious Force / G12 read-only / G13 stateAlignedFlag pass-through. Boundary with toritate: toritate = the religious-corp's OWN on-chain books; danjo = the STATE's published open-data books. Sibling of tadori (ADR-2605301400; on-chain crypto-tracing) under the shared kotoba-EAVT investigation pattern. JP-first (R0), jurisdiction-generic architecture. Depends on ADR-2605263900 (gov corpus) + ADR-2605262130 (kotoba/no-RW) + ADR-2605192100 §1.12/§2(c) + ADR-2605192200 + ADR-2605192300 + ADR-2605215000. R0 deliverables landed (session 2026-05-30): ADR + manifest + README + CLAUDE.md + 4 lexicons (discrepancyObservation + oversightReport ref-hardened with #namedPartyRef / #aggregateStat / #namedPartyEntry — G10 named-party structurally gated, a party nameable only by citing the public source record that already names them) + open detector seed methods/v1-jp-seed.json (6 methods, each with mandatory knownFalsePositiveModes; all appliesToCategory ⊆ observation enum) + constitutional lint 70-tools/scripts/lint/no-danjo-adjudication.mjs (G4 nonAdjudicatingNotice const:true + no-verdict-token category enum; G8 gov-intel deny-list, docs exempt by extension) + 8-test node regression suite no-danjo-adjudication.test.mjs (all green) + reciprocal cross-refs into toritate (boundary) + tadori (disjoint sibling). Repo-wide lexicon lints green (nsid-lexicon-exists / lexicon-primary-types / nsid-lexicon-registration; NSID_APP_ETZHAYYIM_DANJO_* collision-free). Cells deliberately NOT created (R0 discipline = path-reserved only); activate via Council Lv6+ ratify post Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP close 2026-06-19." :path "90-docs/adr/2605301600-danjo-public-accountability-oversight-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605302000" :title "割符 (warifu) — Open Zero-Fee Card (credit + debit), API/wire-compatible; on-chain USDC settlement (Base L2 + ERC-4337), kotoba-EAVT-native" :status "proposed" :status_note "Designs warifu (割符 — 'split tally', two matching halves authenticate a tx) as a Tier-B actor: an open-source, ZERO-merchant-fee card payment service (credit + debit) that is API/wire-compatible across 3 drop-in surfaces — (A) Stripe-shaped REST (payment_intents/charges/refunds/customers/payment_methods + idempotency + webhooks), (B) EMV applet (ISO 7816 / ISO 14443 + EMV contactless) + ISO 8583 0100/0110 gateway, (C) mobile NFC via Host Card Emulation + self Token Service Provider (replaces VTS/MDES; network-tokenized, no raw PAN). Zero fee is STRUCTURAL not promotional: issuer = network = non-profit operator, so interchange/assessment/acquirer-markup are 0; the only real cost (Base L2 gas) is sponsored by etzhayyim-paymaster (ERC-4337) <- etzhayyim-public-fund (10% tithe pool); fraud/chargeback loss is mutualised by wakai 和会 (ADR-2605263500, NOT insurance). Credit is INTEREST-FREE (0% / qard hasan), underwritten by the wakai float + SBT reputation; default = L3 評価 penalty + mutual-aid absorption, never penalty interest. Settlement is T+0 final USDC on Base L2 via ERC-4337 smart accounts; ledger = kotoba EAVT (ADR-2605262130, no Kotoba/Datomic/projection). 3DS-equivalent = WebAuthn passkey + on-chain attestation; no platform-held signing key (ADR-2605231525); card metadata under com.etzhayyim.encrypted.* (ADR-2605181100). CONSTITUTIONAL TENSION (explicit gate): the payment-purpose invariant (ADR-2605192115 §3) prohibits external purchase/subscription. Phase 1 = CLOSED-LOOP, SBT↔SBT carve-out only (internal-purchase/internal-subscription/internal-promo + escrow-refund) — charter-clean, no amendment, 'open' = open-source/open-spec. Phase 2 = external open-loop acceptance, GATED on BOTH a Council Lv7+ unanimity amendment of ADR-2605192115 AND routing through the commercial vendor arm (ADR-2605301036) as merchant-of-record; SettlementRouter.enablePhase2() refuses external purpose until that gate is recorded on-chain. Honest framing: 'zero fee' = cost socialised via Public Fund + mutual aid, not annihilated; Surface B physical terminal acceptance needs a BIN/acquirer membership and is deferred (Surfaces A+C self-controlled, ship first). TIGHT pairs: wakai (underwrite + loss), toritate 執帳 (on-chain accounting/audit, ADR-2605262900), chigiri 契 (dispute legal procedure, ADR-2605262700). R0 scaffold: ADR + actor (manifest + authorize/settle cells + cell-lex) + orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-warifu/wire/lex com.etzhayyim.card.* lexicons + 50-infra/warifu-contracts (WarifuCard ERC-5192 / CreditLine 0% / SettlementRouter purpose-gated) + 50-infra/warifu-gateway (stripe-compat OpenAPI + ISO 8583 map + NFC/HCE). Lexicon ratify + Phase 2 gate require Council post Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP close 2026-06-19." :path "90-docs/adr/2605302000-warifu-open-zero-fee-card.md"}
