  {:id "2605302245" :title "弾正 (danjo) global fiscal-flow extension — generalize budget/procurement ingest beyond JP + add inter-governmental fund-flow datom class + define the danjo(engine)↔kanae(visualizer) handoff (R3-gated, non-adjudicating)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Direction (1) of the 2026-05-30 user request (今の全世界の政府の資金の流れを ingest / LLM 分析 / 可視化 / kotoba 永続化 する actor は設計されているか?). danjo (ADR-2605301600) already cross-references the open-government corpus into kotoba EAVT but is JP-first at R0 and visualization is an explicit danjo non-goal. This ADR is direction (1): generalize danjo's budget_ledger + procurement_graph ingest cells from JP-first to jurisdiction-parametric over the already-global + W1-landed corpus (ADR-2605263900: USAspending / EU Financial Transparency System / IMF SDMX / World Bank / OECD / UN / EU TED / US SAM.gov + JP 予算書 / 政府調達), and reserve a new kotoba EAVT datom class `intergov-fund-flow` (donorJurisdiction ↔ recipientJurisdiction ↔ instrument ↔ amount ↔ period) for flows the domestic budget_ledger cannot express. CONSTRAINT: does NOT change any danjo gate, does NOT move the R3 multi-jurisdiction Council-Lv7+-unanimity gate (ADR-2605301600 §7), does NOT add a renderer or LLM-narrative path to danjo, does NOT create new cells — PROPOSED design + datom-schema reservation only. All danjo gates G1-G13 apply unchanged (passive-only G3, non-adjudicating G4, ≥2 source CIDs G5, open method G6, Murakumo-only G7, no commercial gov-intel G8, aggregate-first G10, Transparent Religious Force G11, read-only G12, stateAlignedFlag pass-through G13). Defines the handoff contract: danjo = non-adjudicating cross-reference ENGINE (emits fiscal + intergov-fund-flow datoms, renders nothing); kanae (ADR-2605302300) = fiscal-flow ASSEMBLY + Murakumo NARRATIVE + kami-engine WASM VISUALIZATION (reads danjo datoms read-only). danjo finds, kanae renders. Depends on ADR-2605301600 + ADR-2605263900 + ADR-2605262130 + ADR-2605192100 + ADR-2605215000." :path "90-docs/adr/2605302245-danjo-global-fiscal-flow-extension.md"}
  {:id "2605302300" :title "鼎 (kanae) — kotoba-native global government fiscal-flow visualization Tier-B actor: assemble worldwide fund flows (domestic full chain + inter-governmental) into kotoba EAVT, narrate with Murakumo-only LLM, render kami-engine WASM visualizations (R0 scaffold)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Answers the 2026-05-30 audit (今の全世界の政府の資金の流れを ingest / LLM 分析 / 可視化 / datomic kotoba api で永続化 する actor は設計されているか?): NO single actor had all four capabilities. The global fiscal INGEST substrate is W1-landed (ADR-2605263900 pins USAspending / EU FTS / IMF SDMX / World Bank / OECD / UN / EU TED / US SAM.gov + JP 予算書 / 政府調達 to IPFS), danjo (ADR-2605301600) cross-references it into kotoba EAVT but is JP-first AND visualization is an explicit danjo non-goal. Creates 鼎 kanae (did:web:kanae.etzhayyim.com, 20-actors/kanae/) as the MISSING visualization+narrative lens — direction (2) (direction (1) = danjo extension ADR-2605302245). User-selected params: name 鼎 (kanae; 鼎の軽重を問う = weigh the worthiness of those who govern; three legs = domestic budget / domestic procurement / inter-governmental transfer), scope = domestic full chain (appropriation→outlay→subaward→procurement-award→recipient) + inter-governmental (IMF/WB/OECD/UN transfer + aid + loan), render = kami-engine WASM (reuse isekai/omniverse WASM viewer assets). danjo finds, kanae renders. 5 cells (flow_assembler + intergov_flow → kotoba EAVT fundFlowEdge on reuben; flow_narrative Murakumo + viz_compiler kami-engine WASM on gad; publish aggregate + Council ≥3 on naphtali). 4 Lexicons com.etzhayyim.kanae.* (fundFlowEdge / flowNarrative / visualizationManifest / methodNote). 15 gates: G1 Charter Rider scan / G2 kotoba EAVT (Kotoba/Datomic/Postgres/Lance PROHIBITED — the maps Kotoba/Datomic backend is NOT a template) / G3 passive-only upstream-only (gov.dataset.* + danjo datoms; no live scraping / no whistleblower intake — §2(c)) / G4 NON-adjudicating UPL-equivalent (flowNarrative.nonAdjudicatingNotice const true, fundFlowEdge.flowClass enum carries no crime/violation/不正 token — legal verdict unrepresentable; characterization via external counsel chigiri + Public Fund) / G5 ≥2 source-CID provenance / G6 open method / G7 Murakumo-only inference (flowNarrative.murakumoInferenceAttestation REQUIRED, inferenceSubstrate const 'murakumo' — vendor-LLM origin unrepresentable; ADR-2605215000) / G8 no commercial gov-intel terminals (GovWin/Bloomberg Gov/Politico Pro/FiscalNote/CQ Roll Call) / G9 PII pass-through (DSARs via chigiri.data_privacy) / G10 aggregate-first visualization + 1 SBT = 1 vote named-element gating / G11 Transparent Religious Force / G12 read-only / G13 stateAlignedFlag pass-through / G14 kami-engine WASM render-only (no Tableau/Power BI/Looker/Palantir Foundry; renderSubstrate const 'kami-engine-wasm') / G15 no ad/analytics SDK in render path (no GA4/Meta Pixel). 14 non-goals. Boundary: danjo = non-adjudicating cross-reference ENGINE; kanae = ASSEMBLY + Murakumo NARRATIVE + WASM VISUALIZATION lens; maps ∥ disjoint (geo + Kotoba/Datomic). R0 deliverables landed (session 2026-05-30): ADR + manifest + README + CLAUDE.md + 4 lexicons (fundFlowEdge #endpointRef / flowNarrative #murakumoAttestation / visualizationManifest #namedElementRef — G10 named-element structurally gated by publiclyNamedBasis + councilReviewCid + oneSbtOneVoteChainCid) + open aggregation seed methods/v1-global-seed.json (4 methods, each with mandatory knownFalsePositiveModes) + constitutional lint 70-tools/scripts/lint/no-kanae-adjudication.mjs (G4 nonAdjudicatingNotice const:true + no-verdict-token flowClass enum; G7 murakumoInferenceAttestation required + inferenceSubstrate const murakumo; G8 gov-intel deny-list; G15 ad/analytics SDK deny-list — docs exempt by extension) + 11-test node regression suite no-kanae-adjudication.test.mjs (all green) + reciprocal cross-refs into danjo (engine/visualizer boundary). Cells deliberately NOT created (R0 discipline = path-reserved only); activate via Council Lv6+ ratify post Bootstrap Council Seats 2-5 RFP close 2026-06-19 + danjo R1. Depends on ADR-2605302245 + ADR-2605301600 + ADR-2605263900 + ADR-2605262130 + ADR-2605261800 (kami-engine) + ADR-2605192100 + ADR-2605192200 + ADR-2605192300 + ADR-2605215000." :path "90-docs/adr/2605302300-kanae-global-fiscal-flow-visualization-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2605311500" :status "accepted" :title "kami-genesis physics maturation (re-issued from 2605310100; concurrently committed by Covenant Transparency ADR) — PlanarChain articulation + clean-room isaacsim.core.api surface + analytical/conservation-law validation + G5 Isaac-reference scorecard" :status_note "Session record (2026-05-31) for the physics-engine maturation loop. (1) PlanarChain = third World articulation topology (N≥3 serial revolute) over the existing RNEA+CRBA+LDLᵀ planar solver; detect_topology recognizes a serial revolute chain from URDF (70-tools/e7m-sim/scenes/arm3/arm3.urdf); step/set_joint_torques/joint_positions/joint_velocities/link_state/reset_to_zero N-DOF aware; World::jacobian() dispatches to planar_chain_link_jacobian (all three topologies share get_jacobians()-shape). (2) kami-genesis/src/isaac_api.rs = clean-room isaacsim.core.api mirror (IsaacWorld + ArticulationView{get_joint_positions/get_joint_velocities/num_dof/get_jacobian/get_world_pose} + ArticulationViewMut::set_joint_efforts); single-env (num_envs=1); NO NVIDIA library/header/binary linked — §2(b) N1..N9 NEVER; batched/sensor surfaces explicitly NOT yet implemented (no 'complete parity' claim). (3) Validation = analytical + conservation law, the clean-room evidence kami agrees with NVIDIA on the same physics without running NVIDIA: kami-genesis uniform-rod α=3g/(2L) + ω=√(3g/L) (2%) + 2-link energy-drift <5%/3s; kami-dec heat Σ conserved (<0.2%, decay=0) + monotone decay + Helmholtz div² <20%. (4) G5 = kami-genesis/tests/g5_scorecard.rs scores a kami rollout vs a reference trajectory CSV, gate ≥0.75; loader PREFERS reference_freefall_isaac.csv (NVIDIA Isaac ground truth captured ONCE on the isolated trial machine — metrics CSV only, never binaries) and falls back to reference_freefall_analytic.csv (regenerated from kami closed-form output → self-consistency 1.0). Dropping in the Isaac CSV activates the real gate with zero code change. Honest limitations: Isaac surface partial; NVIDIA cross-check latent until an Isaac CSV is captured; fluid agreement is conservation-law level only (pixel-identical with NVIDIA Flow/PhysX-fluid impossible and NOT claimed). Verified by direct cargo-test observation: kami-genesis 87 passed/0 failed; kami-dec 9 passed/0 failed. Commits: 11462db08 / e9d55c580 / 24bdf8bbb / 678fdd384 / 245d5ed5a / eef378cd3 (branch feat/kami-genesis-planar-chain-articulation)." :path "90-docs/adr/2605311500-kami-genesis-physics-validation-and-isaac-clean-room-surface.md"}
  {:id "2605302356" :title "kotoba LangGraph actor LLM inference — live end-to-end verification, three runtime fixes, macOS Local Network Privacy root-cause, and durable Murakumo LiteLLM-loopback routing (session closure)" :status "active" :status_note "Session-closure ADR for 'kotoba で langgraph actor は llm 推論なども行なっている? 動いている?'. Establishes EMPIRICALLY (live :8077): a Python LangGraph actor runs in-WASM (aria_kotoba.wasm, gas 15, real output) AND performs LLM inference end-to-end (agent.wasm → KotobaLLM → kotoba:kais/llm.infer → Murakumo gemma4-e4b → '4', gas 1015). Corrects ADR-2605301625's over-stated '✅ verified on prod' (it did not build/run on the launchd daemon as-claimed). Three kotoba runtime fixes shipped (etzhayyim/kotoba branch fix/wasm-runtime-build-json-macro): (a53457e) invoke_run error paths return Err((StatusCode,String)) so --features wasm-runtime builds; HttpInferEngine runs the HTTP call on a dedicated OS thread + fresh per-call reqwest client (the startup client was bound to the wrong tokio runtime → immediate 'error sending request') + connect/timeout diagnostics; kotoba-langgraph-hello agent.py hoists lazy _cbor/_entry/wit_world.imports.llm imports to module scope (componentize-py static analysis doesn't follow lazy imports → call-time trap) and agent.wasm rebuilt (componentize-py 0.23). (5f9d14c) KOTOBA_INFERENCE_API_KEY optional bearer for OpenAI-compatible gateways. ROOT CAUSE of the LAN failure = macOS Local Network Privacy (TCC): the launchd-spawned kotoba daemon is denied access to LAN inference nodes (192.168.1.18:11434 → errno 65 'No route to host') even though curl from Terminal reaches it; launchd daemons don't inherit local-network permission. DURABLE FIX (canonical local): route inference through the loopback Murakumo LiteLLM gateway 127.0.0.1:4000 (TCC-exempt; LiteLLM holds LAN access + load-balances; ADR-2605215000 SSoT) with model alias gemma4-e4b + bearer key — set in com.etzhayyim.kotoba launchd env (secrets uncommitted), session-independent. New operator invariant: never set KOTOBA_INFERENCE_URL to a LAN address under launchd — use the loopback gateway. Parent pointer bumps c1d83789c + 89953d523. Depends on ADR-2605301625 + ADR-2605262130 + ADR-2605215000 + ADR-2605292100 + ADR-2605301030." :path "90-docs/adr/2605302356-kotoba-langgraph-llm-inference-live-verified-and-durable-murakumo-routing.md"}
