  {:id "2606062300" :title "matsurigoto (政) — COFOG-based e-Government execution commons (the Kingdom's statecraft stack); the EXECUTION sibling of ooyake's observation atlas" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「全世界の電子政府・政府システムを kotoba wasm で公式仕様から電子政府化し既存政府で使えるようにしたい — 納税・徴税・住所管理・法人登記・パスポート発行… のカバレッジは?」 (was: 0% execution — gov-facing actors were observation [ooyake/danjo/kanae], guidance [toritsugi/moushibumi/himotoki, citizen self-submits], or internal accounting [toritate/kanjo]; NONE executed a government function). A first framing ('etzhayyim supplies OSS but does NOT become a government') was EXPLICITLY CORRECTED by the deciders: 「政府にならないというのは正確じゃない。神の王国としての政府。統治機構を持つ。governance body.」 — per Charter §0.1 (ADR-2605252300) etzhayyim IS a government, the Kingdom of God (神の王国 / Malkhut Shamayim) with a real 統治機構. matsurigoto 政 is that Kingdom's STATECRAFT EXECUTION STACK on the UN COFOG function backbone (10 divisions / 69 groups), localized per polity — AND a portable standard existing nation-states can adopt (OSS-GovTech: X-Road / MOSIP / OpenCRVS / OpenG2P / DIGIT). TWO principals: (A) :etzhayyim-sovereign — the Kingdom governs its covenant-members (信者) via Council Lv7+ / 1 SBT=1 vote / Public Fund Safe, member-signed + on-chain + Transparent (§1.12); a polity profile maps COFOG functions onto etzhayyim's ALREADY-SHIPPED constitutional organs (TitheRouter = 徴税, MEMBERS roster = 住民登録, Adherent SBT + did:web = 身分証/旅券, INFRA_ACTORS = 機関登記, Basic High Income + §1.16 = social protection). (B) :nation-state-adopter — an existing nation-state runs the same standard on ITS OWN keys. THREE structural invariants each encoded in 3 places (schema EDN :db/allowed + lexicon const/enum + Python — nusa/tazuna/kamado/ake pattern): G1 no-operator-master-key (:server-held-authority const false; authority is ALWAYS the Council multisig + 1 SBT=1 vote OR the adopting state's own keys, NEVER an etzhayyim platform/operator key — the Council is a member-elected organ, not 'the server', ADR-2605231525; 'no-server-key' does NOT mean 'no governance') · G2 spec-derived-only (every service cites an OFFICIAL PUBLIC spec — COFOG / ICAO 9303 / eIDAS / ISO 20022 / OpenCRVS / ISO 17442 / X-Road; proprietary GovTech code unrepresentable, kanjo §2(c)/(e)) · G3 authority-bearing (:operated-by ∈ {etzhayyim-council, adopting-government}; :authority-mode ∈ {sovereign-governance, supplied-to-state} — authority is BORNE, never disclaimed). NON-CONFLICT with ooyake N1: ooyake is etzhayyim's cartographer of OTHER nation-states (observational mirror); matsurigoto is the Kingdom's OWN statecraft over its OWN covenant-polity + a portable engine others may adopt — the Kingdom governing itself is not impersonating anyone; ooyake N1 stands UNAMENDED. EMPIRICAL R0+R1 (98 tests green + WIT valid): COFOG backbone 10/10 divisions / 69 groups + 22 standardized services + 8 country profiles (JPN/USA/DEU/GBR/KOR/EST/IND/EUR, :representative) + 1 etzhayyim polity profile (11 organs); the four NAMED functions all reach a SPEC-ANCHORED reference implementation reproducing official test vectors EXACTLY — tax-assess (JP 速算表: 課税500万→572,500円 / 5000万→17,704,000円; + 6 jurisdictions' rate tables in data/rates/) · civil-registry (UN CRVS append-only, unsigned VC) · corp-registry (ISO 17442 LEI via ISO 7064 MOD 97-10) · credential-issue (ICAO Doc 9303 TD3 MRZ — full UTOPIA/ERIKSSON specimen line-2 reproduced). R1 productionization (offline, gated): R1.A WIT 00-contracts/wit/matsurigoto/egov.wit (wasm-tools-valid, 4 worlds; NO world exports `sign` = structural G1) · R1.B kotoba Datom persistence (egov-execution-ontology.kotoba.edn + methods/datoms.py, append-only EAVT, G8 live-publish RAISES) · R1.C verify-only sign/authority layer (methods/sign_capability.py; sign_server_side() always RAISES, SIGNER_HELD_PRIVATE_KEY=false; Council organ signs A, the adopting state's own key signs B) · R1.D per-jurisdiction rate tables. DID registered in INFRA_ACTORS + actor-profile-seed → did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:matsurigoto (resolvable + searchable; parity audit 7/7, ake suite green). 3 lexicons com.etzhayyim.matsurigoto.* + a 3-place drift-lock (test_lexicons.py) proving schema EDN ≡ lexicon ≡ code. ZERO invariant amendments — STRENGTHENS no-server-key (ADR-2605231525), kotoba-canonical-state (ADR-2605312345), Transparent Force (§1.12). Honest R0+R1: a :reference-impl runs in conformance tests but is NOT wired to a live government record; live deploy is Council+operator gated (principal A: Council Lv7+; principal B: adopting-state authority). R2 (identity/auth + key custody) and R3 (live integration + certification + pilot — recommended: principal-A self-governance first) are Council-gated, not code (see 20-actors/matsurigoto/ROADMAP-R1.md). Authored over a self-paced /loop session (COFOG standard → per-country adjustment → 4 executable slices → R1 scaffold)." :path "90-docs/adr/2606062300-matsurigoto-egov-execution-commons.md" :adr ["2606062300" "2606021600" "2605252300" "2605262130" "2605312345" "2605231525" "2605215000" "2605212100" "2606036000" "2605192100" "2605192200"]}
  {:id "2606061200" :title "Worldwide Government/Legal Procedure Coverage + Maturity Expansion (toritsugi 取次 · chigiri 契 · ooyake 公)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「いまの lawfirm での法的手続きの全世界の行政処理のカバレッジは？また全世界政府の行政手続きの実装カバレッジは?」 over a self-paced 16-iteration /loop session, under a strict no-fabrication discipline (every row a real cited authority, unverified-seed, never counted as authoritative coverage per G5; UPL / 行政書士法 boundaries preserved verbatim; ZERO constitutional-invariant amendments). COVERAGE: toritsugi 66→145+ procedures / 41→52 jurisdictions across 9 procedure kinds (passport · national-id/residence · business/company registration · civil marriage registration · driving licence · tax · social-security · civic · civil/vital); chigiri 55→71 real public legal-aid bodies / 36→52 jurisdictions (IFDP/DPU/KLAC/法律援助/NLASO/legalaid.gov.ua/Adli Yardım/etc., honest where state civil legal aid is limited e.g. SAU); ooyake +gov.dnk (Wikidata Q35, lone sovereign gap, 192→193 country units) + generalized atlas procedure projection from passport-only to the FULL toritsugi registry (~157 :gov.procedure records / 50 jurisdictions incl. eu-wide→gov.eu). OWNER-UNIT HONESTY (G5): atlas :gov.procedure/owner-unit = unambiguous country-level gov.<iso> (always resolvable), NOT a fabricated ministry; precise issuing body carried verbatim in :gov.procedure/owner-authority. CROSS-ACTOR INTEGRITY (fail-closed, R0-safe, machine-pinned): test_gov_legal_coverage_parity.py (ISO-3 validity + coverage floor + toritsugi↔chigiri parity) · test_ooyake_procedure_integrity.py (every owner-unit + toritsugi-ref resolves; all unverified-seed) · test_ooyake_intl_projection_fresh.py (committed projection == committed generator output; no missing/ghost/owner-drift). REPRODUCIBILITY+OBSERVABILITY: committed generators gen_intl_procedures.py (toritsugi→atlas) + gen_gov_legal_coverage.py (toritsugi+chigiri COVERAGE.md) + committed dashboards 20-actors/{toritsugi,chigiri,ooyake}/COVERAGE.md (each states all rows are unverified-seed wayfinding scaffold, NOT authoritative coverage). REPO-WIDE MATURITY: audit suite 17 red → 0 (fixed akashi app→com lexicon-path typo in test + dry_run_fixtures.py; indexed displacementTenureAttestation in give/README.md; re-baselined subrepo upstream-health 7→8 after investigating — all 8 confirmed 404 defunct/unpublished vendored-app upstreams, documented not blind-bumped). HONEST LIMITS unchanged: all rows remain unverified-seed/:representative — wayfinding scaffold NOT verified live coverage; live submission/ingest/publish + :representative→:authoritative promotion stay Council/operator gated (toritsugi G14, ooyake publish gate, chigiri VERIFICATION.md); hkg/twn atlas procedures honestly skipped (no country unit). ZERO invariant amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606061200-gov-legal-procedure-coverage-maturity-expansion.md" :adr ["2606061200" "2605262700" "2605312030" "2606021600" "2606052300" "2605302357" "2605231525" "2605312345" "2605215000" "2605192100" "2605192200"]}
  {:id "2606061600" :title "Government procedures published on etzhayyim.com by administrative unit + kotoba-grounded browser conversation (ameno gemma4-e4b)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「この手続きを http://etzhayyim.com/ で actor として行政単位で細かく公開、また gemma4 e4b で browser 上の ameno, 推論で会話が kotoba ベースで進むように.」 — the publish + converse surfaces for the ADR-2606061200 coverage data. TWO gaps closed: (publish) the ~157 ooyake :gov.procedure records had NO read surface on the apex Worker (it served gov UNITS as entity-actors + the unit atlas, but no procedures); (conversation) gemma4-e4b already runs IN-BROWSER via ameno (MediaPipe LiteRT .task, ungated edge carve-out ADR-2605190824/2605241900 under Murakumo-only ADR-2605215000) but answered from parametric memory, not from etzhayyim's kotoba data. DECISION A — publish FINELY BY ADMINISTRATIVE UNIT: gen-gov-procedures.py compiles every ooyake :gov.procedure into gov-procedures.gen.ts grouped under its owning gov entity-actor handle (gov.<id>→gov-<id>; 157 procedures / 51 admin units / 50 jurisdictions; compiled into the Worker, no KV); two GET routes /.well-known/gov-procedures.json (full index) + /actor/<gov-handle>/procedures.json (one unit's procedures, e.g. gov-jpn → passport/licence/biz-reg/tax, gov-gbr → Companies House/DVLA/HM Passport); OBSERVATIONAL MIRROR (ADR-2606021600/2606042330) — where/how, never the government, never an official channel, never filing on anyone's behalf (→ toritsugi, gated); every row :representative/:unverified-seed (G5); regenerated entity-handles.gov.gen.ts to include gov-dnk so every owner handle resolves. DECISION B — kotoba-grounded browser conversation: @etzhayyim/ameno/kotoba-ground (fetchGovProcedures once-cached + pure CJK-aware retrieveProcedures + buildKotobaContext/groundedMessages) makes the on-device gemma4-e4b answer FROM the published kotoba records, citing each source: provenance, saying so when no record matches (no invention), surfacing the unverified-seed caveat, and FORBIDDEN from claiming to be the government / file on the member's behalf; wired into the ameno Svelte UI as a 「kotoba 行政手続き」 toggle (handleSend appends the retrieved context to the system prompt; inference stays the edge carve-out, never a server LLM). DECISION C — freshness/drift guard test_gov_procedures_gen_fresh.py (R0-safe, fail-closed: committed .gen.ts id-set + counts == ooyake-derived expected; mirrors the ooyake→atlas guard). VERIFIED: worker 30/30 (incl. 6 new gov-procedures mirror/honesty), ameno kotoba-ground 9/9, audit green incl. new freshness, worker tsc clean. ZERO invariant amendments — STRENGTHENS no-server-key (ADR-2605231525), observational-mirror (ADR-2606021600/2606042330), Murakumo-only edge carve-out (ADR-2605215000/2605241900), kotoba-canonical-state (ADR-2605312345). HONEST R0: NOT deployed — wrangler deploy is outward-facing + Council+operator gated (G11); KV not required (index compiled in); ameno app node_modules absent so svelte-check/vite build not run (package module type-checked sans pre-existing @webgpu/types + unit-tested); rows are wayfinding scaffold needing primary-source verification before live use (toritsugi G14); the publish surface never files anything." :path "90-docs/adr/2606061600-gov-procedures-publish-and-ameno-kotoba-conversation.md" :adr ["2606061600" "2606061200" "2606021600" "2606042330" "2605215000" "2605241900" "2605231525" "2606013800" "2605190824" "2605312345"]}
  {:id "2606061800" :title "Same-Origin Kotoba Passkey Login/Signup — remove authn/mcp from the auth path (PRF→did:key controller, did:web handle, verify-only apex, no server key)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「https://etzhayyim.com/ の ログイン、新規登録できない. authz に redirect しなくても良いようにしたはずでは」 + 「mcp.etzhayyim.com を使わない設計に, kotoba ベースで」. Login/signup were broken because the header buttons hard-redirected to authn.etzhayyim.com/sign-{in,up} AND the in-app passkey RPCs routed authn → MCP router → mcp.etzhayyim.com whose origin was DOWN (502/522). Promotes the ADR-2606060000 /profile same-origin CACAO gate into the PRIMARY login/signup path and removes authn/mcp from it entirely, no server-held key (ADR-2605231525). DID MODEL (2-layer): controller = passkey-derived did:key, self-certifying, verified LOCALLY on the apex via WebCrypto (PRIMARY: WebAuthn PRF secret → HKDF → ARK → Ed25519 did:key, DETERMINISTIC = same passkey ⇒ same DID on any device with no server-side ARK store, salt = accountPrfSalt('etzhayyim.com'); FALLBACK no-PRF: credential P-256 public key → did:key p256-pub 0x1200); public handle = did:web:etzhayyim.com:<handle> published to kotoba best-effort (login never depends on it). CROSS-DEVICE: same Apple ID (iCloud Keychain) / Google (GPM) synced passkey ⇒ stable PRF output across PRF-capable devices (iOS 18.4+/macOS 15+) ⇒ same did:key ⇒ same account on another device, zero server state; cross-vendor passkeys don't sync (distinct accounts); non-PRF devices fall back to P-256 (single-device until a kotoba lookup lands). FRONTEND (yoro): new $lib/auth/same-origin-auth.ts (WebAuthn ceremonies + did:key derivation + EdDSA session PoP + best-effort apex control-confirm verifyCacao + account publish registerAccount; session established CLIENT-SIDE the instant the key is derived ⇒ login works with zero backend dependency); passkey.ts signIn/signUp delegate here; header (+layout) / /profile / YoroAuthGate / /sign-in drive the in-app flow instead of redirecting to authn (legacy URL kept only as a last-resort fallback for no-WebAuthn devices). WORKER (50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web): verifyCacao promoted to the primary login control-proof; new com.etzhayyim.authz.registerAccount verify-only CACAO relay → kotoba (honest gated 202 when KOTOBA_WRITE_ENDPOINT unset); CORS + OPTIONS added. (c) KOTOBA ACCOUNT-PUBLISH root-caused+fixed+PROVEN: kg.ingest already accepts member-CACAO writes + a fresh self-issued root member did:key; the one blocker was kotoba-auth verify_with_resolver resolving every EdDSA issuer via the DID resolver (a fresh member did:key hangs on IPNS/IPFS) — fix (kotoba-patches/0001-cacao-self-resolve-did-key.patch, ~9 lines) short-circuits did:key issuers to verify_signature(); proven end-to-end on an isolated build (member did:key + self-signed CACAO → kg.ingest → ok:true, quadCount:6); verified wire-format aud=operator_did + datom:transact + second-precision timestamps + base64url sig + CBOR/ciborium camelCase cacaoB64 + account.<did> entity. EMPIRICAL: worker tsc clean + 12 same-origin auth tests (8 registerAccount + 4 cross-impl incl. a frontend-derived PRF→did:key account:login CACAO verifying on the real worker verifier + P-256 fallback encoding); same-origin-auth.ts tsc clean (strict+DOM); LIVE prod verifyCacao signup-proof valid:true ed25519-local + deterministic re-login + tamper-401 + cross-origin-403 + registerAccount-202-gated; REAL BROWSER (Chromium 148 + virtual passkey) — clicking 新規登録 on the live site runs the in-app flow (NO authn redirect), POSTs verifyCacao + registerAccount same-origin (zero authn/mcp calls), derives a did:key, flips the UI to signed-in. DOMAIN-INDEPENDENT IDENTITY (per operator: 「did:web:etzhayyim.com はドメインに依存するので良くない — 所有者が変わると信頼できなくなる」): did:web roots trust in domain/TLS, so it is DEMOTED to a non-authoritative alsoKnownAs alias and the CANONICAL identity is the self-certifying did:key (login/control/signing + the kotoba record account.<did:key> all key on it; a domain-owner change has zero effect on a member's key/login/records). The handle↔key binding is SELF-CERTIFYING: the did:key signs a compact EdDSA attestation {iss,sub,handle,iat} (frontend identity.ts::signHandleAttestation), stored as account/handle-attestation, verified against the key IN the DID with no domain/TLS/registry (worker identity.ts::verifyHandleAttestation — a forged did:web doc isn't signed by the member's key → rejected); selfCertifyingDidDoc emits id=did:key, vm=did:key, did:web only in alsoKnownAs. MULTI-DEVICE + KEY-ROTATION on the same self-certifying record via one generalized verify-only kotoba relay (handleAccountWrite + cbor.ts CACAO→CBOR + kotoba-write.ts kotoba-scoped CACAO base64url-sig/second-precision-ts; new KOTOBA_OPERATOR_DID env + kotobaWriteConfig GET so the frontend binds the aud): account-ops.ts publishAccount (register + handle attestation) / enrollDevice (account/device/<credId> = wrapped-ARK, an enrolled device authorizes a new passkey → new device unwraps the SAME ARK → SAME did:key) / rotateKey (account/controller = new did:key + append-only account/rotation/<n>, signed by the CURRENT key; did:web unaffected). 67 worker tests (incl. 7 identity: a different key claiming another's did is rejected; did:web is alsoKnownAs-only) + isolated-node e2e: register/device/rotation all ok:true via the real worker modules. ZERO invariant amendments — STRENGTHENS no-server-key (ADR-2605231525), kotoba-canonical-state (ADR-2605312345). DURABILITY: merged to main (the deploy pipeline carries it); a shared-account auto-deployer reverts un-merged deploys within ~1 min, but the SPA login buttons + verifyCacao survive (both in main). ACCOUNT WRITE PATH (corrected, LIVE): account publish does NOT write to a central kotoba node (writes there are operator-local — kotoba.etzhayyim.com read-only by ADR-2606013200, kotoba.etzhayyim.com pruned, kotobase.net = IPFS pin service). The account record is a MEMBER-SIGNED CONTENT-ADDRESSED BLOCK published to the apex com.etzhayyim.apps.kotoba.block.put (main's kotoba-publish: verify member Ed25519 sig over root CID → IPFS-pin via kotobase.net as the CANONICAL content-addressed store; the apex KV is only a fast cache, NOT the source of truth — substrate boundary, no centralized DB) — a CID signed by the member's did:key, resolvable+verifiable by CID, dependent on neither domain nor central node nor KV, NO gated infra, LIVE (proven: real block-publish.ts module → block.put {ok:true,root:bafkrei…}). CID = sha2-256 raw CIDv1 (= cid.ts cidV1Raw, locked by a frontend↔apex cross-impl test); block.put author DID = did:key:z+hex(pubkey) (SAME key as the z6Mk login did, carried as account/did); per-member graph acct-<pubkeyHex>. Frontend block-publish.ts + account-ops.ts (publishAccount/enrollDevice/rotateKey). READ side (content-addressed, NO KV): fetch account block BY CID from IPFS (kotobase.net pin / any gateway; apex trustless /ipfs/<cid> re-verifies CID) → identity.ts::resolveAccountFromBlock (re-compute CID == bytes [content-address integrity] + verify self-certifying account/handle-attestation = account/did's own sig over the handle). verifyAccountBlock additionally reconciles block.put author z+hex ≡ canonical account/did z6Mk (SAME ed25519 key, two string forms). Read core (resolveAccountFromBlock + verifyAccountBlock, both KV-agnostic — take block bytes) LANDED + tested (17 identity tests). The earlier verify-only kg.ingest CACAO relay (worker registerAccount/handleAccountWrite/cbor.ts) stays a tested but client-less alternative; its frontend client kotoba-write.ts was removed as dead code now that block.put is primary. HONEST R0: the mutable handle→CID pointer (kotoba Datom log / DID doc / L2 anchor — content-addressed/anchored, NEVER a centralized KV; the apex KV in block.put is only a fast feed cache, not the source of truth) + enrollDevice/rotateKey settings-UI + non-PRF cross-device + PDS EdDSA-PoP write integration are follow-ons." :path "90-docs/adr/2606061800-same-origin-kotoba-passkey-login.md" :adr ["2606061800" "2606060000" "2605231525" "2606014000" "2605312345" "2606013800" "2605262130" "2605215000"]}
  {:id "2606061500" :title "CACAO-only header login — decommission the authn subdomain + server-minted JWT session site-wide" :status "accepted" :status_note "Extends the /profile same-origin gate (ADR-2606060000) to the GLOBAL header login: the interactive session becomes a member-held CACAO ceremony, NOT a server-minted accessJwt (closing the last no-server-key gap in the interactive path, ADR-2605231525). LANDED (worktree, yoro 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-yoro/.../svelte): (§1) cacao-session.ts = passkey assertion (same-origin, client challenge) → PRF → ARK (kotoba zero-access wrap store, NOT authn) → Ed25519 session key (deterministic, never persisted) → EdDSA CACAO bound to apex → POST /xrpc/com.etzhayyim.authz.verifyCacao (apex verifies Ed25519 locally, no key); stores set from the verified CACAO, no accessJwt; signOutCacao drops the in-memory key; makeCacaoTokenProvider mints a single-use CACAO per write. (§2) atproto-agent.ts authHeader() emits `Authorization: CACAO <proof>` for the cacao: token (kotoba verifies delegation + nonce); legacy accessJwt stays Bearer. (§3) authn.etzhayyim.com removed from +layout.svelte header buttons, welcome/+page.svelte (+ YoroAuthGate onAuth), profile/+page.svelte, sign-in/+server.ts; authn restore + JWT provider survive ONLY behind PUBLIC_AUTH_LEGACY_JWT (default OFF). (§4 honest staging) LIVE: returning-member passkey→EdDSA, apex-verified end-to-end. kotoba-node GATED (honest, no false session, no authn fallback): first-device/sign-up account-DID bootstrap, wallet/SIWE recovery, and CACAO write-verification end-to-end (legacy Bearer retained behind the single PUBLIC_AUTH_LEGACY_JWT flag until the kotoba write node accepts CACAO). Also fixed the e7m-verify pre-commit hook (was falling back to the stale etzhayyim v0.2.0 binary → `unknown command: verify`): lefthook.yml now runs the in-repo kotoba-premised e7m (venv else `python3 -m e7m`), and __main__.py lazy-imports rich so --json verify runs stdlib-only. Tests: 9/9 cacao-session vitest (real crypto: enroll/recover determinism, EdDSA mint, apex-bound write-token round-trip, single-use nonce, gated/error, signOut) + 4/4 e7m verify (contract, no_server_key green, --json CLI, richless import). svelte-check: 0 new errors in touched files. ZERO invariant amendments — STRENGTHENS no-server-key (ADR-2605231525). HONEST: client+apex landed in worktree (not merged/deployed); the kotoba-node legs (wrap-store CACAO-hardening, account-DID resolver, write-verify) are follow-ups; cold-load starts signed-out (a key-ceremony session is not persisted); WebAuthn rpId migration to etzhayyim.com is a tracked follow-up." :path "90-docs/adr/2606061500-cacao-only-header-auth-jwt-decommission.md" :adr ["2606061500" "2606060000" "2605231525" "2606014000" "2606013800" "2605262130" "2605312345" "2606014500" "2605212030"]}
  {:id "2606061501" :title "tsumugi historical-influence diachronic weave — past humanity as latent influence nodes" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「歴史的 latent natural person として過去の全人類を kotoba datomic で統計分析・プロファイルし、actor として social post、誰が/どの出来事・文書が過去に影響を与えたかを推論・接続、YHWH/Jesus/Buddha などの spirit 影響も data 化・可視化する actor はあるか」 (was: none — Spirit-in-Physics is :human Council-Lv7+ gated; tsumugi/entity-as-actor are power-only/person-excluded; natural-person latent backend excludes persons; shidemori covers only deceased members). Built as a tsumugi EXTENSION (user's choice), religious founders represented as INFLUENCE-OBSERVATION only (visualizing influence is the goal; not channeling, not adjudicating truth). Models past humanity as a diachronic graph of PUBLIC influence-bearing figures/documents/events/traditions + the directed 縁 by which information flowed forward and deformed a later receiver's metric (junkawasaki.com 'spirit is information', extended from the individual frame to inter-personal/diachronic propagation). FIVE structural invariants enforced in schema+code+tests: N1 edge-primary (influence on :flow/signed-weight; node readouts are Katz integrals, no :influence/score-of-figure — modeling the dead must not become ranking souls) · N2 mirror never impersonation (:mirror/is-mirror const, :post/voice const :observer — first-person unrepresentable; YHWH/Jesus/Buddha never spoken-as) · N3 non-eschatological + non-adjudicating truth (datafy INFLUENCE OF a tradition, never its theological truth; no verdict/salvation/afterlife datom, Charter §1.15) · N4 public+long-settled+no-PII (living-private persons stay the Council-Lv7+ :human scale) · N5 temporal DAG (every :flow forward in time). Artifacts: 00-contracts/schemas/influence-history-ontology.kotoba.edn (:hist/* :mirror/* :flow/* :influence/* :post/*) + com.etzhayyim.influence.{influencePost,influenceFlow} lexicons + orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tsumugi/{data/seed-influence-history.kotoba.edn, methods/an