  {:id "2606101430" :title "infra-robotics R1 device-in-the-loop — the REAL open-ot WASM cells close the microgrid loop" :status "accepted" :status_note "Executes ADR-2606091800 follow-up #3 per founder direction 「device in the loop を進めてok」 (Council gate exercised as PR merge, ibuki ADR-2606101200 precedent). Device tier = the byte-for-byte deployment artefacts droop_p_f.wasm (2.8 KB) + anti_islanding_rocof.wasm (4.3 KB) — open-ot IEC 61499 Rust BFBs at wasm32-unknown-unknown (the WAMR/Cortex-M7 artefact class) — executed under Wasmtime by the NEW device-loop-host (60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-ot/risk1/, gate-a-rig sibling: LOAD/INIT/TICK stdin line protocol, gate-a memory map, layouts from the existing codegen-cell-types pack/unpack) and driven tick-by-tick by the SAME MicrogridPlant scenarios the Python twin passes (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kuni-umi/robotics/device_loop.py -> committed golden device_loop_trace.json; verification needs no cargo/wasmtime). TWO semantic findings test-pinned: DROOP_P_F is INCREMENTAL (p_setpoint = clamp(current_p + delta); feeding the last command back integrates — observed >180 kW divergence; correct usage feeds the FIXED dispatch base) and unit conventions differ (device per-unit vs twin absolute droop; exact equivalence R_twin = f_nom*R_dev/P_rated, derived not tuned). GOLDEN RESULT: 50.0 Hz restored on normal/load-shed with no trip; the REAL guard LATCHES on the islanding-scale step; per-step twin parity 0.0001 kW (= µkW integer quantisation); device verdicts match twin verdicts on all scenarios. Commissioning gains acceptance_tier python-twin -> device-wasm (consistent evidence only TIGHTENS; inconsistent demotes to punch-list); CommissioningCell commission_test reads the golden. Fixed in passing: validate-cell-abi.py ALLOWED_WIRE drift (test_real_repo_content_passes was red on main -> green, 26 tests). kuni-umi/robotics 36->48 tests (incl. 2 live e2e that execute the wasm when the host is built). Invariants unchanged: offl