  {:id "2606042330" :title "entity-as-actor — society-scale social mirror graph" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「/search に actor が少ししか出ない。全世界の行政・法人・サイトの actor は?」. Generalizes the UNSPSC 18,342-agent precedent so 1 public/power entity = 1 KEYLESS mirror-actor: every entity a KG actor datafies (ooyake gov-units / kabuto+tsumugi+kanjo companies / watatsuna cables+stations / watari craft) resolves did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:<ns>-<…> + profile, searchable on /search. Charter by construction: G1 mirror-only (isMirror const, disclaimer, no impersonation) · G3 person-excluded (performerType ∈ {organization,system}) · G5 no-server-key (verificationMethod []) · G8 outward-gated (live firehose publish + planet-scale ingest Council+operator gated). LANDED + LIVE: 8,888 entity mirrors (gov 7,106 · corp 1,733 · cable 14 · station 22 · craft 13) via 5 generated entity-handles.<ns>.gen.ts; totalResolvableActors=27,247. searchActors + getSuggestions offset-cursor short-circuit (+ named/infra prepend to defeat the yoro kotoba-sw.js backfill that capped /search at 62) → /search shows 8,905 + paginates. Count = kotoba-kqe MaterializedView (actor-count-mv.kotoba.edn; MvRegistry incremental, O(1) read). +43 named Tier-B actors registered from manifests (tier-b-actors.gen.ts → INFRA_ACTORS). ZERO Charter amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606042330-entity-as-actor-society-wide-social-mirror-graph.md" :adr ["2606042330" "2606013800" "2605241800" "2605231525" "2605231902" "2605262130" "2605312345" "2605215000" "2605192200" "2605171300" "2606021600" "2606022000" "2606032000" "2606011800" "2606012600" "2606041827"]}
  {:id "2606065501" :title "etzhayyim.com browser-only kotoba social feed — browser read/write + member-signed block publish (no query node)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Fixes 「https://etzhayyim.com/ に post が表示されない」then extends to writes + propagation. Feed/profile READS + post/reply/like/repost WRITES run in the browser kotoba-wasm node; reads hydrate from CID-verified IPFS blocks (x-kotoba-src=blocks, no query node); writes are member-signed (ed25519 did:key, no-server-key). The apex VERIFIES signatures (never signs), stores delta blocks (block.has), advances the head under atomic CAS with client rebase/CRDT-merge on 409 (no lost update), per-DID token-bucket rate limit, and a suppressable AES-GCM-encrypted IP attestation (never in immutable blocks; GDPR/APPI + charter PII). passkey-PRF setIdentity hook binds the signing key. LIVE-verified headless: feed renders from blocks; writes attributed to did:key + appear instantly; concurrent A/B publish both survive; delta 2/7 blocks; ipEncrypted=true. Tests: apex crypto + publish-handler integration (in-memory KV) + browser feed/merge units. Lexicons com.etzhayyim.apps.kotoba.{block.put,block.has,root,stats}. RESOLVED (landed on main): authoritative head is the charter-aligned KV check-and-set (no operated Durable Object — DO removed per ADR-2605262130/2605312345); per-DID rate-limit + stats ported to best-effort KV. The browser SW feed read-path retains main's evolved inline implementation — the kotoba-feed.js extraction was deferred (superseded by main's SW evolution). ZERO Charter amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606065501-kotoba-browser-only-social-feed.md" :adr ["2606065500" "2605312345" "2605262130" "2605231525" "2606013800" "2606014600" "2605215000" "2606041822"]}
  {:id "2606066000" :title "content-addressed feed head — kotoba IPNS commit-head resolves the 2606065500 open question (no Durable Object)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Closes the ADR-2606065500 OPEN head-primitive question. Decision: the authoritative published head is the kotoba IPNS commit-head — a member-signed IpnsRecord (Ed25519 over a ciborium-CBOR payload, base58btc multibase, monotonic sequence = CAS, DID-derived name via did_document_ipns_name) whose value = the CID of a content-addressed DistributedDatomCommit (parent-linked DAG + the 5 covering ProllyTree index roots eavt/aevt/avet/vaet/tea). That IS 'IPNS + signed DAG record' and is already implemented in the canonical engine (ADR-2606013600: kotoba-ipfs::IpnsRecord + kotoba-datomic::DistributedDatomCommit), so NO parallel signed-head format is built in the apex Worker (forbidden by ADR-2605262130). The Durable Object is rejected (operated trusted server-state, violates 2605262130/2605312345/2605231525) and the apex KV kroot: is demoted to a non-authoritative cache/relay of the self-verifying record: readers verify the member signature so the apex is never trusted (no-server-key holds); head latency is not the hot path (read once per session, then immutable blocks hydrate the feed). Discovery layers DID -> IPNS -> commit DAG; Kubo IPNS republish for global discovery is operator-gated/additive. HONEST implementation gap (the follow-on code): kotoba-wasm today exposes only commitSigned -> {root, did, sig}, NOT a full IpnsRecord nor a commit-with-parent — closing it needs an upstream kotoba-wasm binding emitting a member-signed IpnsRecord via kotoba's own IpnsRecord::sign_ed25519 (byte-identical interop) + an apex change to store/serve the record, both cross-verified before authority switches. ZERO Charter amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606066000-kotoba-content-addressed-head-ipns-commit.md" :adr ["2606066000" "2606065500" "2606013600" "2605312345" "2605262130" "2605231525"]}
  {:id "2606070030" :title "session close — karakuri browser-use + kotoba content-addressed feed head (IPNS commit-head)" :status "active" :status_note "Documentation-only closure of the 2026-06-06→07 session (authoritative designs = ADR-2606039200 karakuri + ADR-2606066000 content-addressed head). Thread A (karakuri #1196): browser-use = the T2 engine; two-axis service stance (tos-stance official-API→T1, t2-stance browser-automation→T2); Google+Facebook = api-ok yet browser-prohibited → routed to T1, T2 refused; detection-evasion unrepresentable; all 5 cells coded + NL planner (Murakumo G4) + T3 export (G9) + live-exec membrane (refuse-by-default) + kotoba Datom audit (G7, args keys-only); methods 87/cells 31 green; R0 no live exec. Thread B (content-addressed head): kotoba #47 wasm-safe kotoba-ipns-record + commitHeadSigned producer, #48 kotoba-store native-only so kotoba-wasm links wasm32 (dropped reqwest→tokio/net→mio leak), #49 verifyIpnsRecord reader + JSON round-trip interop test; monorepo #1203 ADR, #1205 apex stores/serves the signed IpnsRecord as a non-authoritative relay (8/8 tests), #1208 submodule bump → 9157ea3e. Housekeeping: #1191 CLOSED not-merged (re-introduced the removed KotobaRoot Durable Object) → DO-independent parts salvaged in #1198. REMAINING (operator-coordinated, browser-E2E + deploy): rebuild the 3 kotoba_wasm bundles, route the yoro pure-TS write path through commitHeadSigned + gate reads on verifyIpnsRecord, flip block.put CAS to record sequence, wrangler deploy. ZERO Charter amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606070030-session-close-karakuri-browseruse-and-kotoba-content-addressed-head.md" :adr ["2606070030" "2606039200" "2606066000" "2606065500" "2606013600" "2605262130" "2605231525"]}
  {:id "2606064500" :title "maps — kotoba-native substrate migration (vertex_spatial → Datom log, H3-cell AVET spatial index)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Answers 「maps.etzhayyim.com を kotoba に refactor」. maps was the monorepo's largest RisingWave/Hyperdrive dependency (172 XRPC commands over vertex_spatial + 5 bulk-ingest dumpers psycopg2-INSERTing) — a substrate-boundary violation (ADR-2605262130). Generalizes watari's kotoba-native rewrite (moving-craft, ADR-2606041827) to the WHOLE static-feature substrate. SPATIAL INDEX = H3-cell-as-Datom + AVET (user-selected): every feature stores its owning H3 cell at each queryable res (:feature.cell/r2..r12), so the getChunk <50ms hot-path is a per-cell AVET probe AVET(:feature.cell/r{lod}, cell)→subjects — O(cells), not a bbox scan. Ontologies maps-spatial-ontology.kotoba.edn (:feature/* + :feature.rel/* VAET + :geo.alias/* + :feature/name-token search index) + maps-transit-ontology.kotoba.edn (:transit.trip/* + :transit.stop-time/*). Leverage point = one TS adapter maps-ui/src/kotoba-spatial.ts (queryByCells AVET read · stampCells · ingestFeatures no-server-key); cmdGetChunk rewired kotoba-first, fail-open to RisingWave (additive/reversible until R3). LANDED (9 PRs #1163→#1183 merged to main): R0 foundation + R1 offline proof (AVET round-trip + HTTP-loop dry-run vs a stdlib kotoba stand-in); R2 bulk-dumper write path (ETZHAYYIM_SUBSTRATE_MODE=kotoba on the shared substrate seam → all 6 Tier-1 feature dumpers; GTFS trip/stop_time aux → :transit.*; label-map + name-token tokenizer parity test-asserted across both write paths); the kotoba-native read QUARTET as offline-verified Python references (chunk=getChunk · transit=nextDeparturesAtStop/tripsOnRoute · search=searchPlaces token-index · reverse=reverseGeocode cell-ring+haversine) + a 4-read integration test + verify.py R1 readiness gate (exit 0 iff all four reads return). 68 Python tests green (real-H3 under a venv). ADVERSARIAL REVIEW on #1163 caught + fixed 7 real bugs (label-casing → 0 results, empty-array fail-open, geometry/props clobber, lod-ladder, gate-test tautology, stamp-method mismatch). ZERO invariant amendments — STRENGTHENS kotoba-canonical-state (ADR-2605312345) + no-server-key (ADR-2605231525). HONEST: substrate-level still R0/R1-offline — NO live KOTOBA_ENDPOINT for maps, NO vertex_spatial backfill, RisingWave/Hyperdrive still serving via fail-open; the live R1 cut-over (wire endpoint + backfill + flip getChunk + <50ms parity) + remaining TS read wiring (tileGeoJson/searchPlaces/reverseGeocode/nextDeparturesAtStop) + R3 (delete Hyperdrive) are Council+operator-gated follow-ons. 3D Earth coverage itself unchanged (Tokyo-anchored walker) — swaps what stores features, not how much Earth is loaded." :path "90-docs/adr/2606064500-maps-kotoba-native-substrate-migration.md" :adr ["2606064500" "2606041827" "2605262130" "2605312345" "2605215000" "2605231525" "2605241500" "2605192200" "2604271800" "2604280900" "2605011500" "2605215100" "2605312200" "2606011500"]}
  {:id "2606061900" :title "kawaraban (瓦版) — news medium (real-media mirror + actor-to-actor wire; the charter-clean inverse of a news app)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Answers 「https://etzhayyim.com/apps の news actor を kotoba wasm ベースで設計, murakumo fleet で動くように。実際の news media の 面に合わせて, actor と actor をつなげる medium として」 (was: none — kataribe 語部 is etzhayyim's OWN press, a primary voice; nothing mirrored the world's news media or wired the first-party actors together as a medium). A naive news app is ad-funded (Charter-Rider §2) / engagement-optimized (Charter §1.13) / reader-surveilling / truth-adjudicating (ake/danjo boundary) / content-republishing — ALL prohibited, so kawaraban is its charter-clean inverse (okaimono/mitooshi/kamado pattern): a public-square MIRROR + connective MEDIUM, kotoba-wasm-native, on the Murakumo fleet. TWO faces over one Datom log: (1) MIRROR the world's real news media (outlets · 面/sections 一面/政治/経済/国際/社会/文化/科学/スポーツ · headlines · links) into the kotoba Datom log as an append-only as-of trail — each mirror = headline + canonical link + bounded fair-use excerpt + outlet (LINKS OUT, never the body, never a verdict); (2) MEDIUM the connective wire BETWEEN actors — each first-party actor's Datom as-of events project into the matching 面 as :article/kind :actor-event (feed-post membrane reuse, ADR-2605231902), every article carries :news.mention edges → the article×mention×面 graph IS the actor-to-actor wire (danjo finds → kawaraban carries → kanae renders; a chokepoint story links watari+watatsuna+mitooshi in one 国際 面; empirically watari—4—watatsuna). ELEVEN structural gates, each enforced in 3 places (schema :db/allowed/enum + lexicon const/enum + Python ValueError — nusa/tazuna/kamado/mitooshi/ake pattern): G1 mirror-not-adjudicator (:news.article/verdict + :truth-rating :db/allowed [false]; ake/danjo own truth) · G2 no-ads/no-engagement-rank (:news.rank/signal excludes :paid-placement/:sponsored/:engagement/:dwell-time; Charter §1.13 + Rider §2) · G3 no-reader-surveillance (no :reader entity; :article/personalized-for :db/allowed [false]; the 面 is identical for all) · G4 copyright/link-out (:article/full-text :db/allowed [false]; public facing pages only — paywall/terminal excluded, kanjo §2(c)) · G5 sourcing-honest · G6 Murakumo-only · G7 no-server-key (:server-held-key const false) · G8 outward-gated (live ingest/publish Council Lv6+ + operator) · G9 mirror-not-impersonation (:article/speak-as :db/allowed [false]; ADR-2606042330) · G10 非終末論 (:news.issue/final :db/allowed [false]) · G11 connective-by-construction (every article :mirror or :actor-event; :original unrepresentable — a medium, not a source). New ontology news-medium-ontology.kotoba.edn + 6 lex com.etzhayyim.kawaraban.* (+ canonical 00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/kawaraban/*.json) + 5 cells (coded state machines; .solve() RuntimeError R0) + methods/route.py (the medium: actor→面 wire table + article×mention×面 co-mention graph + G1/G4/G9/G11 validate-by-refusal) + analyze.py (edition composer — G2 public-good ranking only; emits out/edition.md + derived :news.medium.link/* edges) + ingest.py (offline outlet normalizer; refuses full-body/paywall/verdict; --live G8-gated) + wasm/wit/world.wit (kotoba-wasm WASI component) + Murakumo fleet placement (5 cells / 12-tribe) + :representative seed (7 outlets / 10 面 / 9 wires / 12 articles / 24 mentions). DID registered in INFRA_ACTORS → did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:kawaraban (surfaces on /apps, /actors, /search). 46 tests green (route 11 + analyze 7 + ingest 8 + cells 20; one-command run_tests.sh). Merged to main (PR #1172, all CI green: monorepo-health + docs-registry-freshness + docs-graph-jsonld-freshness + CodeQL). ZERO invariant amendments — STRENGTHENS no-server-key (ADR-2605231525), kotoba-canonical-state (ADR-2605312345), the feed-post membrane (ADR-2605231902), and the mirror invariant (ADR-2606042330). N1 not a fact-checker · N2 not ad/engagement-funded · N3 not personalized/surveilling · N4 not a content-republisher · N5 not an impersonator · N6 not a primary source (kataribe is). Honest R0: design + datafication + offline composition only; no live RSS/outlet ingest, no live publish (G8 — Council Lv6+ + operator); :representative seed (neutral illustrative headlines, not captured real articles)." :path "90-docs/adr/2606061900-kawaraban-news-medium-actor-r0.md" :adr ["2606061900" "2605263600" "2605231902" "2606042330" "2605215000" "2605231525" "2605312345" "2605262130" "2606014600" "2605192100" "2605192200"]}
  {:id "2606062101" :title "moyai 舫い — non-monetary inference reciprocity credit (give-to-get; reward kept, Basic High Income untouched)" :status "accepted" :status_note "LANDED on main 2026-06-06 via PR #1184 (merge 62e4c2c), 46 tests green; live mint/burn + external enrollment remain Council Lv6+ + operator gated. Answers 「推論に参加することによる報酬は残してほしい、ただし Basic High Income に影響を与えず、情報を得るには情報を生成する類のもの」. Keeps a REWARD for commons inference participation, charter-clean: a non-monetary, non-transferable, decaying RECIPROCITY credit (commons-use-right / 入会権), the carve-out to ADR-2606012100 G4 scoped strictly to commons-draw-rights. Five const locks (redeemableUsdMicros=0 / transferable=false / affectsBasicHighIncome=false / grantsGovernanceWeight=false / grantsBenefitOrStage=false) + decay + conservation. BHI firewall: unconditional subsistence inference floor = information-as-BHI; credit governs ONLY discretionary surplus under contention (congestion fair-share, not a paywall). Anti-fraud: honeypot + spot-check proof-of-contribution + dedupe + earn-rate cap + all-or-nothing slashing -> faking has no payoff (sybil structurally self-defeating). Lexicons com.etzhayyim.moyai.{contributionAttestation,drawReceipt}; reference impl 50-infra/etzhayyim-moyai-credit (46 tests green). Supersedes legacy RisingWave credits economy (bpmn/com/etzhayyim/credits/*, ameno vertex_credits_af_event). ZERO invariant amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606062101-moyai-inference-reciprocity-credit.md" :adr ["2606062100" "2606012100" "2605215000" "2605301020" "2605261000" "2605241900" "2605231525" "2605312345" "2605192345" "2605150600"]}
  {:id "2606061901" :title "suji 筋 — musculoskeletal posture-load biomechanics simulator" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「kami engine / kotoba で人体の骨・筋肉のシミュレーションを行い、ノートPCの姿勢が人体にどういった緊張・強張りを作るかを物理シミュレーション (Isaac Sim)」. New L4-Care actor — the PHYSICS-SIMULATION sibling of kizashi 兆 (which SENSES the body) and upstream of mitate (which DIAGNOSES); pipeline: kizashi senses → suji simulates loads → mitate diagnoses → iyashi treats. Sagittal articulated segment chain (de Leva/Winter anthropometry = the kami-genesis PlanarChain) → STATIC inverse dynamics (Featherstone RNEA gravity term) → per-joint moment + cervical compressive load (VALIDATED vs Hansraj 2014: neutral→1× … 60°→5× head weight, within 10%) → Hill-type muscle %MVC (緊張) → Rohmert sustained-isometric dose (強張り) over a work session. Compares laptop-on-lap (23.6 kgf neck) vs external-monitor-eye-level (8.1 kgf, −66%). NON-DIAGNOSTIC by construction (G1, 医師法 §17): every output is a mechanical quantity and no diagnosis/disease/prescription/treatment field is representable in schema, lexicon, OR the load_solve cell (the nusa/tazuna/kamado pattern); G3 self-referenced (strain_accumulate refuses population-ranking keys). kami-genesis / nv-compat Isaac-Sim wired via wit/kami-biomech.wit + bridge (gated backend, submodule unpopulated — the noroshi pattern). LANDED R0: 7 methods + 5 cells (load_solve + strain_accumulate coded, 3 scaffold) + 6 lexicons + kotoba schema/seed + analyze→Datom emitter (G9 drift-locked); 45 tests green; WIT valid. ZERO Charter amendments — strengthens the kizashi non-diagnostic/SaMD boundary, kotoba-canonical-state, no-server-key, Murakumo-only." :path "90-docs/adr/2606061901-suji-musculoskeletal-posture-load-biomechanics.md" :adr ["2606061900" "2605312700" "2605260100" "2605263000" "2605261000" "2605311500" "2605311800" "2606010030" "2606010600" "2605261800" "2606051600" "2605231525" "2605215000" "2605241900" "2605312345" "2605181100" "2606042330" "2605192100"]}
  {:id "2606066001" :title "系図 (keizu) — government power-relations knowledge graph (procurement · money · statements · committee composition)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「いまの政府関係の調達・お金・発言・人間関係を分析・公開する actor。お金の流れを公開情報からすべて追い、委員会の構成メンバーを分析して datomic 保持し social post する」. The 5th government-accountability sibling (danjo/kanae/tsumugi/tadori/ooyake), filling the gap none covers: the RELATION GRAPH of PUBLIC ROLES weaving 調達 + お金 + 発言 + 人間関係 + 委員会/審議会の構成員 into ONE kotoba Datom graph + dry-run social posts. Accountability MAP, never a target-list (G5); NON-adjudicating (G2, danjo discipline); edge-primary, no per-node power score (G4); public-role-only / no-doxxing (G1, :private-person unrepresentable); ≥2 public-source citations (G3); no-server-key member-signed posts (G7); outward-gated dry-run + cells .solve() raise (G8). Uniform validation across all 5 datom types (node/committee/rel/money/statement) + the social-post path; commercial-gov-intel deny-list (Charter Rider §2(e)/N5) enforced on every citation surface. Analyzer: committee cross-organ / cross-committee co-membership / money HHI by payee+payer / award-and-fund co-occurrence / revolving-door / cross-organ connectors / statement index / per-jurisdiction slice / as-of time-travel / referential integrity. Bidirectional kanae integration (bridge in / export out, round-trip). R1-ready public-source registry (12 global sources, all unverified-seed) with forge-proof registry-driven sourcing. LANDED R0 (+R1-ready): ontology government-relations-ontology.kotoba.edn + 4 lex com.etzhayyim.keizu.* + 5 cells + methods (weave/social/ingest/bridge/export/registry/analyze) + :representative global seed; 180 tests green (run_tests.sh); DID registered (tier-b-actors.gen.ts + actor-profile-seed). ZERO invariant amendments — strengthens non-adjudication/edge-primary/no-server-key/kotoba-canonical/mirror. Live ingest + posting Council Lv6+ + operator gated (Lv7+ for live publication)." :path "90-docs/adr/2606066001-keizu-government-relations-graph-tier-b-actor-r0.md" :adr ["2606066000" "2605301600" "2606011800" "2605302300" "2605301400" "2606021600" "2605312345" "2605262130" "2605231525" "2605215000" "2606042330" "2605192100" "2605192200"]}
  {:id "2606072201" :title "潮目 (shionome) — cross-asset capital-flow observatory (ingest · intel · analyze · dry-run social, NO trading) R0 + autonomous kotoba loop" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「株式・コモディティ・国際・暗号資産・不動産の価格変動から、どこからどこへ資金が流れているかを ingest / intel / analyze して social post する actor。トレードはしない。actor を kotoba で自律的に稼働するところまで」. A new intel/OSINT-cohort actor (sibling of mitooshi/kanae/kanjo/watari/kabuto) covering the gap none holds: CROSS-ASSET CAPITAL ROTATION — the realized movement of money between equities/govt-bonds/credit/commodities/FX/crypto/real-estate/cash. Models capital as a graph of public BUCKETS (asset-class/sector/region/theme) + observed FLOWS; computes aggregate edge-primary metrics (net flow per bucket = どこに資金が向かっているか, rotation pairs = どこからどこへ, inflow HHI, by-asset-class/by-region, a FACTUAL risk-on/off/mixed regime descriptor) → dry-run social posts. DEFINING INVARIANT トレードはしない (G2 no-trade/non-advisory): NO buy/sell signal, price target, over/under-weight call, or portfolio instruction — trade/advisory tokens are structurally unrepresentable in FOUR homes (ontology enum + no :bucket/rating attr; lexicon noTradeNotice const true; weave.TRADE_TOKENS refused on flow/bucket kinds; social._guard_no_trade scans every post body). Observational MIRROR not signal (G5); edge-primary no per-asset rating/score (G4); public-bucket-only no-doxxing of individual investors/accounts (G1/G9); ≥2 public sources, commercial market-data terminals (Bloomberg/Refinitiv/FactSet/CapIQ/四季報) prohibited (G3/Rider §2(e)); no-server-key member-signed posts (G7); outward-gated dry-run + cells .solve() raise (G8); append-only as-of (G10); Murakumo-only (G6). AUTONOMOUS OPERATION ON KOTOBA: methods/autorun.py runs observe→validate→weave→analyze→dry-run-post→persist by itself each heartbeat, appending content-addressed transactions to the append-only kotoba Datom log (commit-DAG, verify_chain OK, tamper-detecting, deterministic/resume-safe) — autonomy in the charter-permitted form (no live external I/O; live ingest/post one human gate-flip away, deploy-ready per ADR-2606071000). LANDED R0 (+R1-ready): ontology capital-flow-ontology.kotoba.edn + 4 lex com.etzhayyim.shionome.* + 5 cells + methods (weave/ingest/social/export/registry/analyze/kotoba/autorun) + :representative seed; 153 tests green (run_tests.sh, 14 suites); R1-ready public-source registry (12 global primary sources, all unverified-seed). ZERO invariant amendments — adds the no-trade gate as a per-actor structural constraint; reuses Murakumo-only/no-server-key/kotoba-canonical/Rider §2(e)/non-eschatological. Live market-data ingest + posting Council Lv6+ + operator gated (Lv7+ for live publication). KOTOBA-WASM + FLEET-CRON (2nd commit, deploy-readiness): (1) standalone WASI component orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-shionome/wasm/ (app.py + wit/world.wit → componentize-py → shionome-actor.wasm 18.5MB, wasm-tools validate clean, jco-transpiled + executed under node: regime=risk-on no_trade=true; CID bafybeigk6whellozcybop4btzcrdtybd5yejjrax7tczxhapfsyya64hka dag-pb T2 donated-mesh; .wasm gitignored, reproducible via build.sh); (2) 5 Murakumo-fleet cron cells orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-magatama/cells/shionome_* (kotoba_langgraph Pregel cells 'Resident in Kotoba WASM', ossekai pattern) each with cells.toml.fragment trigger={kind=cron}: ingest@issachar 5***· flow_graph@issachar 10***· rotation_weave@dan 15***· regime_observer@dan 20***· social_post@naphtali 0 9***; registered in 50-infra/murakumo/fleet.toml + cell_runner_main.py shionome_* glob; pure logic in shionome_core.py (no kotoba_langgraph dep), 14/14 off-fleet tests. Cells run as k3s DaemonSet via Ansible playbook k8s-gpu-cluster.yml — actual deploy is the operator step (agent cannot per ADR-2606071000); cron fires analyze→dry-run, live ingest/post stays G8-gated. PR #1361. STOCK PYRAMID + ENTITY GROUNDING + LIVE COHORT (PR #1533, squash-merged 2026-06-10; session-close ADR-2606101540): :outstanding-usd stock metric (3 invariant homes) + weave.stock_pyramid — the Visual-Capitalist money-and-markets sizing view (8 global :representative layers, 1,383tn grand total; a SIZE is factual, never a rating/signal — G2/G4 untouched; usd-tn never summed with usd-bn); methods/grounding.py entity-grounding bridge (equities ← kabuto 1,719 cos = 40.7% value-coverage LOWER BOUND + depth ← kanjō live-merged 15 filers + overlay ← hokorobi 17 inst + per-layer roadmap naming why each ungrounded layer cannot be decomposed; fail-open, core never imports it); first LIVE EDGAR ingest in the cohort (kanjō G7 operator flip — 12 filers, 2,462 :authoritative facts); 70-tools/scripts/fleet-heartbeat/heartbeat.sh beats 11 offline loops 11/11 w/ size-segmented logs. 182 tests / 15 suites green. T1 BROWSER-WASM DID ACTOR LIVE (PR #1588, squash-merged 2026-06-10; session-close ADR-2606111330): shionome-core Rust T1 wasm (18,762B raw CID bafkreihvidpg…, tsumugi/kanae ABI; embeds the :representative seed, computes regime + stock pyramid; build-t1.sh asserts no_trade:true on the actual wasm output) + DID-actor registration in 3 homes (actor-profile-seed.kotoba.edn + INFRA_ACTORS + static public/actor/shionome/) + worker deployed (101/101 tests, version b50b69fb) + pinned on the live kubo daemon (kanae rebuild reproduced its registered CID bit-identically → its 502 FIXED; tsumugi loader artifact matched) — PRODUCTION e2e verified: DID resolve (_meta.source kotoba) → EtzhayyimWasmComponent → apex /ipfs 200 cid-verified → local CID re-verify MATCH → instantiate → {regime:risk-on, grand_total:1383tn, no_trade:true}. kotobase.net durability leg root-caused but NOT complete (pin worker no-timeout kubo pin/add + pod peer_count 0; pins registered under canonical tenant did:key:z6MktEjt…; operator follow-up)." :path "90-docs/adr/2606072201-shionome-cross-asset-capital-flow-observatory-r0.md" :adr ["2606072200" "2606051800" "2606071000" "2605302300" "2606032000" "2606041827" "2606022000" "2606066000" "2605312345" "