  {:id "2606072801" :title "Session close — 潮目 (shionome) cross-asset capital-flow observatory: R0 actor + kotoba-WASM component + Murakumo-fleet cron cells" :status "active" :status_note "Documentation-only closure of the shionome session (authoritative design = ADR-2606072200). Two commits on PR #1361 (branch feat/shionome-capital-flow). Commit 1 = R0 actor orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-shionome/: ontology + 4 lex + 5 cell scaffolds + methods (weave/ingest/social/export/registry/analyze/kotoba/autorun) + :representative seed + R1-ready 12-source registry; 153 tests green; トレードはしない (G2 no-trade) enforced in FOUR homes (ontology enum + no :bucket/rating, lexicon noTradeNotice const, weave.TRADE_TOKENS, social._guard_no_trade); methods/autorun.py self-drives observe→validate→weave→analyze→dry-run-post→persist into the append-only content-addressed kotoba Datom log. Commit 2 (answering 「kotoba wasm として自律稼働?fleet で cron?」) = two real kotoba-WASM artifacts, both empirically built/verified off-fleet: (1) standalone WASI component orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-shionome/wasm/ (componentize-py → shionome-actor.wasm 18.5MB, wasm-tools validate clean, jco-run under node regime=risk-on no_trade=true; CID bafybeigk6whellozcybop4btzcrdtybd5yejjrax7tczxhapfsyya64hka); (2) 5 Murakumo-fleet cron cells orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-magatama/cells/shionome_* (kotoba_langgraph, cells.toml.fragment trigger={kind=cron}, ingest/flow_graph@issachar, rotation_weave/regime_observer@dan, social_post@naphtali; registered in fleet.toml + cell_runner_main.py glob; shionome_core.py pure logic 14/14 off-fleet tests). Honest boundary: actual ansible deploy onto the physical Mac-mini fleet + live ingest/posting are operator/Council gated (G7/G8 + ADR-2606071000); reachable state = deploy-readiness, one human gate-flip from live. Registries updated (root CLAUDE.md, deps.edn, ADR README, docs/graph sidecars). ZERO invariant amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606072801-session-close-shionome-capital-flow-kotoba-wasm-fleet-cron.md" :adr ["2606072800" "2606072200" "2606071000" "2605215000" "2605231525" "2605312345"]}
  {:id "2606071000" :title "intel/OSINT actor cohort — R1 forecast pipeline + cross-actor synthesis + Murakumo fleet-readiness" :status "accepted" :status_note "Brings the intel/OSINT cohort (mitooshi, watari, watatsuna, kabuto, kanjo, tadori, danjo, himotoki) to 8/8 deploy-ready (227 tests green, 15 persisted kotoba Datom artifacts), additively, ZERO invariant amendments. mitooshi gains a full R1 forecasting pipeline over the Datom log — observe(watari/watatsuna)→bridge→persist(append-only as-of trail)→forecast(leak-free Gaussian, G1 distribution-only)→rolling-origin backtest+scorecard(G12 skill)→online recalibration(cells/online_update, leak-free)→calibration_gate decision(G7/G9/G12)→cross-actor chokepoint resilience composite — both ends proven: the real two-regime trail is honestly REFUSED on G7, a single-regime fixture CLEARS when calibrated+member-signed. watari/watatsuna/kabuto/kanjo/tadori got the missing test suites+runners pinning each charter invariant (G2 resilience-not-targeting, G4 non-adjudication/no-person-tracking, G5/G6/G7). danjo (single-bidder-streak discrepancy analyzer, non-adjudicating) and himotoki (DSAR/FOIA draft generator, own-data-only/no-pretext/PII-encrypted/verify-before-dispatch) went pure-design→R1. New 70-tools/intel-fleet-readiness Murakumo deploy pre-flight (NEVER deploys) reports per-actor READY-PENDING-GATE + the blocking outward gate; found+closed 3 artifact gaps. Live deploy/ingest/publish/promotion remains outward-gated (Council Lv6+ + operator) per each actor's G7/G10/G14; all inference Murakumo-only; all state kotoba Datom EDN (no SQL/RW). PR #1206." :path "90-docs/adr/2606071000-intel-osint-actor-cohort-r1-and-fleet-readiness.md" :adr ["2606071000" "2606051800" "2606041827" "2606012600" "2606022000" "2606032000" "2605301400" "2605301600" "2605302130" "2605262130" "2605312345" "2605231525" "2605215000" "2605192415" "2605192100"]}
  {:id "2606037200" :title "open-kyber as kotoba-Datomic ERP — ISIC industry packs + kotoba-native productivity suite + ERP-as-WASM-actor" :status "active" :status_note "Answers the founder directive 「ISIC のすべての産業に対応した ERP + mailer/drive/docs/sheets/calendar を kotoba datomic で連携・統合」 and the follow-up 「ERP Worker は Kysely/Hyperdrive を使わず kotoba datomic を / worker 自体も kotoba host に WASM/IPFS として」. R0 = erp-ontology.kotoba.edn EAVT vocab + 21 ISIC section packs (A–U) + 15 division packs + suite vocab. R1/R2 = the @etzhayyim/open-kyber-kotoba reference layer — a feature-complete kotoba-Datom-native ERP on the Datom log: exact-decimal money (BigInt), double-entry GL + 非終末論 reversal, AP/AR both spines, payment/settlement, period close, BS/PL/CF three statements, moving-average inventory, multi-currency FX, tax (消費税/VAT), budgeting, AR/AP aging + credit check, asset register + depreciation (SL+DB), ISIC pack resolver + industry-tailored chart-of-accounts (DIVISION_COA_EXT), and the productivity suite with real function (sheets exact-decimal formula engine + sheets↔ERP trial-balance binding, calendar RRULE expansion, drive IPFS file-tree, docs Markdown structuring, mailer over openmail Postage), plus a read-only 5-invariant ledgerAudit (toritate/danjo ethos). 23 test files / 113 tests green, tsc --noEmit clean. R2 KEYSTONE = createXrpcBridge adapts the magatama-host-sdk AT-repo XrpcClient (sdk.pds) to the kotoba Etzhayyim read/write surface, so the ERP Worker (etzhayyim-wasm-kyber-erp-kyb3rerp/src/app.ts) DELETED all createKyselyDb(env.HYPERDRIVE) read paths and routes all 28 commands (incl. billing rewritten as kotoba records) through the tested kotoba functions — app.ts type-checks clean against package sources (PR #1197). R3 (the code moves too, PoC) = wasm/kyber-erp-core/ compiles the ERP to a content-addressed kotoba-node WASM component (Rust, exports run(ctx-cbor) over a {method,args} envelope, imports kotoba:kais/{kqe,auth}, wasm-tools validate ✓) that the kotoba host / e7m-wasm-runner stores on IPFS by CID and runs, writing state straight to the Datom log via kqe — no CF Worker, no XRPC, no PDS hop; CID bafkreigdcmd54zval3z7xwmvmq5tgbsu6rpbxx4gtyhswxhvvfkaltaomi (raw, 119 KB), registered as did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:kyber in infra-actors.ts (PR #1214). NO RisingWave/Postgres/Kysely/Hyperdrive in any ERP path; all state kotoba Datom; Tier-3 HR PII stays in the ADR-2605181100 encrypted envelope (pointer-only Datom). HONEST: deployed live path is still the CF Worker (kyb3rerp); remaining = operator deploy of the Worker build + full 28-command Rust parity + verified Datalog read path + pin/publish of the actor bytes — all Council Lv6+ + operator gated (R2-WORKER-WIRING.md + WORKER-AS-WASM-ACTOR-MIGRATION.md). PRs #1195/#1197/#1214 merged to main." :path "90-docs/adr/2606037200-open-kyber-kotoba-datomic-erp-isic-industry-packs-productivity-suite.md" :adr ["2606037200" "0025" "2605262130" "2605312345" "2605181100" "2606014500" "2606015400" "2606032000" "2606012100" "2606032100" "2605215000" "2605231525" "2605192200"]}
  {:id "2606073002" :title "Session close — app-coverage charter-clean inversion wave + substrate-remediation ratchet" :status "active" :status_note "Answers 「いまの actor で uber, flight scanner, airbnb, hotels, google, sales force, office 365, shopofy などと同等の app の設計、実装 coverage は?」 + the follow-up 「成熟度、coverage を高めて」 (self-paced /loop, 12 iterations). All eight named apps now have charter-clean inversions: uber→ainori, flight-scanner→tsubasa, airbnb/hotels→shukubo, shopify→omise, salesforce/SAP→business-manager, calendly→yotei, drive→organizer, indeed→talent. Prohibited terms are structurally unrepresentable, substrate-boundary ratchet is seeded, and Phase B tracks frozen legacy paths toward kotoba-kqe." :path "90-docs/adr/2606073002-session-close-app-coverage-charter-clean-inversion-wave.md" :adr ["2606073000" "2606071400" "2606071500" "2606071600" "2606071800" "2606072000" "2606072200" "2606072400" "2606072600" "2606072800" "2606012100" "2605262130" "2605312345" "2605231525" "2605215000" "2605181100"]}
