  {:id "2606082100" :title "Mishmar Storage Covenant — social-capital-funded bonded pinning for unstoppable persistence" :status "proposed" :status_note "Session-close ADR for the 2026-06-08 persistence/economic-security gap review. Chooses the Charter-clean incentive model for third-party data persistence: non-yielding bonded pinning, slash-to-commons through TitheRouter/Public Fund, social-capital-denominated retainers, moyai-family social-capital reuse, and kotoba read+verify-only observation. It closes the design gap without creating live staking resources, Kubernetes resources, external-payment paths, or a yield-bearing/security-like token. Follow-ups: Social Capital ledger predicates, MishmarBondEscrow, witness challenge scheduler, and mKOTO retainer settlement." :path "90-docs/adr/2606082100-mishmar-storage-covenant-social-capital.md" :adr ["2606082100" "2605262130" "2606062100" "2605231400" "2605282100" "2604261717" "2605192100" "2605192200" "2605192130" "2605192145" "2605172100" "2605172300" "0075" "2605240001" "2605231525"]}
  {:id "2606072002" :title "嵩 (kasa) — worldwide computing-capacity growth statistics observatory (storage · memory · GPU/CPU · FLOPS · datacenter)" :status "proposed" :status_note "Answers 「年間のコンピューターのストレージサイズ・メモリサイズ・GPU・CPU などのコンピューティング能力の全世界での増加量を、統計・公開情報から推測する actor は設計されているか?」. Was: no — kanjō reads ONE company's 決算, kabuto holds the supply graph, handotai tracks semiconductor news, and mitooshi 見通し forecasts but had no measured-actuals feeder for compute. kasa is the demand-side, industry-aggregate observatory the roster lacked: reads PUBLIC info only (WSTS/SIA, TrendForce, IDC, JPR, TOP500, Epoch AI CC-BY, OWID CC-BY) into the kotoba Datom log as :compute.obs/* across four founder-named domains — STORAGE (HDD+SSD exabytes), MEMORY (DRAM+NAND revenue), GPU/CPU (units + DC-accel $), COMPUTE/FLOPS (TOP500 + frontier training) — plus DATACENTER power, then computes the annual increase (年間増加量) YoY + CAGR + coverage-honest domain aggregates. Industry-aggregate sibling of kanjō 勘定; demand-side counterpart of the silicon actors (handotai/iwakura/fuigo); feeds mitooshi 見通し but NEVER forecasts itself (G4 — load-bearing boundary). 13 gates: G1 public-sources-only (paid Gartner/IDC-report/Omdia/Bloomberg/S&P/Statista-Pro terminals PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c), encoded in sources.py::admissible) · G2 non-adjudicating (no country/company ranking) · G4 no-forecast · G5 sourcing-honest (:representative/:estimated-with-method/:synthesized) · G9 planning-lens-not-targeting-list · G12 coverage-honest aggregates (memory ⊂ semiconductor → distinct domain keys → never double-counted; :petaflops never summed with raw :flops). LANDED R0: ontology compute-capacity-ontology.kotoba.edn + 4 lex com.etzhayyim.kasa.* (path-reserved) + 3 cells (sources/ingest/analyze) + :representative/:estimated seed (8 sources / 11 series / 52 obs, 2020–2024); 23 tests green (run_tests.sh); DID registered (INFRA_ACTORS.kasa). ZERO invariant amendments. Live full open-dataset parse Council Lv6+ + operator gated (G7); no :authoritative rows yet." :path "90-docs/adr/2606072002-kasa-world-computing-capacity-growth-statistics-observatory-r0.md" :adr ["2606072000" "2606032000" "2606022000" "2606051800" "2605263800" "2605262130" "2605312345" "2605215000" "2606013800" "2606013600" "2605242500" "2605192100" "2605192200"]}
