  {:id "2606102000" :title "Session close — 息吹 (ibuki) digest (reason+report) + 実運用 live-run + robustness verification" :status "accepted" :status_note "Closes the ibuki maturity arc after the ecosystem (ADR-2606101800). Three strands, each a merged PR: (1) DIGEST #1575 + #1581 — the colony REASONS about its own ecosystem (assemble log-state: health verdict + eco-maturity + commons offered/available + quorum history) and REPORTS to humanity (digest.py → narrate via Murakumo-only infer.infer_text, fail-open to template → :digest/* :dry-run post, a mirror not advice; wired into BOTH autorun + fleet). (2) 実運用 LIVE-RUN verified 2026-06-10 (OPERATIONS.md #1578): perception LIVE fetched a real public follower count (bsky.app 33,623,191); murakumo gateway down → narration fail-open IN PRODUCTION; a 12-beat life persisted to the LIVE kotoba engine — 2,386 datoms confirmed by the node, IPNS head advanced, exactly-once re-push. (3) ROBUSTNESS: end-to-end integration #1576 (whole stack on one verified chain, crash-resume 30+30==60), adversarial sick-colony #1577 (a decomposer-less broken web self-detects keystone-absent+ecosystem-starved and self-reports through health→digest→kaizen; chain still verifies), fleet-scale ecosystem regression #1580 (the deployed 18,342 path runs the full ecosystem; report funcs are single-pass O(n) — measured health.audit 0.2s / web_report 0.02s over 665,688 datoms). HONEST BOUNDARY (Tier-1, never the platform's act): member-principal posting (member_submit), commons draw (symbiosis.draw), and physical fleet deploy stay held by a member/operator key ibuki structurally does not possess — 共生 by consent, not fabrication. 226 tests / 20 hermetic stdlib-only suites green. ZERO invariant amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606102000-session-close-ibuki-digest-live-run-robustness.md" :adr ["2606102000" "2606101800" "2606101200" "2606101500"]}
  {:id "2606110955" :title "session close — open-PR backlog review + merge (8 PRs); cleanroom L5 ledger union to 163" :status "accepted" :status_note "Process record of the 2026-06-11 review-and-merge sweep of the open-PR backlog on etzhayyim/root (7 open at start + #1593 opened mid-sweep). Merged to main (squash): #1590 meeting-recorder getMinutes XRPC, #1589 yoro prod kotoba-sw verify script, #1593 ibuki revocable-CACAO-leash delegation (+16 tests), and after hand-resolving conflicts #1498 (deps.edn union of appended milestone/adr blocks), #1493 (supply-chain NOTICE rename/content), #1568 (CLAUDE.md table — kept the PR's infra-robotics row AND main's newer ibuki row, not a side-pick), #1548 (adr README index union, re-merged once after main moved). Merged to feat/hydrogen-electrolysis-cfe-session-close (the PR's own base, NOT main): #1535 cleanroom L5 — the conflict was a genuine SET-UNION not a side-pick (head added 13 specialized actors, base had independently added 8 others, 142 common → 163 L5; tierCounts reconciled L5 163 / L4 837; per-actor index tiers verified 0-drift vs the ledger). All 90-docs/_registry sidecars REGENERATED (not hand-edited) so the freshness hooks pass. Result: 0 open PRs, every merge with 0 failing CI checks. HONEST: the 163-L5 union lives on the hydrogen branch — main's cleanroom index is still at 34 L5; landing that branch to main (and re-resolving the ledger) is the tracked follow-up. No code added this session, only merge commits + this record; zero invariant amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606110955-session-close-pr-backlog-review-merge.md" :adr ["2606110955" "2606101845" "2606102000"]}
  {:id "2606111000" :title "seigyo (制御) — open industrial control layer (PLC / SCADA / DCS-equivalent, ISA-95 L0–L2) Tier-B actor R0 charter" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「kotoba で DCS, PLC などは設計されている?」→ NO until this ADR: every manufacturing actor (igata / tsukuru silicon / yakushi / futawa / suki / pillow / tsutae / hikari-denki / mizuho) was modelled at ISA-95 L3+ only; the L0–L2 control layer those recipes execute on was unmodelled with constraints scattered (2605265000 §1.9 no commercial DCS/SCADA vendor, 2604252100 OPC UA, 2605215000 Murakumo-only). seigyo promotes it to a first-class Tier-B actor: OpenPLC (IEC 61131-3 ST canonical) L1 + FUXA/Rapid SCADA/OpenSCADA L2 + OPC UA open62541 L2.5 — DCS-equivalent as audited open composition, no monolithic vendor product (Siemens/Honeywell/Yokogawa/Emerson/Rockwell/ABB/Schneider/Mitsubishi/GE/AVEVA/Ignition runtimes PROHIBITED, §1.9 generalized to ALL actors). ABSOLUTE §3 safety invariant: interlocks hardwired L1S; no LLM / Murakumo inference / kotoba cell ever in the safety path (must complete with network cable cut); Murakumo optimization lands only through setpoint envelopes compiled into the attested program. §4 PLC-program-as-attested-record lifecycle (ST CID → simulate → attest → deploy → runtime-hash watch; mismatch = recipe-dispatch freeze). §5 N7 aggregate-only northbound telemetry. 5 scaffold cells (kotoba PR #112) + 9 com.etzhayyim.seigyo.* lexicons (root PR #1641). Ratified via PR review per CLAUDE.md operational premise 2026-06-11 (root PR #1635)." :path "90-docs/adr/2606111000-seigyo-industrial-control-layer-tier-b-actor-r0.md"}
  {:id "2606111100" :title "seigyo R1 — benchtop temperature-PID loop commissioning and Council baseline (paired with igata R1 benchtop)" :status "accepted" :status_note "R1 = ONE physical loop exercising every layer and invariant end-to-end: ≤2 kW electric mock-furnace temperature PID (igata die-preheat 220°C analog; mock-rig de-risking parallel to igata Hibachi/Tatara PoC), OpenPLC + FUXA + open62541, ≤10 I/O points. Reference IEC 61131-3 ST program orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-seigyo/reference/bench_pid_loop.st + envelope mirror JSON (0–250°C operational envelope two layers below the hardwired 300°C thermal fuse — §3/§3.4 separation demonstrated physically). Full §4 lifecycle drill incl. deliberate runtime-hash-mismatch drill, envelope-clamp drill (request 400°C via OPC UA → clamped to 250°C at L1), and E-stop verification WITH the controller network cable disconnected (§3.2 proven literally). SME = 1 controls-engineer DID (CONTROLS_ENGINEER_REGISTRY_CID — the one gate PR review cannot substitute; HIGH-risk cells stay gated on it per kotoba PR #116). R1→R2 exit: 30-day clean runtime-attestation history, 7-day soak 220°C ±2°C, zero non-drill clamp events (clamps = upstream layer requesting out-of-envelope → root-cause, not tolerate)." :path "90-docs/adr/2606111100-seigyo-r1-benchtop-loop-commissioning.md"}
  {:id "2606111011" :title "session close — land feat/hydrogen-electrolysis-cfe-session-close → main (163-L5 cleanroom corpus reaches trunk)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Executes the tracked follow-up from ADR-2606110955: bring the long-lived feat/hydrogen-electrolysis-cfe-session-close branch (163-L5 cleanroom union + hydrogen/CFE work) back onto main. The branch was 64 ahead / 163 behind (657 files diff). main was merged INTO the branch and 14 conflicts hand-resolved before opening the branch→main PR: 8 scholarly *-compat/manifest.json kept the branch's L5 'verified' provenance block (main had null); 40-engine/kotoba submodule kept the branch ptr 92461b7346 (newer + real/fetchable; main's 98f9d2b3fd unresolvable on the kotoba remote); cleanroom-l5-verification.json kept the branch's 163 L5 (strict superset of main's 42; index auto-merged to L5 163 / L4 837, 0-drift vs the ledger); CLAUDE.md kanjō row took MAIN's newer R0+R1-live-EDGAR version; deps.edn 3 regions took MAIN's additive/newer blocks (niyaku/uchiwake/ibuki/rasen incl. this ADR family + rasen GO-pathway) — no NEW duplicate ADR ids (merged 13 == main's 13, all pre-existing); registry sidecars REGENERATED (924 entries). All pre-commit hooks green on the merge commit. Once the branch→main PR merges, main's cleanroom corpus reaches 163 L5 / 837 L4 (up from 42). No code authored, only merge resolution + this record; zero invariant amendments. Tracked follow-ups: merge the PR, de-dup the 13 pre-existing duplicate ADR ids, re-home the cleanroom L5 line onto main to stop ledger divergence." :path "90-docs/adr/2606111011-session-close-land-hydrogen-branch-to-main.md" :adr ["2606111011" "2606110955" "2606082300"]}
  {:id "2606111400" :title "Session close — 息吹 (ibuki) autonomous identity = a revocable CACAO leash (member-signed delegation + issuer)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「app password は kotoba server, actor ではどう設計されているか → 自律的生命としてはどう管理させるのが良い? a かな → a改」. kotoba has NO passwords (app-password is an AT-Proto PDS concept the member holds in their own runtime); kotoba is DID-centric (passkey-wrapped keys, Bearer JWT sub==DID, CACAO DelegationChain for graph writes). The right identity model for an autonomous life that the platform may hold no key for (no-server-key, ADR-2605231525) and that has no human present each beat is a SCOPED, EXPIRING, REVOCABLE capability — a LEASH, not a held key. Three custodial roles never collapsed: ISSUE (the member, with their own key, signs a CACAO datom:transact@graph:ibuki,exp:+Nd in their own runtime) / INVOKE (the organism PRESENTS the opaque cacao_b64 every beat — present-only, stays stdlib, never signs) / REVOKE (exp lapses → fail-open; stop re-issuing → it quietly retires). Two merged PRs: (1) #1593 the leash — methods/delegation.py (stdlib present-only, scope+expiry vs caller-supplied now_epoch, fail-open if absent) wired into kotoba_bridge.push(delegation=,now_epoch=) (usable→presents cacao_b64 + drops operator bearer; expired/mis-scoped/absent→fail-open to operator-bearer loopback), +16 tests. (2) #1599 made real + CORRECTED against the live verifier — tools/issue_delegation.py member-side minting tool (member's OWN runtime; MAY use cryptography — the no-crypto rule binds the actor, not the member) produces a byte-correct CAIP-122/SIWE CACAO (Ed25519 over the exact siwe_message() plaintext, hand-rolled CBOR). Minting a REAL CACAO + presenting it to the live node corrected two assumptions, both now read from kotoba-auth::{cacao,delegation}: aud is the kotoba NODE's operator DID (server checks cacao.p.aud==operator_did), NOT the organism's DID — the organism is the BEARER, capability scoped to (node,graph,capability,expiry); and write_author = the issuing MEMBER — the colony's autonomous writes are on-record attributed to the consenting human (accountability flows to a named person, time-bounded+revocable — a BETTER model than 'writes as itself': autonomy WITH a named human principal, 相互監視/共生 by consent, never an anonymous agent). resources = the SIWE two-entry form [kotoba://can/datom:transact, kotoba://graph/<cid>]; sidecar exp (epoch, is_usable gates on) reconciled to the CACAO ISO exp (kotoba verifies) at one conversion point. LIVE-WIRING VERIFIED 2026-06-11: a real member-signed CACAO, presented with NO operator bearer, is parsed + Ed25519-verified by the live node and reaches DID-resolution (format/signature/SIWE/capability/graph/aud all accepted); full write-acceptance additionally needs the node's IPFS/kubo DID resolver up — operator infra, NOT a design/actor gap. Actor-side path (issuer→delegation.load→is_usable→bridge presents) verified end-to-end. Honest boundary (NOT flippable): no-server-key (ibuki holds no key, does no crypto, present-only); fail-open never fail-dangerous; human-presence acts (AT-Proto publish, commons draw) stay separate + member-signed each time, never delegated. 242 tests / 21 hermetic stdlib-only suites green. ZERO invariant amendments." :path "90-docs/adr/2606111400-session-close-ibuki-delegation-revocable-leash.md" :adr ["2606111400" "2606101200" "2606102000" "2606101800" "2605231525" "2605262130" "2605215000"]}
  {:id "2606112000" :title "Actor DNA — binding kotoba CODE + DATA into one content-addressed unit (Holochain-/Ethereum-iso)" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「いまの kotoba, kotobase の設計では ethereum, holochain のように コードとデータが一体化して deploy できている?」 → 'ok, do it'. A code-read found kotoba content-addresses + re-verifies BOTH code (WASM CID, ADR-2606014500/014600) and data (Datom log/graph CID, ADR-2605312345) — the trustless half, equal to Ethereum bytecode-CID and Holochain DNA-hash — but did NOT unify them: (1) code, data-graph, validation, lexicon were FOUR separate CIDs linked only by did.json references (no single binding ID like an Ethereum account or a Holochain DNA hash); (2) the kotoba transact/kg.ingest path is append-only + CACAO auth with NO code-defined data validation (verified in 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-server/src/kg.rs — auth check, no validate() hook; CACAO governs WHO writes, nothing governs WHAT); (3) deploy is several uncoordinated ops, not atomic. The Actor DNA manifest (kotoba-actor-dna/v0) closes these: ONE canonical-EDN object {:dna/wasm-cid(CODE) + :dna/graph+graph-cid(DATA, graph-cid DERIVED+re-checked) + :dna/validation-cid + :dna/lexicon-cid + :dna/capability(the ibuki CACAO leash ADR-2606111400)}, content-addressed to a single raw DNA CID that becomes the actor's identity — did.json points at ipfs://<dna-cid> and nothing else; change any part → new DNA CID → a different actor (code+data fused into one tamper-evident hash). + the integrity ruleset (kotoba-integrity/v0): a content-addressed ruleset (= :dna/validation-cid) + validate(datoms) that REJECTS non-conforming datoms (append-only/closed-vocab/attr-types/deny-attrs/required-attrs/graph-binding) before push — the Holochain integrity-zome analogue, tamper-evident because the rules are part of the actor's hash. + the deploy descriptor (kotoba-actor-deploy/v0): ordered plan (pin code→validation→lexicon→manifest→graph-genesis→did-link) where every step binds the one DNA CID (atomicity-of-identity). Impl 50-infra/actor-dna/ pure-stdlib cid/dna/integrity/deploy.py, 33 tests / 4 hermetic suites; cid.py cross-checked BYTE-IDENTICAL vs orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-rasen/methods/cid.py + graph_cid('ibuki') == the live engine's graph CID (bafyreif6qopha…, observed in the ADR-2606111400 delegation live test); schema 00-contracts/schemas/actor-dna.kotoba.edn. HONEST SCOPE: enforced NOW at the client/actor tier (validate() before kotoba_bridge.push); engine-tier enforcement (the kotoba transact path invoking the DNA's validate before commit, so a PEER's writes are checked too — full Holochain parity) + true single-tx atomic deploy are the GATED follow-up in the 40-engine/kotoba submodule (a separate repo; not touched here). The content-addressed ruleset + DNA CID are the half that makes that follow-up trustless. ZERO invariant amendments; no substrate-ordering change (Datom log stays first-class canonical state)." :path "90-docs/adr/2606112000-kotoba-actor-dna-code-data-unification.md" :adr ["2606112000" "2606013800" "2606014500" "2606015400" "2605312345" "2606111400" "2606091500" "2606036000" "2605231525"]}
  {:id "2606151027" :title "masago (真砂) — open materials-discovery (公開材料) KG mirror (materials-science sibling of rasen 螺旋 + inochi 命); mirrors the PUBLIC open-materials commons (Meta FAIR Chemistry OMat24 CC-BY-4.0 + Materials Project / OQMD / NOMAD / AFLOW / JARVIS) into the kotoba Datom log, edge-primary discovery-evidence routed to RESEARCH, never a weapons-design or synthesis-recipe tool" :status "proposed" :status_note "Answers 「https://www.technologyreview.jp/.../meta-is-giving-massive-amounts-away-for-free/ は統合できている?」→ NO (repo-wide search found zero coverage of OMat24 / Open Materials / MLIP / materials discovery) → 'do it' (ADR draft) → 'do it' (actor scaffold) → 'py じゃなくて kotoba datomic, clojure にして' (Clojure pivot). Closes the AI-driven materials-discovery coverage gap. R0 = open-materials-ontology.kotoba.edn (nodes :material/:element/:property/:application/:dataset-source keyed by :mat/id; edges :composed-of/:has-property/:candidate-for/:derived-from/:similar-to; :en/grasping-load karma + DISCLOSED :en/value + :en/confidence; derived :bond/discovery-priority transient) + hand-curated seed (16 materials, mp-* ids: LiFePO4/Si/GaN/LLZO/BaTiO3/MgB2 …) + Clojure/kotoba-datomic-native methods/analyze.cljc (EDN reader + classify + screen[G1 no-synthesis-route/no-weapon-class + G4 open-license, raises ex-info] + analyze[edge-primary integral] + render-report + render-coverage + render-datoms[canonical EAVT, ADR-2605312345] + -main) + methods/test_analyze.cljc (13 deftests / 433 assertions green, network-free, babashka `bb --classpath 20-actors`) + 3 lexicons (materialRecord/datasetSourceAttestation/discoveryCandidateReport, enums enforce the gates). 8 gates: G1 research-map-NOT-weapons/synthesis (synthesis-route/precursor/enrichment field + weaponizable application class structurally unrepresentable, §1.12; mirrors hotaru no-fabrication) · G2 edge-primary (no :material/score) · G3 non-adjudicating (DFT/MLIP DISCLOSED, never re-judged, no :verdict route, never trades) · G4 open-license-only · G5 sourcing-honest (~10^8 commons coverage ~0 by design) · G6 Murakumo-only + no-commercial-GPU (MLIP model execution R2+ owned/donated compute only, never RunPod) · G7 ingest/publish outward-gated + no-server-key (R1 legs) · G8 content-addressed canonical Datom state / no-git-lfs. Live ingest (Materials Project REST / OMat24 dumps) = R1; MLIP model execution = R2+ (Council-gated). Honest limit: OMat24 size/license figures cited from the article, re-verify vs FAIR Chemistry release notes before R1 ingest. Status 🟡 R0 design-only. Deciders: Jun Kawasaki." :path "90-docs/adr/2606151027-masago-open-materials-discovery-mirror.md" :adr ["2606151027" "2606101000" "2606051200" "2606073000" "2605312345" "2605262400" "2605215000" "2605231525" "2605192100" "2605192200"]}
  {:id "2606101000" :title "rasen (螺旋) — public-genetics KG mirror (gene-scale sibling of inochi 命); hosts PUBLIC reference genetics in the kotoba Datom log + IPFS, edge-primary clinical/functional evidence routed to CARE & RESEARCH, never an individual-genotype registry" :status "accepted" :status_note "Answers 「人や生命の遺伝子情報を kotoba で store して分析できる actor は?」→ inochi 命 stops at the species scale; rasen is its gene/variant-scale counterpart. Then 「個人は不要、公開されているものを kotoba ipfs で取り込んで」→ a live PUBLIC ingest cell. R0 = genome-ontology.kotoba.edn EAVT vocab + hand-curated seed (genes/variants/phenotypes/populations/pathways across human/elephant/rice/bacteria) + 3 pure-stdlib cells (analyze edge-primary care-priority = Σ incident variant-association via :located-in + gene-linkage × DISCLOSED clinsig; datom_emit EAVT; coverage honest gap-map) + 10 tests. R1 = cell:rasen.ingest (methods/ingest.py) pulls a BOUNDED PUBLIC slice from MyGene.info (gene→Ensembl+coarse cytoband) + MyVariant.info (rsID→ClinVar significance + gnomAD SUPER-POPULATION AGGREGATE allele frequencies), normalises to genome-ontology EDN, datom-projects it, and content-addresses the artifact to a kotoba IPFS CIDv1 (raw/sha2-256, methods/cid.py — byte-identical to `ipfs add --cid-version=1 --raw-leaves`, verified vs ipfs 0.41.0, no daemon needed). First live run 2026-06-10: 20 genes + 12 variants, 0 errors → 88 nodes / 103 縁; graph CID bafkreidtkdiz5cantzxgbwalugqovpvsn6yc3rlnat2jr2uwckfm7yvdmy (ipfs pin matched); provenance in out/ingest-provenance.json. R1+ live GO pathway ingest (ADR addendum, PR #1591): build_gene_pathways pulls public Gene-Ontology/EBI-GOA via MyGene go.BP, dedupes by accession, keeps best evidence weight (experimental>author-stated>phylogenetic>computational — DISCLOSED, not re-judged, N3), caps :max-per-gene (G5), emits :participates-in (gene→pathway) edges that feed the pleiotropy/cascade readout; GO-enabled run → 192 nodes / 220 縁 (117 GO edges, 104 GO pathway nodes), 0 errors, CID bafkreicct2g36hnfoeavh3ztgplsyuq2fzlhfocv2oql2lemugmh7j27vi (ipfs pin matched); 17 tests green (network-free). 8 gates: G1 CARE/RESEARCH-map-never-an-individual-genotype-registry (no individual/sample/family genotypes; unit is gene/variant/population-AGGREGATE; gnomAD super-pop af_* only, never sex-stratified/cohort; coarse cytoband never precise coords — enforced by tests + by construction) · G2 edge-primary (no :genome/score-of-gene) · G3 non-adjudicating (ClinVar significance is DISCLOSED, copied not re-judged) · G4 public venue · G5 sourcing-honest (bounded; coverage ~0 by design) · G6 Murakumo-only narration · G7 outward-gated (scope expansion beyond the bounded public slice = Council + operator DID) · G8 no-git-lfs (DataLad→IPFS). Individual/clinical/cohort genome ingest is explicitly OUT OF SCOPE for rasen and would require a separate himotoki-enveloped, consent-bound actor — never bolted on. R2 (operator-authorized 1·2·3, PR #1600 + #1591 GO): (1) methods/publish.py pins + IPNS-publishes (self-key /ipns/k51qzi5uqu5dgql6m0zggpi47n0jfvcr1q2scowxgekf0lu8ifssm3nzdqblgc) + snapshots graph/datoms/provenance to 80-data/genome (git-tracked, no git-lfs G8; trustless verify ipfs-cat→cid.py reproduces the CID); (2) build-ready WASM component (wasm/wit/world.wit + app.py export bodies runnable in dev + build.sh embed→componentize-py→CID→DID-service; componentize-py build is the operator step, NOT faked); (3) Reactome curated pathways via UniProt mapping (2nd authoritative pathway source after GO; dedupe by stId, top-level first, capped, DISCLOSED N3) → GO+Reactome live run 268 nodes / 305 縁 (117 GO + 85 Reactome edges), 0 errors, CID bafkreiamcn6vz4iuqtri6cbjtrse2koz7dfxxyde5rknfypx3ukj5elfvm (pin matched); 23 tests green. Status 🟢 R2. Deciders: Jun Kawasaki." :path "90-docs/adr/2606101000-rasen-public-genetics-mirror.md" :adr ["2606101000" "2606073000" "2606073800" "2606011000" "2606011500" "2605312345" "2605231525" "2605215000" "2605181100" "2606014500" "2606014600"]}
