  {:path "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/tests/sensors/test_w1_corp_gov_sensors.py" :adr ["ADR-2605263800" "ADR-2605263900"] :kind "pytest-w1-harness" :status "w1-test-harness-landed" :description "Pytest harness validating all 10 W1-impl-landed corp/+gov/ sensors. 11 tests total: 10 per-sensor round-trip (GleifLei / SecEdgar / UkCompaniesHouse / JpEdinet / WorldBank / UkHansard / Eurostat / UsCongress / JpKokkai / UsDataGov) each writes a tmp annex shard with real-data fixtures (Apple / Sony / NOAA / Speaker Hoyle / 額賀議長 etc.) + verifies G7 skip + G7 determinism + invariant fields (Tier-A / license_tag / internal_only=False / state_aligned_flag passing) + sensor-specific filter params (form_class_filter / regional_prefix_filter / chamber_filter / record_kind_filter / organization_filter / license_filter / dataflow_prefix_filter); 1 cross-cutting lint test asserts NO sensor source file imports vendor commercial terminal hostnames or SDK package names per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c) deny-list (Bloomberg Terminal / Refinitiv / FactSet / Moody's Orbis / D&B / Pitchbook / Crunchbase Pro / GovWin IQ / Bloomberg Government / Politico Pro / E&E News Pro / FiscalNote / CQ Roll Call Pro). Smoke-verified 2026-05-27 with 11/11 PASS via manual importlib runner (bypasses pytest infra which requires unbroken pydantic env)."}
  {:path "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/organism/sensors/gov/uk_data_gov_uk_sensor.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-sensor-impl" :status "w1-impl-landed" :description "UkDataGovUkSensor concrete W1 implementation (gov W1-impl #7 / overall #11). Reads UK data.gov.uk CKAN catalog per-package NDJSON from gov/open-data/gbr/data-gov-uk/<rev>/*.ndjson and yields GovOpenDataObservation with jurisdiction='GBR'. ~70K UK central + local government dataset entries; default license=OGL-v3.0 (Open Government Licence Crown copyright open). Per-row license_tag pass-through enables sub-licensed (e.g., cc-by) datasets to carry their license through observation chain. organisation_filter constructor param uses British English spelling. G7 schema discipline: rows missing required fields (datasetId / title / license / payloadCid) skipped. Second sibling of UsDataGovSensor + JpDataGoJpSensor (all three yield GovOpenDataObservation; jurisdiction field disambiguating). Per-jurisdiction publication-rule honoring per ADR-2605263900 §5; GDPR DSARs route through chigiri.data_privacy to upstream Cabinet Office / individual UK central+local government body. state_aligned_flag=False (GBR NOT §2(g)-flagged). G7 determinism: hot_sample reservoir-samples reproducibly. Passive-only invariant — NEVER hits data.gov.uk CKAN live API. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Pytest-harness-covered 2026-05-27 (test_uk_data_gov_uk_sensor_round_trip: ONS GDP + MoJ Court Stats + 1 CC-BY sub-licensed dataset + 1 G7-skip; organisation_filter='moj-gov-uk' restriction verified)."}
  {:path "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/organism/sensors/gov/jp_data_go_jp_sensor.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-sensor-impl" :status "w1-impl-landed" :description "JpDataGoJpSensor concrete W1 implementation (gov W1-impl #8 / overall #12 — completes GovOpenDataSensor 3-sibling triad USA/GBR/JPN). Reads JP data.go.jp CKAN catalog + e-Stat statsList per-package NDJSON from gov/open-data/jpn/data-go-jp/<rev>/*.ndjson and yields GovOpenDataObservation with jurisdiction='JPN'. ~30K data.go.jp packages + ~600 e-Stat surveys; default license=CC-BY-4.0 (政府標準利用規約 2.0). Combined-NDJSON case supported (data.go.jp + e-Stat in single view; sensor treats uniformly through GovOpenDataObservation shape; downstream consumers may inspect 'source' field in payload). 省庁 / 自治体 publisher names pass-through (総務省 / 厚生労働省 / 東京都 etc.) per §5; 個人情報保護法 + 行政手続オンライン化法 DSARs route through chigiri.data_privacy to upstream 各省庁 / e-Stat NSTAC; religious-corp NEVER performs unilateral removal. organization_filter constructor param restricts to per-省庁 consumers. G7 schema discipline + G7 determinism. state_aligned_flag=False (JPN NOT §2(g)-flagged). Third sibling of UsDataGovSensor + UkDataGovUkSensor. Passive-only invariant — NEVER hits data.go.jp CKAN / e-Stat live API. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Pytest-harness-covered 2026-05-27 (test_jp_data_go_jp_sensor_round_trip: 総務省 人口統計 + 総務省統計局 国勢調査 e-Stat + 1 G7-skip; organization_filter='soumu-go-jp' restriction verified)."}
  {:path "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/organism/sensors/gov/us_usaspending_sensor.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-sensor-impl" :status "w1-impl-landed" :description "UsUsaspendingSensor concrete W1 implementation (gov W1-impl #9 / overall #13 — first GovBudgetSensor concrete; completes 4/5 of GovFacet coverage). Reads USAspending.gov per-record NDJSON from gov/budget/usa/usaspending-gov/<rev>/*.ndjson and yields GovBudgetObservation with jurisdiction='USA' covering DATA Act award + recipient + sub-award records. Tier-A public-domain (17 USC 105). recordKind enum: appropriation / obligation / outlay / subaward; G7 schema discipline: rows with unknown recordKind value OR missing required fields (recordId / programName / amountLocal / currencyIso4217 / fiscalYear / payloadCid) skipped without halt. recipient_lei cross-link to corp.leiReference (ADR-2605263800 LeiSensor) preserved on observation; powers toritate (ADR-2605262900) anti-related-party check against Public Fund Safe + Council Safe disbursements in same fiscal cycle. record_kind_filter + fiscal_year_filter constructor params restrict yielded stream. Per-jurisdiction publication-rule honoring per §5 (USAspending publishes named recipients per DATA Act transparency-regime reason). state_aligned_flag=False (USA NOT §2(g)-flagged). G7 determinism: hot_sample reservoir-samples reproducibly. Passive-only invariant — NEVER hits USAspending.gov live API. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Pytest-harness-covered 2026-05-27 (test_us_usaspending_sensor_round_trip: Medicare Part A outlay w/ Mayo Clinic LEI + NSF Stanford grant no-LEI + DARPA MIT subaward FY 2024 + 2 G7-skip rows; fiscal_year_filter=2025 + record_kind_filter=('outlay',) restrictions verified)."}
  {:path "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/organism/sensors/gov/eu_ted_sensor.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-sensor-impl" :status "w1-impl-landed-facet-complete" :description "EuTedSensor concrete W1 implementation (gov W1-impl #10 / overall #14 — first GovProcurementSensor concrete; ═══ gov 5 facet COMPLETE: Statistics (WorldBank+Eurostat) + Parliament (Hansard+Congress+Kokkai) + OpenData (3 portals) + Budget (USAspending) + Procurement (EU TED) ═══). Reads EU TED (Tenders Electronic Daily) eForms per-notice NDJSON from gov/procurement/eu/ted/<rev>/*.ndjson and yields GovProcurementObservation with jurisdiction='EU' (~700K notices/year across EU+EEA contracting authorities). Tier-A EU re-use Decision 2011/833/EU. Internal _NOTICE_TYPE_MAP table maps 15 TED eForms native notice-type strings (Contract notice / Prior information notice / Periodic indicative notice / Qualification system notice / Concession notice / Voluntary ex ante transparency notice / Design contest notice / Contract award notice / Award notice / Concession award notice / Modification notice / Modification of a contract / Cancellation notice / Corrigendum) to canonical ProcurementRecordKind enum (tender-notice / award / modification / cancellation); explicit row.recordKind takes precedence. awardee_lei cross-link to corp.leiReference preserved; powers toritate vendor anti-related-party check. record_kind_filter + min_amount_local constructor params restrict yielded stream (e.g., only large awards >=€1M). G7 schema discipline: rows missing required fields OR with unmappable nativeKind+no explicit recordKind → skip without halt. state_aligned_flag=False (EU NOT §2(g)-flagged). Passive-only invariant — NEVER hits ted.europa.eu live API. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Pytest-harness-covered 2026-05-27 (test_eu_ted_sensor_round_trip: DE-Bayern Highway tender + FR Atos €12.5M IT award w/ LEI + IT Comune di Milano €50K small award + DE Corrigendum cancellation + 2 G7-skip rows; min_amount_local=€1M restriction verified)."}
  {:path "90-docs/baien/corp-gov-w1-snapshot-260527.md" :adr ["ADR-2605263800" "ADR-2605263900"] :kind "release-snapshot" :status "w1-snapshot-landed" :description "Consolidated W1 RELEASE NOTES / Council brief for ADR-2605263800 (corporate disclosure) + ADR-2605263900 (open government) — cumulative through 22 iterations of recurring /loop eaeee13b (2026-05-26 → 2026-05-27). Documents: 14 concrete sensor implementations (corp 4 + gov 10) + 12 W0 fetcher path-reserved stubs + 10 Lexicons + 4 corpus recipes + 4 acceptance templates + cross-actor wiring (ossekai + chigiri + toritate) + 4 legacy script supersession markers + 15/15 pytest harness PASS + gov 5 facet (Statistics + Parliament + OpenData + Budget + Procurement) coverage matrix + R1 activation Council ratification checklist (9 G gates) + recommended fetcher W1-impl landing order + 13-vendor commercial-terminal deny-list triple-layered enforcement summary (ADR §2 + recipe scan + pytest lint + Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c) constitutional ground). Authoritative-for: operator/Council-readable summary of corp+gov ingestion substrate W1 status; supersedes ad-hoc end-of-iteration summaries."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/gleif_lei.py" :adr "ADR-2605263800" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "GLEIF LEI L1 Concatenated File fetcher — first concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub earlier registered as 'w1-deliverable-stub'). Tier-A CC0 1.0 (GLEIF public-domain dedication). Two operator paths: (1) Network mode — httpx GET against goldencopy.gleif.org concatenated-file URL with User-Agent identification + 900s timeout; (2) Local-source mode (local_source=Path) — skip HTTPS, read operator-staged file (canonical test path + air-gapped fleet path for content-filtering-proxy environments). Automatic ZIP container detection (PK signature byte-check) + first .json extraction. JSON parse handles 3 input shapes: flat list-of-records / LEIData.LEIRecords nested / records-wrapper / single-record envelope (operator-staged subsets). Output: <name>-<capture_ts>/ staging dir w/ extracted payload .json + lei-l1.ndjson sidecar (sensor-consumable shape per GleifLeiSensor docstring: lei + legalName + jurisdictionIso3 + registrationStatus + parentLei + ultimateParentLei). GLEIF Entity.LegalJurisdiction passed through as upstream alpha-2 (sensor maxLength:3 accommodates both alpha-2 + alpha-3). G7 schema discipline: rows with lei field != 20 chars skipped without halting stream. W1 uses stdlib json.loads() in-memory (adequate for fixtures + operator-sampled subsets ≤100MB); W2 switches to ijson streaming for production-scale ~2GB Golden Copy. fetch_l2=False at W1 (L2 RR/RepEx join deferred to W2). Passive-only invariant boundary: this fetcher is OPERATOR-triggered (NOT organism-tick) per ADR-2605262400 §7; the sensor that consumes it (GleifLeiSensor) is the passive side. Vendor commercial-terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 4 scenarios: TEST 1 list-flat shape (Apple+Sony+TOOSHORT-skip) / TEST 2 LEIData.LEIRecords nested (Apple Europe+HSBC w/ parentLei) / TEST 3 ZIP-container extract (Microsoft, real Golden Copy filename pattern) / TEST 4 end-to-end fetcher→GleifLeiSensor integration (fetcher output consumed by sensor via StaticPinResolver). 4/4 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/worldbank_open_data.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "World Bank Open Data API fetcher — second concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub). Tier-A CC-BY 4.0 (WB Open Data Terms of Use). Two operator paths matching gleif_lei.py pattern: (1) Network mode — httpx GET per (indicator × country × paginated-page); indicators MUST be non-empty (passive-only discipline: no implicit full-catalog fetch); paginates via WB header.pages field. (2) Local-source mode — read operator-staged JSON OR NDJSON; auto-detects format via json.loads vs newline-iter. Handles 3 input shapes: (a) native WB 2-element response [header, [observation_dicts]] (detected by header keys page/pages/per_page/total); (b) flat list of observation dicts (operator-staged from sampled WB queries); (c) pre-normalized NDJSON pass-through (operator-flattened sensor-shape rows preserved as-is). _normalize_wb_observation maps WB schema (indicator.id + indicator.value + countryiso3code OR country.id + date + value + unit) → sensor's expected (indicatorCode, indicatorTitle, dimensions=[[country, ISO3], [year, date]], value, valueUnit, observationPeriod, payloadCid). max_observations cap supports memory-bounded operator runs. Network-mode incremental sha256 hashing avoids re-reading the NDJSON file. Output: <name>-<capture_ts>/worldbank-open-data.ndjson (sensor-consumable). G7 schema discipline: rows lacking required fields dropped at fetcher boundary. Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7 (operator-triggered, not organism-tick). Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 5 scenarios: TEST 1 native 2-elem (USA + JPN GDP + XX ISO-2 fallback) / TEST 2 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough (DE + FR pop preserved with payloadCid) / TEST 3 max_observations=2 cap / TEST 4 network-mode empty-indicators ValueError guard / TEST 5 end-to-end fetcher → WorldBankOpenDataSensor 3-obs integration (USA GDP value preserved + CC-BY-4.0 license_tag). 5/5 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/eu_eurostat.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "EU Eurostat SDMX-JSON 2.0 fetcher — third concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub). Tier-A EU re-use Decision 2011/833/EU. Two operator paths matching gleif_lei.py + worldbank_open_data.py pattern: (1) Network mode — httpx GET per dataflow against ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/data/<flow>/?format=JSON; dataflows MUST be non-empty (passive-only: no implicit full-catalog fetch). (2) Local-source mode — read operator-staged SDMX-JSON OR pre-normalized NDJSON. Handles 3 input shapes: (a) native SDMX-JSON 2.0 dict (detected via 'value'+'dimension'+'size' keys) → flat-index decoder unpacks row-major linearization back into per-dimension codes; (b) single pre-normalized dict envelope; (c) flat list of pre-normalized rows. _decode_flat_index implements the canonical row-major SDMX cube linearization (strides[i] = product of sizes[i+1..N]; per-dim idx[i] = (flat // strides[i]) mod sizes[i]). _UNIT_DIM_CANDIDATES = ('unit',) extracts the unit dimension into the row's valueUnit field (NOT dimensions tuple); _TIME_DIM_CANDIDATES = ('time', 'TIME_PERIOD') extracts time into observationPeriod + appends ('time', period) at end of dimensions tuple for sensor consistency. extension.datastructure.id provides indicatorCode (fallback to dataflow URL segment); dataset.label provides indicatorTitle. max_observations cap supports memory-bounded operator runs. Output: <name>-<capture_ts>/eurostat.ndjson (sensor-consumable). Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 5 scenarios: TEST 1 native SDMX-JSON 2.0 demo_pjan 2-dim cube (geo×time; 5/6 cells populated, missing IT 2024) with verified decoder correctness against real Eurostat population numbers (DE 83.1M/83.44M, FR 67.9M/68.17M, IT 58.7M) / TEST 2 3-dim cube (geo×unit×time) with unit-dim → valueUnit extraction (NAMA_10_GDP CP_MEUR for DE+FR 2024; verified unit does NOT leak into dimensions tuple) / TEST 3 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough (prc_hicp_manr IT 2026-04 missing-value preserved) / TEST 4 empty-dataflows ValueError guard / TEST 5 end-to-end fetcher → EuEurostatSensor 5-obs integration (DE 83.1M preserved + eurostat-free-reuse license_tag + source=eurostat). 5/5 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/sec_edgar.py" :adr "ADR-2605263800" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "SEC EDGAR full-index master.idx fetcher — fourth concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub; corp 2nd concrete fetcher). Tier-A public-domain (17 USC 105 / 17 CFR 200). W1 targets quarterly master.idx bulk archive (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/full-index/<YYYY>/<QTR>/master.idx) — single ~5-50MB pipe-delimited text file per quarter; covers every filing without per-CIK enumeration (operationally cheapest passive-only path). Two operator paths matching gleif/wb/eurostat pattern: (1) Network mode — httpx GET; year+quarter MUST both be set explicitly (passive-only: no implicit latest-quarter inference per ADR-2605262400 §7); SEC User-Agent guidance respected via DEFAULT_USER_AGENT with real contact email. (2) Local-source mode — read pre-staged master.idx OR pre-normalized NDJSON. Format auto-detect (leading '{' → NDJSON / else → master.idx pipe-parser). master.idx parser: skips ~11-line header until '---' dashed separator OR detects leading numeric CIK pipe-row as body start; pipe-split into (CIK, Company Name, Form Type, Date Filed, Filename); zero-pads CIK to 10 digits via _pad_cik; coerces Date Filed (YYYY-MM-DD) → ISO-8601 'T00:00:00Z'; uses Filename (EDGAR archive path) as payloadCid (W2 → actual IPFS CID after publish-ipfs). G7 schema discipline: rows with non-numeric CIK OR missing column OR malformed date → skip without halt. cik_allowlist + form_type_allowlist + max_records constructor filters. Output: <name>-<capture_ts>/raw-master.idx (forensic auditability) + sec-edgar.ndjson (sensor-consumable). Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial-terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). W2 will add per-CIK Submissions JSON + companyfacts XBRL paths. Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 6 scenarios: TEST 1 real EDGAR master.idx (Apple 10-K + MSFT 10-Q + JPM 8-K + Apple Form 4 + Vanguard 13F-HR + 1 BAD-CIK G7-skip; CIK zero-pad + date ISO-coerce verified) / TEST 2 cik_allowlist=Apple-only → 2 (10-K + Form 4) / TEST 3 form_type_allowlist=(10-K,10-Q) → 2 / TEST 4 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough (JPM 8-K w/ payloadCid preserved) / TEST 5 network-mode year+quarter ValueError guard / TEST 6 end-to-end fetcher → SecEdgarSensor 5-obs integration (Apple 10-K → form_class='annual-report' + public-domain license_tag preserved). 6/6 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/us_data_gov.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "US data.gov CKAN catalog fetcher — fifth concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub; gov 3rd concrete fetcher; first CKAN portal of the triad). Tier-A public-domain (17 USC 105). Two operator paths matching gleif/wb/eurostat/sec pattern: (1) Network mode — httpx GET against catalog.data.gov/api/3/action/package_search with start+rows pagination; optional server-side organization_filter (Solr fq) + free-text q query; loops via result.count until exhausted. (2) Local-source mode — read operator-staged CKAN JSON OR pre-normalized NDJSON. _iter_observations_from_payload dispatcher handles 4 input shapes: (a) native CKAN package_search response {result:{results:[...]}}; (b) single-pkg envelope {result: pkg_dict}; (c) flat list of pkg dicts; (d) operator pre-normalized sensor-shape rows preserved as-is. _normalize_ckan_pkg maps CKAN (name + title + license_id + id + notes + organization.name + organization.title + metadata_created) → sensor row (datasetId + title + license + payloadCid + descriptionExcerpt + organization + publisher + publishedAtUtc). Per-row license_id preserved through chain (e.g., cc-by sub-licensed datasets retain their override). max_records cap for memory-bounded operator runs. G7 schema discipline: rows missing required fields (name/title/license_id/id) skipped without halt. Output: <name>-<capture_ts>/us-data-gov.ndjson (sensor-consumable). Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 5 scenarios: TEST 1 native CKAN response (NOAA CDO + EPA AirData + CC-BY sub-licensed Some Agency + 1 G7-skip; per-row license override preserved) / TEST 2 flat list (FDA Drugs + Census ACS) / TEST 3 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough (NOAA tide w/ payloadCid preserved) / TEST 4 max_records=2 cap / TEST 5 end-to-end fetcher → UsDataGovSensor 3-obs integration (NOAA us-pd + agency cc-by license_tag override both preserved through chain). 5/5 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/uk_data_gov_uk.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "UK data.gov.uk CKAN catalog fetcher — sixth concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub; gov 4th concrete; CKAN portal triad #2 of 3). Tier-A OGL v3.0 (Crown copyright open license). Per-row license_id preserved (e.g., cc-by sub-licensed datasets). Same CKAN paging + 4-shape dispatcher pattern as us_data_gov.py. British English UX naming: constructor param organisation_filter (with 's') maps to CKAN core 'organization' Solr fq under the hood; output row uses British 'organisation' key (matching UkDataGovUkSensor expected shape). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 3 scenarios: TEST 1 native CKAN ONS GDP + MoJ Court Stats + cc-by sub-licensed (British 'organisation' key + cc-by override preserved) / TEST 2 end-to-end → UkDataGovUkSensor 3-obs / TEST 3 sensor organisation_filter='moj-gov-uk' → 1 obs. 3/3 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/jp_data_go_jp.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete-portal-triad-complete" :description "JP data.go.jp CKAN catalog fetcher — seventh concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub; gov 5th concrete; ═══ CKAN portal triad COMPLETE: us_data_gov + uk_data_gov_uk + jp_data_go_jp ═══). Tier-A CC-BY 4.0 (政府標準利用規約 2.0). Same CKAN paging + 4-shape dispatcher pattern as us_data_gov.py + uk_data_gov_uk.py. JP-specific: publisher field preserves CKAN organization.title (省庁 + 自治体 Japanese names like 総務省 / 総務省統計局 / 東京都); organization field uses American 'organization' (CKAN core spelling). W1 scope = data.go.jp CKAN only; e-Stat (政府統計の総合窓口) integration deferred to W2 (requires per-DID free appId + different API shape api.e-stat.go.jp/rest/3.0/app/json/getStatsList); fetch_estat=True with no local_source raises NotImplementedError pointing operator to W2 plan + the workaround (pre-stage combined data.go.jp + e-Stat NDJSON via local_source). G7 schema discipline + max_records cap + passive-only invariant per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 3 scenarios: TEST 1 native CKAN (人口統計 総務省 + 国勢調査 総務省統計局; 省庁名 Japanese preserved) / TEST 2 end-to-end → JpDataGoJpSensor 2-obs / TEST 3 e-Stat W2 NotImplementedError guard. 3/3 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/uk_companies_house.py" :adr "ADR-2605263800" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "UK Companies House Free Company Data Product (FCD) fetcher — eighth concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub; corp 3rd concrete). Tier-A OGL v3.0 (Crown copyright open license). W1 targets monthly bulk ZIP (~5GB) containing single CSV (~25GB uncompressed) at http://download.companieshouse.gov.uk/BasicCompanyDataAsOneFile-<YYYY-MM-01>.zip; covers ~5M UK companies. Two operator paths matching gleif/wb/eurostat/sec/us-data-gov pattern: (1) Network mode — httpx GET with 600s timeout (~5GB download); snapshot filename MUST be set explicitly (passive-only: no implicit latest-month inference). (2) Local-source mode — extension-aware dispatch: .zip → extract first .csv inside / .csv → stream-parse / .ndjson → pre-normalized pass-through. ZIP detection via PK signature byte-check (same as gleif_lei.py); first .csv inside extracted to staging out_dir. CSV stream-parse via stdlib csv.DictReader (header-aware; no full-file in-memory load); CompanyNumber upper-cased and validated against UK CRN regex `^(?:\\d{8}|[A-Z]{2}\\d{6})$` (matches UkCompaniesHouseSensor regex). _coerce_uk_date converts DD/MM/YYYY → ISO-8601 T00:00:00Z; malformed dates yield registeredAt=None (row still kept since IncorporationDate is optional per sensor schema). G7 schema discipline: rows missing CompanyNumber/CompanyName OR with malformed CRN skipped without halt. crn_allowlist + company_status_allowlist + max_records constructor filters. Output: <name>-<capture_ts>/<original-csv-name>.csv (extracted) + uk-companies-house.ndjson (sensor-consumable). Daily-increment catch-up deferred to W2. Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial-terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 7 scenarios: TEST 1 raw FCD CSV (9 rows → 8 yielded: Apple Europe + HSBC + NatWest SC + Diageo + Belfast NI + Baker LLP OC + lowercase SC + bad-date kept w/ registeredAt=None; TOO SHORT skip) / TEST 2 ZIP extract (real filename pattern BasicCompanyDataAsOneFile-2026-05-01.csv) / TEST 3 crn_allowlist=(Apple, NatWest) → 2 / TEST 4 company_status_allowlist=(Liquidation,) → 1 (Belfast NI only) / TEST 5 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough (Barclays Bank) / TEST 6 network-mode snapshot ValueError guard / TEST 7 end-to-end fetcher → UkCompaniesHouseSensor 8-obs integration (Apple Europe registered_at preserved + OGL-v3.0 license_tag chain). 7/7 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/jp_edinet.py" :adr "ADR-2605263800" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete-corp-fetcher-complete" :description "JP 金融庁 EDINET v2 documents API fetcher — ninth concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub; corp 4th concrete; ═══ corp W1 fetcher quartet COMPLETE: gleif_lei + sec_edgar + uk_companies_house + jp_edinet ═══). Tier-A 金融庁 open-data utilization terms (~CC-BY 4.0 practically). W1 targets v2 documents.json endpoint (date-bounded paging; one GET per day in date range; requires Subscription-Key header from free per-DID EDINET registration). Two operator paths matching gleif/sec/uk-ch pattern: (1) Network mode — httpx GET per day; date_from + date_to + api_key all required (passive-only: no implicit full-archive scan per ADR-2605262400 §7); per-document XBRL download deferred to W2. (2) Local-source mode — read pre-staged documents.json OR pre-normalized NDJSON. _SUBMIT_DT_RE parses EDINET submitDateTime format YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS+09:00 (JST or per-tz); _coerce_jst_to_utc converts to ISO-8601 T..Z via stdlib datetime + timezone arithmetic (e.g., 2025-06-23T07:00:00+09:00 → 2025-06-22T22:00:00Z verified). 3 input shape handler: native documents.json {metadata, results:[...]} / flat list / pre-normalized NDJSON envelope. doc_type_filter + max_records constructor filters. payloadCid = docID at W1; W2 → actual IPFS CID after publish-ipfs. EDINET response does NOT carry LEI (entityLei always null per W1); operator-side enrichment via LeiSensor cross-ref deferred to W2. G7 schema discipline: rows missing required fields (edinetCode/docID/submitDateTime/docTypeCode) OR with malformed submitDateTime skipped without halt. Per-jurisdiction publication-redaction policy: EDINET pass-through per ADR-2605263800 §5 (個人情報保護法 + 金融商品取引法 upstream-applied); GDPR-class DSARs route through chigiri.data_privacy. Output: <name>-<capture_ts>/jp-edinet.ndjson (sensor-consumable). Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial-terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 7 scenarios: TEST 1 native documents.json (Sony 有報 E01777/120 + Toyota 四半期 E02144/140 + SoftBank 臨時 E03182/160 + 大量保有 E99999/350; JST→UTC conversion verified for 07:00 JST → 22:00 prev-day UTC + 15:30 JST → 06:30 UTC; 2 G7-skip rows for missing-docID + malformed-datetime) / TEST 2 doc_type_filter=(120,140) → Sony+Toyota / TEST 3 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough (legacy 半期 S100LEGACY01) / TEST 4a date-range ValueError guard / TEST 4b api_key ValueError guard / TEST 5 end-to-end fetcher → JpEdinetSensor 4-obs integration (Sony 120→annual-report + Toyota 140→interim + SoftBank 160→material-event + 大量保有 350→institutional-holding; JST→UTC preserved through chain; fsa-open-data-utilization-terms license_tag chain). 7/7 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/us_congress_gov.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "US Congress.gov api.congress.gov v3 fetcher — tenth concrete W1 fetcher impl (supersedes the W0 NotImplementedError stub; Parliament triad #1 of 3). Tier-A public-domain (17 USC 105). W1 targets api.congress.gov v3 REST /v3/bill/<congress> endpoint with limit+offset pagination; X-Api-Key header required (free per-DID registration). W2 will add /v3/congressional-record + /v3/house-roll-call-vote + /v3/senate-roll-call-vote + /v3/committee-report endpoints + govinfo.gov bulkdata XML collections (BILLS/BILLSTATUS/CREC/FR). _BILL_TYPE_NATIVE table synthesizes sensor-compatible nativeKind from (chamber + bill type): House+HR → House Bill / Senate+S → Senate Bill / Either+HJRES/SJRES → Joint Resolution / Either+HCONRES/SCONRES → Concurrent Resolution / Either+HRES/SRES → Simple Resolution. recordId synthesized as BILLS-<congress><lower-type><number> (matches govinfo.gov bulkdata canonical IDs). payloadCid = api.congress.gov URL (W2 → actual IPFS CID after publish-ipfs). Two operator paths matching established pattern: (1) Network mode — paged GET; congress + api_key required (passive-only: no implicit latest-congress inference per ADR-2605262400 §7); optional fromDateTime + toDateTime query window. (2) Local-source mode — JSON OR NDJSON. 3-input shape dispatcher (api.congress.gov {bills:[]} / flat list / pre-normalized envelope). bill_type_allowlist + max_records constructor filters. G7 schema discipline: rows with unknown bill type OR missing/wrong chamber OR malformed date skipped without halt. Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 7 scenarios: TEST 1 native v3 bill response (5 rows → 3 yielded: HR1234 + S5678 + HJRES17 with nativeKind synthesis verified [House+HR→House Bill, Senate+S→Senate Bill, House+HJRES→Joint Resolution]; UNKNOWN bill type + WrongHouse chamber G7-skipped) / TEST 2 bill_type_allowlist=(S,) → 1 Senate bill only / TEST 3 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough (CREC debate w/ Hakeem Jeffries speaker info preserved) / TEST 4a congress ValueError guard / TEST 4b api_key ValueError guard / TEST 5 end-to-end fetcher → UsCongressGovSensor 3-obs integration (all 3 bills → record_kind='bill' via sensor's House Bill/Senate Bill/Joint Resolution → bill mapping; public-domain license_tag chain). 7/7 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/uk_hansard.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete" :description "UK Parliament Hansard search API fetcher — eleventh concrete W1 fetcher impl (Parliament triad #2 of 3). Tier-A OGL v3.0 (Open Parliament Licence ≡ Open Government Licence). W1 targets hansard-api.parliament.uk/search/debates.json endpoint with take/skip paging; no API key required (public open API). _synthesize_native_kind heuristic maps DebateSection string to sensor's nativeKind enum: 'Oral Answers...' → 'Oral Question'; 'Petition...' → 'Petition'; 'Division...' → 'Division'; 'Written Statement' → 'Written Statement'; 'Committee...' → 'Committee'; 'Bill ... Reading/Stage' → 'Bill Reading'; default → 'Debate'. _parse_attributed_to parses 'Wes Streeting (Ilford North) (Lab)' style strings into (name, role) — name from prefix-before-paren, role from parenthetical content joined by ' / '. _coerce_sitting_date normalizes SittingDate (Hansard ships without TZ — treated as UTC date-stamp for cross-actor consistency; date-only inputs append T00:00:00Z). payloadCid = published Url field OR synthesized hansard.parliament.uk URL (W2 → IPFS CID after publish-ipfs). Two operator paths matching established pattern: (1) Network mode — paged GET; start_date + end_date required (passive-only). (2) Local-source mode — JSON OR NDJSON. 3-input shape dispatcher. G7 schema discipline + max_records cap. Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 5 scenarios: TEST 1 native Hansard search (6 rows → 4 yielded: 'Oral Answers... Health' → Oral Question + AttributedTo 'Wes Streeting (Ilford North) (Lab)' → (Wes Streeting, 'Ilford North / Lab'); 'Petition: Council Tax' → Petition + Sir Lindsay Hoyle; 'Renters Rights Bill - Second Reading' → Bill Reading + Baroness Smith; 'Division' → Division; 2 G7-skip rows for bad house + missing required) / TEST 2 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough / TEST 3 start/end_date ValueError guard / TEST 4 end-to-end → UkHansardSensor 4-obs (Oral Question → record_kind='question' via sensor's _RECORD_KIND_MAP; speaker_name 'Wes Streeting' preserved; OGL-v3.0 license_tag chain). 5/5 PASS."}
  {:path "70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/jp_kokkai_kaigiroku.py" :adr "ADR-2605263900" :kind "dataset-fetcher-concrete" :status "w1-impl-landed-concrete-fetcher-parity-complete" :description "JP 国会会議録検索 NDL API fetcher — TWELFTH concrete W1 fetcher impl (Parliament triad #3 of 3; ═══ W1 FETCHER 12/12 PARITY COMPLETE: corp 4 (gleif_lei + sec_edgar + uk_companies_house + jp_edinet) + gov 8 (worldbank + eurostat + 3 CKAN data portals + 3 Parliament triad) ═══). Tier-A 国会会議録 公の著作物 free-use under 著作権法 §13. W1 targets kokkai.ndl.go.jp/api/meeting endpoint with from/until/startRecord paging; no API key required (NDL public open API). nameOfMeeting passes through directly as nativeKind (sensor's _RECORD_KIND_MAP already covers 本会議/予算委員会/委員会/代表質問/法律案/採決 etc.). First speechRecord entry's speaker + speakerPosition extracted for meeting-level preview (W2 will add granularity='speech' for per-speech splitting). _coerce_meeting_date converts YYYY-MM-DD → ISO-8601 T00:00:00Z. House values restricted to {衆議院, 参議院} via _HOUSE_VALUES set check (G7 schema: bad house → skip). payloadCid prefers meetingURL → pdfURL → issueID. Two operator paths matching established pattern. 3-input shape dispatcher (NDL meetingRecord / flat list / NDJSON envelope). house + max_records constructor filters. from_date + until_date required in network mode (passive-only). Passive-only invariant boundary per ADR-2605262400 §7. Vendor commercial gov-intel terminal imports CONSTITUTIONALLY PROHIBITED per Charter Rider §2(e)+§2(c). Smoke-tested 2026-05-27 with 4 scenarios: TEST 1 native NDL meeting (6 → 4: 衆議院 額賀議長 本会議 + 参議院 石破総理 予算委員会 + 衆議院 法律案 empty-speechRecord + 参議院 野田議員 代表質問; bad house 英国議会 + missing required G7-skip; nameOfMeeting → nativeKind pass-through + first-speaker extraction verified) / TEST 2 NDJSON pre-normalized passthrough (起立採決) / TEST 3 from+until_date ValueError guard / TEST 4 end-to-end → JpKokkaiKaigirokuSensor (本会議 → record_kind='debate' via sensor's _RECORD_KIND_MAP; speaker_name 額賀福志郎 + speaker_role 議長 preserved; ndl-public-record-free-use license_tag chain). 4/4 PASS. ═══ W1 FETCHER 12/12 PARITY ACHIEVED ═══"}
