  {:id "no-server-key-stage-c2-c3-c4-auth-worker-key-devolution" :status "pending" :blocked_on "Stage C-1 complete → vertex_etzhayyim_key_signing.private_key_b64 D1 schema migration drops column → per-agent com.etzhayyim.auth.createAgentSession refactored to expect device-generated public key + WebAuthn PoP → 30-day SS_REPO_SIGNING_KEK quarantine window with zero reads logged → wrangler secret delete SS_REPO_SIGNING_KEK" :authoritative_doc "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-auth/STAGE-C-IDENTITY-SIGNING-DEVOLUTION.md" :authoritative_adr "ADR-2605231525" :scope "auth Worker: per-agent ES256 keypair generation (715+ keys), AT Protocol session JWT HS256 signing, SS_REPO_SIGNING_KEK envelope encryption master" :description "Stage C-2: agent runtime generates own P-256 keypair via WebCrypto crypto.subtle.generateKey on the operator's own device, POSTs public key + WebAuthn-style PoP attestation to com.etzhayyim.auth.registerAgentKey. auth Worker stores only public key in vertex_etzhayyim_key_signing projection. Stage C-3: WebAuthn passkey derives ES256 session keypair on member's device; session token becomes DPoP-style PoP signed by passkey. Stage C-4: SS_REPO_SIGNING_KEK 30-day quarantine (worker logs all reads, expects zero) then secret deletion. kotoba-datomic-projection manifest at 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-auth/kotoba-datomic-projection.edn already declares D1 AUTH_DB / KEYS_DB tables as L0-rebuildable from com.etzhayyim.encrypted.record envelopes (ADR-2605181100) keyed innerType = com.etzhayyim.auth.credential — scaffold APPLIED for the projection contract; the integration into passkeyVerifyRegister / linkOAuthStart / linkEmailVerify / smsOtpSend handlers is the Stage C-2 PR." :last_verified "2026-05-23"}
  {:id "no-server-key-stage-d-external-api-handover" :status "pending" :blocked_on "Stage B per-pod handover progresses → each upstream credential (RESEND_API_KEY / B2_* / MAPILLARY_ACCESS_TOKEN / RUNPOD_API_KEY / ODPT_API_KEY / EMBED_AUTH_TOKEN) moves with the corresponding pod's operator → wrangler secret delete on each Worker, kubectl delete secret on each pod" :authoritative_doc "_working/STAGE-D-EXTERNAL-API-HANDOVER.md" :authoritative_adr "ADR-2605231525" :target_count 6 :scope "External SaaS / cloud credentials currently held by etzhayyim-operated Workers + pods: RESEND (auth + yatabase email), Backblaze B2 (maps bulk-ingest blob upload), Mapillary (gsplat trainer), RunPod (gsplat trainer GPU), ODPT (gtfs-rt realtime feeds), EMBED service-to-service token (maps embedder)" :description "Each external integration migrates to a community-operator-owned credential. etzhayyim publishes only the lexicon (inbound record shape) — never the credential. Inbound lexicons: Resend/SMTP → com.etzhayyim.apps.email.outbox + delivered; B2/S3/IPFS → com.etzhayyim.encrypted.record.ciphertextBlob CID; Mapillary → com.etzhayyim.maps.gsplatAsset; RunPod → com.etzhayyim.maps.gsplatJob (carries cost_usd); ODPT → com.etzhayyim.maps.vehiclePosition/tripUpdate/serviceAlert; Embedder → com.etzhayyim.maps.visionResult. Sequencing depends on Stage B per-pod handover. Acceptance: zero hard-coded credential VALUES in any etzhayyim-operated wrangler.jsonc / k8s manifest / GitHub Action." :last_verified "2026-05-23"}
  {:id "no-server-key-stage-e-internal-hmac-dissolution" :status "pending" :blocked_on "Stages A-D complete → no internal Worker ↔ pod path remains across an etzhayyim-owned trust boundary → wrangler secret delete DISPATCHER_INTERNAL_SECRET on every Worker + kubectl delete secret on bpmn-dispatcher → wrangler secret delete YATA_AGENT_ADMIN_KEY → admin surfaces migrated to Council Safe multisig (1 SBT = 1 vote)" :authoritative_doc "90-docs/adr/2605231525-no-server-key-religious-corp-architecture.md §4 Stage E" :authoritative_adr "ADR-2605231525" :scope "DISPATCHER_INTERNAL_SECRET (Worker ↔ bpmn-dispatcher HMAC), YATA_AGENT_ADMIN_KEY (single-operator admin gate for yatabase outbox approve + batch trigger), per-agent ES256 keypair shared-secret fallback" :description "Once Stages A-D land, the remaining etzhayyim-internal trust boundaries dissolve. DISPATCHER_INTERNAL_SECRET disappears with the last internal pod (Stage B removes bulk-ingest pods; remaining bpmn-dispatcher proxies XRPC through public PDS firehose subscription). YATA_AGENT_ADMIN_KEY admin surfaces (yatabase outbox approve, batch usage-alert trigger) migrate to ChartersComplianceRegistry attestation via Council Lv6+ multisig (1 SBT = 1 vote per ADR-2605192300 §3-tier enforcement). Acceptance: e7m verify --no-server-key reports zero violations + zero exemptions across the entire monorepo." :last_verified "2026-05-23"}
  {:id "tsukuru-nsid-com-etzhayyim-conversion-2606020000" :status "complete" :authoritative_doc "90-docs/adr/2606020000-tsukuru-com-etzhayyim-nsid-conversion.md" :authoritative_adr "ADR-2606020000" :overrides "repo-wide com.etzhayyim.apps.* standard, for tsukuru namespace only (operator-directed)" :scope "87 files: 46 tsukuru lexicons (id + git mv com/etzhayyim/etzhayyim/apps/tsukuru → com/etzhayyim/apps/tsukuru), kotoba + orchestration + kotodama.toml + 20-actors/tsukuru, cross-app refs (aidesk/hc/open-robo/kotodama cells/graph seed migrations/ADRs), catalog dir, 7 generated registries" :description "Operator-directed follow-up to ADR-2606011700 (hakken com.etzhayyim). Converts tsukuru from main's com.etzhayyim.apps.tsukuru.* to com.etzhayyim.apps.tsukuru.* so the two sibling OEM-discovery ingest actors share one namespace. Mechanical 87-file rename, symmetric diff, no behavioural change. Payment (com.etzhayyim.apps.payment.* — escrowOpened/escrowRefunded/sent, shared authority read by treasury/tithe) is NOT renamed. lexicons.gen.json REGENERATED (build-bundle.mjs); _manifest/apps.openapi/docs.json/graph.jsonld/bpmn-coverage/process-catalog updated via contained token+path swap (full registry regen via CI/maintainer recommended). DIVERGENCE: tsukuru+hakken are now the only com.etzhayyim.apps.* record actors vs repo-wide com.etzhayyim.* standard (15758 vs now ~tsukuru/hakken); com vs app record-NSID convention still needs org ruling — if standardised on com.etzhayyim both revert in one sweep. Deploy prereq: gen-pds-lexicon-registry.mjs + Worker redeploy." :last_verified "2026-06-02"}
  {:id "hakken-etzhayyim-ingest-migration-override-2606011700" :status "code-moved-etzhayyim-refactor-pending" :authoritative_doc "90-docs/adr/2606011700-hakken-etzhayyim-migration-override.md" :authoritative_adr "ADR-2606011700" :overrides "vendor ADR-2606011400 (Consensys pattern) — hakken vendor-keep verdict" :scope "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-hakken (scaffold + kotoba ingest + lg/lg_hakken pipeline), 00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/hakken/* (4 lexicons)" :description "User-directed move (2026-06-01) of hakken's product-discovery INGEST FRONT (trend_scan / gap_analysis / supplier_search / quality_eval + branded-product + supplier-candidate write path) to etzhayyim, overriding the same-day vendor-keep verdict of vendor ADR-2606011400. Structure of 2606011400 preserved: product front → etzhayyim, regulated fulfillment tail (okaimono_register Ph1 dropship + Stripe, import_order Ph2, tsukuru_order Ph3) stays a etzhayyim function consumed via consent capability. Phase 1 (DONE): scaffold + 4 com.etzhayyim.apps.hakken.* lexicons + kotoba ingest reference (@etzhayyim/sdk e.write, kotoba + on-chain, float→integer encoding weightG/ratingMilli). Vendor hakken.etzhayyim.com unchanged. NSID = com.etzhayyim.apps.hakken.* by operator direction; OPEN: reconcile vs the com.etzhayyim.* record-NSID convention used elsewhere in repo (consent/council/encrypted/esign). Phase 2: rehome LangGraph discovery nodes to etzhayyim Murakumo fleet. Phase 3: fulfillment via etzhayyim consent capability. Phase 4: vendor discovery-node sunset. SIBLING (separate PR): main already migrated tsukuru to com.etzhayyim.apps.tsukuru.* (~86 files, repo-wide com.etzhayyim.* standard = 15758 occ vs 0 com.etzhayyim). Per operator direction tsukuru will be converted to com.etzhayyim.apps.tsukuru.* in a DEDICATED follow-up PR (overrides merged work + 4 generated registries regen); this hakken PR does not touch tsukuru. Payment stays shared com.etzhayyim.apps.payment.* (different authority). UPDATE 2026-06-02 (session close): all PRs MERGED — #697 (contract surface) + #724 (actual LangGraph pipeline code moved from vendor VERBATIM: lg/lg_hakken graph/state/edn/kotoba/kotoba_datomic + 11 nodes + pyproject/uv.lock/wasm, byte-identical to vendor HEAD) + #718 (tsukuru → com.etzhayyim, ADR-2606020000). Moved code is UN-REFACTORED by design (still references vendor kotoba/RW/Stripe + com.etzhayyim.* NSIDs); refactor (RW→kotoba/PDS, Stripe tail→etzhayyim consent capability, com.etzhayyim.*→com.etzhayyim.*, wire pipeline to kotoba ingest) happens on the etzhayyim side per operator. Vendor hakken.etzhayyim.com unchanged (Phase 4 sunset pending stable etzhayyim deploy). Ingest-actor CODE MOVE complete; remaining = etzhayyim-side refactor + LangGraph pod rehome/deploy + vendor sunset (operator/infra, not code moves)." :last_verified "2026-06-02"}
