 :session_summaries {:ameno-wave-2026-05-19 {:date "2026-05-19" :chronicle "90-docs/ameno-wave-session-2026-05-19.md" :adrs_added 19 :prs_merged ["#62" "#64" "#66" "#68"] :description "Ameno browser-daemon ecosystem wave: 17 ADRs land the\nTier-2 browser appview (MediaPipe Gemma 4 + reflection + active\ninference + ReAct tools + long-term memory vault + multi-tab swarm\n+ viewer mode), Path A (Bun/Node) + Path B (Python kotodama)\nheadless daemons, full K3s Mac-mini-fleet deploy (lima-k3s dry-run +\nlg-ameno + ollama-fleet + ameno-ingress + anchor-cron-ameno),\nsubstrate pipeline activation (MstCheckpointSaver Stage 2 + IPFS\nStage 3 + L2 anchor Stage 4 manifests), `com.etzhayyim.swarm.lease`\nlex schema, did:key Ed25519 challenge-response auth with allowlist,\nbrowser ↔ daemon checkpoint pull-sync, swarm leader election, and\nADR-2605172000/172100 substrate-boundary enforcement at both\nlefthook pre-commit and CI levels." :follow_up ["substrate swarm lease MST write impl (lex shape committed)" "bi-directional checkpoint sync (push from browser + LWW)" "HTTP Message Signatures (RFC 9421) full body signing" "Signal Protocol did:key binding (ADR-2605181100 integration)" "anchor-cron monitoring + alerting" "native macOS Ollama ansible (DaemonSet alternative)" "browser CryptoKey HSM (replace localStorage JWK)" "memory vault inspector UI" "CF exit ADR (long-term self-host)" "end-to-end automated smoke test runner"]} :yobel-amnesty-debt-release-wave-2026-05-20 {:date "2026-05-20" :adrs_added 2 :prs_merged [] :prs_open ["#73 (yobel)" "#75 (amnesty)" "etzhayyim#1312 (vendor cross-actor wire)"] :description "Religious-corp doctrinal runtime for monetary debt release.\nTwo symmetric sibling actors fill the Charter §1 (構造的労働解放)\nmonetary-debt dimension under voluntary opt-in + Council ratification +\n3-axis split governance.\n\n  yobel.etzhayyim.com   (ADR-2605201800) — natural-person (自然人) only\n    shmita 7yr / yobel 50yr / 徳政令 / Catholic Jubilee /\n    political_amnesty (= mass amnesty for individual debtors).\n    8 lexicons + 5 LangGraph cells (judah/gad/issachar/asher/reuben) +\n    YobelOrchestrator + 2 Solidity contracts + 3 web3 ports + EIP-712\n    signed-consent verifier. 72 pytest unit + 4 anvil integration +\n    28 forge tests + 1024-run fuzz of one-way invariant + shmita 5786\n    fixture dry-run golden check.\n\n  amnesty.etzhayyim.com (ADR-2605202000) — legal-person counterpart\n    sovereign_multilateral (HIPC / Paris Club) / sovereign_bilateral /\n    corporate_chapter_11 (≥ 2/3 each impaired class per §1126(c)) /\n    corporate_workout / debt_for_nature_swap.\n    8 lexicons + project marker (Phase 1 ADR + lexicons only; cells +\n    Solidity + governance deferred to follow-up PRs).\n\nDefense-in-depth: lexicon schema enum (single-value 'natural_person' for\nyobel debtorEntityType, excludes natural_person for amnesty) → cell DMN\nR14/A14 short-circuit gates → Solidity revert for §2(b) one-way\nviolation (1024-run fuzz). Symmetric mutual deferral: yobel returns\ndeferToAmnesty=true for legal-person debtors; amnesty returns\ndeferToYobel=true for natural-person debtors.\n\nCross-repo: vendor etzhayyim#1312 adds the consumer-side\nrecordYobelRiteReference lexicon + yobel-bridge CLI utility + 12 anvil\nintegration tests + vendor:bankruptcy CLAUDE.md cross-actor doc.\nAmnesty counterpart (recordAmnestyRestructuringReference) follows in\nlater vendor PR." :follow_up ["amnesty Phase 2-7 (BPMN + cells + tests + Solidity + web3 + governance)" "vendor:bankruptcy recordAmnestyRestructuringReference lexicon" "Council Lv6+ × 3 + Lv9 chair ratification of ADR-2605201800" "Council Lv9 × 3 + Five-Bootstrap ratification of ADR-2605202000" "Base Sepolia deploy + verify YobelRiteRegistry + YobelReleaseRegistry" "vendor:bankruptcy CF Worker scaffold (S0 → S1 graduation)" "yoro UI Card for rite browsing (debtor + creditor self-service)" "Charter Rider §2 compliance scanner (automated regression防御)"]} :public-malak-scaffold-2026-05-21 {:date "2026-05-21" :prs_open [] :description "public-malak.etzhayyim.com — Phase 1 scaffold mirror landed.\n\nVendor (etzhayyim/etzhayyim-root) deps.edn\n`tranche-f-public-malak-classification-2026-05-20` (status\n`judgment-recorded`) confirmed public-malak as an etzhayyim move target\nvia 3-axis OR-test (Liability + Custody + Settlement all clean — TLP\nCLEAR/GREEN only, no fiat, no citizen PII).\n\nThis commit lands the etzhayyim-side scaffold mirror so the project\nboundary is recorded in this repo before the worker rewrite happens:\n\n  60-apps/etzhayyim-project-public-malak/\n    CLAUDE.md       — etzhayyim-domain spec + Tranche F status + substrate notes\n    OWNERS          — junkawasaki approver/reviewer\n    PROJECT.jsonld  — Phase 1-4 milestone roadmap (scaffold → kotoba → corpus → vendor sunset)\n    kotodama.jsonld — public-malak.etzhayyim.com manifest (did:web:public-malak.etzhayyim.com)\n  00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/publicMalak/\n    14 lexicons sed-mirrored from vendor (5 procedure + 9 query)\n\netzhayyim already had the BPMN (00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/public-malak/\n{analyzeAd,crawlAds}.bpmn) since the earlier Tranche F wave.\n\n## Deferred (per user direction 2026-05-21)\n\n- **kotoba implementation**: `src/app.ts` + per-domain kotoba modules\n  defer until project切り分け is complete across all Tranche F move\n  targets. The Phase E pattern (cnt.ts / escrow.ts in tsukuru kotoba)\n  is the reference once we resume.\n- **Corpus residency activation**: Option A (vendor RW mirror;\n  etzhayyim worker ingests fresh from public APIs) is the\n  architectural choice, mirroring ADR-2605202400 GTFS-RT carve-out.\n  No code change today — the 923-file `data/ingest/` corpus stays\n  vendor-side as historical artifact; activation happens when the\n  etzhayyim worker lands in Phase 2.\n- **Vendor sunset**: vendor 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-public-malak/\n  project dir + lexicons retained until etzhayyim worker passes the\n  7-day soak per ADR-2605211000 tier-1 pattern.\n\n## Cross-repo\n\n- vendor: `tranche-f-public-malak-classification-2026-05-20` (judgment-recorded — unchanged this PR)\n- etz BPMN: `00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/public-malak/{analyzeAd,crawlAds}.bpmn` (present pre-this-PR)\n- ADR refs: 2605172000 (kotoba substrate) / 2605172400 (3-axis split rule) / 2605203000 (Phase E write-target) / 2605202400 (GTFS-RT carve-out pattern) / 2605211000 (worker XRPC deploy runbook)" :follow_up ["Phase 2 kotoba implementation (src/app.ts + ad-library API ingest + PDS XRPC writes)" "Phase 3 corpus residency Option A activation (vendor B2 mirror retention contract)" "Phase 4 vendor sunset (etzhayyim git rm of 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-public-malak/ + publicMalak/ lexicons)" "Worker XRPC adapter wiring per ADR-2605211000 (when kotoba lands; public-malak slots into Tier 1 or Tier 2 depending on user-session exposure)"]} :open-jpn-mynumber-carve-out-2026-05-21 {:date "2026-05-21" :prs_open [] :description "open-jpn-mynumber.etzhayyim.com — Tranche F classification +\ncorpus residency Option A recorded.\n\nVendor (etzhayyim/etzhayyim-root) deps.edn\n`tranche-f-open-jpn-mynumber-classification-2026-05-20` judged this\nproject an etzhayyim move target (3-axis OR-test all clean: PUBLIC\ngov-published policy docs, no fiduciary, no citizen PII, no commerce).\nThe vendor classification entry also recommended Option A (vendor RW\nmirror) for the 923-file ~177 MB corpus.\n\n## Cross-repo state at this commit\n\n| Artifact | Vendor | etzhayyim |\n|---|---|---|\n| Spec / CLAUDE.md | absent | present (pre-existing 2026-04-26) |\n| Worker / BPMN / DMN / forms / lg / ingest | absent | present (full project dir) |\n| Lexicons (openJpnMynumber/health.json) | present → mirrored | present (this commit) |\n| Corpus blobs (~177 MB) | present (data/ingest/) | absent (read-fresh) |\n| corpus.sqlite3 / corpus.jsonl / manifest.json | present | absent |\n\n## What this commit lands\n\n- `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/openJpnMynumber/health.json` —\n  the single health lexicon mirrored from vendor (vendor has only 1\n  lexicon for this project; not 14 like publicMalak).\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-jpn-mynumber/CLAUDE.md` — adds Tranche F\n  status section + cross-repo state table + substrate-boundary notes.\n  Domain reference flipped from `*.etzhayyim.com` → `*.etzhayyim.com`.\n- This session_summary entry.\n\n## Corpus residency Option A — activated, not migrated\n\nPer ADR-2605172000 (etzhayyim kotoba substrate), large blob corpora\ndo not belong in etzhayyim-root git. Vendor classification entry\nrecommended Option A: vendor corpus stays as historical mirror;\netzhayyim worker reads fresh from gov sources (data.go.jp + 自治体\n公開 PDF/Excel/HTML). Same shape as ADR-2605202400 GTFS-RT carve-out\nand public-malak Phase 3.\n\nNo worker code change in this PR. The existing etz worker already\ningests fresh from gov sources; the activation is purely the policy\ndecision to leave vendor `data/ingest/` in place rather than mirror\ninto IPFS pinner (deferred Option B).\n\n## Deferred\n\n- IPFS pinner (Option B) — Tier 2 follow-up if 50-infra/ipfs-pinner\n  matures; no current need.\n- Worker kotoba audit — per user direction 2026-05-21, kotoba\n  quality fixes are post-migration.\n- Vendor sunset of `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-jpn-mynumber/data/` —\n  retained per Option A; not slated for deletion.\n\n## Cross-repo\n\n- vendor: `tranche-f-open-jpn-mynumber-classification-2026-05-20`\n  (judgment-recorded; this PR triggers a follow-up amend to add\n  `code_side_complete = true` + `corpus_residency = \"vendor-mirror-option-a\"`)\n- ADR refs: 2605172000 (kotoba substrate) / 2605172400 (3-axis split\n  rule) / 2605202400 (GTFS-RT carve-out, same pattern)" :follow_up ["Phase 2 worker kotoba audit (deferred — post-migration per user direction)" "Vendor amend: add code_side_complete=true to tranche-f-open-jpn-mynumber-classification-2026-05-20" "Phase 3 corpus residency Option B (IPFS pinner) — Tier 2 follow-up only if 50-infra/ipfs-pinner matures"]} :dougaka-split-confirmed-2026-05-21 {:date "2026-05-21" :prs_open [] :description "dougaka SPLIT — etzhayyim-side confirmation of the\nmechanically-in-effect split state per vendor\n`tranche-f-s6-dougaka-split-confirmation-2026-05-20`.\n\n## SPLIT shape (per vendor classification entry)\n\nC-group SPLIT pattern: lexicon JSON → etzhayyim; team-based production\nworkflow with customer custody (lg/ pod) → vendor.\n\n## Cross-repo state (2026-05-21 audit)\n\n| Artifact | Vendor (etzhayyim/etzhayyim-root) | etzhayyim (this repo) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lexicons (`apps/dougaka/`) | present (2 JSON files) | **present** (`health.json`, `render.json` — 2 files, already mirrored Phase 3 wave 6) |\n| BPMN (`bpmn/com/etzhayyim/dougaka/`) | absent | absent |\n| Project dir (`60-apps/etzhayyim-project-dougaka/`) | present — only `lg/` subtree | absent (matches SPLIT — pod is vendor) |\n| `lg/` LangGraph pod | **present** (Python — render.py uses B2 keys per vendor 3-axis judgment) | absent (per ADR-2605172000 kotoba + per SPLIT) |\n| kotodama primitives | (none specific to dougaka) | n/a |\n\n## Why no etzhayyim project dir\n\nPer the vendor SPLIT confirmation entry: the C-group production\nworkflow with B2-backed customer custody (video rendering pipeline)\nstays vendor-side per all 3 axes (Liability/Custody/Settlement HIT\non the pod). Only the lexicons cross the boundary because they're\nspec-only — no operator binding.\n\netzhayyim consumers that need dougaka lexicons (e.g., for cross-actor\ncontract checks) import them from\n`00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/dougaka/`.\n\n## What this commit lands\n\n- This session_summary entry (no code changes — the SPLIT is already\n  in effect mechanically).\n\n## Deferred / not in scope\n\n- BPMN for dougaka — neither side has any. Add per use-case if a\n  workflow becomes necessary.\n- kotodama primitives for dougaka — none today; vendor lg/ pod\n  handles render orchestration directly.\n- Vendor sunset — out of scope; the lg/ pod is structurally vendor.\n\n## Cross-repo\n\n- vendor: `tranche-f-s6-dougaka-split-confirmation-2026-05-20`\n  (judgment-recorded; bulk closure marked\n  `code_side_complete = true` via\n  `tranche-f-vendor-confirmed-actors-closure-2026-05-21` PR #1336)\n- ADR refs: 2605172000 (kotoba substrate) / 2605172400 (3-axis split\n  rule, C-group SPLIT pattern)" :follow_up ["No follow-up — SPLIT is the steady state. Re-check on quarterly Tranche F re-judgment cycle (2026-08-17 / 2026-11-17 / 2027-02-17 per ADR-2605172400)."]} :ransomwatch-scaffold-2026-05-21 {:date "2026-05-21" :prs_open [] :description "ransomwatch.etzhayyim.com — Phase 1 scaffold mirror landed.\n\nVendor `etzhayyim/etzhayyim-root` deps.edn\n`tranche-f-post-freeze-7-actors-audit-2026-05-21` (vendor PR #1339,\naudit-recorded) classified ransomwatch as MOVE TARGET: 3-axis OR-test\nall clean (TLP:WHITE public OSINT, no victim PII, no commerce), and\nthe vendor `kotodama.jsonld` already declared `profile.operator =\n\"etzhayyim\"`. This commit formalizes the existing intent.\n\n## What this commit lands\n\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-ransomwatch/{CLAUDE.md, OWNERS,\n  PROJECT.jsonld, kotodama.jsonld}` — scaffold mirror sed-transformed\n  for etzhayyim domain (`did:web:ransomwatch.etzhayyim.com`)\n- `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/ransomwatch/` — 4 lexicons\n  (seedGroup procedure + listGroups/listPosts/getStats queries)\n  mirrored from vendor\n- This session_summary entry\n\n## Cross-repo state at this commit\n\n| Artifact | Vendor (etzhayyim) | etzhayyim (this repo) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Spec / CLAUDE.md | absent (only kotodama.jsonld + wrangler.jsonc at appview path) | present (this commit) |\n| Lexicons (apps/ransomwatch/) | present (4 JSON) | present (this commit, mirrored) |\n| Worker / appview | present (vendor wasm/etzhayyim-wasm-ransomwatch-r4ns0w4t01/) | absent (Phase 2 follow-up) |\n| LangGraph pod | present (in-cluster ransomwatch-l