s net-positive (surfaces +server.ts routes that the previous stub silently dropped) but deserves explicit awareness on every future build"]} :gemma4-26b-a4b-mac-mini-m4-disk-inference-260525 {:closed_at "2026-05-25T20:30 JST" :adr "2605253000" :status_row "n/a" :host "Mac mini M4 base (16GB unified memory, 10-GPU-core)" :model "gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-UD-Q3_K_M.gguf (12.73 GB on disk, Unsloth Dynamic)" :download_source "huggingface.co/unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF" :runtime "llama.cpp b9290 + ggml 0.12.0 (Homebrew)" :working_invocation "llama-cli -m <model> -ngl 0 -c 2048 -fa 1 -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 -t 4 -no-cnv -st --simple-io < /dev/null -p <prompt>" :measured_generation_tok_s 8.4 :measured_prompt_eval_tok_s 3.5 :measured_first_token_latency_sec 80 :measured_wall_time_sec 113 :measured_peak_rss_gb 8.5 :measured_peak_memory_footprint_gb 7.2 :measured_page_faults 2300000 :measured_swaps 0 :metal_recommended_max_working_set_mb 12713.12 :failed_paths ["Metal full offload (-ngl 99): res=-3, exceeds 12.7 GB Metal working set" "Metal partial offload (-ngl 4,8,12,16): res=-3, gemma4 MoE expert tensors not splittable" "--no-conversation alone: gemma4 chat template forces interactive mode, dropped to `>` prompt, 57 min idle wait, 2.5 GB swap accumulated, 942k swapouts"] :mandatory_flag_set "-no-cnv -st --simple-io < /dev/null (all three required, gemma4 chat template aggressive)" :tb5_ssd_speedup_prediction "1.5-1.85× → 12.5-15.5 tok/s generation" :tb5_ssd_speedup_basis "Current 119 ms/token breakdown: ~9.5 ms compute (3.8B active × 2 FMA / 800 GFLOPS) + ~110 ms disk read (92% disk-bound). TB5 SSD real-world 6.0-6.4 GB/s vs internal 3.1 GB/s ≈ 2× raw bandwidth → disk time halves to ~55 ms → total ~64.5 ms/token → ~15.5 tok/s upper bound. Lower bound 12.5 tok/s accounts for 4K random read IOPS bottleneck (Apple internal SSD ~700k IOPS comparable to TB5 enclosures 600-900k)." :tb5_ssd_speedup_prediction_post_empirical_correction_260525_2130 "OVERESTIMATED. Empirical A/B (internal AP0256Z 2.30 GB/s vs SanDisk USB 3.2 Gen 2 0.836 GB/s, 2.75× raw bandwidth gap) showed generation tok/s 7.7 vs 7.9 = only +3% delta. MoE × mmap hot working set (active 9/128 experts × ~100 MB held in page cache) makes steady-state generation STORAGE-INDEPENDENT. Disk bandwidth only matters for cold-load first-token (~80 sec wall). Revised TB5 prediction: steady-state generation +3-5% (= 8.0-8.8 tok/s, NOT 12.5-15.5), cold-load -50% (~80 sec → ~40 sec). TB5 investment justified ONLY for interactive chat UX (many short turns) not batch throughput. See ADR-2605253015 and 70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/results/baseline-260525.md for full A/B data." :tb5_correction_authority "ADR-2605253015 (this correction lands as part of nvme-disk-inference substrate project R0 wave)" :recommended_tb5_candidates ["OWC Envoy Ultra (TB5, claims 6 GB/s sustained, thermal-managed)" "Acasis TBU401E enclosure + WD SN850X 2TB (modular, ~6 GB/s)"] :constitutional_compliance ["ADR-2605215000 Murakumo-only inference: Mac mini M4 already fleet node, no commercial GPU rental" "ADR-2605241900 baien edge-target untouched: fleet-side path only, iPhone/Android/WASM-32 trunk still ≤4B BitNet 1.58" "ADR-2605215000 §2 no commercial GPU rental: NVMe + internal mmap only"] :followup_required ["TB5 SSD A/B benchmark (separate ADR; hardware purchase decision)" "fleet.toml entry for gemma-4-26B-A4B-it on Mac mini M4 nodes (currently only EVO-X2 judah serves it)" "Speculative decoding investigation: draft=gemma3:4b (EVO-X2 LAN) / target=gemma-4-26B-A4B (Mac mini M4 local)" "Context extension >2048: peak RSS approaches 16 GB ceiling at ctx 4096, swap thrashing risk"] :durable_artifacts ["90-docs/adr/2605253000-mac-mini-m4-16gb-gemma4-26b-moe-disk-inference.md" "~/Models/gemma-4-26B-A4B/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-UD-Q3_K_M.gguf (12.73 GB; local-only, not committed)"] :upstream_references ["Apple LLM in a Flash (ICLR 2026)" "ml-explore/mlx Issue #3393 (gemma4 MoE bug on base M4 10-core GPU; rationale for llama.cpp backend choice)" "Modelfit: Qwen3.5-35B-A3B UD-IQ3_XXS @ 17.3 tok/s on Mac mini M4 16GB (peer reference for MoE disk inference feasibility)"]} :nvme-disk-inference-storage-tier-ab-260525 {:opened_at "2026-05-25T21:30 JST" :adr "2605253015" :parent_adr "2605253000" :status "R0 scaffold landed, R1 TB4 enclosure A/B pending hardware procurement" :project_path "70-tools/nvme-disk-inference" :finding_summary "Steady-state generation throughput is STORAGE-INDEPENDENT for MoE × mmap disk inference on Mac mini M4 16GB. SanDisk USB 3.2 Gen 2 (0.836 GB/s raw) achieves 7.9 tok/s vs internal AP0256Z NVMe (2.30 GB/s raw) at 7.7 tok/s = +3% delta despite 2.75× raw bandwidth gap. Wall time +7% (cold-load only)." :measured_internal_ap0256z {:raw_read_gb_s 2.3 :gen_tok_s 7.7 :prompt_tok_s 3.2 :wall_sec 119.0 :peak_rss_gb 10.3 :page_faults 2348015 :swaps 0} :measured_sandisk_usb32_gen2 {:raw_read_gb_s 0.836 :gen_tok_s 7.9 :prompt_tok_s 3.1 :wall_sec 127.7 :peak_rss_gb 9.99 :page_faults 2327311 :swaps 0} :sandisk_device_id "USB 0x781:0x55BB SanDisk Extreme Portable SSD (UsbLinkSpeed 10 Gbps, USB 3.2 Gen 2)" :mechanism "MoE 9/128 active experts × ~100 MB held in 8-10 GB macOS page cache; per-token disk read only on expert turnover (~6.25%) = ~85-170 MB/token = ~0.7-1.3 GB/s effective demand at 7.9 tok/s = within both tiers" :mechanism_deep_5_layer_analysis "ROOT CAUSE — why ADR-2605253000 §5 prediction overestimated by 15×:\n\nPredicted: per-token = compute (9.5 ms) + disk read (110 ms), disk = active_params (1.5 GB) / disk_bandwidth\nReality:   per-token disk demand = 1-13 MB, not 1.5 GB\n\nLayer 1 — MoE expert sparsity (known but insufficient): 9/128 = 7% active → 105 MB/token UPPER BOUND\nLayer 2 — Router routing stability (BLIND SPOT): adjacent tokens have STRONG router correlation; only 0.5-1 expert changes per token (not all 8) → marginal new = 6-13 MB/token. Was the largest miss in the prediction.\nLayer 3 — macOS unified memory page cache LRU: 16 GB RAM × ~60% = ~10 GB cache budget; hot expert set (20-30 experts = 3-5 GB) stays resident; cache hit rate ~80-90% after warm-up → marginal disk demand = 1-2 MB/token\nLayer 4 — Compute UNDERESTIMATED: predicted 9.5 ms FMA only; actual ~50-75 ms (Q3_K_M→FP16 dequant 20-30 + matmul 10 + attention KV q8_0 r/w 15-20 + softmax+LN 5-10 + sampling 2-5). Of total 127 ms, disk pure contribution = only ~25-40 ms.\nLayer 5 — Kernel async I/O + readahead: llama.cpp MAP_PRIVATE + sequential → kernel prefetches during compute; effective disk impact = max(0, disk_time - compute_time) ≈ ~0.\n\nCORRECTED per-token disk demand:\n  1.5 GB naive\n  × 0.07 sparsity     = 105 MB\n  × 0.12 stability    = 13 MB\n  × 0.15 cache hit    = 2 MB\n  overlap w/ compute  → effective 0-2 MB\n@ 7.9 tok/s × 13 MB worst-case steady = 103 MB/s actual disk demand\n= 12% of SanDisk USB 3.2 Gen 2 (836 MB/s) capacity\n= 4% of internal NVMe (2300 MB/s) capacity\n→ both tiers have huge headroom; bandwidth NOT the bottleneck\n\nREAL bottleneck: compute (50-75 ms/token) — storage-tier-independent.\n" :mechanism_evidence_from_measurements "Measurement       Internal NVMe    SanDisk USB 3.2   Delta   Interpretation\nPage faults       2,348,015        2,327,311          -1%    Identical cache miss pattern\nPeak RSS          10.30 GB         9.99 GB            -3%    Both saturate ~10 GB cache budget\nPeak mem fp       7.20 GB          7.20 GB             0%    IDENTICAL working set size\nWall (200 tok)    119.0 sec        127.7 sec          +7%    Cold-load 80 sec disk-bound portion only\nGen tok/s         7.7              7.9                +3%    Run-to-run noise (statistical tie)\nPrompt tok/s      3.2              3.1                -3%    Run-to-run noise\n" :applicability_scope "APPLIES to:\n  - MoE active ratio ≤10% (Gemma 4 26B-A4B, Qwen3.5-A3B, Mixtral 8x7B, GPT-OSS 20B/120B)\n  - Single-session inference (not parallel streams)\n  - Context ≤4K (KV cache must not evict experts from page cache)\n  - Mac mini M4 16GB unified memory class\n\nDOES NOT apply to:\n  - MoE active ratio 20-50% (DeepSeek-V2 21B/236B): sparsity effect halved\n  - Dense models (Llama 3.1 70B, Qwen2.5 72B): all params touched per token, no cache benefit\n  - Long-context (ctx ≥16K): KV cache eviction destroys expert cache\n  - Multi-stream concurrent inference: cache contention destroys hit rate\n  → Dense model substrate validation deferred to R5\n" :implication "TB5/TB4 NVMe upgrade for inference throughput is UNJUSTIFIED for MoE workload on M4 16GB. Only cold-load latency benefits (~80 sec → ~40 sec). For interactive chat UX consider warm-up daemon instead of storage upgrade. Existing USB 3.2 Gen 2 SanDisk Extreme sufficient for batch throughput." :storage_tier_selection_policy ["Interactive chat (first-token-latency critical) → TB5/TB4 NVMe (or warm-up daemon)" "Batch generation (throughput only) → internal NVMe OR USB 3.2 Gen 2 (equivalent)" "Capacity warehouse (multi-GGUF) → cheap USB SSD (SanDisk Extreme class)" "24/7 fleet member (wear protection) → internal NVMe + USB SSD swap offload"] :anti_pattern "Buying TB5 NVMe purely to speed up Gemma 4 26B-A4B inference throughput on Mac mini M4 16GB → empirically +3-5% benefit only. Verify with bench-storage-tier.sh before purchase." :followup_required ["R1: TB4 NVMe single + ×2 別ポート並列 A/B (hardware purchase: Acasis TBU405 / Yottamaster TR1-C4 + WD SN850X 2TB)" "R2: TB5 NVMe single (requires Mac mini M4 Pro upgrade)" "R3: Speculative decoding (draft=gemma3:4b@EVO-X2 / target=gemma-4-26B-A4B@Mac mini)" "R4: Murakumo cell-runner fleet.toml disk-inference node tag + auto-routing" "R5: Dense model (Llama 3.1 70B etc.) disk inference feasibility (working set大、別 carve-out)" "Inline correction of ADR-2605253000 §5 TB5 prediction (separate commit after this ADR accepted)"] :durable_artifacts ["90-docs/adr/2605253015-nvme-disk-inference-substrate-project.md" "70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/README.md (project authoritative doc)" "70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/scripts/cache-flush.sh (14 GB junk evict, user-space)" "70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/scripts/bench-storage-tier.sh (A/B protocol)" "70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/bench/llama-cli-flags.txt (reference invocation + 3-flag rationale)" "70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/results/baseline-260525.md (A/B finding writeup)" "70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/results/internal-cold-260525-2130.txt (raw)" "70-tools/nvme-disk-inference/results/sandisk-cold-260525-2130.txt (raw)"] :process_notes ["Same-session 1-hour-gap correction precedent: ADR-2605253000 §5 prediction (TB5 1.5-1.85×) was empirically falsified within 1 hour of its acceptance via A/B SanDisk test. Future 'prediction' ADRs should declare an empirical validation gate before being treated as actionable. Documented in ADR-2605253015 Consequences/Negative."]}}
